window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2801,"title":"Chapter 2801: Chapter 2753: The Truth","paragraphs":["Contrasting with Zu An’s grim expression was Firework’s beaming smile. “Shouldn’t you look happier? We've finally reunited after such a long time!”","Zu An coldly uttered, “Why should I be happy? Do you know how many people have died trying to save you?”","“Those people harbored ulterior motives. They died because they weren’t strong enough.” Firework was unfazed.","Zu An frowned. Even though those guests did harbor ulterior motives, her words were still displeasing to hear.","Isabella got angry and roared, “Uncle Alfred didn’t harbor ulterior motives, but he met with danger trying to save you. How can you utter such cold words!”","She rarely yelled at others, but she was truly angry this time.","Firework realized she had gone overboard with her joke, so she quickly said, “Calm down, Isabella. Your old butler might not be dead yet.”","“What do you mean?” Isabella wiped her tears as she asked in confusion.","“The spider might have bound them, but it won’t kill them just yet,” Firework replied.","“How do you know?” Isabella recalled the earlier sight of Divine Calculator being slaughtered by the monster, and that made her face turn pale.","“Because you escaped. The monster has plenty of reasons to keep them alive as hostages,” Firework explained.","“Would that bloodthirsty monster have such considerations?” Isabella hoped for that to be the case, but she rationally doubted that possibility.","“Big miss, do you think a being that powerful would have no intelligence?” Firework sighed.","Isabella widened her eyes in realization. That spider was the strongest monster she had ever seen. An entity of this level would be a powerhouse even in the Myriad Worlds. There was no way it would lack intelligence.","Firework turned to Zu An and said, “Big brother Zu, I'm touched. You took such a huge risk to save me.”","Hearing her coy words, Zu An retracted his hand and asked, “Are you in cahoots with that sea monster?”","He hadn’t suspected anything initially, but once he calmed down, he realized there were many dubious points about this incident.","In the first place, it didn’t make sense for such a huge sea monster to approach the beach without alarming any of Dreamland’s experts. It was also weird for the sea monster to hold someone hostage. Furthermore, Firework was no weakling, so for her to have been captured so easily...","There were many anomalies regarding this issue, and he had already thought them through along the way. But considering their prior interactions, he didn’t think Firework would attempt to harm him, so he'd decided to play along and see how the situation unfolded.","He hadn’t expected the journey to be so fraught with dangers.","“The sea monster is indeed my friend. We staged this show to lure you here. Otherwise, you would have turned into a zombie at the Dream Gathering by now.” Firework harrumphed.","“What?” Isabella was taken aback. “Are you saying the Dream Gathering is a scheme?”","“Of course. It’s a play staged to reap the attendees’ souls. Isn’t it laughable how many experts across the Myriad Worlds are aware of its dangers, but they're unable to rein in their greed?” Firework sneered.","Isabella hurriedly turned to Zu An with astonished eyes, only to see him composed, as if he had guessed as much.","“That can’t be right. Dreamland hosts the Dream Gathering once every millennium. It’s one of the most famous gatherings in the Myriad Worlds. How could other powers remain oblivious if there is a problem with it?” Isabella was confused.","“The previous Dream Gatherings were the real deal, but the same cannot be said about those hosted in the recent millennium. Do you know who I am?” Firework asked.","Isabella glanced at Zu An, knowing the two were friends.","But Zu An had only met Firework on the spaceship. He had no way of knowing if the information she'd shared with him was correct or not.","“Let’s see. I’m guessing someone from Dreamland told you that they would be holding their big miss’ coming-of-age ceremony soon, and the Dream Gathering would be held after,” Firework said self-deprecatingly.","A thought popped into Zu An and Isabella’s minds. “You're Dreamland’s big miss?”","“That’s right.” Firework smiled bitterly. “But to the current Dreamland, that is of no significance...”","“If you’re Dreamland’s big miss, who was the person in the hotel?” Isabella found the situation absurd.","“It’s a fake, of course!” Firework sneered. “Everyone you see in Dreamland is an impersonator!”","“Does big sister Yani know about it, too? She saved us many times during our journey here. She’s the guard captain. I don’t think she’d turn a blind eye to the situation,” Isabella asked.","“Yani?” Firework scoffed. She glanced at Zu An. “I bet he already knows what’s going on. Someone like him wouldn’t leave a beauty in the lurch and escape alone.”","Isabella looked at Zu An with confused eyes.","Zu An said, “There is something wrong with Yani.”","After he received the Eye of Truth from the Deity of Memory Meng, he'd returned to the frigate and scanned Yani and all the crew members. To his astonishment, all of them were fakes. But he hadn't known what Yani’s motives were, so he'd chosen to hold his tongue.","But he still didn’t trust Firework yet. The latter hadn’t told them everything yet. “You said you’re Dreamland’s first miss, but Dreamland started meeting with problems a thousand years ago, yet you’re only having your coming-of-age ceremony now. There’s a discrepancy in your age.”","Firework looked at him with an unreadable smile. “How old do you think I am?”","Zu An assessed her. She looks at most sixteen or seventeen.","Firework finally answered the question. “Our Dream Clan has existed since immemorial. We have been around since before the ascension of the universal deities. There are several races like ours in the Myriad Worlds.”","Isabella nodded. As the Acadias’ first miss, she had heard about such races.","Firework looked at Zu An with a mischievous smile. “Unlike short-lived humans like you, our race enjoys a long lifespan. We barely reach adulthood at a thousand years of age.”","Zu An was speechless. You’re even older than my grandmother’s grandmother!","“What happened to Dreamland?”","“My mother died an early death. My father doted on me and refused to remarry, until he suddenly met that woman a thousand years ago. She's beautiful and knows how to charm a person’s heart. My father hasn't been the same since meeting her. He no longer spends time with me and spends his day fawning over that woman.” Firework recalled the past.","“At the start, I was happy for my father, thinking he'd been alone for too many years. Had I known that woman was a venomous scorpion, I would have stopped them.” She gritted her teeth.","“Ever since that woman became Dreamland’s matriarch, bizarre things began happening. Old subordinates loyal to my father suddenly vanished, but they would return shortly after. No one paid it any heed at the start, but thinking back, they must have already become her puppets.”","Isabella asked, “Who’s that woman?”","“You know her, and you have become familiar with her in recent days,” Firework sneered.","A person popped into their minds, and the thought left Zu An and Isabella with goosebumps."]},{"number":2802,"title":"Chapter 2802: Chapter 2754: Life Creation","paragraphs":["“Yani!” Isabella thought about the woman who could shatter space. Even though she was beautiful, it was hard to imagine her as a homewrecker.","Zu An was perplexed as well. He hadn't thought Yani would be into such things.","Firework shook her head. “She approached my father as Diodora.”","Both Zu An and Isabella thought about the seductive female elder who'd appeared at the hotel. Ah, that fits the impression better.","“Hold on.” Isabella thought of a problem. “You said it was someone we have become familiar with recently. Only Yani accompanied us on this voyage.”","“That’s because Diodora and Yani are the same person,” Firework replied with a sigh.","Isabella was stunned. She couldn’t see those two completely different women as the same person. “How is that possible? They appeared in the same place simultaneously, and Yani came out to the ocean with us while Diodora remained in the hotel to host the other guests. If they are the same person, how can she pull that off?”","“That’s her special ability, Life Creation. She's capable of conjuring countless clones. In fact, everyone you've seen in Dreamland, except for the outsiders, is a puppet she conjured.”","The thought that all the staff members she'd met were just clones made shivers run down Isabella’s spine. “I can’t believe no one has been able to see through her tricks. Isn’t her ability too powerful?”","The guests visiting Dreamland were experts from different civilizations. One couldn’t hope to deceive them all with just ordinary clones. Yet not a single person had seen through her act.","Zu An asked, \"Isn't Life Creation an ability rivaling that of the universal deities?”","Destruction was far easier than creation. The creation of life would normally be an ability in the domain of universal deities.","Firework shook her head. “The lives created by universal deities are sentient beings who are capable of growth, perhaps to the extent of becoming universal deities themselves in the future. In contrast, the lives created by Yani are superficial. They aren’t true living beings. Their souls and wills are merely extensions of her own.”","Zu An had met many people in Dreamland thus far, but it had never occurred to him that they were all clones. To play so many characters at once... Isn’t she afraid of developing dissociative personality disorder?","“If she's already replaced everyone in Dreamland, how did you escape from her?” Zu An stared at Firework intently.","“I wasn’t in Dreamland for the last thousand years. My father had sent me away, perhaps because he was worried that I’d get in the way of him and the demoness,” Firework said with a sigh. “It happened that a Beauty worshiper thought I conformed to the dao of beauty and had been inviting me to study with her. My father took this chance to send me to the Deity of Beauty’s academy. That move unexpectedly saved my life.”","“How did you know about what happened in Dreamland?” Isabella asked.","“None of the participants who attended the Dream Gathering a thousand years ago left. We've had participants who relished in the event and were unwilling to leave, but never had all the participants been unwilling to leave before,” Firework said. She continued with a melancholic look, “Several people in the academy asked me about it, but I was confused too. It occurred to me that it had been a long time since my father contacted me, so I tried contacting him through a projection artifact. He acted the same as before, but I knew it wasn’t him.”","Zu An nodded. No matter how good someone’s disguise was, they couldn’t hope to fool their closest kin. He had tried impersonating others, but he had always struggled to fool those who were close with the impersonated.","“Perhaps noticing my skepticism, she sent assassins into the Deity of Beauty’s academy to kill me. Fortunately, perhaps we were too far from Dreamland, or she was afraid of the experts in the academy, so the assassins weren’t too strong. I managed to escape alive. However, I didn’t dare to harbor hope since. I left the Deity of Beauty’s academy to investigate what happened to my homeland.” Firework looked fearful. “I never expected her to wield such a strong ability. I barely escaped with my life many times...”","Zu An could imagine how dangerous the situation had been.","“I've tried verifying it many times over the years, but my final conclusion is that everyone in Dreamland is a puppet.” Firework had always been all smiles, but she couldn’t bring herself to smile at this moment.","“What do you intend to do? Aren’t you leaping straight into danger now?” Zu An asked.","“I planned to use the Dream Gathering to scout my father’s whereabouts. The staff members she conjured might be her clones, but not all of them are linked to her central consciousness. With my aura concealment artifacts, as long as I'm not spotted by the more important figures in Dreamland, she shouldn’t notice me,” Firework explained. “But I don’t have the power to exact vengeance alone, so I was intending to borrow the strength of the experts from the Myriad Worlds. But I didn’t expect the Dream Gathering to be held so soon. There was no time to convince the other guests of the truth, so I could only pretend to be captured by a sea monster to lure you all here, lest you be harmed by the Dream Gathering.\"","Zu An frowned. “What if I hadn’t taken the risk to save you?”","“You’d have died in vain if you were that heartless.” Firework scoffed. She hopped over and grabbed Zu An’s arm. “I knew I didn’t judge you wrongly. You're a true friend. The same goes for big sister Tingxue, too. She might appear cold on the surface, but she still willingly came all the way here to save me.”","Isabella felt stifled, especially when she saw Firework grabbing Zu An’s arm. It feels as if I've been toyed with.","“Unfortunately, Tingxue went missing. I don’t know how she’s faring now.” Zu An was worried.","“That woman was intimidated by big sister Tingxue’s strength, so I had to separate big sister Tingxue from the rest of the group. Don’t worry. Considering her strength, big sister Tingxue has to be safe. It’s only a matter of time before she breaks free,” Firework consoled him.","Zu An was relieved to hear that Tingxue was safe. “So, what will happen at the Dream Gathering? Why will all the attendees die?”","Firework sighed. “We, the Dream Clan, have the unique ability of dreamweaving. We can weave beautiful dreams that our guests relish. Many people refuse to wake up from them of their own volition. Since that demoness took control of Dreamland, she's been exploiting this opportunity to devour our guests’ souls, causing our guests to die amid their dreams.”"]},{"number":2803,"title":"Chapter 2803: Chapter 2755: Main Body","paragraphs":["“She devours their souls?” Isabella’s face paled in fright.","Zu An was disappointed. “Your Dream Clan’s ability is to weave dreams? So, it’s all fake?”","He'd come here to find ways to help Chu Chuyan and Mi Li, as well as to see if there was a way he could reunite with the ancient Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain. If the Dream Clan was only capable of weaving dreams, that wouldn’t solve his problems. What was the point of only finding solutions in his dreams?","Firework indignantly retorted, “Dreamweaving isn’t meaningless. It comforts wounded souls and brings peace and solace to those who have been through too much. Our dreams also guide one toward the future they seek.”","Zu An narrowed his eyes. “Your dreams can guide one toward a certain future?”","At this point, Isabella interjected, “Big brother Zu, I have heard about their ability and even asked my father about it. Their ability is indeed extraordinary. It is on par with powerful divination methods. They first ascertain the outcome before influencing causality toward it.”","Fearing her explanation was too vague, she listed an example, “If the Dream Clan declares that someone is going to die, that person’s enemies might be compelled to do everything they can to kill them. Or if the clan declares that someone is going to live, even if that person is terminally ill, they might encounter all kinds of fortuitous encounters that will eventually save their life.”","“How mysterious...” Zu An wasn't unfamiliar with such divination methods. His ‘Keyboard Come’ turned his declarations into reality. He asked the crucial question, “Can you fulfill all dreams?”","“Of course not,” Firework replied bitterly. “That demoness would have been dead by now if it were that easy. We can only guide a person’s dream, and the process will consume one’s karma. The greater the wish, the more karma is required. Furthermore, if one fails to fulfill the dream, one will suffer a severe backlash.”","Zu An nodded. It was the same for ‘Keyboard Come’; it was just that he hadn’t figured out what the standard for quantification was.","“What is karma?” he asked. He wondered if ‘Keyboard Come’ depleted a similar resource. If he could make sense of this, he could better control ‘Keyboard Come’ and not risk disintegration each time.","Firework explained, “Many believe that karma is about doing good and accruing virtue, but heaven is dispassionate. In truth, kindness may carry no karma, whereas committing evil deeds like going on a massacre may result in a lot of karma. Karma is generated based on whether one's deeds are beneficial to the world.","“If an Annihilation worshiper goes on a massacre on an overpopulated and overdeveloped planet, this might seem like an evil deed, but from the world’s point of view, it is considered a good deed.”","Zu An fell into deep thought. These words had opened his eyes, as he had never considered things from that perspective. It reminded him of the concept of ‘heaven’s will’, which the people of the Cultivation World often talked about. It wasn't necessarily tangible, but it most definitely existed.","If a world can possess a will, how can an entire universe not possess a will, too? Perhaps universal deities might even be a manifestation of some will.","Isabella asked, “Have you gathered any news about your father yet?”","“Through my skills and years of investigation, I have gathered some news. My father should be alive. That demoness likely has him imprisoned somewhere. I wanted to lure big brother Zu and big sister Tingxue here to help with the investigation, but I never expected to draw the demoness here as well,” Firework said with a sigh.","“It’s a good thing she was captured by the spider. You don’t have to worry about her anymore,” Isabella consoled her, though that also reminded her about Alfred’s capture and her expression darkened.","“That demoness wouldn’t die that easily. The spider merely captured a clone. It won’t affect her main body.” Firework harrumphed.","“Where’s her main body?” Isabella was confused. “Do we have to kill all the staff members in Dreamland to kill her for good?”","Firework shook her head. “I don’t know where her main body is either. I've been investigating her for many years now, but I was unable to trace her background or the origin of her abilities.”","Zu An suddenly spoke up. “I know where her main body is.”","“You do?” Firework was perplexed. She had investigated this matter for many years, but to no avail, yet Zu An had uncovered it within days of arriving at Dreamland?","Faced with the two women’s curious gazes, Zu An looked in the direction they had come from and said, “Her main body is right here.”","“Right here?” Firework’s hair stood on end. She glanced at Isabella, wondering if the latter had been controlled by the demoness as well.","Isabella also stared at Firework in horror. She instinctively stuck closer to Zu An.","Taking in their reactions, Zu An laughed. “It’s not what you’re thinking. Yani is that spider outside.”","“What?!” The two women exclaimed in horror, especially Firework. She had seen Yani fighting valiantly against the spider earlier, so she struggled to come to terms with the idea that they were the same entity.","“I have an ability that allows me to see through all facades. From the first time I met Yani, she was already a demon spider.”","After Zu An obtained the Eye of Truth, he'd inspected everyone on board. That was why he knew something was amiss with Yani and the crew members. He'd seen a spider silhouette behind Yani, but didn’t understand what it meant at first. It was only after seeing the terrifying demon spider that he'd made sense of the situation.","“Big brother Zu, how do you have so many special abilities?” Isabella was amazed.","She had met many experts who were far stronger than Zu An, but none of them had as many methods as him. Perhaps he appeared weak, but he wouldn't necessarily lose to those experts in an all-out fight!","“Spider. Puppets. Control...” Firework looked shaken up. “You’re right. Why did I never think of that? But why is she doing all of this when she’s already this powerful?”"]},{"number":2804,"title":"Chapter 2804: Chapter 2756: Sandwiched","paragraphs":["Zu An replied, “Even powerhouses have their own problems. She might be strong, but she’s bound to have enemies who are as strong as her, not to mention the universal deities.”","The two women agreed. Their information was limited. There was no point speculating about the demoness’ motive.","“Why don’t we rescue my father first? We’ll stand a better chance against the demoness with his strength and knowledge,” Firework said with a hopeful gleam in her eyes.","“Have you found your father’s whereabouts?” Zu An agreed that her father, as Dreamland’s master, would have a better idea as to how they could quell the demoness.","“I don’t have a concrete location yet, but I have some clues,” Firework replied.","“Alright. Let’s try rescuing your father first.” Zu An knew there was no other solution at hand. That demon spider transcended the concept of strong and weak. There was no way they could defeat it, so their only option was to find other solutions.","Isabella meekly asked, “Will you help me save Uncle Alfred after we rescue your father?”","“That goes without saying!” Firework exclaimed. “We’re in the same boat now. We’ll definitely save Uncle Alfred after rescuing my father.”","Firework’s guarantee brought Isabella relief. Isabella perked herself up and said, “Alright, let’s go rescue your father!”","Firework led the two of them down a convoluted path, until they finally arrived before a door. She peeked outside the door and cursed, “Damn. There are many small spiders outside.”","Zu An took a look outside. There were indeed many little spiders scuttling around, searching for their whereabouts.","“These little spiders don’t seem too strong. Why don’t we...”","Before Isabella could finish her sentence, Firework interjected, “That won’t do. Their consciousness is linked to the demon spider. If we attack the small spiders, the bigger spider will immediately be alerted to our location. That’ll spell the end of us.”","“Are there any other paths?”","“There’s no way to go around this path.”","“I have some concealment artifacts.”","“That won’t work. These spiders don’t rely on vision. Normal concealment artifacts won’t conceal our presence from that demoness.”","Isabella looked defeated. “I guess we can only wait for the small spiders to leave on their own accord.”","But the three of them knew that was unlikely to happen.","“I have an idea,” Zu An said.","Isabella exclaimed in delight, “You’re incredible, big brother Zu.”","Even Firework was amazed. How is this fellow so resourceful?","Zu An spent a moment in thought before asking, “Isabella, do you have artifacts that can completely remove light from the surroundings?” It’s a pity Manman isn’t here, or else I could have used Fu Hao’s owl statue [1] .","“I have something like that, but didn’t big sister Firework mention earlier that the little spiders don’t rely on vision?” Isabella pulled out a black jewel from her bag. Their surroundings were immediately plunged into darkness.","Zu An was overjoyed. Isabella’s bag is truly like Doraemon’s pouch. It has everything inside!","“I don’t know if it’s enough to fool the demon spider. Let me give it a try first.”","He had the ability to meld into the darkness, such that no one could find him in a dark environment, but the demon spider was so strong that he wasn’t confident he could fool the other party with it.","Firework and Isabella exclaimed, “Be careful!”","Even so, they understood that they were in dire straits, and they had no choice but to take risks. Isabella handed the black jewel to Zu An and was shocked to see him disappear right before her eyes.","The two women exchanged delighted looks. There might be a chance.","Moments later, Zu An returned and stowed away the black jewel, thus revealing himself. He said with a voice tinged with excitement, “I just gave it a try. The spiders couldn’t see me.”","It was already dark outside, so the spiders hadn’t noticed anything amiss even when he used the dark jewel.","“How did you do it?” Firework asked excitedly.","“I have an ability that allows me to meld into darkness.”","“How many more abilities do you have that we don’t know about?”","An ability that could deceive the demon spider’s senses had to be of the highest caliber. This man carried many secrets, and that made him fatally charming to them.","“But what about us?” Isabella asked with a pitiful frown. “We don’t have such an ability.”","Zu An pulled out a cloak from his Brilliant Glass Bead and said, “Don’t worry, I’ll take you out. It might be a bit uncomfortable, but bear with it.”","He had once successfully carried Shang Liuyu with him using this method.","He had also considered putting an item far away and taking the two women out of here using the position swap skill, but he'd decided against that. He had to extend his divine sense to use his position swap, and that could alert the demon spider to their presence.","Firework excitedly climbed onto Zu An’s back and said, “This looks fun. Isabella, you can take the front.”","“All right.” Isabella’s face reddened, and she bit her lip. She knew this wasn’t the time to be kicking up a fuss, so she slipped into Zu An’s arms. His warmth made her face redden further, and her heart couldn’t stop beating.","Zu An took in the fragrances of both women, and it stirred something in his heart. Even the coolest man would struggle to remain calm when he was sandwiched between two youthful and vibrant ladies.","He had planned to carry both women in front, but Firework had climbed onto his back and was hugging him like a sloth. He decided to let her do whatever she wanted. He took in a deep breath and told himself not to focus on the amazing buoyancy pressing against him.","“Don’t make any noise later on.”","“Orh~” the two women replied in unison.","Zu An took out the black jewel and plunged the surroundings into darkness. He melded into the darkness and walked out.","He had to proceed slowly because the area was filled with little spiders. Perhaps they wouldn't be able to sense him, but if he touched them carelessly, they would notice him right away. Furthermore, there were invisible spider threads hanging along the corridor. Touching them would alert the demon spider as well.","Luckily, he had a strong constitution, and he'd scouted the traps earlier. Otherwise, it would have been a struggle to carry these two women along while making precise movements.","He suddenly felt an itch from behind. Firework was writing on his back, “You have an amazing waist.”","He'd had to bend his body at a gravity-defying angle earlier to avoid a dense congregation of spiderwebs.","Zu An was speechless. This lass sure is something to joke under such circumstances. Luckily, we’re almost out of this corridor.","Just then, a slightly larger spider sensed something and looked in their direction.","For a moment there, Zu An’s blood nearly froze.","1. Chapter 556: Pei Mianman obtained it from a tomb, and it allows her to see in the dark. ☜"]},{"number":2805,"title":"Chapter 2805: Chapter 2757: A Special Bridge","paragraphs":["Despite knowing it made no difference, Zu An held his breath and kept completely still, fearing that his movements would further alarm the slightly larger spider.","The spider stood there, looking in their direction with an entire row of eyes. Moments later, it began moving toward the three of them.","Zu An was horrified. He stared intently at the spider, not daring to make a reckless move.","The spider soon arrived before him, looking confused. It extended its chelicerae over.","Zu An barely avoided the spider’s chelicerae by leaning backward. He could sense their hairs less than a centimeter away from him. Even so, he maintained his composure and didn’t make any overly large movements, lest the other party sense something.","The spider moved its chelicerae around the vicinity, which Zu An dodged by carefully maneuvering his body. In the end, the spider didn’t find anything, lost interest, and scuttled off elsewhere.","Zu An didn’t move right away. He waited for the spider to fully depart before flitting out of the corridor. When they were finally out of danger, he put Isabella and Firework down. Both their faces were as red as apples. The earlier intimate contact was too much stimulation for them.","“That scared me!” Isabella patted her chest. Her cultivation was high enough to see through absolute darkness, and she'd gotten a clear enough view of the earlier situation to understand how close of a shave they'd had earlier.","“I thought that demon spider found us!” Firework stuck out her tongue. She regretted teasing Zu An earlier, which had nearly resulted in them being discovered.","“It’s a relief we survived the ordeal. I don’t think there are any spiders here.” Zu An scanned their surroundings. There were no spiders ahead of them; only fog.","This fog was different from the one they'd encountered on the ocean. Zu An felt a burning sensation on his skin, which was astounding considering his body’s sturdiness and poison resistance. The fog had to be extremely poisonous.","“Careful. This miasma corrodes one’s ki, flesh, and blood, reducing one to a pile of bones.” Firework spotted a few skeletons lying not too far away. Those had to be people who had reached this point but died to the miasma.","Isabella took out three jewels from her bag. “These are Poison Warding Beads. They should provide you with immunity to most poisons in the Myriad Worlds.”","They'd worked on all known poisons to date, but there were too many unknown things in the Myriad Worlds, so she didn’t dare to speak of it in absolute terms.","Firework was awed. “I’d expect no less from the Universal Conglomerate’s big miss. You have all kinds of treasures stashed away.”","Isabella’s face reddened. “Don’t tease me, big sister Firework. Aren’t you Dreamland’s big miss as well? Dreamland is a place countless in the Myriad Worlds look forward to.”","“But Dreamland has fallen. A demoness has taken control of it,” Firework said with a sigh.","“I’m sorry, big sister Firework...” Isabella was apologetic for mentioning something upsetting.","“Don’t worry about it. I've gotten used to it. I should be thanking you for helping me instead.” Firework quickly regained her smile.","Thanks to the Poison Warding Beads, they were able to travel within the miasma without suffering from its poison. Thus, they explored the area and quickly found their surroundings weirdly familiar.","“Another labyrinth?” Isabella frowned. The earlier labyrinth had nearly traumatized her. They had barely found the exit, only to bump into that terrifying demon spider.","Zu An shook his head. “It’s not a labyrinth. It’s just a trick of the eye.”","Proper labyrinths couldn’t be easily overcome unless one understood the trick behind them. This place was different. It merely induced a sensation that made one feel as if one were moving in circles.","Such tricks would be harder for others to unravel, but Zu An had the Eye of Truth. He could see through all trickery and deception. Worried that the two ladies would lose their way, he grabbed their hands and led the way.","“Are you taking advantage of Isabella now?” Firework teased.","Isabella’s face heated up. “Aren’t you holding his hand too?”","Firework was unfazed. “We’re close. It’s normal for us to hold hands.”","Isabella bit her lip, not knowing how to reply.","“Stop teasing her.” Zu An glared at Firework.","Firework stuck out her tongue as she turned her attention to the road he walked. Zu An paid no heed to the convoluted paths and walked straight in a single direction. Twice, the ladies noticed him leading them into a wall, but for some reason, they didn’t bump into it. The wall turned out to be an illusion, and there was a path through it.","It didn’t take long for the miasma to scatter. The convoluted labyrinth disappeared, replaced by a massive underground rift valley. The area beneath was cloaked in darkness, as if it were a pathway into the netherworld.","The rift valley was shrouded in demonic air, death energy, and similar energies that were uncomfortable to the living. Their divine senses could only sense what was within a fifty-meter radius. A bizarre wind blew, carrying with it terrifying noises reminiscent of demonic murmurs.","Those noises made Isabella shudder. She pressed closer to Zu An and grabbed his arm.","Zu An scanned the rift valley. The rift was so wide that he couldn’t see what was on the other side. He could only see eight chains extending from one side to the other, as if they were bridges linking both ends.","He couldn’t recognize the material the chains were made out of, but he could tell they were a precious material. They were densely inscribed with ancient runes that subtly moved as if they were breathing. They felt old and solemn.","“Are you sure your father is imprisoned here?” Zu An asked Firework. For some reason, he felt intimidated by the chains.","“I've investigated this place for many years, but the opposite side of the rift valley is the only place I have yet to check. If the demoness has imprisoned him, that is the best place for her to do so,” Firework said.","She could also tell this place was dangerous."]},{"number":2806,"title":"Chapter 2806: Chapter 2758: Choosing Life and Death","paragraphs":["“Should I head to the other side of the chain to take a look first?” Firework looked around but couldn’t find another path. In the end, she had to set her eyes back on the eight chains. It wasn't a real bridge, but with her cultivation, crossing a chain wouldn’t pose a challenge.","Zu An stopped her. “We can’t see what lies beneath the rift valley, and there’s something amiss about the chains, too. It’s too dangerous to cross it.”","“We won’t achieve anything standing around like this.” Firework’s worry about her father’s safety stoked her anxiety.","“I have an idea.” Isabella reached into her bag and pulled out a metal sphere. “This is a Planet Detector. It can withstand extreme environments, from a star's heat to the depths of space. Its unique material also allows it to withstand an expert’s full-powered attack for an hour. We can use it to scout the situation.”","Zu An took a second look at her bag. How can such a small bag store so many treasures? As expected of the Acadias’ big miss!","Firework hugged her and said teasingly, “I’m starting to get tempted by your bag. So much so that I want to snatch it over.”","Isabella shook her head. “It won’t work even if you snatch it from me. This Bag of Treasures is bound to my soul. Only I can open it.”","Firework was speechless. A long time later, she retorted, “As expected of the Acadias’ big miss. You’re so innocent that I can’t bear to bully you.”","Isabella blinked in confusion. She didn’t understand what those words meant.","Her Planet Detector flew above the rift valley and emitted a red light to scan the environment. Soon, Zu An and the others received some images.","It was then that an anomaly happened. A light wind blew, and the Planet Detector, crafted to withstand extreme environments, tried its best to maintain its position. Even so, it only lasted a second before crumbling into countless parts that fell into the rift valley.","Firework was intrigued. “Didn’t you say it could withstand the attacks of an expert for an hour?”","Isabella’s face reddened. She'd still been bragging about her gear’s functionality a second ago, only for it to unravel to a light wind right away. She spent a moment in thought before taking out the Wind Quelling Pearl. “Let me try with this.”","Zu An stopped her. “I’ll do it.”","Isabella wasn't weak by any means, but she'd grown up in a sheltered environment and lacked ferocity and tenacity. It was too much to ask her to do something this dangerous on the spur of the moment.","Isabella handed the Wind Quelling Pearl to him. “Big brother Zu, you’re more capable than me. I’m sure you can do it.”","Before Zu An stepped onto the chains, Firework suddenly stopped him. “Hold on, big brother Zu. Have you wondered why there are eight chains here instead of one?”","Zu An widened his eyes. Indeed. Anyone with the means to reach this place can’t be ordinary. If they wanted to make a bridge, a single chain would have sufficed. Yet there are eight chains here. Do seven of the chains lead to doom, and only one leads to our destination?","The first thing he thought about was the Eight Trigrams, but there was no other commonality between that and the eight chains other than the number eight.","“Big brother Zu, can you see the right path with your Eye of Truth?” Isabella asked.","Zu An shook his head. “These chains are real objects and not illusions.”","“What should we do? There might not be a second chance if we choose the wrong chain.” Isabella panicked. They had witnessed the fate of her Planet Detector. Even if the Wind Quelling Pearl could suppress the wind, there could be other threats awaiting them on the chains.","Just then, Firework began singing. It was a peculiar song with bizarre intonations, but it induced a feeling of relaxation in the listeners.","Zu An looked at the golden notes gathering around him and quickly understood what was going on. “Is it a blessing?”","Firework smiled sweetly. “Have you forgotten I’m from Dreamland, too? I just used an ability passed down within my clan. I've just bestowed you with great fortune. I’m sure you’ll be able to choose the right chain now.”","Zu An remembered that the Dream Clan had the ability to consume their karma to influence cause and effect to help others achieve their goals.","“But your karma...” Zu An was worried. Those who depleted their karma would be condemned to terrible luck. The backlash wasn't something to be joked about.","“Don’t worry, I can take it,” Firework replied with a smile. “Our ability only guides cause and effect, but it doesn’t ensure the outcome. To increase the chances of success, you’ll have to employ your own methods and do everything you can to improve the odds.\"","Zu An nodded. Basically, the Dream Clan’s ability greatly increased one's chances of success, but nothing would happen if one remained idle. Only by doing everything within one’s means to fulfill the theoretical possibility of success would the effect of the blessing be magnified.","Zu An tried to analyze the chains. He was adept at formations, and he suspected the eight chains were imbued with formations. The runes on each chain were different, so they could each have different effects. Those effects would be triggered once he stepped on the chains.","Too bad my knowledge of runes is only superficial at best. If Xie Daoyun were here, given her experience as Yumen Beiqing, she might just be able to read the runes and derive the functions of the ones on each chain.","Wait, with her main body being a talisman paper, Jing Teng might also see through the runes.","Unlike his other lovers, he'd been able to bring Jing Teng into Dreamland as it was unlikely Dreamland’s staff would find her, given her main body was a talisman paper; not to mention that she was hiding in the blessed cave inside the pendant.","He was about to call Jing Teng out when he remembered the two ladies he was with. Ugh, it might be another bloodbath. And there’s no guarantee she can read the runes...","Hold on, I have The Book!","The Book was capable of prophesizing future danger. Wasn’t his current one-in-eight selection the perfect place for it to shine?","So, he walked to the leftmost chain and raised his foot. An image of him plummeting into the rift valley surfaced in his head.","Not this one.","He moved on to the second chain and did the same. He saw himself going berserk and his soul being siphoned dry, eventually ending up as a mindless zombie.","Zu An was speechless. Not this one either!","While The Book could foretell the future, it could only read what would happen in the next few seconds. It was likely due to the Dream Clan’s blessing that he could peer into the future so clearly.","For the third chain, he saw his flesh being sliced away by an invisible power until he was reduced to a skeleton.","He did the same for the remaining chains, and they all showed him a tragic way to die. By the time he was done testing the eighth chain, his face paled in horror. “How can this be?”"]},{"number":2807,"title":"Chapter 2807: Chapter 2759: White Bones","paragraphs":["“What’s wrong?” The two women were taken aback by his reaction.","Zu An explained severely, “I have the ability to foresee danger, and with Firework’s blessing, I was able to see further ahead than I usually can. I foresaw my death on every chain I stepped on, and every death was as tragic as could be.”","“How’s that possible?” Isabella’s face paled. She grabbed Zu An’s arm. “You shouldn’t go then. It’s a path of certain death.”","Firework frowned. “It doesn’t make sense for all eight paths to lead to death. Big brother Zu, try to look back on what you saw. Do none of the routes provide a hope of survival?”","Zu An shook his head as he shared his deaths for each of the eight chains. He then said, “If there’s a chain that offers a glimmer of hope, it would be the first one. I didn’t witness my death after plummeting into the rift valley. There might be a shot at surviving after falling in there.”","Firework stopped him. “No, that won’t do. The rift valley is too dangerous. Even its wind carries immense destructive power. You’ll die a tragic death if you fall in there.”","“Indeed!” Isabella exclaimed. She held onto Zu An, afraid that he would recklessly attempt the first chain.","“But we’ll be dead meat if we return without giving it a try,” Zu An replied worriedly. It hadn’t been easy for them to get here, and the terrifying demon spider was waiting for them behind. They didn’t stand a chance against the spider. He was the type to choose to gamble instead of facing certain death.","“Big brother Zu, aren’t you capable of instantaneous movement and swapping positions? Can’t you move to the other side right away?” Isabella suggested.","“Those skills are limited to the range of my divine sense, but I’m only able to extend my divine sense across fifty meters here. It isn’t enough for me to reach the opposite side.” Zu An shook his head.","Isabella crumbled into despair.","Firework pondered about it and asked, “Big brother Zu, is it possible that one of the chains doesn’t lead to certain death? Perhaps the vision you saw wasn’t the end. Try to look back on what you saw. It might be possible that you came back to life in one of the visions.”","Zu An widened his eyes as he remembered the words Yumen Beiqing had left him back then: ‘ The end can also be the beginning’ . He should have understood that better than anyone, being a Time Scribe as well as an Enigma and Chaos envoy.","Indeed. What I saw might not necessarily spell death. Let me see which situation I could possibly come back to life in.","Realization struck him moments later.","“Allow me a moment of silence.” Zu An walked up to the cliff and stared at the chains contemplatively.","Firework and Isabella held their breaths and kept completely silent lest they disrupt him.","In truth, Zu An wasn't doing any thinking. Instead, he took out his Spring and Autumn Brush and Time Annal[1]. He wrote a sentence in it. Moments later, he walked up to the third chain.","Seeing this, Isabella exclaimed with a quivering voice, “No! Your flesh will be sliced off and you’ll turn into a skeleton!”","Even Firework asked, “Are you sure that’s the right chain?”","Zu An replied, “I practice a unique cultivation skill. I won’t die even when reduced to a skeleton.”","The Primordial Origin Sutra granted him tremendous regenerative prowess, whereas his position as the Netherworld’s master gave him a deeper grasp of death than anyone else.","“That might be true elsewhere, but it’s too dangerous here.” Isabella’s eyes were filled with concern.","Zu An agreed that this place couldn’t be evaluated with common sense. To be safe, he squeezed out a droplet of blood essence and handed it to Isabella. “If a mishap happens, put this blood essence droplet on my skeleton. It will bring me back to life.”","Isabella bit her lips and nodded. I’ll guard this blood essence droplet with my life.","“Since you've made up your mind...” Firework bit her lips as she activated her Dream Clan’s blessing once more. “...I’m sure you’ll succeed!”","A golden light shrouded Zu An. All their lives were at stake here, so he didn’t stand on ceremony. He patted her shoulder before making his way to the third chain. He lifted his foot and stepped on it.","The old, grayish chain lit up, bringing slight illumination to the thick darkness. Runes flowed across its surface like water.","Unfortunately, the light appeared to have drawn the notice of something beneath the rift valley. Several eerie red lights glowed below. Sometimes, there were also flickering green lights that resembled the eyes of terrifying behemoths. This made the sinister environment feel even more stifling and nerve-wracking.","Isabella nervously followed Firework to the edge of the cliff. They didn’t dare breathe loudly, fearing that they would alarm Zu An. They clenched their fists so tightly that their nails were digging into their flesh.","A strange wind blew up from the rift valley. Recalling that was how her Planet Detector had shattered, Isabella was so nervous that her heart thumped up into her throat.","Zu An lifted the Wind Quelling Pearl he'd received from Isabella. The destructive wind assailed him, but it couldn’t breach the space within a meter of him. In the end, it slowly dissipated.","The two women on the cliff’s edge exhaled in relief. It’s good that the Wind Quelling Pearl works.","Zu An continued his journey.","More gusts of wind blew up from the rift valley, each one stronger than the previous. However, they were unable to breach the safety zone created by the Wind Quelling Pearl. Eventually, the wind died down as if it understood the futility of its endeavor.","Even so, Zu An showed no relief, as the wind dying down suggested that the attacks were coming from a sentient being. Could there be something below?","But it was too late for regrets. He could only muster his courage and march on.","As he advanced further, the runes on the chain grew brighter. Zu An felt immense pressure crushing him, so much so that it eroded his cultivation. He should have been strong enough to easily flit across even a metal wire, but with the unraveling of his cultivation, the stress he was under amplified greatly. He felt as if he was marching with a mountain on his back.","The previously stable chain shook violently, and it looked as if he would fall at any moment. Furthermore, he felt countless malevolent gazes staring at him from the shadows around him. Fear, regret, and despair gripped his mind.","I shouldn’t have come here. Why did I take such a huge risk to save someone else’s father? Maybe it’s not too late to turn back.","...","Doubts gushed into his mind, and they only made the chain shake more.","“Big brother Zu!”","“Be careful!”","Zu An suddenly heard the familiar cry of a bird. Hundredwarble unfurled its wings and soared into the sky. The miscellaneous voices distracting him slowly quieted down, and his eyes regained clarity.","I’m not just saving someone else’s father. I’m saving myself, too!","His willpower had been tempered by countless life-and-death situations. It didn’t take long for him to dispel unnecessary thoughts and continue on with stable footsteps.","But Isabella clutched her mouth. She saw Zu An’s flesh disappearing with each step that he took, such that even his bones could be vaguely seen.","1. Chapter 2631. These two tools are used together to allow him to turn whatever is written into reality, but it has to be within reasonable grounds. It’s similar to Keyboard Come, but he doesn’t have to pay a price straight away. Instead, he risks suffering a backlash if the outcome is not ‘plausible’ enough. ☜"]},{"number":2808,"title":"Chapter 2808: Chapter 2760: Chang’e and the Goddess of Wu Mountain","paragraphs":["To Isabella’s bewilderment, Zu An continued advancing as if he was unaware of his disappearing flesh. She shouted, “Big brother Zu! Big brother Zu!”","No matter how she shouted, Zu An didn’t respond. He had entered another space. He was no longer walking on the chain; instead, he was on the moon. The surroundings were frigid, and the space was barren except for a nearly withered osmanthus tree.","There was a palace in the distance, and he was excited to see it. It was the Frost Palace.","He had been wanting to meet Chang’e, also known as the ancient Mermaid Queen Gong Suyin, once more. He ran over, but to his astonishment, he couldn’t open the door no matter how he pushed.","“Suyin! Suyin!” He knocked on the door and shouted.","Moments later, a perplexed voice echoed, “Who are you?”","Zu An was excited to hear that familiar voice. “Suyin, I am Zu An!”","“Zu An?” The person inside murmured the name. Moments later, she replied, “I don’t know you.”","Zu An was taken aback, but he quickly realized what was going on. “I’m sorry, Suyin. I know you’re angry at me, but I have been looking for ways to return, albeit to no avail. It’s only now that I’m able to reach you.”","His heart was filled with guilt. It didn’t occur to him how he had gotten here in the first place.","The door finally opened, and a woman dressed traditionally walked out. She had well-sculpted eyebrows reminiscent of a painting, and her robes fluttered gracefully. She was ravishing.","The sight of her made Zu An gasp. He leaped forward to hug her.","But the other party dodged with a cold expression. “Please have some self-respect, sir!”","“Suyin, it’s me!” Zu An was appalled.","“Suyin... You kept calling me Suyin, but I’m afraid you've gotten the wrong person. I’m not Suyin. I am Chang’e,” the beautiful woman replied with a frown. “But Suyin sounds familiar. I appear to have heard the name somewhere.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat as he realized she wasn't putting on an act. “You are Chang’e, but you are also the ancient Mermaid Queen Gong Suyin...”","He told her about their transmigration into the past, how she had become the Chang clan’s saintess, and how she had been forced to consume the immortal medicine and ended up being trapped in the Frost Palace.","“It’s an interesting story...” The beautiful woman nodded.","Noticing her composure, Zu An’s heart sank. “It’s not a story. It’s what happened between us.”","The woman eyed him. “Your words spark some memories in me. I have been waiting for someone all these years. Are you that person?”","Zu An became excited once more. “That’s right! Have you remembered it?”","“I do remember it. I remember how grueling the first thousand years were. Every time I heard the wind blow and the grass rustle, I’d think you had returned. But each time I opened the door, there was no one there. It was an endless cycle of disappointment.”","“I’m sorry.”","“You don’t have to apologize. It’s all in the past.”","“...”","“The following ten thousand years weren’t easy either. By then, I had stopped rushing to the door whenever I heard any movements outside because I feared disappointment.”","“Another hundred thousand years passed afterward. I thus lost all expectations. I knew you would never come, but I still continued to wait out of habit. Even our image started to blur in my mind. I tried to draw you, but I could never get your face.","“In the next three hundred thousand years, I forgot about my wait and our past. I grew accustomed to my life in the Frost Palace.”","Her words plunged Zu An’s heart into ice.","“I’m sorry, Suyin. You waited in agony for so many years because I came too late.” Zu An looked distraught. That was three hundred thousand years! What a despair-inducingly long time that was!","The beautiful woman shook her head. “You don’t have to apologize to me. It has all come to pass. I have grown accustomed to all these things. Time can indeed heal all pain. I no longer feel pain or excitement when I recall the past; there is only serenity.”","Zu An wanted to say something, but the beautiful woman turned around and left. The door slowly closed. “You should leave. That was an immature relationship from three hundred thousand years ago. I have lived for far too long; the days I spent with you are insignificant in comparison. The current me harbors no feelings for you. Farewell.”","The moment the door closed, Zu An felt as if someone had plunged a blade into his heart.","He couldn’t criticize Gong Suyin. What promise could possibly withstand the trial of three hundred thousand years? He only had himself to blame for losing her and failing to find her for so many years.","The next second, the world warped. He found himself transported from the lifeless Frost Palace to a verdant mountain shrouded in clouds. The grass and trees here felt familiar. His heart skipped a beat. This is Wu Mountain.","He anxiously rushed to the mountain peak to look at the beautiful Goddess Peak.","“You’re finally here,” a gentle voice said with a sigh.","Goddess Peak turned around to look at him as if it had come to life.","Zu An asked with a quivering voice, “Is it you, Yaoji?”","“Have you forgotten me...” the voice sounded begrudging.","“No, I was afraid you would forget me.” Zu An recalled his earlier encounter at the Frost Palace, and that filled his heart with pain.","“How could I ever forget you? I have been waiting for you. But I am stuck in this ugly form now.” The Goddess Peak sounded downtrodden. Dark clouds appeared around the Wu Mountain and drizzled, as if the goddess herself was weeping.","“Are you unable to revert to your human form?” Zu An asked fearfully.","“Too much time has passed. Has it been three hundred thousand years? I envy Chang’e. She consumed the immortal medicine and haf an eternity to wait for you, but I was unable to live that long. I could only morph into the Goddess Peak and await your arrival.","“But still, it has been too long. My sentience is about to dissipate,” the Goddess Peak lamented.","“What?!” Zu An hadn’t expected such an outcome for their reunion. He cast his avatar to expand his body, so he could embrace the Goddess Peak as if it was the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","“Don’t weep. I am glad that I was able to meet you right before I dissipate.” Her voice was as gentle and ethereal as ever."]},{"number":2809,"title":"Chapter 2809: Chapter 2761: The Undying Skeleton","paragraphs":["“How can I save you? Will an immortal medicine work?” Zu An thought of the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine and the other legendary immortal medicines. The only thought on his mind was how he could save Yaoji.","“I’m a mountain peak now. What can an immortal medicine do to help?” It sounded as if the Goddess of Wu Mountain was smiling at him. “Ah Zu, don’t grieve for me. I’m already happy that you could make it here before my final moments.”","Zu An embraced her tightly as tears rained down his cheeks. “It’s all my fault. I should have found you earlier. Suyin has forgotten everything, and now you’re leaving me too...”","“Don’t blame her. I remembered because I morphed into a mountain peak, but it’s different for her. She might have consumed the immortal medicine and attained eternal life, but over time, her memories were bound to fade. It’s normal for her to forget about the history you shared and the feelings she had for you.”","“I never blamed her. I only blame myself.”","Zu An wanted to say more, but the Goddess Peak suddenly morphed into the appearance of the Goddess of Wu Mountain. She gently placed her hand on Zu An’s cheek and said, “Farewell, my love...”","Zu An was alarmed. He reached out to grab her, but he failed to grab anything. His lover dissipated into countless specks of starlight and vanished into thin air. His outstretched hand froze in midair. Despair crashed down on him.","Perhaps he'd accomplished much in his life, but what was the point if he couldn’t even save the women he loved? He might as well die.","As this thought surfaced, his body began to disintegrate. His flesh and blood broke down, but he no longer cared. There was no longer joy in life, so why should there be fear in death?","His mistake had caused Chang’e and the Goddess of Wu Mountain to wait for a long time. Chang’e no longer remembered him, and the Goddess of Wu Mountain had passed away.","I've kept her waiting alone for such a long time, so how can I let her leave alone?","He watched as his body broke down into a skeleton, but he only felt at ease.","So be it...","But to the spectating Isabella and Firework, they felt as if their world was on the verge of collapse. To them, Zu An had been walking along the chain when he suddenly trembled as if he had encountered something shocking. His body and flesh began to disintegrate, revealing his bones.","The plan had been for Zu An to use his unique cultivation skill to repair his body, but he stood motionless, as if he had given up on himself.","Isabella shouted in a panic, but no matter how she strained her throat, her voice didn’t seem to reach Zu An.","Firework went over to her side and spoke commandingly, “Hand his blood essence to me.”","“But...” Isabella hesitated. I promised big brother Zu to guard his blood essence with my life. Big sister Firework might not be an outsider, but...","Before she could finish her thought, Firework interrupted, “Do you still want to save him?!”","Isabella gritted her teeth. She could think of no other options, so she handed the blood essence over.","Firework took the blood essence and rushed down the chain, straight toward Zu An.","Sensing her entry, a furious wind blew toward Firework.","“Be careful!” Isabella shouted. Firework wasn't holding onto the Wind Quelling Pearl, and they had all witnessed what the bizarre wind was capable of.","Firework twisted her waist in a show of unbelievable flexibility, dodging the bizarre wind in the nick of time. But being on the chain, she was limited in where she could step. Her large movement resulted in a misstep, and she began plummeting into the rift valley.","“AH!” Isabella cried in horror.","But Firework’s foot hooked onto the chain, and using that as a point of leverage, she pulled herself back onto the chain.","Isabella didn’t have time to celebrate her turnaround as she shouted a warning, “Be careful, the wind is coming again!”","The earlier encounter appeared to have given Firework a better grasp of how the wind worked. Instead of making reckless movements, she waited for the wind to approach her before leaping up and twirling a few times in the air to dodge the wind.","Feeling provoked, several more gusts of wind swept up from the rift valley, threatening to tear her into pieces.","Isabella was initially worried, but her eyes soon gleamed with awe.","Firework moved with incredible lightness and flexibility, as if her body had no bones. Somehow, she managed to dodge every attack by the closest shave. Her movements were so graceful that it looked as if she were dancing.","Isabella was amazed. As expected of someone pursuing the dao of Beauty. Her movements are such a pleasure to look at.","By then, Firework had already reached Zu An’s side. She dripped the blood essence onto the forehead of his skeleton.","Zu An was embracing the Goddess Peak when he suddenly realized something. He had rushed to visit Wu Mountain after returning to the present, and the Goddess of Wu Mountain had left him with a message. She'd said that she often visited the Frost Palace to chat with Chang’e. If that was the case, how could Chang’e have forgotten about him?","No, this doesn’t make sense. How could a true promise disintegrate because of time? My relationship with Chang’e transcends time and generations, so how could she forget about me so easily?","This must have been the fear I was harboring in my heart. I was afraid that I’d lose the two of them over the passage of time.","Chang’e consumed the immortal medicine, so I wasn’t afraid of her death but of her forgetting. The Goddess of Wu Mountain didn’t take the immortal medicine, so I was afraid of her death.","I remember it now. I was crossing a chain on the rift valley. This must be an illusion conjured by the runes on the chain.","Feeling a warm tinge on his forehead, he hurriedly channeled the Primordial Origin Sutra to repair his collapsing body. Houtu had bestowed him with a droplet of Shaman blood back then. Shamans boasted tremendous life force, and they could heal their bodies with just a single droplet of blood essence. Thus, it didn’t take him long to make a full recovery.","It was only when he saw Firework that he realized she had saved him. “Thank you.”","He thought back about everything that had just happened and felt fear.","If I hadn’t left that droplet of blood essence behind, if Firework hadn’t risked danger to save me, and if I hadn’t written those words in the Time Annal, I might have been dead by now.","Qi Yaoguang’s prophecy of me turning into bones should have been referring to this.","The eight chains suddenly glowed with a reddish-orange light, and then transformed into whips that flailed at the two of them as if they had come to life."]},{"number":2810,"title":"Chapter 2810: Chapter 2762: The Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation","paragraphs":["The reddish-orange whips flailed from all directions like divine retribution. Their sheer momentum caused space to freeze up, making it impossible to avoid them.","“Be careful, big brother Zu!” Firework flitted behind Zu An and used her back to block the whip coming from the most challenging angle.","Pah!","The strike ripped her robe open, and her blood and flesh splattered. Her fair skin was charred black, as if singed by intense flames.","More whips flew in their direction. Zu An took Firework in his arms and hurriedly dodged them.","There should only have been eight whips, yet they covered the area. Despite his movement skills and special abilities, not even Zu An could dodge all of them. To make things worse, even the chain he was stepping on was flailing around like a whip, moving up and down like a wave and robbing him of stable footing. This forced him to jump to and from different chains.","All those factors made it more difficult for him to keep up. He could only hold Firework in his arms and use his body to protect her from the whips reminiscent of divine retribution.","Pah!","One of the whips struck Zu An, inflicting him with immense pain that hurt not just his body but his soul as well. Goosebumps rose across his body.","He had sustained many injuries in his lifetime, including from whips. The one that left him with the strongest impression was Chu Huanzhao’s Wailing Whip. But the pain inflicted by this whip was a thousand times greater!","Despite his resilience, he still let out a groan. It had to be even worse for Firework.","More whips flailed over. Zu An quickly used Annals of History, the ability bestowed upon him by Deity of Memory Meng. Glimmering with starlight, the river of history appeared around him. Firework was enchanted by the river’s beauty.","The reddish-orange whips fell into the river of history.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. The river of history had stopped even the terrifying demon spider’s attack, so it likely wouldn't have a problem blocking these attacks.","The next second, however, he widened his eyes in astonishment. The whips flailed through the river of history and struck his body, nearly knocking his soul out.","What is wrong with these whips? Why is the river of history unable to stop them? There are at least tens of thousands of years to the river, if not more! Are these whips forces that transcend time?","Zu An had no time to ponder this. He could only endure the whips while doing everything he could to avoid them. He had already attempted flight, but it was impossible to do so above the rift valley.","No matter how he dodged, the whips continued their assault relentlessly. He realized that the only thing he could do was to try his best not to fall into the rift valley while withstanding the whips.","He simultaneously channeled the Heaven-Devouring Sutra and the Primordial Origin Sutra, the former to absorb the whips’ destructive prowess and the latter to heal his injuries.","Even so, he still quickly reached his limit. The pain inflicted on his soul was unbearable.","Firework felt a droplet of blood falling on her face. She raised her head to look at the man embracing her. His dashing face was distorted by intense pain, and she could smell charred flesh coming from him. She fell into a daze.","“Why do you treat me so well?” she whispered.","Zu An couldn’t answer the question. He didn’t even hear her words, as his mind was already strained to its limit.","Just then, a golden tortoiseshell silhouette appeared around him. Isabella had been scouring her bag in a fluster and finally pulled out a set of defensive armor. That greatly lifted the burden on Zu An, and he finally had the energy to think about how he could overcome this crisis. He noticed that the eight flailing chains were extending from the shadows.","An idea popped into his mind. While a chain was striking him, he grabbed it and used its returning force to propel him and Firework forward. He was planning to use it to travel to the opposite side of the rift valley!","But the other chains flailed over, refusing to give him a chance to escape. If he didn’t let go, the other chains would cut him to pieces. As a result, he had no choice but to let go.","But his eyes gleamed. He noticed there was a skill he could learn from the chain—the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation!","This must be the formation behind the eight chains. If I can grasp the formation, I might be able to control the chains. Otherwise, I’ll be whipped to death.","He wanted to learn the formation, but when he saw the astronomical Rage points required for it, he was gripped by despair.","The Keyboard system swiftly notified him that there was a connection between the Netherworld Book of Life and Death and the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation, which greatly reduced the amount of Rage points needed to a million.","Even so, that was beyond Zu An’s means. He only had 97,460 Rage points left.","Do I have no choice but to be struck to death by this formation?","Foreseeing his impending death, an idea suddenly popped into Zu An’s mind. He shouted at Isabella, “Do you have an artifact that provides soul energy?”","Over the years, he'd slowly come to understand that Rage points were the manifestation of a person’s soul energy. A person’s soul fluctuated the most when feeling anger, making it the ideal moment to harvest their soul energy. Given the Universal Conglomerate’s influence, they would likely know about soul energy.","Isabella was panicking when she suddenly heard those words and shouted, “Yes, I do!”","She reached into her bag and pulled out a black card. Zu An had no idea how she did it, but the card suddenly appeared in his hand the next moment.","He was taken aback. This card resembled the credit cards he had seen in his previous life, just that it was made of a special material. This thing can provide me with soul energy?","But there was no time for him to think. He invoked the Keyboard System’s ability to learn the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation. His Rage points were emptied right away, but just when he felt a force dragging his soul out, the black credit card in his hand suddenly glowed and paid the remaining 902,540 Rage points required.","Before Zu An had time to be amazed, a formation blueprint appeared in his head, and he widened his eyes in enlightenment. He swiftly formed a series of hand seals while murmuring an obscure incantation.","The whips froze in midair. The runes on the chains reorganized themselves, causing the reddish-orange light to slowly vanish and be replaced by a gentle glow. At the same time, the chains settled down, and a light barrier formed between them, giving rise to a bridge that extended into the distance."]},{"number":2811,"title":"Chapter 2811: Chapter 2763: Prison of White Bones","paragraphs":["Zu An stood on the bridge firmly, gasping for air. The relentless attacks had finally stopped.","Overjoyed, Isabella ran over. “Big brother Zu!” She stuffed all kinds of medicine into his mouth.","Zu An burst into laughter. She’s truly a kind one. He could heal up quickly enough himself, but he didn’t want to turn down her goodwill, not to mention that her pills were indeed useful.","He initially intended to take the pills from her, but she fed them straight into his mouth.","The touch of his hot lips made Isabella’s heart skip a beat. It would be even more awkward for her to abruptly retract her hand, so she suppressed her embarrassment and asked, “Big brother Zu, are you feeling any better?”","“Of course. I received your kind sentiments and blessings, and your medicine works like a charm.” Zu An regretted saying those words right away. People tended to run their mouths after surviving a crisis, and he was too used to teasing his lovers, so he blurted those words out.","It wasn’t appropriate for him to say those words to Isabella, who was like a little sister to him.","Isabella’s heart beat quickly. She hurriedly retracted her hand and said, “I’m glad you’re fine, big brother Zu.”","Firework scoffed, “I’m injured too. Why don’t I get any medicine?”","“S-Sorry.” The embarrassed Isabella fumbled to take out a pill and hand it over.","Firework sighed. “You fed the pill to him earlier, but you’re passing it to me now. Isn’t this discrimination?”","“Ah...” Isabella’s face reddened. She felt so ashamed that she wanted to hide in a hole.","Zu An glared at Firework and said, “Stop teasing the young lady. Hurry up and circulate your energy.”","Firework glanced at him. “How much longer do you intend to carry me? I’m a young lady as well. You’re making me flustered. I can’t calm down to circulate my energy.”","Zu An was speechless.","It belatedly occurred to him that he was still hugging Firework tightly. He'd been too focused on protecting her, so releasing her had slipped his mind, even after the formation was resolved. Only when she mentioned it did he notice the soft sensation pressing against him.","How voluptuous. Her figure doesn’t feel like that of a young lady.","“My apologies.” Zu An hurriedly released her.","Isabella chuckled. Seeing how even big brother Zu was being teased by Firework, she felt a bit better.","“It would've been fine even if you didn’t release me. I wouldn’t mind.” Firework smiled. She still remembered how he had protected her desperately earlier.","Isabella’s heart jolted. Is big sister Firework confessing to big brother Zu? She nervously glanced at Zu An, and she breathed a sigh of relief when she noticed a lack of response on his part. Then, she quickly berated herself for having such a thought.","Zu An coughed lightly. “Since we've all recovered, let’s continue our journey.”","Isabella’s medicine was extremely useful. His bone-deep injuries had recovered, his soul had been nourished, and his mental state was much better than before.","The two women nodded and followed him to the opposite side.","Isabella was awed by the bridge of light. Firework asked out of curiosity, “How did you subdue the eight chains?”","“I have an ability that allows me to grasp the powers of those I touch,” Zu An scanned their surroundings for threats as he replied.","“How can there be such a formidable ability in the world? Doesn’t that mean you can grasp every ability there is out in the world?” Firework was taken aback.","“It isn’t that easy. I have to pay a price for the powers I learn through this ability. The stronger the power, the greater the price I’ll have to pay. The earlier chains are a good example. If not for Isabella’s card, I wouldn’t have been able to grasp their power and decipher this formation.”","Zu An passed the card back to Isabella. “Thanks for the card. I nearly forgot to return it to you.”","Isabella replied with a smile, “You should hold onto it for the time being, big brother Zu. We aren’t out of danger yet. This card provides you with not just credit but common currencies in different worlds, and it also resolves the negative effects of certain skills. It should be useful.”","Firework’s eyes bulged. “What’s your credit limit?”","“I have no credit limit.”","“???”","“I got this card from my grandfather. I don’t think there's a limit to it. He told me that, with the Universal Conglomerate’s wealth, there is nothing we can’t afford in the world.” Isabella innocently revealed what her grandfather told her back then. She wasn't even trying to boast.","Firework was rendered speechless. “I’m envious. She’s flexing without knowing it.”","She was also a renowned scion in the Myriad Worlds, but her financial ability was nowhere near on par with that of the Universal Conglomerate, especially with Dreamland’s current crisis.","“I’m not flexing.” Isabella was embarrassed. “Big brother Zu, you saved my life. I would have given this card to you in return, but my grandfather bound it to my soul, so I’m unable to pass it on to anyone else. However, you should have no trouble using it as long as I’m with you.”","Zu An smiled. “I’m happy to be able to use it here. Thank you.”","He had to expend Rage points for many of his abilities. Now that he had depleted his Rage points, this card was even more valuable to him.","It had to be one of the greatest treasures in the Myriad Worlds. Isabella was too young to protect a treasure of this caliber, so her grandfather had bound the card to her soul for her safety.","When she saw that he didn’t mind, Isabella breathed a sigh of relief.","While they were chatting, the trio reached the opposite end of the rift valley. The terrain resembled a mountain that had its upper half sliced off, leaving a flat plain on top. It was surrounded by the deep rift valley.","A white bone cage sat at the center of the flat land, and in it sat a dashing and scholarly, middle-aged man. He bore some resemblance to Firework. His eyes were tightly shut, as if asleep.","“Father!” Firework rushed over as she called out.","The man had eight chains coiled around his arms and legs, but perhaps due to Zu An unraveling the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation, the chains dissipated into starlight and vanished. The man’s eyelashes fluttered, as if he was about to regain consciousness.","Zu An went over and secretly asked, “Are you sure he’s your father?”"]},{"number":2812,"title":"Chapter 2812: Chapter 2764: Found","paragraphs":["“Of course. I wouldn’t fail to recognize my father. What’s wrong?” Firework asked.","“Didn’t you say the demon spider could clone anyone? What if he...” Zu An was skeptical because the white bone cage looked eerie, as if it was intended to seal off some demonic creature.","“That demoness likely imprisoned my father here because she wants to obtain Dreamland’s secrets from him. If this were her clone, she could have used him to fool us right from the start. There would have been no need for her to imprison him here,” Firework replied with a smile. “If you're still worried, I’ll ask some questions to verify his identity later on.”","While they were speaking, the imprisoned master of Dreamland woke up. He was initially confused when he opened his eyes and saw Firework, but then his eyes lit up in delight. He stood up in excitement and exclaimed, “Firework, what are you doing here?”","“Father, I’m here to save you.” Firework dropped her usual light-hearted attitude, and her eyes brimmed with tears. She couldn’t wait to shatter the white bone prison and leap into his arms.","“My good daughter...” Tears also flowed down the eyes of Dreamland’s master.","Worried, Zu An scanned Dreamland’s master with the Eye of Truth but didn’t find anything anomalous. Only then did he breathe a sigh of relief.","Dreamland’s master noticed his gaze and asked out of curiosity, “My good daughter, who is your friend over there?”","Firework’s face reddened. She pulled Zu An over to introduce him. “Father, this is Zu An. It’s thanks to him that I was able to get here to save you.”","Heartened, Dreamland’s master looked at Zu An with gentle eyes. “What an outstanding youth you are.”","Firework was embarrassed. “Father, you should be thanking him instead of saying such nonsense.”","Dreamland’s master laughed heartily. “My daughter has grown up. You’re mature now.”","Isabella felt uncomfortable. It didn’t sit well with her to see her big brother Zu meeting another woman’s parent.","Fortunately, Firework noticed it and quickly introduced her, too. “Father, this is Isabella, the Acadias’ big miss. She also contributed a lot to your rescue.”","Dreamland’s master bowed to Isabella. “I have long heard about your grandfather. I didn’t expect his granddaughter to be so outstanding as well. Dreamland will remember this favor.”","Isabella quickly responded with a greeting. “Uncle, you know my grandfather?”","Dreamland’s master smiled. “Who doesn’t know about the Acadias of the Universal Conglomerate? It’s just that we have never had the chance to meet. I’ll make sure to pay your family a visit in the future to relay my gratitude.”","After trading some pleasantries, Zu An got to the point and said, “Elder, we're currently being pursued by the demon spider. Do you know of any way to deal with her?”","Upon hearing the words ‘demon spider’, the expression of Dreamland’s master warped.","“That vile demoness! She made us suffer so much! We’re in a forbidden land that has been passed down through generations. There’s a powerful formation here that can suppress her, but the formation has been idle for too long, so we’ll have to reactivate it.”","“How do we reactivate the formation?” Zu An asked.","“Come with me.” Dreamland’s master stretched his limbs before standing up to lead the way.","Zu An hurriedly followed him.","They soon arrived before a circular metal platform. Profound patterns reminiscent of a dark red blood moon were inscribed on its surface.","A red jewel embedded in the center of the headdress worn by Dreamland’s master lit up and shot a light beam at the blood moon, causing it to glow. The moon's color turned as vibrant as fresh blood, and the light reflecting off it made it seem as if it was indeed filled with fresh blood.","A loud rumble echoed, as if some hidden gears had begun spinning. The ground trembled, and Isabella instinctively leaned against Zu An for security.","“Come up.” Dreamland’s master beckoned them to step on top of the circular platform, and the circular platform began descending.","Looking at the stone walls around them, the group quickly realized they were riding on an elevator. Dreamland’s master was probably the only person in the world who knew how to activate it.","Their surroundings grew darker the deeper they descended, but the elevator’s tiles continued emanating a vibrant red glow. It felt eerie.","Zu An suddenly recalled the destructive wind that had risen from the rift valley earlier and asked, “Elder, what lies beneath the rift valley?”","Dreamland’s master shook his head. “I don’t know. Our ancestors only tasked us with the mission to guard this place. If not for the demoness, I probably would have never come here in my lifetime.”","Zu An fell silent.","Dreamland has been guarding this place all this time, but they don’t know what they're guarding. Does he really not know, or is he reluctant to reveal it to an outsider? No matter which case it is, this place has been running amok since a thousand years ago.","I wonder if it’s due to the demon spider’s infiltration.","Some time later, the elevator reached the bottom. The door in front of them automatically opened, revealing a long, well-lit passageway. Zu An couldn’t help but feel as if he had entered a sci-fi movie.","While traveling through the passageway, Dreamland’s master said with a tinge of nervousness, “It’s my first time here as well. Our ancestors strictly forade us from coming here unless it was a matter concerning Dreamland’s life and death. My predecessors have probably never been here, either. But with the demoness having massacred everyone in Dreamland, there’s no better time than now.”","Zu An put up his guard. Isabella took out a couple of defensive artifacts and handed them around. After all the dangers they had been through, they were now more vigilant than ever.","Surprisingly, there were no traps along the way. They soon arrived at a semi-spherical room covered in giant screens. None of the screens lit up, likely because they had run out of energy after a long time.","Dreamland’s master walked up to a metal pillar that was around his height. A crystal sphere sat on top of the pillar. He formed hand seals while murmuring an obscure incantation. Then, he slit his finger and dripped his blood essence on the sphere.","It then lit up and scattered light around. The screens began projecting live images of the surrounding area, such as the devastating storm outside, the fog ocean that warped directions, the labyrinths, and the rift valley Zu An and the others had just overcome.","But what caught their attention were the scuttling little spiders and a massive figure on one of the screens.","All of a sudden, the demon spider sensed something and looked over. Even across the screen, the group still felt her suffocating pressure.","Dreamland’s master was horrified. “Oh no! She has found us. It’ll take her no more than thirty breaths to find this place. We have to activate the formation to seal her right away!”"]},{"number":2813,"title":"Chapter 2813: Chapter 2765: True Identity","paragraphs":["Zu An and the others were startled. The demon spider had left a deep impression on them. Even if they gave it their all, they still wouldn’t stand a chance against it.","They had Dreamland’s master on their side now, but the latter was in a severely weakened state after being imprisoned for a long time. It was unlikely he could put up a fight against the spider.","“What do we have to do to seal the demon spider?” Isabella asked.","“The seal should have been activated when the nine stars were aligned, so we could tap into the natural energies of the world to channel the formation. But we don’t have the luxury of waiting now. We can only use the Dream Clan’s bloodline power to suppress that demoness for now and wait for a better time to seal her off completely.”","Dreamland’s master and Firework slit their fingers and infused their blood essence into the crystal, which glowed with a brilliant red light. The ground quaked as if a formation was whirring to life.","A sharp shriek echoed in the distance. The demon spider appeared to have sensed an impending crisis and started rushing over.","“This isn’t good!” Dreamland’s master exclaimed. “This formation draws energy from five earth veins located across this forbidden land, but two of them have been corrupted and energy is no longer flowing through them. I can’t activate the formation.”","“We’ll handle that!” Zu An said.","Dreamland’s master knew there was no time to waste. “All right. I’ll teleport you over with this formation disc. I’ll try to buy as much time as possible, but you’ll have to make haste.”","His fingers moved so quickly that they became a blur. He activated a series of ancient formations that hindered the demon spider rushing across the screens. The spider tore through the formations in an instant, but Dreamland’s master used his authority to relentlessly create more formations to hinder it.","“I won’t be able to stall it for long.” Dreamland’s master spat blood. His face was pale, and sweat rained from his forehead.","Firework’s eyes were closed, her face pale. Her father was in a weakened state, so she needed to channel more blood essence and power into the formation to compensate for him.","Zu An and Isabella’s surroundings blurred as they were teleported to different corners of the forbidden land.","Zu An stood before an earth vein resembling a majestic dragon. The area was rich with energy, so much so that he could greatly raise his fighting prowess if he utilized the earth vein’s energy using One Drop of Heaven’s Essence[1].","But he quickly dropped that thought. The demon spider’s strength transcended conventional notions of strong and weak. This wasn't a gap he could bridge with just better utilization of his skills.","He looked up at the vein. There was a reddish-black mass there resembling a massive heart. Pure earth veins wouldn’t take on such a color. This must be the corruption Dreamland’s master spoke about.","Approaching the corrupted mass filled with his mind with negative emotions of violence, bloodthirst, and death. If not for the strong mental fortitude he had built up from the storms he had weathered, he would have lost his senses.","Knowing the demon spider could arrive at any moment, he didn’t waste time and began cleansing the demonic energy using the method taught by Dreamland’s master. His Primordial Origin Sutra harnessed the ability to cleanse demonic ki, so it didn’t take him long to expel a pitch-black aura from the lump, leaving behind a pristine red earth vein.","He wondered if things were going well on Isabella’s side, but he quickly realized his worry was unfounded and laughed as he remembered the mountain of treasures she had in her bag. She might even be more efficient than me.","Now that the earth vein was cleansed, he couldn’t help noticing that the massive earth vein contained a plate with a keyhole in the center.","At the same time, something was glowing from his chest. He took it out. It was the key he had received from Alati. The key emanated a beam of light at the keyhole, and the plate lit up.","Even a fool could tell that the key belonged to the hole. Thus, Zu An walked up to the plate, only to suddenly stop when a thought flashed through his mind.","Many things had happened since they entered this forbidden land, and there had been a nudging feeling in his head that something was amiss. However, crises had kept happening one after another, leaving him no time for contemplation.","Unease simmered in his heart. He knew the demon spider could arrive at any moment, but he still refrained from making a move. He had a feeling that if he didn’t figure things out first, there was a good chance he might make a decision he would regret.","“Little brother, you need to quickly unlock it for the earth vein’s energy to flow. I can’t activate the formation otherwise,” Dreamland’s master said.","Zu An looked upward and asked, “You can see what I’m doing here?”","“Of course. I am in the forbidden land’s control room. Didn’t you see it earlier?” Dreamland’s master replied.","Zu An remembered the display screens he had seen earlier. “Why didn’t you mention that a key was required to unlock the earth vein earlier?”","“It’s my first time here as well, and I didn’t know you had that key. My knowledge about this forbidden land comes from my predecessors, so it can be off,” Dreamland’s master replied with a frown. “You seem to be doubting me?”","Zu An didn’t answer the question. “I don’t think I've heard Firework speak for a while now. Is she still fine?”","Firework said, “Big brother Zu, I couldn’t speak earlier because I was focused on channeling the formation.”","“But you can speak now?”","“It’s a bit better now that you have cleansed the earth vein’s corruption. Big brother Zu, we don’t have time. Hurry up and unlock the earth vein’s energy.”","Zu An sighed. “Firework, why do you have such a high opinion of me? You expressed tremendous goodwill to me right from the start even though I was just a countryside bumpkin from a fringe world.”","“I already told you—I am a Beauty worshiper. From the moment I saw you... Gah! Big brother Zu, do you have to make me say such words in front of my father?” Firework’s embarrassment could be heard in her voice. Zu An could imagine her stomping her feet shyly.","Zu An continued the questions. “What’s the situation on Isabella’s side?”","“She has cleansed the corruption on that side, too. You’ll be able to meet her once you return.” Firework sounded anxious. “Our formations can’t stall that demoness for much longer. We only have ten seconds left. You need to hurry!”","But Zu An still refused to move. “Firework... Or should I call you Diodora, or Yani?”","1. First introduced in Chapter 1266, this book exists in real life. It's one of the foundational texts for your Bazi (Eight Characters) divination, and it talks about Yin-Yang, Five Elements, Ten Heavenly Stems, Twelve Earthly Branches, etc. ☜"]},{"number":2814,"title":"Chapter 2814: Chapter 2766: Show of Hands","paragraphs":["An unnerving silence loomed.","Moments later, Firework’s voice called out, “What are you saying, big brother Zu? How can I be that demoness?”","Zu An sighed. “You don’t need to hide it anymore. I only regret not realizing it earlier.”","A light distortion manifested not far away from where Zu An was, and Firework emerged from there. She was as beautiful as ever, but she showed none of her usual cutesy demeanor. She felt cold and lofty, as if she had become someone else.","“When did you see through me?” ‘Firework’ asked coldly.","The air grew viscous. A familiar pressure bore down on Zu An, trampling on his final sliver of hope. “I wouldn't have expected someone of your stature to lie low for so long. You’re a devoted actor.”","Zu An was impressed by how this major boss had the patience to play a sweet character and address him as big brother Zu. He'd thought he was a good actor, but he was nothing compared to 'Firework'.","“Is it the Eye of Truth? No, that can’t be. I'm holding onto a universal deity-level artifact. Your Eye of Truth shouldn’t be able to see through me.” ‘Firework’ frowned as she wondered where she had given herself away.","Zu An hadn’t obtained the Eye of Truth when they first met, so he couldn’t have figured her out then. It was later that the Deity of Memory Meng had paid Zu An a visit. Other guests might not have known what was going on, but she was strong enough to sense something amiss.","That was especially so when Zu An looked at Yani after returning. She knew right away that Zu An had figured out Yani’s identity, but she hadn’t panicked. She'd decided to play along and let Zu An think that he had it all figured out.","Later, when she reunited with him as Firework, she'd made sure to carry the universal deity-level artifact along. Only such an artifact could deal with a universal deity’s ability. Just as she had expected, Zu An failed to notice the anomaly.","Everything should have gone according to plan. Where did I go wrong?","“I was already skeptical when you approached me on the spaceship,” Zu An said. There was no glee on his face despite his having figured out the mystery.","“You suspected me over that? Isn’t it normal for a young lady to be attracted to a dashing guy, not to mention a capable one?” ‘Firework’ was perplexed. “You’re obviously someone who often attracts the attention of the opposite sex, so why would you single me out?”","“Because you’re too mysterious.” Zu An sighed. “Someone with your looks and strength is bound to have no lack of suitors. I saw no reason for you to be drawn to me. Initially, I thought you coveted my Wonderpoint World, but I quickly realized that wasn’t the case.”","“Wonderpoint Worlds might be an invaluable treasure to others, but that means nothing to me,” ‘Firework’ replied proudly. “But I should have given you an apt reason afterward—I was seeking help to save my father. Did that pique your suspicion?”","“Indeed. Your actions were peculiar. You showed no interest in Dreamland and were instead more eager to drag me to the beach, after which you then feigned anger, dove into the ocean alone, and ended up being captured by a sea monster.”","“That’s all? But that fits within ‘Firework’s’ eccentric persona. I don’t see anything amiss with that.” ‘Firework’ remained confused.","Zu An eyed ‘Firework’. “You seem to enjoy acting.”","“Of course.” ‘Firework’s’ eyes gleamed. “While my clones can impersonate others, they can’t fool close kin and friends if there are discrepancies in their personality, speech, and gestures. That would be my greatest failure!”","“That worked against you. Do you remember asking me, as Yani, how much I knew about Firework? You mentioned that it was suspicious how she was captured near the hotel’s beach.” Zu An chuckled. “Yes, you were merely playing each character according to their personality and circumstances. But your words were so convincing that, for the first time, I began pondering my relationship with Firework.”","‘Firework’ looked stifled. “I didn’t expect my thoroughness to work against me. But did you suspect me just because an outsider said a couple of words? I didn’t think you trusted me so little.”","“There’s more to it, of course. Later, when we reunited in this forbidden land, you revealed that your main body was capable of creating many clones and had replaced everyone in Dreamland.” Zu An briefly paused as his expression turned grim. “It was then I wondered that, if everyone in Dreamland had been replaced, was there a chance you were a fake, too?","“But your story about studying abroad was reasonable, and your motive of wanting to rescue your father made sense. I didn’t see anything amiss through my Eye of Truth either, so I didn’t think too much of it.” Zu An looked frustrated at his carelessness.","“So what made you suspect me?” ‘Firework’ remained confused.","“I couldn’t figure out why the demon spider refused to kill your father and instead chose to imprison him here,” Zu An said. “If the demon spider could replace everyone in Dreamland without anyone in the Myriad Worlds noticing, it should have been able to figure out the secrets this place held, too. I didn’t think Dreamland’s master could have overcome its methods.”","“There could have been a restriction on his memories, preventing me from taking forceful measures.” ‘Firework’ wasn’t satisfied with Zu An’s explanation. She didn’t think there were any discrepancies here.","“I didn’t discard that possibility, but the demon spider had proven itself to be a highly resourceful being. Since it had already impersonated everyone in Dreamland, surely it could impersonate Firework or someone close to Dreamland’s master to extract his secrets? It seemed inefficient to just imprison him here without doing anything.”","At this point, Zu An added with a harrumph, “I’m guessing Dreamland’s master is one of your clones, too.”","“You’re a smart one, but you still haven’t revealed the real reason you suspected me.” ‘Firework’ sneered. Her appearance began to change swiftly, switching between the weakened Dreamland’s master, the valiant Yani, and the seductive Diodora. “You were beating around the bush, refusing to get to the point. You were planning to use the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation against me, right?”"]},{"number":2815,"title":"Chapter 2815: Chapter 2767: The Real Firework","paragraphs":["Zu An’s heart skipped a beat.","‘Firework’ sneered. “You listed many reasons, but they were all just chasing shadows. I was also reflecting on where I went wrong, and the only thing I could think of was on the rift valley’s chain bridge.”","“Indeed.” Since things had already gotten to this point, Zu An decided to speak the truth. “I was moved when you took the first whip for me. Which man wouldn’t be when a beauty puts herself on the line for him?","“But when I put my earlier suspicions together and considered the situation, a thought occurred to me. Could the chains have been targeting not me, but you? You took the first whip and misled me into thinking that you were protecting me, and that prompted me to foolishly protect you from the remaining attacks.”","There was actually another important factor at play here—Mi Li’s absence. Perhaps she'd been in hibernation, but with all the dangers he had been through, it didn’t make sense for her to still remain asleep. The only explanation he could think of was that her appearance would draw attention and plunge him into greater danger. She could only signal for him to resolve the crisis by himself via her silence.","They had been together for so long that words weren’t necessary for them to convey their thoughts.","Of course, Zu An wasn’t so foolish as to reveal that to ‘Firework’.","‘Firework’ smiled after hearing his analysis. “You’re smart, but it’s not a good thing to be too smart. I was getting lonely after spending so much time alone. It’s rare for someone to catch my eye. If you were more foolish and more cooperative, I could have taken you in as my plaything. You would have been happy for a long time.”","“I’d have liked to feign ignorance as well, but I couldn’t hold it in.” Zu An sounded regretful.","“That’s not an issue. I can erase your memories. I’d still be your Firework, and you’d be my big brother Zu. How does that sound?” ‘Firework’ looked at Zu An playfully.","Even though this man is weak, I’m sure he’ll be quite a different experience. I don’t mind spending more time with him. It’s rare to meet someone this interesting.","“I’d rather live with my eyes open. Even if it doesn’t end well, I think it still beats living in ignorance.” Zu An shook his head. “Besides, I've been chosen by the Deity of Memory. I wouldn’t dare to relinquish my memories that easily.”","‘Firework’s’ expression darkened. “Do you think I’d be intimidated just because you brought up Meng?”","Zu An’s heart thumped.","She didn’t hesitate to call the Deity of Memory by name! And it sounds like they know each other. How can she be this fearless...","Universal deities were transcendent entities. They could sense disrespect, even in private settings, and that could result in divine retribution. That was why the Myriad Worlds tread very carefully around universal deities to avoid blasphemy.","Sensing Zu An’s confusion, ‘Firework’ harrumphed. “Don’t expect Meng to save you. Even universal deities are reluctant to approach this place.”","“Oh? What is this place?” Zu An asked. Supposing that was true, this place had to be more than just Dreamland’s forbidden land. Universal deities wouldn’t fear a mere Dreamland.","“Why don’t you take a guess? I’ll reward you if you get it right.” Despite still looking like a youthful lady, ‘Firework’s’ tone and demeanor had changed to that of a mature older sister instead.","Zu An thought about everything he had encountered en route, and his mind gradually cleared. “This place could be related to the Deity of Death. There are rumors floating around that the Deity of Annihilation has killed the Deity of Death, or that the Deity of Death has gone missing. Regardless, there’s no question he's gone missing. Could this be where he lies?”","“As expected of someone who caught my eye. Congratulations, you’re right.” ‘Firework’ smiled, looking beautiful but dangerous.","“Didn’t you promise a reward if I get it right?”","“What do you want?”","“Can you return Isabella to me?”","“Don’t you think it’s unwise to speak up for another woman in my presence?” ‘Firework’ clicked her tongue. “Ah, why didn’t you suspect Isabella to be one of my clones?”","The thought of Isabella brought some warmth to Zu An’s heart. “You wouldn’t have sent us to two separate earth veins if she was your clone. You’d have kept her with me to control me.”","“It would indeed have been troublesome to impersonate that lass. Her bag contains too many treasures,” ‘Firework’ remarked. “In particular, that black card of hers is a marvel. It synergizes well with you. As a safety precaution, I figured it would be best to separate you two.”","She turned to Zu An and said, “I advise you not to try anything funny. You have interesting skills, but I doubt you can pay the price for them without her card forking out the cost.”","Zu An responded with a bitter smile. That had indeed been his intention. He'd contemplated using Isabella’s card to pay the price for his ‘Keyboard Come’, but even though the card was in his hand, he couldn’t use it without her approval.","“Is the real Firework dead?” he asked.","“Why? Feeling sorry for her?” ‘Firework’ paced to and fro, as if she were a cat toying with a mouse.","“She did bring me some happy memories. I’m guessing you used her real personality as a model, right?” Knowing that the real, bubbly Firework was dead made Zu An a bit melancholic.","“Hmph, I was the one who brought you those happy memories, not her!” ‘Firework’ harrumphed in displeasure.","You have successfully trolled Firework for +199... +199... +199...","Zu An was surprised to see the name on his long-inactive system. “Your name is really Firework?”","Firework was taken aback. “How did you know? Do you have the ability to see through a person’s true name as well? Hold on, you have a soul-related skill, and you’re able to figure out a person’s true name. I remember hearing about a skill like that...” She suddenly clutched her head as if in pain.","Zu An was startled. Does she know about the Keyboard System?","Having reached his current level and met experts from different worlds, he no longer thought that the Keyboard System was a typical cheat often seen in his previous life’s webnovels. It was likely to be an artifact, the most powerful kind at that."]},{"number":2816,"title":"Chapter 2816: Chapter 2768: Irresistible Terms","paragraphs":["Zu An had never been able to determine the origin of the Keyboard System. Even Mi Li seemingly had no idea.","Perhaps she knew, but withheld the information from him. Secrets posed danger in this world, after all. Perhaps Mi Li thought he wasn’t strong enough to know such things yet.","He understood where she was coming from, but he couldn’t curb his curiosity. It seemed the demon spider knew something. It was the strongest entity he had ever met aside from the universal deities, so it could know some secrets. It would be a worthwhile trip if he could acquire some intelligence from it.","“It should be related to a universal deity.” Firework lifted her head. “To think I can’t recall it. Either too much time has passed, or a universal deity has tampered with that piece of memory.”","She reassessed Zu An. “I wouldn’t have expected someone as weak as you to carry a secret concerning a universal deity. That would explain the skills you have.”","“A universal deity...” Zu An fell into deep thought.","Was the Keyboard System created by a universal deity? Who could it be? So far, I've met the Deity of Chaos and Enigma Mi Li and the Deity of Memory Meng, and they were fairly amicable. Could they be behind the Keyboard System?","While Zu An was in contemplation, Firework suddenly appeared next to him, traced his cheeks with her finger, then propped up his chin. “It may have just been a whim earlier, but now, I intend to make you my plaything.”","Feeling her cold touch, Zu An replied, “You haven’t answered my question. What happened to the real Firework?”","“Tsk tsk. I didn’t expect you to care so much about me. Don’t you already know my name is Firework?” Firework chuckled, her voice echoing in the room. She was dangerous, yet seductive.","“No, you aren’t Firework.” Zu An shook his head. How can this flirtatious woman possibly be the youthful and bubbly Firework?","Firework fell silent. A moment later, she asked, “Did you really fall in love with that lass? Even though you know she was a fake?”","Zu An shook his head. “No, I believe she exists. Many things can’t be faked.”","His words angered Firework. “How am I any less than her? Not only can I take her personality, but I can also turn into other women as well.”","Her body expanded into a two-meter-tall beauty. “You appear to be fond of Yani. You snuck glances at her and ogled her thighs. You don’t need to be secretive about it anymore. It’s now within your reach.”","Zu An calmly replied, “It’s normal for a gentleman to show interest in a lady, not to mention someone that outstanding. It would be abnormal for me not to look.”","“Aren’t you thick-skinned?” ‘Yani’ harrumphed. “Am I not beautiful? Why don’t I see desire in your eyes?”","Zu An fell silent.","“Does this physique intimidate you now that you’re seeing it close up?” ‘Yani’ laughed. Her physique changed once more, morphing into the graceful and ravishing Elder Diodora. “Then what do you think about Diodora? She’s a famed beauty in Dreamland. You saw how guests across the Myriad Worlds were mesmerized with her at the hotel. Just give the word, and she’ll become your dream lover.”","Zu An sighed. “But aren’t they all you?”","“What’s bad about me?” Firework harrumphed. “If you have me, you can have any woman in the world. I can turn into whoever you like; you can have your way with anyone you like in bed, all at the same time.”","“It’s a tempting offer. No man can turn down such temptation,” Zu An remarked.","“I hear a but.” Firework frowned.","Zu An sighed. “Yani and Diodora are beautiful in their own ways, but I prefer that bubbly, youthful Firework. Can you tell me what happened to her now?”","Surprise flickered across Firework’s eyes, but her gaze soon turned cold. “She’s dead.”","“You killed her?”","“Indeed. Do you plan to avenge her?”","“I would, but I am no match for you,” Zu An replied with a sigh. He had been simulating ways to defeat Firework in his mind, but none of them worked. The difference in strength was too great.","“Hmph. Men are all talk,” Firework grumbled.","“It sounds like you've been hurt by a man before,” Zu An remarked.","Firework’s face darkened. “Don’t you think you’re talking too much? It’s time for you to do what you have to do. I’ll spare your life on account of the time we have spent together.”","“You want me to be your plaything?” Zu An frowned.","“You can also choose to be devoured instead.” Firework smiled. “You know my main body. There’s nothing female spiders relish in more than devouring their male partners.”","Zu An said, “...There’s one more option. You can let Isabella and me go.”","Firework scoffed, “Are you mad, or are my ears failing me? Do you think you get to choose?”","“I’ve been thinking about it. You’re probably trapped here by some powerful formation, and everything you've done was in order for me to free you. That means you require my help. If so, there should be room for negotiation,” Zu An replied with a smile.","Firework narrowed her eyes. “You’re a smart man, but have you not considered the possibility that you've already released the seal?”","Zu An widened his eyes in shock. “The rift valley’s Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation?”","“Indeed. That formation was relentlessly striking me, but you put your life on the line to protect me. Being protected by you made me feel something I've never felt before. I wouldn’t have wasted my breath on you if not for that,” Firework scoffed, and the surroundings cooled.","Zu An felt goosebumps, but he didn’t cower. “You’re lying. If you'd been released, you wouldn’t have had to urge me to release this formation under the pretext of cleansing the earth vein.”","“Hah, men. At this point, do you still think you’re indispensable?” Firework waved her hand, and the key Alati had entrusted to Zu An appeared in her hand. She walked up to the heart-like stone and inserted the key."]},{"number":2817,"title":"Chapter 2817: Chapter 2769: Nebula’s Envoy","paragraphs":["Zu An’s expression darkened. It’ll be over if she opens the seal.","He instinctively activated the position swap to pull her away from the seal, but his body suddenly turned icy cold the moment he activated the skill. He was still stuck to the spot, and he was unable to move at all!","Firework laughed. “Big brother Zu, we've been together for some time now. I've seen all your skills. Do you think I’d fall for your tricks? Your position swap is an incredible skill, but it has a weakness. Your divine sense has to reach its target first, but that’s as good as offering it up for me to grab.”","Zu An’s heart plunged. This woman is too strong, not to mention she's been with me all this time and has seen many of my skills. I don’t stand a chance against her. If only I'd seen through her ploy earlier...","Firework continued, “You do have many interesting skills that someone of your cultivation shouldn’t have. Let me see what else you have, lest I get caught off guard later on.”","She extended her divine sense into Zu An’s mind. He felt a surge of cold infiltrating his thoughts. His Hundredwarble’s ability reflexively counterattacked.","Firework harrumphed. “A paltry trick!”","Hundredwarble shattered, and Zu An felt a sharp pain in his mind. Blood seeped from his mouth and nostrils.","“Why put yourself through this suffering? Since you don’t stand a chance against me, you should just sit back and relax. It hurts me to see you in pain,” Firework said as she wiped off the blood on his face.","She should have been a distance away, but somehow, her hand reached Zu An’s face. Yet there were no signs of her arm stretching like a rubber arm. This bizarre spatial distortion felt incomprehensible.","Cold sweat trickled down Zu An’s back. Every cell in his body was warning him of danger, but the earlier misstep had sealed his fate. With his divine sense suppressed, he couldn’t activate any of his other abilities. Once Firework learned about his other skills, he wouldn’t stand a chance at all. Not to mention he had many secrets that mustn’t be leaked.","“Oh? You are hiding a secret. Let me see what it is.” Intrigued, Firework’s divine sense dug deeper into Zu An.","All of a sudden, there was a spatial distortion, followed by a brilliant cold flash. Firework’s arm dropped to the ground.","A gorgeous woman dressed in snowy clothes stepped out from the distortion with an air of nonchalance. It was Tingxue.","Her intervention created an opening for Zu An to retract his divine sense. He exclaimed in delight, “Miss Tingxue!”","Tingxue directed a nod at him before coldly turning to Firework. “You expelled me into the void. We should settle the score.”","FIrework chuckled. Her body glowed, and her arm regenerated instantly. “As expected from Nebula’s envoy. Your prowess is formidable.”","Zu An was startled. Despite knowing Tingxue was related to the Deity of Nebula, he hadn’t expected her to be a Nebula envoy. Unlike other universal deities, the Deity of Nebula was known to not have any envoys.","He turned his attention back to the crisis at hand. Worried that Tingxue wasn’t aware of the latest developments, since she had been missing for a long time, he warned, “Be careful. She’s the sealed demon spider. Firework, Yani, Diodora, and all the other people in Dreamland are her clones.”","Tingxue remained unfazed.","Firework clicked her tongue. “It’s true that all who join Nebula lose their emotions. How boring.”","“I might not have my emotions, but I intend to exact vengeance for this grudge. I considered you a friend, and I don’t like being deceived,” Tingxue coldly spat.","“I am grateful that you thought of me as a friend and risked your life to save me,” Firework replied with a grin. “That’s why I chose to banish you instead of hurting you. I knew you would be fine. Look, didn’t you return safe and sound?”","Zu An remarked, “I bet you banished her because you witnessed her ability to tear open the void and were intimidated by her strength.”","Tingxue hadn’t drawn her sword on the frigate. While her strength was amazing nonetheless, it wasn't enough to threaten the demon spider. It was only after arriving at the forbidden land that Tingxue had drawn her blade against the Soul Siphoning Beetles.","The demon spider had likely felt threatened by that, and thus sent Tingxue away.","If the demon spider is intimidated by Tingxue, we might stand a chance against her if we join forces.","Firework noticed Zu An’s excitement and sneered, “Do you honestly think you stand a chance against me? Indeed, Tingxue was stronger than I expected, so I had to banish her lest she get in the way of my plan. But I regained most of my powers after you deciphered the Eight Barren Netherworld Formation. You won’t be a match for me even if you join hands.”","Zu An was speechless. Thinking about how he had risked his life to protect her earlier, he felt so ashamed that he wanted to find a hole to hide himself in.","Tingxue didn’t waste her breath talking and instead slashed with her sword.","It was an attack strong enough to slice a world apart, but Firework stopped it between her slender fingers. “Didn’t I say you aren’t a match for me? I’ll spare you on account of our past ties...”","Tingxue flicked her wrist and rotated her blade. Even Firework had no choice but to release her fingers. Tingxue thrust her blade forth once more like a merciless machine.","Firework harrumphed. She raised her hand and lightly tapped with her fingertip. Each time she moved, she never failed to block the incoming sword.","Meanwhile, her other hand moved the key into the keyhole. Once she lifted the final seal, she would regain her full strength, thus completely assuring her victory. She wasn't worried about Zu An, as she had wrapped the key with her divine sense. He couldn’t hope to stop her.","But the key suddenly dropped to the ground right as it was about to enter the keyhole.","Taken aback, Firework immediately turned around to look at Zu An, only to see a copper coin rotating on his palm. It was the Treasure Sinking Coin!","The key could be considered a treasure. Once it was out of Firework’s hand, it could be influenced by the Treasure Sinking Coin.","Zu An rushed to the seal and grabbed the key. His presence suddenly flared, emanating an aura that intimidated even Firework.","Firework sensed that Zu An was charging up for some kind of terrifying move. She didn’t think he was strong enough to threaten her, but considering all the strange moves he had, she didn’t dare let her guard down either. She flicked Tingxue aside and heightened her vigilance.","The next second, Zu An grabbed Tingxue’s hand and said, “Let’s go!”","The two of them vanished into thin air.","This was the move he had learned from the True Demon Emissary—Bravado. It involved convincing the enemy that one was going to put one’s life on the line, but the goal was to create an opening to escape.","——","T/N: Tingxue means ‘Listening to Snow’ in Chinese.","I could have translated it into English, as per the norm for the Myriad Worlds, but I kept it as it is because both her name and Yan Xuehen’s contain ‘Xue (Snow)’, and there appears to be a link between the two characters (not a spoiler)."]},{"number":2818,"title":"Chapter 2818: Chapter 2770: This Is Love","paragraphs":["The True Demon Emissary wasn't strong by the Myriad Worlds’ standard, but he'd had his fair share of fortuitous encounters. Bravado was a skill he'd learned that disregarded the gap in strength to cause a lapse in the opponent’s judgment.","That very skill was at the level of a law.","Caught off guard, Firework fell for it. She was initially taken aback before she was assaulted by a mix of anger and embarrassment. She hadn’t expected to be fooled by a mere ant.","You have successfully trolled Firework for +233... +233... +233...","“You want to escape?”","She grasped the fabric of space, and astonishingly, she found where Zu An was.","Zu An was taken aback. In the brief opening created by Bravado, he'd quickly activated a spatial teleportation to flee from the scene. It shouldn’t have been possible for anyone to chase him once he slipped into the fabric of space.","But Firework wasn't limited by such laws. She reached right into the fabric of space and grabbed him.","Tingxue immediately reacted with a slash. Zu An also took out the Poisonous Prick to secretly stab Firework’s hand.","“Hmph, is that the dagger of certain death? Big brother Zu, I know what you’re capable of.” Firework mocked him with a coy laugh. “I showed you mercy, but you sought to claim my life. Don’t you think you’re being heartless here?”","Her hand moved with incredible dexterity, flicking aside Tingxue’s sword and dodging Zu An’s assault to land on his shoulder.","“Heh, I’ve caught you... AH!” Firework suddenly retracted her hand with a yelp.","Zu An exploited this opportunity to finish the teleportation.","Firework stared at the prick on her finger. It was seeping black blood. She murmured with an awful complexion, “What kind of poison is this? To think it can hurt and inflict pain on me!”","She expelled the poisonous blood with a wave of her hand. It splattered and corroded a hole in the floor.","Her face was livid for a while before she burst into manic laughter. “Little man, you have caught my attention!”","Space distorted at the rift valley, and Zu An and Tingxue appeared by the cliff.","Tingxue awkwardly pulled back her hand before asking in confusion, “What did you use to hurt her earlier?”","Even her world-severing slashes struggled to hurt Firework, yet Zu An had managed to hurt her. That miserable yelp earlier reflected how much pain she'd been in.","Zu An noticed her movements and felt down despite knowing she wasn’t Yan Xuehen. Not only do they look identical, but even their hands are equally cold.","He pulled out a pitch-black stinger and explained, “This is the Scorpion King’s tail sting. It was rumored that its poison would be potent enough to kill any expert in the Myriad Worlds, though I doubt that woman can be killed by it.”","Tingxue nodded in agreement. “She is very powerful.”","A coy laugh echoed. “You know me well, big brother Zu.”","Zu An and Tingxue widened their eyes in shock.","Firework slowly descended from the sky as if walking down an invisible staircase. Her fair, smooth feet left gentle ripples in space, resembling blossoming flowers heralding her descent. Zu An might have swooned if not for the tremendous pressure she emanated.","“How did you catch up with us so quickly?” Zu An was taken aback.","He had grasped the essence of space in the Monster World, and Yumen Beiqing had generously imparted her knowledge to him in bed. His understanding of spatial teleportation was extremely high. He'd thought that he could shake off Firework with this, but she still caught up with them in the blink of an eye.","“Spatial manipulation is an easy feat for me, not to mention you’re still within the forbidden land,” Firework explained with a smile as she eyed their surroundings. “But isn’t that your goal? You’re hoping to lure me back to the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation.”","Worried that he would be suppressed by Firework, Zu An immediately activated the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation. The eight chains on the bridge turned reddish-orange as they lashed at Firework as if they were whips.","Firework harrumphed. “Do you think those whips are what stopped me all these years?”","She raised her fair hand and simultaneously grabbed all eight whips. They turned crimson, and runes furiously flowed across their surfaces. They were channeling all their strength to break free of Firework’s grip.","But it was to no avail. The whips couldn’t even char her skin.","“It would have been one thing for you to seal me when I was in a weakened state, but do you think I’d let you walk over me now that I’m out?” Firework flicked her hand, and the imposing chains shattered and fell into the rift valley.","Zu An was speechless. He had set the teleportation destination here because he could control the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation. He definitely hadn’t expected it to be destroyed right away.","I took so many blows for you when you could have destroyed the formation so easily...","Firework smiled. “Those whips caused you so much pain earlier. I've helped you get even with them. Aren’t you happy?”","More like horrified!","Tingxue frowned. “It seems almost as if she has fallen in love with you?”","Zu An was speechless. Is this the time to be wondering about that?","Surprisingly, Firework murmured in confusion, “Hm? Something seems off. While I do harbor goodwill for you, this seems overboard. Did you use some kind of weird ability on me?”","Zu An said nothing.","He had an ability from the Golden Phoenix called ‘Love Is More Solid Than Gold’. It made women fall in love with him. Coincidentally, he'd only used that ability against Yan Xuehen because the latter was after his life. That made him eye Tingxue with guilt-ridden eyes.","Since then, he'd vowed not to use that despicable skill. It was underhanded to exploit someone else’s feelings like that.","That said, he wasn't an inflexible person. He would still use the ability if he was cornered.","He had indeed considered using it. It was a pity he didn’t have the Heiress Ball of Delights[1] anymore, so his only option was to use ‘Love Is More Solid than Gold’.","But he hadn’t even used that power yet. What was going on?","1. This item converts pain inflicted by a richer woman into sheer bliss ☜"]},{"number":2819,"title":"Chapter 2819: Chapter 2771: Conditions","paragraphs":["Even Tingxue looked at Zu An with a frown. Why does this feel weirdly familiar?","Firework also suspected that Zu An had used some weird skill on her.","Faced with their suspicions, Zu An was forced to respond, “Have you never felt warmth in your life?”","Firework’s expression darkened. “Rubbish! That has nothing to do with that!”","Zu An looked at Firework with eyes of pity. “I have an ability called ‘Love Is More Solid Than Gold’ that induces such effects, but I never used it against you. Your reaction likely stems from a lack of love in your life. That’s why you catch feelings quickly whenever someone treats you well.”","Tingxue’s expression flickered upon hearing the words, ‘Love Is More Solid Than Gold’, but walking down Nebula’s path had made her forget many things. Her miscellaneous thoughts scattered as ripples, and her mind reverted to its previous impassiveness.","Firework, on the other hand, reacted explosively, “I lack love? What a joke! Countless men queue up just to lick my feet. Powerhouses vie to send me precious treasures. Do you know how many people would die on my behalf? Yet you say I lack love?”","Her vehement response evoked a sigh from Zu An. “You know that isn’t love.”","Firework fell silent. She knew that as well. Some were afraid of her and wanted to get into her good books. Others coveted her beauty. Regardless, they had their motives for approaching her.","Nothing compared to the moment Zu An protected her from the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation. He'd held her so tightly in his arms that she hadn’t suffered the slightest damage other than the first whip. His desperation to protect her had been pure, untainted by any desires. That was why she was moved.","But there was no way she would admit to that. She proudly replied, “You arrogant brat! Just because I favor you doesn’t mean you can run your mouth as you please. I’m merely showing you magnanimity in view of the time we have spent together. How dare you lecture me? You must be tired of living!”","Firework’s aura flared, unleashing pressure comparable to that of a universal deity.","Tingxue frowned. She gripped her sword tightly, ready to launch a counterattack.","Breathing suddenly became difficult for Zu An. He barely held on by simultaneously using One Drop of Heaven’s Essence to tap into the earth vein’s energy and using the Heaven-Devouring Sutra to absorb more energy.","Just then, a spiderweb appeared in the sky.","A cold gleam flashed. Tingxue brandished her sword and sliced the web in two.","But it appeared to have a life of its own. It transformed into countless serpents that lunged at Tingxue and Zu An.","Tingxue brandished her sword without rest, tearing down wave after wave of attacks. However, during a momentary lapse in attention, a web coiled around her wrist and stalled her movements.","That opening was more than enough. In just an instant, she was thoroughly wrapped up, to the point where she could no longer move.","Zu An wasn’t faring any better. He unleashed the White Lotus Flame and the Phoenix Fire, thinking it could curb the spiderweb. However, it was completely unaffected by flames. That left him with no choice but to dodge the threads, but he was still caught in the end.","Firework smirked. “Let’s see where you can run now.”","Tingxue stared at Firework nonchalantly, her bright eyes slowly becoming murky like the nebula. She was charging up for a powerful move.","Firework frowned. “What a troublesome foe a Nebula envoy is...”","She was about to make her next move when Zu An suddenly spoke up. “You just want the key to release the seal, right? I’ll hand the key to you if you promise to free Tingxue, Isabella, Alfred, and the others.”","Firework burst into laughter. “I didn’t expect you to be a sentimental person. By being this soft-hearted, you’ll only bring harm upon yourself and your loved ones.”","Zu An pointed out, “Those people gathered here to save you. You shouldn’t repay goodwill with enmity.”","“They joined the expedition under the pretext of saving me, but all of them harbored ulterior motives. Only a fool like you would believe their words.” Firework harrumphed as her face turned cold. “I am the type of person to repay goodwill with enmity, anyway. You’re now all my prisoners. What right do you have to negotiate with me?”","“I am indeed no match for you, but I can bring you down with me. I hope you don’t force my hand,” Zu An calmly replied.","Firework frowned. “Oh? Are you trying to intimidate me again?”","Zu An shook his head. “It’s my last resort. I’ll have to pay a hefty price to invoke it. I’ll lose my life, and my soul might be condemned for all eternity. You've shown me mercy several times now. I don’t want to go to that extent, but if you continue cornering me, I’ll have no choice.”","He wasn’t even sure if Keyboard Come would work on Firework. She was so powerful that he risked being destroyed before the skill could even take effect. But he had no other option. He could only take a gamble.","“Are you threatening me?” Firework’s expression darkened. The surrounding air turned cold.","“It’s not a threat, but advice from an old friend. I''ve already thought things through. It doesn’t matter to me whether you escape from your seal or not; I have no interest in maintaining order in the Myriad Worlds.”","Zu An had gotten a rough grasp of Firework’s temperament. She was more of a carrot person than a stick person. It wouldn’t be wise to agitate her. That said, those were his earnest thoughts.","Even if Firework was a heinous villain, the Myriad Worlds were large enough for her to wreak havoc upon. Besides, the responsibility of dealing with such a powerful entity was supposed to fall on the universal deities and not a small fry like him.","Firework smiled. “That’s more like it. At least you aren’t an inflexible fool. I’d expect no less from a man I regard highly. Hand over the key, and I’ll release them.”","Zu An opened his palm and revealed the key.","Firework was surprised. “Aren’t you worried about me reneging on my promise?”","Zu An smiled. “I might not have spent much time with you, but I believe you aren’t that kind of person.”","Of course, he wouldn’t hesitate to bring Firework down with him if she reneged, but it was unnecessary to voice such jarring words.","Firework was pleased. “You’re getting more and more likable. All right, I’ll give you my word.”","The key appeared in her hand, and the cocoon around Tingxue and Zu An unraveled. She pulled a cocoon out from the fabric of space—it was Isabella, with only her face showing.","Upon seeing Zu An, her lips quivered and her eyes reddened. “Big brother Zu, be careful! Firework is...”","“Stop acting coy. He knows everything.” Firework harrumphed. This lass irks me.","Zu An consoled her. “Don’t worry, Isabella. It’s all right now.”","Firework flung her sleeves. “Come with me!”","She tore the fabric of space and headed to where the seal was."]},{"number":2820,"title":"Chapter 2820: Chapter 2772: Awakening","paragraphs":["Zu An replied grimly, “You've already obtained the key. Why do you need us to go with you?”","Firework coldly replied, “Can’t I just have you come with me? Didn’t you say I was lonely and empty? The least you can do is to accompany me.”","Zu An was stunned. Didn’t expect my words to come back and bite me so quickly.","As soon as Isabella broke free of her restraints, she ran to Zu An’s side to grab his arm, but Firework’s earlier ferocious glare made her hesitant to do so.","“Don’t worry, it’s fine now.” Zu An patted her hand to console her. He then turned to Firework and asked, “What about the others? Didn’t you agree to free them?”","“The sight of them irks me, so I didn’t take them with me. I've released them elsewhere,” Firework replied coldly.","Zu An was worried that she had secretly eliminated them, but he didn’t dare to point that out lest she be provoked by that question. That could prompt her to kill them for real if they weren’t dead yet. So, he could only suppress his curiosity.","Isabella tugged his sleeves and secretly asked him what was going on.","“I made a deal with her... Firework is one of her identities, and so is Yani...” Zu An roughly explained the situation. In truth, he was confused as well. What’s that woman’s real identity? And what’s the deal with Firework?","Isabella was startled by the revelations. At the same time, she was amazed. “Big brother Zu, you’re amazing to have overcome this sure-death crisis.”","She'd experienced Firework’s strength, and she couldn’t find any solutions against her despite her resourcefulness. Yet Zu An had somehow found a way to calm Firework.","Firework, who was walking in front, didn’t turn around, but she could see Isabella’s twinkling eyes. She knew no man could resist a young lady’s gaze of admiration. She would have killed Isabella if the latter were a scheming green tea bitch[1], but the girl was earnest. She couldn’t find a reason to make a move.","Isabella had sincerely come here to save her, and had even been calling her ‘big sister’ along the way...","Tingxue is much better. She’s cold, lofty, and doesn’t flirt with Zu An at all.","Zu An, Tingxue, and Isabella walked through the spatial passageway opened by Firework and returned to the heart-shaped stone.","Firework was about to insert the key when she thought about something and tossed the key to Zu An. “You do it.”","Zu An asked, “...Why are you letting someone else release your seal?”","Firework smiled. “You also know that it’s a seal targeted against me. What if there are some special measures embedded in it against me? I’d be courting my own death.”","Zu An had to concede that her words made sense. Being on the weaker side here, he had no choice but to take the key and march up to the stone.","“Be careful!” Isabella reminded him.","Despite Firework’s light-hearted demeanor, she stared intently at Zu An in case he attempted something. She was so focused on him that she overlooked Isabella’s ‘green tea bitch-esque’ demeanor.","Zu An chuckled. He took a deep breath before inserting the key. A brilliant light shone from the stone, making it appear like a beating heart.","At the same time, the rift valley where the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation was located emitted a red light, as if an entity had opened its eyes. No, it felt as if the rift valley was just a small part of its eye.","A desolate aura settled over the forbidden land, emanating pressure that was of even higher stature than Firework.","Firework was the first to sense the changes. She instantly appeared beside Zu An, grabbed his collar, and exclaimed, “You brat! What did you do?”","Tingxue hurriedly drew her sword and brandished it.","Isabella also ran over while searching her bag for an artifact that could help Zu An.","Zu An was dumbfounded. “I didn’t do anything. I merely followed your instructions and inserted the key.”","“Impossible. This is the seal restraining me, so why would it awaken Him...” Firework had maintained a lofty demeanor ever since she revealed her identity, as if everything was in her grasp. This was her first time panicking.","“Who are you talking about?” Zu An asked.","Just then, a blinding white light burst out from the heart-like stone and devoured everything, including him, Tingxue, and Isabella.","Firework was appalled. She tried to escape, but a mysterious force held her in place. What should have been an easy feat for her under any other circumstances became nigh impossible. She fought back with all her might, but her body was still devoured by the white light.","Despair seeped into her eyes as she screamed, “NO!”","She had schemed for countless years and was finally on the verge of breaking free, but everything had come crashing down on her at the last moment. She felt indignant, but that didn’t stop her from vanishing in the white light.","The white light soon faded. All four of them disappeared as if they had never been there.","...","When Zu An was devoured by the white light, he tried escaping via Rainbow Morph, but he quickly realized it didn’t work. It felt like his means were being restricted by some compelling force.","Before he knew it, he had already been transported from the dark, forbidden land to a world of bleak whiteness. He searched his surroundings, but Tingxue, Isabella, and even Firework were nowhere to be seen.","In the distance were winding stairs formed out of white clouds that led into the sky. The world was empty, except for the cloud stairs. This appeared to be a sign for him to scale them.","Zu An had experienced countless bizarre events in his life. Since there were no other clues, he decided to advance.","So, he walked to the stairs, only to lurch in shock. He'd been mistaken. The stairs weren't made out of clouds, but skulls stitched together. It merely looked like clouds from afar.","Unlike normal, gloomy skulls, these skulls emanated pristine white light as if they were the most exquisite works of art. It was just unnerving to see so many skulls gathered in one place.","As if sensing his arrival, the skulls suddenly turned to him and chanted, “Go up... Go up...”","Zu An was speechless.","Being the Netherworld’s master, this wasn't his first time seeing talking skulls, but it was terribly unsettling to be simultaneously stared at and talked to by tens of thousands of skulls.","He took a breath to calm himself before stepping on the chanting skulls and making his way up into the sky.","1. Green tea bitch refers to people who pretend to be innocent but are actually manipulative. ☜"]},{"number":2821,"title":"Chapter 2821: Chapter 2773: Death’s Mystery","paragraphs":["“Ugh! This fellow is very heavy.”","“Audacious, who dares to step on this exalted one’s head?”","“Wake up. You’re already dead!”","“What? I have conquered worlds and dominated universes. How can I possibly be dead?”","“His illness is flaring up again.”","The surrounding skulls shook their heads.","...","Zu An’s head hurt from the skulls’ chattering.","They had to have been top-notch experts back when they were still alive. They retained an imposing air despite being reduced to skulls, so much so that even their chattering was as potent as a barrage of mental attacks. Those who lacked mental fortitude would have long lost their minds from the simultaneous remarks of the tens of thousands of skulls.","Zu An pulled himself together. He considered using the Deity of Memory’s ‘Annals of History’ to banish these mental attacks into the River of History, but on second thought, the person at the end of these stairs could very well be antagonistic to Meng. It was best not to expose himself just yet. So, he channeled the Unshakable Daoist Manual to empty his mind as he continued scaling the stairs.","As he advanced, his flesh and blood gradually disappeared. It didn’t take him long to be reduced to a skeleton. The impact between his bony feet and the skull stairs produced eerie clacking sounds.","Zu An remained composed. He didn’t feel any pain despite having been turned into a skeleton. His mind remained clear. As he inspected his current form with his divine sense, he couldn’t help but marvel at the machinations of fate.","Qi Yaoguang had prophesied that he would be reduced to a skeleton. He'd thought that the prophecy had already been fulfilled at the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation, but who could have thought this would be it instead?","He had no idea how long he had been climbing for, as time seemed to lose its meaning here. Eventually, he arrived at the top of the stairs.","At the top was a throne made out of white bones. But even calling it a throne felt like an insult, as no throne in the world was as domineering as it. Even the majestic skulls weaved into the stairs quivered in the face of the white bone throne, as if they were peasants before the emperor.","The throne was empty, but the aura lingering on it was frightening. No one would dare take it lightly.","Zu An was taken aback. He recognized that unique aura to be divinity. He'd encountered something similar when he met the Deity of Chaos and Enigma and the Deity of Memory. The nature of the auras was different, but they shared a similar air of divinity.","“You’re here,” a dispassionate voice echoed.","Zu An raised his head and saw a pair of red eyes in the sky. Each eye extended beyond the horizon. They were so huge that even planets looked insignificant before them, let alone individuals.","Somehow, Zu An didn’t feel pressured by the eyes; if anything, he felt some intimacy toward the other party. He found this feeling inexplicable.","Zu An bowed. “Are you the Deity of Death?”","“You know me?” The eyes looked at Zu An.","Zu An sighed. “I would have died a long time ago if I couldn’t even figure this out.”","He had met a Death envoy in the ocean, and later, he'd heard a lot about the Deity of Death. There were also the overly conspicuous skull stairs, as well as his subsequent transformation into a skeleton. Everything was related to Death.","The massive red eyes in the sky rippled. “It's been a long time since anyone called me that.”","It looks like the rumors about the Deity of Death’s demise are untrue, Zu An thought.","“I am dead,” a voice echoed from the sky.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Shit. I nearly forgot that universal deities can hear thoughts. Worried that the other party would read more of his thoughts, he quickly changed the topic and asked, “Can the Deity of Death really die, too?”","“Do you find it ludicrous?”","“I dare not.”","“It goes without saying that the Deity of Death can die as well,” the voice calmly replied. “Nothing is fairer in the world than Death. Be it the strong or the weak, the wealthy or the poor, all beings are bound for death. I may be the Deity of Death, but I am not beyond this law myself.”","Zu An felt as if he had an epiphany, but that feeling quickly slipped away from him. “I heard rumors that you were ambushed by the Deity of Annhilation, and that’s why you...”","Since he was currently in the Deity of Death’s presence, he wasn’t worried about catching other universal deities’ gazes.","“The Deity of Annihilation is powerful, but he doesn’t have the means to kill me,” the Deity of Death replied proudly.","Zu An was perplexed. But you’re dead.","The Deity of Death was enraged by his thought. “The Deity of Annihilation wasn’t the only one who made a move.”","Zu An was astonished. It sounds like a huge secret at play here. I hope it isn’t another riddle. So, he got to the point and asked, “Did the Deity of Annihilation join hands with other universal deities?”","“It wasn’t just one or two of them. All of them were involved.” The Deity of Death dropped a bombshell.","Zu An was flabbergasted. He wouldn’t have been surprised if the Deity of Annihilation had a helper, but to think all the other universal deities were in on it. Wow, the Deity of Death must have been very hated. Good thing I didn’t use...","He quickly cut his thoughts short.","“What are your thoughts on the universal deities?”","“They are the strongest entities in the Myriad Worlds, the end points of their respective paths. Do you think such omnipotent beings would accept death?”","Those words provided enough clues for Zu An to figure out the other universal deities’ motive for killing the Deity of Death. Beings who had reached the top would be even more reluctant to accept death.","Only by slaying the Deity of Death, the embodiment of death, could one be eternal.","“We are fated.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Damn! I’d have celebrated if I heard that before learning the truth. This is a huge fortuitous encounter, a chance to inherit the Deity of Death’s legacy. But the Deity of Death was lynched to death by other universal deities! I might end up dead before I know it if I get involved with this karma.","“This is fate. You can’t escape it.” The Deity of Death knew his thoughts but didn’t lose his temper. “I sense death energy from you. You’re a Deity of Death in a minor world.”","Zu An was stunned. Indeed, he was the Netherworld’s master in the World of Cultivation, so that technically made him a Deity of Death as well.","“That was the reason I guided you here,” the Deity of Death said with a hint of excitement.","Zu An widened his eyes. It suddenly occurred to him that he was only able to enter this forbidden land because of Death Envoy Alati’s key...","He'd thought this was all Firework’s scheme, but from the looks of it now, Firework was just an unknowing pawn in the Deity of Death’s karma.","“Is that powerful demon spider your worshiper, too?” Zu An asked.","“No, she’s the gatekeeper of this forbidden land.”"]},{"number":2822,"title":"Chapter 2822: Chapter 2774: An Impossible Trial","paragraphs":["“Gatekeeper?” Zu An was startled. Wasn’t Firework sealed here? How did she become the gatekeeper?","“She’s also a pitiful one,” the Deity of Death calmly said. “She pledged allegiance to a certain universal deity to exact vengeance, but that resulted in the demonification of her body. In the end, she could only stay here to keep watch over me. She’s a prisoner as much as a warden.”","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected Firework to have such a background. So, which universal deity did Firework pledge allegiance to?","“Pardon my candid question. I understand she is strong, but does she truly wield the strength to keep watch on a universal deity?”","“I’m dead,” the Deity of Death stated impassively as if he wasn’t talking about himself. “I’m merely a sliver of consciousness, and her job is to keep that sliver from leaving this land.”","Zu An looked at the eyes in the sky. He’s a universal deity indeed. Even a sliver of his consciousness commands such great power. Just approaching him strips me of my flesh and blood.","“May I ask which universal deity Firework pledged allegiance to that resulted in her demonification?” he asked.","“This information is too dangerous for you right now. The closer you approach, the easier it will be for you to land in her plight,” the Deity of Death warned.","Zu An’s heart quivered. The Deity of Death had divulged so much information to him that he'd nearly forgotten how dangerous secrets were.","“If it’s not too rude, may I ask why you have summoned me here?” Since he had no inclination to remain here as a skeleton for the rest of his life, he had to advance the conversation.","“We are fated. You’re the most likely candidate I have met in the past ten thousand years to inherit Death’s will. Are you willing to take on this legacy?” The pair of massive, elongated red eyes stared at him.","Zu An felt inexplicable pressure weighing on him. He meekly asked, “What will happen if I refuse?”","“You’ll become one of them.” The red eyes glanced at the stairs of skulls.","Zu An was dumbfounded. He immediately changed his tune and said, “It will be my utmost honor to receive the revered Deity of Death’s teaching.”","You must be kidding me!","The Deity of Death was lynched to death by other universal deities. If I inherit his will, I’d potentially draw the ire of other universal deities. But that will at least be a problem to deal with in the future.","Right now, if I don’t accept the Deity of Death’s offer, I’ll die on the spot. It’s obvious what I should choose!","“You’re indeed fated with the path of Death. I shall open a trial for you. Clear it, and you shall inherit my legacy and the Dao of Death,” the red eyes in the sky said.","Zu An was dumbstruck. “I have to do another trial? Can’t you just impart your legacy to me?”","“Of course not,” the red eyes sternly replied. “It’s the rule I set before my death. Not even I have the power to change it. What you’re inheriting is not just my legacy but the Dao of Death as well. You have to clear the trial to earn Death’s recognition.”","“What if I fail the trial?” Zu An frowned.","“You’ll become one of them.” The Deity of Death glanced at the stairs of skulls once more.","Zu An was stunned. You must be kidding me! Even if I accept the trial, there’s still a huge chance of me becoming a foothold for others?","“Almost all of the skulls you see were powerhouses in their respective worlds. They coveted my legacy, but they failed the trial. Tread carefully. I have expectations for you. Don’t let me down,” the Deity of Death spoke concernedly.","Zu An stared at the endless stairs of skulls with his mouth agape. “So many people have challenged your trial?” Isn’t he sealed here? How did so many people find their way here?","“I may be dead, but Death persists. Death senses those inclined to the Dao of Death, no matter where they are, and guides them here.” The Deity of Death harrumphed. “There has been no lack of attempts from ambitious fools and spies from other universal deities to usurp my authority over Death, but they all became a part of that staircase.","“Hm? You seem intent on keeping your mind empty. Are you withholding something from me?” The Deity of Death suddenly eyed Zu An warily.","“There’s no way I could hide anything from a revered universal deity like yourself,” Zu An hurriedly replied. “If you have expectations of me, why don’t you offer me some clues to help me out?”","“That’s out of the question.” The Deity of Death rejected the request.","Zu An gestured to the endless stairs of skulls. “You said these people were powerhouses from their respective worlds; their strength and wits are bound to surpass mine. If they all failed, no matter how arrogant I am, I can’t say that I have the confidence to clear the trial.”","The Deity of Death impatiently interjected, “What are you trying to say? This is Death’s trial. Obtaining the Deity of Death’s legacy means there’s a high chance you may grow to become a universal deity. Those who strive for such heights should be prepared to fall to their deaths.”","“Is there a chance this trial is impossible to clear? So many people have attempted it and failed. If there’s a way to clear the trial, someone should have found the method by now.”","“There is a way to clear this trial, but these people aren’t fated with Death, so they can only return to Death’s embrace.”","“When did you prepare this trial?”","“What do you mean?”","“Was it before or after you were ambushed by the other universal deities?”","The Deity of Death fell silent. Even though he was just a sliver of consciousness, it didn’t take him long to fathom a possibility.","Zu An took this chance to push his case. “They ganged up on you to be freed from Death’s restraints. Why would they allow someone else to inherit your legacy?”","“You’re suggesting that they might have tampered with the trial?”","“I don’t know the other universal deities. You should know their temperament far better than me.” Zu An didn’t dare to gossip about other universal deities behind their backs, so he could only subtly lead the Deity of Death toward his conclusion.","The two elongated red eyes in the sky trembled. “Those motherfuckers! That sounds like something they are capable of! ¥%#@*&...”","What followed was a long string of furious curses. Zu An, despite having inherited Fleeting Baldie’s knowledge of languages, struggled to understand many of the phrases used, but he didn’t need to understand the language to figure out that there was a high concentration of expletives in the words.","After cursing for a long time, the Deity of Death finally regained his composure and said, “There’s not much I can tell you due to the rules I set back then. You won’t be the only one entering the trial. Your three companions will be there as well...”","Zu An said, “...Firework is far stronger than me. How can I be a match for her if she enters too?”","“You don’t have to worry about that. I have taken that into consideration. That world limits all supernatural abilities.”"]},{"number":2823,"title":"Chapter 2823: Chapter 2775: A Familiar World","paragraphs":["“Forbids all supernatural power...” Zu An was surprised.","He hadn’t expected the trial to have such a peculiar setting. They had cultivated for so long that they were already accustomed to their superhuman powers. It was unnerving to suddenly be robbed of their powers and reverted to mortal status.","“I have a question. You said that I was fated with death, so why are you bringing them into the trial as well?” Zu An was confused.","Putting aside the fact that having Firework in the trial would make things far more dangerous for him, he was also reluctant to put Isabella and Tingxue in danger. No one had been able to clear the trial thus far, so there was a huge chance of them becoming part of the skulls in the stairs.","I’m sure their skulls would be delicate and beautiful... Pui pui pui, I shouldn’t be thinking about that now!","The Deity of Death replied, “There’s a chance they could be favored by the Dao of Death. Not many people have been able to get here, and the path of Death needs an inheritor. To boost the chances of finding the right person, the trial must involve everyone who makes their way here.”","Zu An was speechless. You’re just scattering your net as wide as possible. But looking at the stairs of skulls, it feels like quite a lot of people have reached this place.","He hurriedly cleared his mind and asked, “Is that all? Isn’t there more useful information?”","“I have made an exception by offering you two pieces of information. You should be satisfied!”","“What two pieces of information?!”","“One, the trial takes place in a world where supernatural powers are limited. Two, your companions will be participating in the trial as well.”","Zu An was stunned. He would have been cursing in his mind if he hadn’t known that the Deity of Death could read minds. The information offered was worthless!","“These two pieces of information aren’t helpful in the trial. Aren’t you looking for someone to inherit Death’s will? You can offer me more help since we’re fated.”","“That won’t do. The trial has to be impartial.”","“But the trial has likely been tampered with by other... entities! Challengers like me would be severely handicapped if we entered the trial without prior information. That goes against your principle of having a fair trial.”","The red eyes in the sky shook. Seconds later, he replied with a sigh, “I have met no lack of sharp-witted fellows who tried to gather information from me over the years, but you’re the first one to convince me. Alright, I’ll reveal another piece of information to you. I noticed that the world this trial is set in has some relation to you.”","Zu An was first overjoyed before confusion set in. “How is it related to me?”","The Deity of Death had prepared this trial to select his successor. He couldn’t fathom how the trial’s world could have anything to do with him.","Hold on, did he read my memories?","“The trial’s world is grounded in what I heard from a good friend. That friend was the death god of his respective world, and the stories about his world left a deep impression on me. So, when I rushed to create the trial’s world, I used his world as the backdrop.”","Zu An’s heartbeat quickened—it was bizarre how he still had such sensations even though he was only a skeleton now. “Was your friend called the Necropolis Emperor?”","“No, he’s known as Yama in his world.”","Zu An was stunned. There are indeed ten Yamas in the Netherworld. I wonder which one it was. It’s a pity all the Yamas and the ghost guards were gone by the time I took over the Netherworld, so there’s much I don’t know about it.","“He remains impartial before the world, thus establishing a fair order.”","A figure appeared in Zu An’s mind. But just as he was about to probe further, the Deity of Death said, “I have revealed too much. You have to enter the trial now, or else you’ll be sanctioned by the restriction I imposed back then.”","Zu An felt the world spin around him, as if he had been pulled into a massive temporal vortex. Some time later, everything fell silent.","He found himself lying on a bed. He pulled the blanket off and breathed a sigh of relief after confirming he wasn’t a skeleton anymore. Despite retaining his sense of self as a skeleton, who could get used to such a body?","A feeling of weakness suddenly gripped him, and he nearly fell to the ground.","He had indeed lost his cultivation. He had considerable vitality compared to his peers, but he was indescribably weaker than his usual self. To make things worse, his massive divine sense had vanished. He now had to rely on his eyes and ears, and that made him feel crippled.","He tried to execute his skills, but none of those overpowered moves could be used. He even tried summoning Mi Li, but there was no response.","It makes me feel so helpless to be a mortal...","The only silver lining was that Firework had been turned into a mortal as well. She was bound to have lost more than him. That realization lifted his spirits a little.","He grabbed a copper mirror to scrutinize his appearance. When he saw that he still had his own face, he breathed a sigh of relief.","He proceeded to survey the surroundings. His room wasn't opulent, but it was tidy and well-furnished. This suggested that the identity he'd taken on in this world was from a decent background.","Hold on. Copper mirror? And this layout resembles medieval shows as well. Have I been transported into one of the older Chinese dynasties? No wonder the Deity of Death said the trial’s world was related to me.","To think that he could read my memories. I feel as if I was stripped bare before him.","He suddenly remembered the impartial Yama whom the Deity of Death mentioned. It wasn't too difficult to figure out that Yama’s identity.","The Song Dynasty’s Bao Zheng was known for his impartial and upright nature. The populace lauded him as Justice Bao. It was often rumored that he dealt with mortal cases in the day and interrogated souls at night. He was also believed to have become a Yama after his death, and there was indeed such an impartial figure in the Netherworld.","Am I in the Song Dynasty?","Hold on. I've been to the Xia, Shang, Qin, and Tang Dynasties’ dungeons. If this is the Song Dynasty, could this be an Unknown Region, too? But this is the Deity of Death’s trial. Surely it can’t be that coincidental, right?","Just then, someone knocked on the door. “Third Young Master, are you awake? The old master and old madam are calling for you. They have something they would like to discuss with you.”","Zu An was surprised. Third Young Master?","Who am I? Am I Sword God Xie Xiaofeng? No, Xie Xiaofeng isn’t from this dynasty.","He opened his door, and the eyes of the servant outside lit up. “Third Young Master, you’re amazing. You recovered quickly after sustaining such severe injuries!”","“Was I injured...” Zu An was perplexed. He considered asking where he was and who his parents were, but he was worried he would give himself away. Thus, he decided to withhold his questions and let things run their course first.","Soon, he was brought to a remote room. As soon as he stepped in, a beautiful middle-aged woman grabbed his hand and worriedly asked, “Polu, how are your injuries?”","Zu An was speechless.","—","Guo Polu is a side character from Return of the Condor Heroes (a very famous Wuxia work in China that almost everyone knows about), and the story is set in the Song Dynasty."]},{"number":2824,"title":"Chapter 2824: Chapter 2776: The Secret Plan","paragraphs":["While Zu An was heading over, he'd noticed wounded soldiers bandaging themselves and black smoke rising from the distant city center. The scent of blood and gunpowder lingered in the air.","That led him to think he was from a general clan, and they had just fought a war. Judging from the wounded soldiers all around, they appeared to have lost the battle.","But the beautiful middle-aged woman calling him ‘Polu’ made his mind come to a halt. That name was terribly familiar. The first thought that came to his mind was Guo Jing and Huang Rong’s son, Guo Polu.","I thought dungeons emulated history. Why is there novel content in them as well?","On second thought, a universal deity could grasp all knowledge and culture about a world in an instant. It wouldn’t be surprising for them to combine different elements to create a unique trial.","“I’m fine now,” Zu An replied.","Had the middle-aged woman not mentioned it, he wouldn’t have noticed it. There were indeed parts of his body where blood flowed more slowly, but those could hardly be considered an injury. Even the lightest injury he'd sustained in recent years was far more severe than this.","But it struck him that his current body was different from his usual superhuman one. He couldn’t compare them using the same standards.","“You must have been diligently practicing Quanzhen Inner Energy[1] in recent years to have recovered so fast.” The stern middle-aged man sitting in the center chair finally revealed a heartened smile.","“It could be the Nine Yin Manual[2]. I imparted it to him recently,” the middle-aged woman said.","“Rong’er, you dote on our children too much. It’s still too early for Polu to be practicing the Nine Yin Manual. It might work against him,” the middle-aged man replied sternly.","Zu An was silent, but that affirmed his guess.","The couple in front of him were Guo Jing and Huang Rong from the Legend of the Condor Heroes, and his identity was that of a side character who had only appeared on Guo Xiang’s birthday, Guo Polu.","Hold on, I thought supernatural powers were banned? Why is the setting a Wuxia world?","But then again, compared to the powers displayed in the Cultivation World and the Myriad Worlds, I guess martial arts are hardly supernatural abilities. They can, at most, be considered physical training.","Taking a closer look, the couple before him was beyond middle-aged. Guo Jing’s hair was turning white. Huang Rong had maintained her complexion better, but wrinkles could be seen at the corners of her eyes. Time had still left its mark on her.","Zu An couldn’t help remembering a famous phrase—’beauties are like famous generals; their gradual withering is not meant for the world’s eyes’. But then it quickly struck him that Huang Rong was now his mother, and that made him feel terribly awkward.","Huang Rong harrumphed. “The Mongols have already invaded the Central Plains. I ought to impart everything I can to him while I can.”","Guo Jing fell silent. The atmosphere in the room became grim.","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected to hear such depressing words from top experts in this world.","Hold on. He suddenly remembered the reflection he'd seen in the copper mirror earlier. I should be in my twenties or early thirties in this world. Guo Jing and Huang Rong have been guarding Xiangyang [3] against the invading Mongols in the south. Could it be...","“Guo’er won a decade of peace for us by assassinating the Mongol’s Möngke Khan[4], but the Mongols have made a comeback and have erected their base camp right outside Xiangyang. The imperial court’s resources have dried up from reinforcing Xiangyang. It’s unlikely we can turn the tide of the battle.” Guo Jing’s resolute eyes looked downcast.","“Big brother Jing, you have already done your best. Xiangyang would have succumbed years ago if not for you. This time, the Mongols invaded Persia, cutting off the imperial court’s access to the Silk Road. On top of that, the Mongols are also harassing our southwest border over at Dali. Our other battlefronts are struggling. This is not a problem you can resolve alone,” Huang Rong consoled him.","Guo Jing sighed. He understood all those things, but a defeat was still a defeat. In this case, no justification would make a difference.","Huang Rong changed the subject and said, “Polu, Xiang’er, we called you here today to plant a seed for the future.”","It was only then that Zu An noticed a young lady sitting in the corner of the room. She had a delicate appearance, exuding an air of sweetness and valiance. She was Huang Rong’s second daughter, Guo Xiang, though they looked nothing alike.","Of course they don’t look alike. Zu An looked at the young lady, who was staring intently at him, and chills ran down his spine.","She was Firework! Just as Zu An's appearance hadn’t changed, Firework’s appearance remained the same as well. It turned out that they were all roleplaying here.","“Second sister...” Zu An greeted Firework.","“Heh. Yes, my good third brother.” The young lady chuckled.","Zu An was speechless. This sarcastic tone. No doubt about it. She’s Firework.","Huang Rong frowned. “What’s wrong with you two? Why do your tones sound so weird?”","Zu An and Firework were startled. Neither of them knew the criteria for clearing and failing this trial. There was a chance they would be eliminated if their identities were exposed. They didn’t dare risk it, so they decided to play their roles.","But Firework knew next to nothing about this world. She was still too shaken up from losing her immense powers to quickly adapt to the situation.","Fortunately, Zu An quickly changed the subject. “We were curious as to why our big sister isn’t here.”","Huang Rong shook her head. “Too much is at stake here; Fu’er is not sharp-witted enough to participate in this plan.”","Firework was impressed by Zu An’s swift reaction. He’s a sharp one. So, we have a big sister named Fu’er in this world?","Zu An had to hold back his laughter. I guess Guo Fu’s reputation is truly terrible.","At the same time, he understood why the Deity of Death had said he had an advantage in this trial. Firework, Tingxue, and Isabella knew nothing about this world’s backstory, and that was bound to be to their disadvantage.","“All right, let’s get back to the topic at hand,” Huang Rong said. “We have tried everything against the Mongols in recent years, but we have no choice but to conclude that fate is siding with the Mongols now. The Central Plains’ downfall is set in stone. It’s nigh impossible to fight against fate.","“But fate will not side with them forever. Just as quickly as the grassland tribes have conquered the world on horseback, they will eventually fall off their high horses and lose the world. It might take decades or even centuries. The only thing we can do is to plant a seed for the future, so that our descendants can reclaim the world once the tides no longer favor the Mongols.”","“Our secret plan is named the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan[5]!”","1. The Quanzhen Sect is a nominally righteous daoist sect in the story, though they play an antagonist role. ☜","2. The Nine Yin Manual is one of the legendary skills in the series that even top experts seek to obtain ☜","3. Xiangyang was an important fortress city in the Song dynasty, used against the Mongols. ☜","4. Khan is the leader of the Mongolian tribes. ☜","5. This term is literally translated as ‘Following providence to slay the dragon plan’. The dragon that they are seeking to bring down here refers to the Mongols. ☜"]},{"number":2825,"title":"Chapter 2825: Chapter 2777: Soul-Crushing Interrogation","paragraphs":["Zu An was stunned.","This plan had only been briefly touched on in the original series. A hundred years passed before it became known to the world. Zu An had never thought he would become a part of this plan.","“We shall follow heaven’s will and slay the dragon known as the Yuan Mongols!” Huang Rong said with a determined look. “Since ancient times, no dynasty has remained eternally strong. An empire built by nomads is bound to be unstable. So, we have to make preparations. We will tide through the darkness and bring light and order back to the world!”","Firework finally snapped out of her daze. “How do you intend to do that?”","Huang Rong frowned. Don’t you think your tone is rude here?","She'd had a scare giving birth to Guo Xiang, so she favored Guo Fu a bit more. Guo Fu was dense, but she was caring and sweet-tongued as well. In contrast, Guo Xiang was eccentric, and it was hard to read her thoughts.","But ultimately, Guo Xiang was still her child...","Thus, Huang Rong suppressed her displeasure and explained, “We intend to forge two godly weapons.”","Firework frowned. Her cultivation had been sealed, but she had the brains to figure out that a world devoid of supernatural powers couldn’t possibly make truly powerful weapons. To hope to change fate with just two mortal weapons was a pipe dream.","Are the people of this world so shallow? And of all people, they had to be my parents. Can’t I kill them?","The intelligent Huang Rong keenly sensed Guo Xiang’s contempt. She was annoyed but relieved at the same time. Such an important responsibility can only be entrusted to someone as smart as Xiang’er. Fu’er is too dumb for this.","“Big brother Jing, why don’t you explain it to them?” The meticulous Huang Rong deferred to her husband out of respect.","Guo Jing was more concerned about the success of the plan. “We’ll forge two weapons, the Heavenly Sword and the Dragon Slaying Saber. We’ll hide the Book of Wumu, which contains the crystallization of King Yue’s military insights, in the Dragon Slaying Saber. When the tides turn, the heroes of the world will rally the Han[1] to overthrow the Mongols. The Book of Wumu will teach them warfare, so that we can triumph in every battle.","“To prevent the Dragon Slaying Saber from falling into the wrong hands and scourging the populace, we’ll place the Nine Yin Manual into the Heavenly Sword. This way, we can nurture powerful martial artists capable of assassinating tyrants and corrupt officials, so that they will have to treat their subjects kindly.”","Guo Jing spoke passionately, as if he could already see the bright future ahead.","Huang Rong looked at Guo Jing gently. Despite being in his fifties, his heroic spirit remains as charming as ever.","While the couple was feeling moved to tears, Firework suddenly interjected, “I have a question.”","Guo Jing smiled. “Xiang’er, you are involved in this plan as well. Feel free to speak your mind. We should work out the kinks to increase our chances of success.”","Firework frankly asked, “You should be well-versed in the Book of Wumu, right... Father?”","Under normal circumstances, she wouldn’t have even glanced at this insignificant being. It killed her a little inside to call Guo Jing ‘father’. But this was the Deity of Death’s trial, and she had no idea what awaited her if she failed the trial, so she dropped her obstinacy.","“Of course,” Guo Jing replied right away.","“Then, why don’t you lead the army and win every battle against the Mongols?” Firework looked straight at Guo Jing with large eyes.","Guo Jing’s face turned bright red. He stuttered, “Perhaps due to my lacking aptitude, I’m unable to grasp its essence.”","Zu An was amused. Firework is delivering critical strikes with her questions.","Huang Rong knew Guo Jing wasn't good with words, so she explained on his behalf, “You rascal. No matter how well-versed your father is with military tactics, our Great Song doesn’t have the resources to fight against the Mongols. As the saying goes, even a skilled housewife struggles to cook anything up without grains.","“Also, I said earlier that fate is siding with the Mongols. Their army is unstoppable right now. But a hundred years from now, when fate no longer favors them, the inheritor of the Book of Wumu will be facing a completely different situation.”","Entities like Firework had a deeper understanding of fate. Fate could make everything go smoothly, as if the world was coordinating things to ensure one’s success, but it could also spell the doom of even the mightiest heroes in the world.","Huang Rong’s words rang true.","“Father and mother, you have learned the Nine Yin Manual. Why don’t you assassinate the Mongol tyrant?” Guo Xiang probed on. “If even the two of you can’t do that, there’s no guarantee the next person who learns the Nine Yin Sutra will be stronger than you. How can you expect them to be the executor of tyrants?”","Guo Jing and Huang Rong were speechless.","Guo Jing murmured in shock, “Rong’er, were we wrong? Is this plan doomed to fail right from the start? Is there no way to pass down the seeds of the Han?”","Upon seeing his heartbroken appearance, Huang Rong become agitated. “Xiang’er, you shouldn’t be talking nonsense for something as important as this!”","Firework calmly replied, “I'm not talking nonsense. I’m considering the feasibility of your plan.”","She had no idea what the criteria for clearing the Deity of Death’s trial was, but it had to be related to this plan. However, if it was that simple, someone would have succeeded by now. Naturally, she ought to understand every detail of the plan.","Huang Rong was angered by Guo Xiang’s talking back. She was starting to regret involving the latter in this plan.","It was then that Zu An interjected, “I think it’s feasible. Fate is siding with the Mongols now. Their armies are unrivaled, and many experts have pledged allegiance to them. No matter how strong our... father and mother are, it’d be hard for them to assassinate the Khan under the protection of so many experts.","“But a hundred years from now, when fate no longer sides with the Mongols, things won’t be as smooth for them. The people will rise up against them, and competent individuals will no longer side with them. Someone who wields the Heavenly Sword and has mastered the Nine Yin Manual will have room to do much more.”","Huang Rong was heartened. “Polu, you have always been reticent, so I didn’t expect you to have thought things through so clearly. Your father and I can finally put our hearts at ease.”","Firework spent a moment in thought before acknowledging Zu An’s explanation. “We have the Book of Wumu and the Nine Yin Manual. What about the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber?”","Her willingness to cooperate evoked a sigh of relief from Huang Rong. “It all falls on Guo’er.”","Huang Rong looked at Firework with sympathetic eyes and said, “Xiang’er, I know you have been traveling around in search of Guo’er. You’re already an old maiden now...” Had I known this would happen, I wouldn't have been so guarded against Guo’er back then.","Firework stayed silent. She had no idea what was going on or who Guo’er was at all.","Huang Rong reined in her feelings and said, “We need your help here. You should also know that there have been conflicts between Guo’er and our family. You’re the only one he’s not averse to. We need you to persuade him to offer his Xuan Metal Sword to forge the godly weapons.”","1. The Han have been the dominant and majority ethnicity of ancient China across multiple dynasties. ☜"]},{"number":2826,"title":"Chapter 2826: Chapter 2778: Do You Submit?","paragraphs":["Firework was confused, but Zu An understood the context. He stepped in and spoke up on her behalf. “Second sister has searched for Hero Yang for many years now, but to no avail. He might be avoiding her intentionally.”","Huang Rong looked at Firework with pity. “Guo’er and Miss Long faced many tribulations before their love finally bore fruit. They don’t want to be interrupted, which is why Guo’er has been avoiding Xiang’er. But if he sees you with your second sister, he should understand that Xiang’er is seeking him not to court him, but for more important business.”","With her sharp wits, it wasn’t too difficult for her to decipher Yang Guo’s intentions. She had refrained from voicing that aloud to spare her daughter’s dignity, hoping that the latter would back down after hitting a wall. She hadn’t expected her daughter to be this obstinate, devoting the golden years of her youth to searching for Yang Guo.","Firework finally grasped what was going on. So I’m just a total simp in this world? Audacious! There is no guy in this world who's worth me simping over!","She turned to Zu An. How does he know the background of this world? Did he arrive here earlier than me?","Huang Rong turned to Zu An. “Polu, I want you to accompany your second sister to Mount Zhongnan’s Tomb of Living Dead[1] to see if Guo’er is there. As long as he’s willing to meet you, I believe he should be willing to offer his Xuan Metal Sword for this plan.”","Zu An nodded. “Is there anything else I should do?”","“Your father and I will be devoting our energy to condensing the Nine Yin Manual and the Book of Wumu. The space within the two godly weapons will be limited, so we’ll have to pick our words carefully,” Huang Rong said with a frown. This was easier said than done.","Guo Jing instructed, “The Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan is confidential. You mustn’t let anyone else know about it.”","Huang Rong added, “Polu, I know you care greatly for your big sister, but you mustn’t let her know about this.”","Zu An was, once again, impressed by how low Huang Rong’s impression of Guo Fu was.","After leaving the hidden chamber, Firework pulled Zu An over to her room. Guo Jing and Huang Rong smiled, heartened by the siblings’ good relationship.","Upon reaching her room, Firework pushed Zu An onto the bed before planting her foot in between his thighs. She looked down on him with a dangerous glint in her eyes.","Zu An remarked, “We're twins in this world. It will be terrible if others see us like that...”","Firework harrumphed. “Cut the crap and tell me what’s going on.”","Zu An carefully moved her foot aside before sitting upright. “Don’t you already know what’s going on?”","“Why did my cultivation suddenly disappear? This body is too weak!” Firework couldn’t get used to the immense nerf she'd suffered.","“You don’t know? This world forbids all supernatural powers.” Zu An was surprised.","“Why is there such a setting?” Firework frowned.","I guess the Deity of Death wasn’t lying to me, after all. The information he revealed to me beforehand is at least worth something. That lifted Zu An’s spirits a little. “It could be to make the trial fairer. We would be slaughted by you otherwise.”","“Do I look that scary to you?” Firework was displeased.","Shouldn’t you have some self-awareness? Zu An thought.","“Hold on. When did you enter this trial?” Firework asked.","“We came in together,” Zu An replied in confusion, intrigued by the intent of her question.","“That can’t be. You know a lot more about this world than I do,” Firework said icily.","Even though they'd been devoured by the white light at the same time, there were plenty of methods in this world to alter the flow of time, meaning Zu An could have spent years in here before her.","“I was lucky. This world has some connection to my previous world,” Zu An replied. I wonder where Tingxue and Isabella are, and what identities they've taken on in this world.","“Oh?” Firework’s eyebrows shot up. “That old scamp Death opened a backdoor for you!”","Zu An found it hard to deny that.","“What’s going on here? They mentioned Mongols, Great Song, and some Yang Guo fellow. Hurry up and fill me in on the details,” Firework urged.","Zu An looked at her weirdly. “Why would I do that?”","Speaking of which, I still have no idea what the condition for clearing this trial is. Do I need to ensure the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber plan goes smoothly? But Firework appears to be in the same camp as me.","If the plan goes smoothly, will I inherit the Deity of Death’s legacy or will she? Surely we can’t both inherit the legacy, right?","Also, those who failed the trial are doomed to become skulls on the stairs. What if Tingxue and Isabella aren’t in the same faction as me? Will they die if I clear the trial?","Firework clenched her fists, the sounds of her cracking knuckles echoing loudly. “Do you think you can defy me just because this world bans supernatural powers?”","Zu An chuckled. “Why should I obey you when this world bans supernatural powers?”","Bam!","A fist flew into his abdomen, smashing him into the wall.","“You didn’t give a warning! That’s so unsportsmanlike!” Zu An got up and fought back.","He thought he'd have an advantage over Firework, as the latter would likely be unaccustomed to her mortal body given how strong she had been. Given they were the same age and had learned the same martial arts, he, with a man’s physique, was supposed to have the upper hand.","They quickly traded ten blows.","Zu An first started out confident. He possessed a Wonderpoint World’s World Law Beacon, and that granted him a deeper understanding over martial arts and world laws than even those who were far stronger than him. In fact, if they were pulled down to his level, he'd thought that he could rival even universal deities.","But this was the moment he realized he was a frog in a well.","Given his vast knowledge, it only took him the blink of an eye to assimilate all of Guo Polu’s martial arts. He could even exert strength far surpassing that of the original Guo Polu.","But Firework didn’t pale in comparison. Her grasp of martial arts even appeared to be superior!","Zu An struggled right from the start, and several blows even breached his defense and struck him squarely. However, he wasn’t the type to give up easily. He gritted his teeth and continued trading blows with Firework while contemplating her moves.","Some time later, Firework found an opening and pressed his hands down to the bed.","“Do you submit?” Firework asked gleefully.","“I don’t!” Zu An wriggled his body. He was attempting to pincer her with his thighs to flip her over and pin her down.","But Firework easily neutralized his attempts to turn the tables with precise movements. She even found a chance to pin him down completely, stopping him from making any moves.","“You should finally submit now, no?” Firework asked.","Now that she had lost her supernatural powers, her stamina was much lower; just the earlier fight was enough to make her breathless. Now that she had pinned him down, it suddenly struck her just how close they were.","Just then, the door opened. “Xiang’er, Polu, why did mother call... What are you doing?”","1. This is the Ancient Tomb Sect’s base, where Xiaolongnu first met Yang Guo and trained him. ☜"]},{"number":2827,"title":"Chapter 2827: Chapter 2779: Where’s the Risk?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2779: Where’s the Risk?","A gorgeous lady with crescent eyes and pink cheeks stood by the doorway.","She wore an extravagant blue damask[1] shirt with leopard skin at the collars. Such clothes would have appeared excessive on most women, but not her. On the contrary, it felt as if only such luxurious clothes were worthy of her beauty.","Zu An swiftly realized she was Guo Jing and Huang Rong’s oldest daughter, Guo Fu. It was commonly said that she had inherited her father’s head and her mother’s beauty.","Guo Fu’s mind had frozen up. She'd come here to scout the situation, curious to know why her parents had called her siblings but not her. She hadn’t expected to stumble upon this sight as soon as she opened the door.","Firework was sitting on Zu An’s body, her hands pinning down his. As there was no longer a vast disparity in their strength, she needed to exert her full force to keep him in place. As a result, their bodies were pressed against each other. Their faces were so close to each other that it looked as if they would kiss the next second.","What are they doing? I thought Xiang’er liked Yang Guo?","Maybe she’s feeling lonely from years of failing to court Yang Guo, so she's seeking other men for company. But most men don’t even catch her eye, so she must have decided to go for her little brother instead.","Countless thoughts surged into Guo Fu’s mind, causing her already dull brain to stall to a halt.","Firework and Zu An had been too busy fighting to pay heed to their positions. It was only when they saw Guo Fu’s horrified expression that they realized how inappropriate their current posture was.","Firework suddenly became aware of Zu An’s air of masculinity. His heat was palpable even through their clothes.","Meanwhile, Zu An clearly felt Firework’s shapely and youthful body. Even though Firework had never shied away from physical contact, this was the first time they had gotten into such an intimate posture.","The two of them quickly backed off. Firework awkwardly tidied her clothes and hair. “This rascal refused to listen to me. I was teaching him a lesson.”","She looked at Zu An tauntingly. “Do you submit?”","Zu An harrumphed. “Of course not. We’ll have a rematch another day.”","Despite his words, he was impressed with Firework. Her grasp of combat was at a transcendent level. Their brief clash had taught him much more than his fights with other experts.","Firework was also impressed by Zu An. She had spent some time with him now, and that gave her a good grasp of his strength. Even though he had several interesting skills, she hadn’t thought he was much of a fighter, especially considering his low cultivation.","While this world forbade supernatural powers, it wasn't as if she had been born strong. She had climbed a step at a time, undergoing countless life-and-death battles before she finally reached her current level. Her higher cultivation also granted her a deeper insight into the utilization of strength.","She'd thought that she could easily subdue Zu An even without tapping into her supernatural powers, but the battle turned out to be a surprisingly close one. How long has it been since I had such a tough battle?","Looking at how composed those two were, Guo Fu’s face reddened. How can I think of my siblings in such a light? What a sin! But she wasn't the type to admit her mistakes, so she put on a stern appearance and reprimanded them. “You aren’t young anymore. You should watch your boundaries even when fighting with each other. What if others see you like that?”","Firework’s eyebrows shot up. A mere ant dares talk to me like that?","Zu An quickly stepped in to clear the air. “Big sister, what brings you here?” He was worried Firework would murder Guo Fu in a moment of recklessness. That would turn their mission into hell mode.","“I heard that father and mother called you over. Did something happen? Why didn’t they call me as well?” Guo Fu sounded displeased.","“We made a breakthrough recently, so father and mother called us over to review our martial arts,” Zu An explained. “Big sister, are you interested in training? Shall I talk to them on your behalf?”","“Forget it.” Guo Fu waved her hand, not wanting to suffer by practicing martial arts. Zu An’s explanation had dispelled her curiosity. Worried that her younger siblings would see through her cowardice, she put on her big sisterly airs and instructed, “If you want to spar, do it in the training field. It’s unseemly to fight in the bedroom.”","She turned around and left, but Zu An hurriedly asked, “Big sister, where’s brother-in-law?”","“He’s too busy dealing with the Beggar Sect’s[2] affairs to accompany me. How annoying,” Guo Fu grumbled before leaving.","Firework asked, “Why did you suddenly ask about our brother-in-law?”","Someone who could grow to her extent couldn’t possibly be dumb. She was already getting into the flow of things. She knew Zu An wouldn’t ask an insignificant question.","Zu An hesitated, but considering they were in the same boat, he figured he should still share critical intelligence. “Our brother-in-law is Yelu Qi. His father, Yelu Chucai, was a member of the Liao royal family. When the Liao Country fell, they were left to wander the world. Yelu Chucai later became a powerful Mongolian official, wielding influence comparable to a prime minister.”","Firework was taken aback. “You’re saying they'll betray Great Song to join the Mongols?”","Zu An shook his head. “I don’t know. This is a world created by the Deity of Death, so it might not necessarily follow the trajectory of history. Yelu Qi doesn’t exist in real history, either.”","“That can’t be said for sure. You’re a Memory worshiper, so you should be well-versed with the tricks Time Scribes use. When a character doesn’t appear in history, they're either unimportant, or have been erased for some reason,” Firework sneered.","Zu An was also perplexed as to where the true danger was. The plan didn’t look too difficult to pull off, so it was baffling to him why everyone who came before him had failed.","Does the trial have nothing to do with whether the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan succeeds? Or is there some compelling reason causing the plan to fail?","He racked his brain and concluded that the biggest threat was the Yelu Family. Yelu Chucai had to have contributed greatly to the Mongols to have become such a powerful official in the future.","The Yelu Family’s close ties with the Guo Family made it likely for them to learn about the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan. In fact, Zu An even suspected Guo Fu’s motive for probing them for information.","Guo Jing and Huang Rong had secretly called them over to not alert Guo Fu, yet she'd still learned about it. Did Yelu Qi instigate her to gather information from the Guo Family, and she foolishly did so without knowing she was being exploited?","1. A woven patterned silk fabric ☜","2. The Beggar Sect is a righteous power that helped the Song Dynasty resist the Mongols. It is a massive sect, consisting of beggars across cities that form a huge intelligence network. ☜"]},{"number":2828,"title":"Chapter 2828: Chapter 2780: Variables","paragraphs":["“Do you think the key to the trial is completing the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan?” Zu An asked Firework. She was highly intelligent, evident from how she had woven an elaborate scheme and played them like a fiddle.","“It’s probably not that simple.” Firework returned the favor since Zu An had offered her some intelligence. “Think about it. How can the Deity of Death choose between us if the plan is completed? I’ve never heard of a universal deity’s legacy being shared between two people.”","“Could it be based on contribution? Whoever contributes more wins,” Zu An asked.","Instead of answering the question, Firework asked, “You should know that those who fail the trial will face death, right?”","“Indeed.” As he recalled the stairs of skulls, Zu An’s heart became heavy.","“If your contribution theory is true, those who are going to lose have no reason to help others. They will try their best to drag others down and foil the plan. It’s more satisfying for everyone to fail together than to let one person win,” Firework said coldly.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. That’s true. One can never underestimate what humans are capable of when pushed into a corner.","“We might appear to be in the same boat, but that doesn’t mean we’ll be able to join forces.” Firework paused before continuing coldly, “Only one can clear the trial. Those who fail the trial are doomed to die.”","Zu An’s heart was chilled. Tingxue and Isabella are here as well. Will we have to eventually turn against one another? But he quickly calmed down and said, “There should be a way out. I’ll find a way for all of us to survive.”","Firework scoffed, “What naivete. When you try to save everyone, it’s more likely that you won’t save anyone at all.”","Despite her skepticism, there was a small part of her that trusted him. She had witnessed his tenacity in tackling and overcoming seemingly impossible situations... But she quickly snuffed out that thought. This is a universal deity’s trial. There’s no way to bend the rules.","“Let’s work together. Even if we’re destined to become enemies, it’s still beneficial for us to join forces for now.” Zu An didn’t want to engage in infighting. There was no way he could clear this trial if someone as smart and strong as Firework was determined to sabotage him.","“What’s the point of such superficial partnership? I’d rather not work together if we’ll eventually have to turn against each other,” Firework said coldly as she stood up and left. She intended to clear the mission by herself.","“What if I find a way for us all to survive?” Zu An shouted.","Firework stopped by the doorway. Without turning around, she scoffed, “Empty promises hold no meaning.”","“It’s not an empty promise,” Zu An said. “I am very familiar with this world. That’s an advantage no one else has ever had.”","“That only means you have a higher chance of clearing this trial; it doesn’t mean you can save the others.” Firework finally turned around, revealing a dangerous gleam in her eyes. “Now that I think about it, you’re my greatest rival here. I ought to kill you first.”","She might have lost her supernatural powers, but given her grasp of martial arts, she could still pull it off.","Zu An’s expression darkened. “You’ve overlooked something crucial. Not everyone would coincidentally stumble upon this trial with their comrades. Why do you think they still failed?”","Firework widened her eyes and fell into deep thought.","Such opportunities are hard to come by. Not everyone who entered this trial would have been friends, and some of them might have even been alone. The latter would have been highly beneficial, as the challenger wouldn’t have to worry about being sabotaged.","But that only made it even more baffling as to why no one had cleared the trial to date.","Zu An continued, “You already know that the other universal deities ganged up on the Deity of Death and killed him. It should be safe to assume that they don’t wish to see the rise of another Deity of Death. The easiest way to do so would be to tamper with the trial.”","“That’s possible. Those fellows are capable of that,” Firework narrowed her eyes and sneered. She appeared to harbor animosity against the universal deities. “But that only makes the trial harder to clear. It just shows that it’s more likely for the four of us to die, not for the four of us to survive.”","Zu An shook his head. “Other universal deities tampering with this trial introduces variables, giving rise to more possibilities.”","Firework was silent for a few seconds before finally conceding with a nod. “There is some sense to your words. I hope you do find a way to ensure everyone’s survival.”","Zu An and the other two women had, to some extent, helped her. While she wouldn’t sacrifice herself to save them, if there was a way for all of them to survive, she wasn’t inclined to let them die, either.","She quickly added, “Our priority should be to find Tingxue and Isabella, right?”","Zu An shook his head. “This might just be a trial world, but it’s still a huge place. Searching for them here without supernatural powers is as good as searching for a needle in a haystack.”","“Are you going to abandon them?”","“Of course not. We’re in the Deity of Death’s trial; I’m sure fate will somehow bring us together. What’s more important is for us to find Yang Guo and obtain his Xuan Metal Sword.”","“You’re more familiar with this world. Where should we look for them?”","“The Beggar Sect has a huge intelligence network, with eyes and ears all over the world. However, Yelu Qi is the current sect leader. We’ll risk feeding crucial information to him if we go through the Beggar Sect.” Zu An thought about it before adding, “Let’s make a trip to the Tomb of Living Dead first.”","“What kind of place is that?”","“Pack your things. I’ll explain it to you on the way.”","The two of them quickly made preparations before bidding farewell to Guo Jing and Huang Rong and secretly leaving Xiangyang City.","Looking at the huge army of Mongol soldiers stationed opposite the river, Firework grimly remarked, “The Mongols are indeed at the peak of their power. That far surpasses the troops we have at Xiangyang. If not for the river, Xiangyang wouldn’t have lasted this long.”","“Our destination is part of Mongolian territory. Let’s disguise ourselves first to avoid trouble,” Zu An suggested.","Firework replied, “There’s no need for that. I might have lost my supernatural power, but I am strong enough to protect myself in this world. Not even Guo Jing is a match for me.”"]},{"number":2829,"title":"Chapter 2829: Chapter 2781: Eternal Pain","paragraphs":["Zu An was speechless. But he had no objection to that. The so-called martial arts experts in this world had a shallow understanding when it came to utilizing energy.","For instance, by tapping into ‘Guo Polu’s’ memories, he'd immediately grasped the Quanzhen Sect, Peach Blossom Island, and Beggar Sect’s inner energy methods and could even use them at a higher efficiency.","Less needed to be said about martial arts moves. He understood the openings in every move with just a single glance, not to mention he could still employ the moves he already knew, it was just that they were no longer reinforced by ki.","While supernatural powers were restricted in this world, they still retained their memories and judgment. Even the strongest skill in this world, the Nine Yin Manual, was easy for him to grasp. Guo Jing and Huang Rong thought it was beyond him, but he had already grasped the gist of it.","The Nine Yin Manual was ingenious, living up to its reputation as a supreme martial art in this world. Unfortunately, this world was limited by the absence of ki, so those dwelling in this world could never hope to reach the level of a cultivator.","To higher entities like them, the Nine Yin Manual was like an innovative application of elementary school level concepts to resolve rudimentary problems. As ingenious as it was, these rudimentary problems could be easily circumvented upon becoming a higher being. Due to that, the manual wasn't noteworthy in the Myriad Worlds.","That said, it wasn't completely useless. The restriction of supernatural powers meant Zu An couldn’t use most of his techniques. The Nine Yin Manual allowed him to maximize what was possible with his current mortal body.","Firework, with her deeper grasp of energy utilization, was likely more skilled at modifying the Nine Yin Manual to maximize her strength. With their combined prowess, unless they foolishly marched into the enemy camp, it was unlikely anyone could pose a danger to them.","...Murphy’s law struck, however.","Firework suddenly decided to scout the Mongolian camp without any warning. Zu An hurriedly followed her, worried that a mishap would befall her.","It wasn’t tough for them to sneak into the camp. They snuck into a watch tower and made quick work of the sentries inside before examining the camp’s layout.","In the end, Firework shook her head and sighed. “If they were in a normal mansion, I could have easily assassinated their general, but in a camp like this, even if I succeeded in my assassination, I would still end up getting surrounded and killed by the enemy soldiers.”","Killing the enemy commander would have been the most efficient way to alleviate Great Song’s crisis, but she wasn’t so noble as to lay down her life for that cause.","“You shouldn’t let your guard down. A few of the Five Greats[1] of this world once snuck into the Mongols’ barracks and nearly lost their lives after being encircled.”","If they were at their usual level, Zu An and Firework could have massacred the enemy troops , but with their strength capped, brute force wouldn’t work.","“You rascal! How many more things have you not told me?!” Firework glared at Zu An.","After they agreed to work together, Zu An had shared the background of this world with her, but here he was, dropping a piece of information she knew nothing about!","“I’m not intentionally withholding information from you. This scene just so happened to trigger my memories. People like us have been through so much that it’s hard to remember everything at hand,” Zu An replied.","They were sticking close to each other so they could speak as softly as possible, lest they draw attention to themselves. They were so close that Zu An could feel Firework’s breathing and smell a light fragrance coming from her.","Zu An’s heart was momentarily moved, but he quickly remembered that she was a spider demoness. What am I thinking?","“There’s something weird about your gaze.” Firework frowned. It’s uncomfortable not having my supernatural powers, or else I could have sensed his thoughts.","Zu An coughed. “Let’s retreat. We should prioritize finding the Xuan Metal Sword.”","Firework ignored him. “Do you think we could clear the trial if we circumvent the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan and move straight to assassinating the Mongolian Khan?”","She could already tell that there were many ways the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan could go awry, and it would be best to circumvent it.","Zu An jolted in shock. “Don’t be reckless. Fate is favoring the Mongols right now. Many experts are serving the Mongolian Khan. It would be nigh impossible to pull it off even if we join forces; it’d be no different from courting death.”","Firework harrumphed. “Coward.”","She kicked one of the dead sentries, and the latter flew out of the watchtower and crashed into the ground.","Zu An was stunned.","That naturally caused an uproar. Many soldiers rushed over right away. Firework fearlessly leaped down the watchtower and valiantly fought the soldiers.","Zu An thought that it was a foolish move, but he had to admit that her valiance was charming, like a rose blooming on the battlefield. Her disposition resembled Yani’s. Perhaps this was her true personality.","He cut his thoughts short and joined the battle.","More soldiers arrived, but the two of them were no ordinary experts. Their judgment and fighting prowess far surpassed this world’s Five Greats, and there was a natural rapport between them. They covered each other’s blind spots and protected each other from harm. They managed to slaughter a path out of the Mongolian camp and escape.","The Mongolian soldiers were startled. The general hurriedly wrote a letter to report the incident to his superiors.","Zu And Firework fled into a stream. They'd survived the crisis, but due to the restrictions on their supernatural powers, they had still incurred considerable injuries.","While Firework was cleaning her injuries, Zu An grumbled in displeasure, “That was very rash. We could have snuck away quietly.”","They could have slipped away without alarming anyone, but Firework just had to kick the sentry out of the watchtower and draw the attention of the Mongolian soldiers.","“You know nothing at all. Do you know the first thing a tiger ought to do upon arriving in a foreign environment?” Firework scoffed. Before Zu An could speak a word, she continued, “It’s to pick a fight with the animals there. Only then will it know its standing in the new environment.”","Zu An had told her about the Five Greats and the power levels in this world, but those were theoretical. The easiest way to know what she was up against was to get into a fight.","She had wanted to spar with Guo Jing, but the latter was her ‘father’ and could suspect something if she suddenly became strong enough to beat him up. So, she'd instead decided to pick a fight with the Mongols to gain a rough grasp of her standing.","Zu An looked at her with pity. “You’re instinctively thinking like a wild beast even though you used to be a human. What happened?”","Firework’s nonchalant expression warped in fury. She flitted to him, grabbed his neck, and exclaimed, “You bastard! Where did you hear that from?”","1. The five strongest people in this world, with two of them being Guo Jing and Yang Guo ☜"]},{"number":2830,"title":"Chapter 2830: Chapter 2782: Woo Her","paragraphs":["Zu An hadn’t expected such an intense reaction. He quickly pushed her hand aside and retreated. “Are you out of your mind?”","Firework didn’t chase him, but she glared at him icily and asked, “How did you know?”","“The Deity of Death told me before I entered this trial,” Zu An replied. “He said you were a pitiful person. What drove you to make such a huge sacrifice?”","“What a joke! Someone who died is pitying me?” Firework harrumphed. “You’re in no place to pity me. Don’t blame me for getting nasty if you dare mention that again.”","She pulled down her clothes and stomped away.","Whatever happened back then must have hurt her greatly. If she ever opens up about that to me, it would mean that she's finally opened her heart to me and considers me a true friend.","“How long did you guard the forbidden land?”","“None of your business.”","“It must have been a long time. Did you feel lonely?”","“Hmph. You must have forgotten about my ability. I can have countless clones. I can single-handedly create a country, so how could I possibly be lonely?”","“But they're all you. Wouldn’t the bustle just make you feel emptier?”","“You darned brat! Are you asking for a beating?”","“There’s nothing much to do on the way, so I figured we could chat.”","Firework suddenly turned to him and asked, “Why don’t you talk about your past then?”","“Sure. What do you want to know?” Zu An smiled radiantly, showing his teeth.","Firework harrumphed. “How many wives do you have?”","“...” Zu An hadn’t expected this to be her first question, but he still answered it. “I have an official wife whom I properly wedded, but I have lovers as well.”","He suddenly fell into a daze. Come to think about it, I did go through the marriage ceremony with the ancient Mermaid Queen after she became the Chang clan’s Saintess...","Firework continued asking, “Is the person who resembles Tingxue your official wife?”","Zu An replied, “No, she’s my wife’s master.”","“Oh?” Even though Firework was still fuming just a moment ago, Zu An’s response piqued her interest. “Tell me what happened.”","Zu An was speechless. The desire to gossip is innate even for ridiculously powerful entities. However, he didn’t mind talking about himself, since he sought reconciliation. He told her about how Yan Xuehen had tried to kill him to end her disciple’s secular attachments, as well as how they'd eventually gotten together.","Firework was thoroughly entertained. Halfway through the story, she suddenly asked, “She spared you because you used that ‘Love is More Solid Than Gold’ skill, right?”","Zu An sheepishly replied, “I knew I wouldn’t be able to hide it from you. I was cornered and couldn’t find any other way out, so I could only resort to such despicable methods.”","“It’s not despicable. All is fair in a fight for survival. It’d be foolish to withhold your skills when your life is on the line,” Firework said with a smile. All of a sudden, her expression darkened. “Did you secretly use that skill on me as well?”","Zu An rolled his eyes. “I already told you I didn’t. Why would I have revealed that skill if I planned to use it against you?”","“It could be reverse psychology,” Firework sneered.","“So, are you in love with me?” Zu An asked.","Firework was stunned. Perhaps she'd arrogantly declared that she would make him her plaything, but that was because she had a favorable impression of him after spending some time together. He was merely different from other guys.","An entity like her wouldn’t fall in love with anyone.","Zu An continued, “You don’t need to worry about that skill—it isn’t omnipotent. It’s not just because of that skill that Xuehen and I got together. Many things happened in between that led to our eventual union.”","Firework heaved a sigh of relief. “That better be the case. I’ll say it upfront. If you dare to use that skill against me, I’ll rip you to shreds even if I fall in love with you. Your lovers will be next.”","Zu An’s expression turned cold. “You need not worry about that. I have no interest in spiders.” He flung his sleeves and walked away.","Even though he had expressed goodwill for the sake of working together, Firework had still threatened not just him, but his loved ones as well. That was beyond what he could tolerate. If that was going to be the case, he would rather not work with her.","“Spider?” Firework was so maddened that one could almost see steam puffing from her nostrils. If not for the restriction on supernatural powers, she would have shown Zu An the true horror of spiders.","You have successfully trolled Firework for +444... +444... +444...","Shortly after they parted ways, Zu An sensed footsteps behind him. He turned around and frowned. “What are you doing here?”","Firework beamed at him. “Don’t be so stingy. I came back because I was worried about you.”","Zu An frowned. She’s speaking in that girlish voice she used when we first met again. “Which one is the real you? Aren’t you worried that you might catch schizophrenia if you keep switching between the two?”","“My mind isn’t that weak, and these are all my real personalities,” Firework smiled. “Which one do you prefer?”","“I prefer sincerity.” Zu An couldn’t tell which of her personalities were real, and he couldn’t be bothered to figure that out either.","“I’m already being very sincere by offering to make you my plaything. I don’t even spare a glance at most men.” Firework jogged to his side. “Aren’t you going to consider me? Having me is as good as having all the women in the world. I can turn into anyone you want.”","Hmph, you brat. I’ll make you fall in love with me hard before dumping you. Let’s see how arrogant you’ll be then!","Zu An looked at her and asked, “You don’t know the way to the Tomb of Living Dead, do you?”","Firework’s smile stiffened up. “What a tactless man you are. How did you get so many women to fall in love with you?”","“Because we treat one another with sincerity.”","Firework snorted. “Ridiculous. That's just what simps say to comfort themselves. I don’t believe that you haven't met a woman who tried to exploit your feelings for her.”","Zu An shook his head. He couldn’t be bothered to waste his breath.","Firework continued prattling along the way. It felt as if the two of them had returned to the time when they first met. They traveled for half a month before reaching the foot of Mount Zhongnan.","Much to their surprise, many Mongol martial artists were gathered around the perimeter of Mount Zhongnan. From their conversations, Zu An learned that a Mongol prince had learned that there was a ravishing beauty at Mount Zhongnan and wanted to woo her."]},{"number":2831,"title":"Chapter 2831: Chapter 2783: Exposed","paragraphs":["Firework nudged Zu An with her shoulder. “Are they talking about Xiaolongnu? You told me she was the number one beauty in this world.”","Zu An scoffed, “Xiaolongnu is beautiful, but think of her age. Even if she maintains her appearance well, I don’t see how she can make a Mongol prince go to such an extent for her.”","Meeting the aged Huang Rong had driven home the fact that Xiaolongnu wasn’t young anymore for him.","“Then who’s the beauty they’re talking about?” Firework was intrigued.","“I don’t know.” Zu An was confused. 'Return of the Condor Heroes' started with Huodu[1] bringing an army of experts to the Chongyang Palace to request marriage with Xiaolongnu. To think that history would repeat itself decades later.","He knew that he was in a trial world and the events were likely fabricated, but it still left him feeling wistful.","“I’m curious about that woman now. How beautiful must she be to drive a prince to do this?” Firework suddenly thought about something. “Could it be Tingxue or Isabella?”","Putting the gorgeous Tingxue aside, Isabella was beautiful as well. The Mongol prince could be a lolicon[2].","“Let’s take a look.” Zu An’s eyes lit up. It would be great if we could reunite with the two of them.","The two of them began scaling Mount Zhongnan. Along the way, they saw buildings covered in algae and Quanzhen disciples with dead looks in their eyes. The Quanzhen Sect used to be the number one sect in the world, but they've fallen into decline.","The Quanzhen Sect had previously fought against the Mongols, but its disciples had now grown accustomed to seeing Mongol soldiers strutting in and out of the Quanzhen Palace. Mount Zhongnan must have fallen into Mongol hands, leaving the Quanzhen Sect with no choice but to surrender to the Mongols.","“Quanzhen Sect’s teachings are very aligned with cultivation. Its founder must have been a formidable individual. It’s a pity this world is devoid of ki, so his cultivation methods are only theories at most,” Firework said. This was her evaluation from eavesdropping on bits and pieces of the disciples’ training along the way.","“Their founder, Wang Chongyang, is an amazing man. He’s the only one whom the Five Greats recognized as number one,” Zu An replied.","“Ah, so he’s the Central Divinity[3]. He’s not all talk,” Firework said, though it wasn't a very high evaluation.","The two of them secretly followed the trail of the Mongol soldiers and soon arrived at the mountain behind the Quanzhen Sect.","Firework asked in confusion, “Is the Ancient Tomb Sect located on the mountain behind the Quanzhen Sect?”","“It is.” Zu An found the irony in the situation amusing. They were searching for the Xuan Metal Sword to deal with the Mongols, but it just so happened there was a group of Mongols here, too.","There was an opulently dressed young man surrounded by a group of Mongol soldiers. The young man shouted at the mountainous slope, bragging about how noble his liege was and imploring the lady to come out and meet him.","“That prince appears to be the incumbent Mongol Khan’s most doted-on son, their future ruler?” Firework swiftly grasped the gist of the message.","Zu An nodded. “He seems to be Kublai Khan’s son, Prince Yan Zhenjin.”","After the previous Mongol Khan died in battle, Kublai Khan had taken over his mantle. Zhenjin was the oldest son he had with his empress, and was currently the most likely candidate to inherit the imperial throne.","To think such a person would travel southward in search of some beauty. With his stature, he should be able to get all the beauties he wants in the world.","Firework was thrilled. “If we capture this fellow, won’t Xiangyang be saved? We won’t have to carry out that nonsensical Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan anymore.”","She keenly sensed that a huge pitfall was awaiting them if they carried out the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan, and that it would be best if they went down a different path.","Zu An frowned. “He’s bound to have many experts accompanying him. We shouldn’t make a reckless move.”","He could already sense several strong auras around the prince. Unfortunately, his senses were too suppressed here to gauge their strengths from afar.","“Hmph, you’re too indecisive. Wait here. I’ll settle it,” Firework sneered as she strutted forth.","Zu An couldn’t stop her, though he was also curious to know what her plan was.","Instead of charging in recklessly, Firework calmly made her way over. Even though her features were sweet, her strut was graceful and seductive, reminiscent of Dreamland’s Diodora.","Zu An was amazed. She wasn't boasting when she said she could play all kinds of women. That’s probably how she grasped her ability.","Firework's approach alarmed the Mongol soldiers, and they instinctively reached for their swords. However, upon seeing it was a beauty, they breathed a sigh of relief.","“Miss, who are you looking for?” a middle-aged Quanzhen daoist asked.","This was the Quanzhen Sect’s turf. It would spell disaster for them if a mishap were to befall Prince Zhenjin here.","Judging from his clothes, he should be in the upper echelons of the Quanzhen Sect, perhaps from the ‘Zhi’ generation[4].","Zu An had previously introduced some of the key members of the Quanzhen Sect to Firework, but she couldn’t be bothered to remember them.","“You’re asking who I am looking for? Weren’t you the one looking for me? I’m here now. You can state your business with me.”","The crowd exchanged looks. They'd followed their prince here in search of a ravishing beauty, and looking at Firework... She was indeed worthy of being called that.","The Mongol prince was indeed drawn to her. “You’re as beautiful as the rumors say...”","A few Mongols traded conflicted looks. This woman doesn’t fit the description of the woman our prince is looking for... but our prince was throwing a tantrum at being ignored earlier, so it might be good to have a substitute.","As the Mongol prince walked over, Firework’s smile brightened. He has some experts accompanying him, but as long as he takes three steps closer, I’ll be able to hold him hostage. Those experts won’t be able to do a thing at all.","It was then a Mongol soldier suddenly spoke up in their native tongue, causing Prince Zhenjin to halt his footsteps. An expert stepped in front of him and glared at Firework, saying, “You’re the girl we held hostage back when Möngke Khan died!”","Firework was confused. She had no idea what had given her away.","Zu An facepalmed. He hadn’t expected veteran Mongol soldiers who participated in the Xiangyang battle many years ago to be here.","Back then, Guo Xiang had been tied up atop a platform to serve as a hostage. Given her appearance, it was hard for anyone who had seen her to forget her. The death of Möngke Khan by a flying stone only made that incident more memorable.","“That’s the girl the Golden Wheel Reverend wanted to take as his disciple? Her physique is indeed extraordinary. Girl, why don’t you come under me? Let’s study Esoteric Buddhism’s Pleasure Tantra[5] together.” An old lama[6] dressed in a red kasaya robe stepped forward.","1. A Mongol prince who serves as an antagonist in the story. ☜","2. Lolicon is a Japanese term referring to people attracted to smaller-sized girls, though they don’t necessarily have to be children. ☜","3. The Five Greats are named with a direction and a descriptor, such as East Heretic and North Beggar. ☜","4. Those in the same generation carry the same character in their names. ☜","5. The proper translation is Annutarayoga Tantra. A portion of this tantra celebrates sex between a male and female practitioner, though it is more than that. ☜","6. A monk who practices Tibetan Buddhism ☜"]},{"number":2832,"title":"Chapter 2832: Chapter 2784: Amazing Woman","paragraphs":["His words made the smiling Firework’s expression turn cold, and she launched a kick. She was so fast that it produced a sonic boom.","The middle-aged lama had been admiring Firework when his eyes widened in shock. He wasn't a grandmaster for nothing, though. He formed a hand seal, and his presence suddenly felt heavy like a mountain.","A loud thud ensued as Firework’s leg whipped into the middle-aged lama.","The lama hurriedly defended himself with his arm, but he was still pushed fifteen steps back before he regained his balance.","“Red Sun Reverend, are you sure you’re up to par? You often brag about your hand seals, but you can’t even catch a lass’ kick?”","A man carrying a jade flute at his waist laughed. He had a young face, but his hair was all white. He looked dashing in a feminine way, but there was an unnerving glint in his eyes.","A flirtatious woman voiced her agreement. “Aiyo! Senior Brother, the Red Sun Reverend might just be going easy on the young miss. It’s called playing the long game!”","The Red Sun Reverend’s face turned bright red. He had proclaimed himself as Esoteric Buddhism’s number one expert ever since the Golden Wheel Reverend died in Xiangyang City, sometimes even expressing his disdain toward the Golden Wheel Reverend. He believed he was better than a failure who had died in enemy hands.","Yet he was pushed back so much by a lass whom the Golden Wheel Reverend had wanted to take as his disciple back then. If this became widely known, he would lose respect in the Mongols’ upper echelons.","His expression turned livid. Without any hesitation, he charged at Firework to continue the battle, determined to restore his honor before the Prince of Yan. The latter was likely to inherit the mantle of Khan in the future. Being underestimated by the prince would spell the end of his career.","Firework’s eyebrows shot up. “Interesting.”","While she hadn’t used her full strength for the earlier kick, she was still surprised that he had withstood it.","Zu An was perplexed. Red Sun Reverend? Why does that name sound so familiar? That’s a character that appeared in one of Huang Yi’s novels [1] , right?","Why is he here? Was there such a person in the history of Esoteric Buddhism?","Zu An was baffled. How did the Deity of Death design this trial world?","The Red Sun Reverend was shocked. He dished out thirty moves in succession, but somehow, his opponent neutralized every single attack with ease.","His signature move, Death Seal, was known for its unpredictability. He could instantly switch between light and heavy blows, which made it difficult for his opponents to deal with his attacks. His opponents would swiftly exhaust themselves and eventually reveal an opening, which he could exploit and claim victory.","Yet this lass had perfectly neutralized his earlier barrage of attacks. It was as if she could see through his inner energy circulation and predict his move... but that was impossible!","With the Prince of Yan and his peers watching this battle, the Red Sun Reverend didn’t dare hold back. His hands began moving so fast that shadows appeared in their wake. This was his other signature skill, Nine Characters Mantra Hand Seal.","Unmoving Foundation Seal. Great Vajra Seal. Outer Tiger Seal. Inner Tiger Seal. Outer Bind Seal. Inner Bind Seal. Wisdom Seal. Sun Disc Seal. Treasure Vase Seal.","His hand seals moved so quickly that he felt that he was exerting 120% of his usual strength. Never had he utilized his Nine Characters Mantra Hand Seal to this extent.","Yet the lass easily unraveled his hand seals. She didn’t even use any profound moves, relying on simple punches, kicks, and pokes. Her moves weren't particularly fast either, but somehow, she still tore down his attacks.","Firework nodded in approval.","The person who created this cultivation skill must have realized that the body was a vessel for salvation, containing the world’s secrets. The body could commune with the world through hand seals and inner energy circulation pathways to borrow the world’s energy. It was half a step into the road of cultivation.","Unfortunately, the ki concentration in this world was abysmal. It was like climbing trees in search of fish—a lesson in futility.","Initially, the Mongol soldiers were still laughing at the Red Sun Reverend for embarrassing himself, but their expressions slowly turned grim. The first kick might have caught the Red Sun Reverend off guard, but he was going all out now, yet he was still unable to do anything about the lass.","She was only using common moves, but somehow, they neutralized the Red Sun Reverend’s profound martial arts. It looked almost as if an elder was guiding a junior along.","This should have been impossible!","They were from rival factions, but they knew how strong the Red Sun Reverend was. It wasn't overly arrogant of the Red Sun Reverend to put down the Golden Wheel Reverend. Many Mongol soldiers had met the Golden Wheel Reverend and knew the two were experts of the same caliber.","Yet such a powerful expert couldn’t even curb a young woman?","One of Prince Zhenjin’s aides leaned over and whispered something to him. Moments later, the prince smiled. “Ah, so you’re the daughter of the Golden Saber Prince Consort[2]. I can see where you inherited your valiance from. Given our old ties, there’s no need for us to resort to blows. Shall we have a temporary ceasefire?”","The Red Sun Reverend took this chance to retreat. “Since Your Highness has said so, I’ll temporarily cease the battle.”","Firework harrumphed. She was too proud to give chase.","The Red Sun Reverend secretly wiped off his cold sweat. I nearly humiliated myself today.","“I heard you are likely to become the next Khan. Do your words hold weight in Mongolia?” Firework asked Prince Zhenjin.","“You’re flattering me, Guo second miss. My father is the one who decides who becomes the next Khan.” Prince Zhenjin clasped his fist toward the north. “But my words do carry some weight in Mongolia. Guo second miss, feel free to speak your mind if you need anything. I might be able to offer you my assistance.”","Firework wasn’t so foolish as to tell Prince Zhenjin that she had come here in search of the Xuan Metal Sword to deal with Mongolia. “Get your soldiers out of Xiangyang, and you are not to invade Great Song in the future.”","Prince Zhenjin was initially taken aback before revealing a smile. “Pardon me, Guo second miss, but the invasion of Great Song is the collective will of several generations of Khans and Mongolia’s upper echelon. It’s not something I can change alone. Why don’t you advise your father to surrender to Mongolia instead, so we can avoid bloodshed?”","Thinking his words weren't convincing enough, he quickly added, “Most of my teachers are Han, and I have the highest appreciation for the Han culture and system of governance. I promise that I’ll treat your people with kindness after you surrender to us. Your people will live better lives under us than under the Song imperial court.”","Firework’s expression turned cold. “If you can’t call the shots, I’ll hold you hostage and see how much Hubilie[3] cares about his son!”","She charged forth as she said those words.","The Mongol soldiers were already prepared against that. They stepped forward to stop her. But Firework was a tiger in a flock of sheep; normal soldiers couldn’t hope to deter her.","Witnessing her valiance, Prince Zhenjin remarked, “To think there’s such an amazing woman in the world. If I can have her as my wife, my trip will have been worthwhile.”","1. The novel was adapted into a drama called ‘ Lethal Weapons of Love and Passion ’. The Red Sun Reverend is one of the top experts of Esoteric Buddhism, and he stood his ground against the other experts in the novel. ☜","2. Guo Jing once fought for the Mongols and was engaged to their princess, but he defected when he realized they were going to invade the Song dynasty ☜","3. Kublai Khan’s name ☜"]},{"number":2833,"title":"Chapter 2833: Chapter 2785: The Plan","paragraphs":["A pale-faced elder grimly warned, “Be careful, Your Highness. She’s an astonishingly powerful martial artist. Even the Red Sun Reverend wasn’t a match for her.”","The Red Sun Reverend harrumphed, but he didn’t retort against that remark. The woman’s fighting prowess was indeed at a ridiculous level.","“The wilder the steed, the greater the satisfaction in conquering it.” Prince Zhenjin’s eyes gleamed with excitement.","He had come here to meet the legendary beauty, but the woman before him was also gorgeous and carried a unique air of wildness. The latter piqued his interest more than the legendary beauty.","Meanwhile, the Mongol soldiers toppled like domino pieces, with none withstanding more than a single blow from Firework. The Quanzhen Sect’s daoists feared being implicated by this scuffle, so they tried to persuade Guo Xiang to step down. They thought that given the ties between the Quanzhen Sect and the Guo Family, the Guo second miss would step down.","But Firework wasn’t the real Guo Xiang. She ignored them and even sent a Quanzhen daoist flying.","That enraged the Quanzhen Sect. They quickly constructed the Big Dipper Formation to confront her.","Firework, with her keen eye, easily saw through the formation’s crux and sneered, “That’s an interesting formation, but it’s a pity you've failed to grasp its essence.”","She dismantled the Big Dipper Formation with ease.","The faces of the Quanzhen daoists crumbled in despair.","They knew that they were lacking compared to the Quanzhen Seven Masters, as well as the already deceased Yin Zhiping and Zhao Zhijing. But they had been training diligently in recent years, and they'd thought they could at least protect their sect with the Big Dipper Formation.","Only now did they realize how weak they were.","“Looks like the Quanzhen Sect is going to disappear in our generation.”","That was the thought dominating the minds of the Quanzhen Sect’s upper echelon.","Seeing that neither the Mongol soldiers nor the Quanzhen daoists could stop Firework, the experts surrounding Prince Zhenjin finally made a move.","While Firework was busy fighting others, the flirtatious woman who had mocked the Red Sun Reverend earlier suddenly flicked a silk ribbon at Firework’s arms and legs. While the ribbon looked flimsy, it was a lethal weapon that viciously claimed the lives of the unsuspecting.","The white-haired man also made a move. He lifted his jade flute and blew a peculiar melody. This was his skill, Soul-Stirring Demonic Melody. His melody seeped right into the heart, evoked one’s lust, disrupted their psyche, and led them toward a fatal cultivation deviation.","“What a beautiful lady you are. Do you have a man you’re interested in? Why don’t I teach you how to give a man an unforgettable night?” the flirtatious woman’s voice echoed loudly.","The two martial siblings specialized in such coordinated attacks. The flirtatious woman’s seduction was amplified by her senior brother’s demonic melody.","Even though the lass was a formidable martial artist, it was obvious at a glance that she was inexperienced in the realm of physical pleasure. It would be difficult for her to withstand such temptations.","If they could apprehend this lass, especially after she had defeated so many experts, it would surely raise the Prince of Yan’s opinion of her. His Highness might even allow me to serve him...","The more the flirtatious woman thought about it, the more excited she became.","“What a shabby tune!” Firework harrumphed.","Her voice resounded like a thunderous roar in the white-haired man’s head, causing him to spurt blood. His glee gave way to horror.","At the same time, Firework stepped on the silk ribbon and twisted it with her foot, causing the flirtatious woman to fly through the air and slam into the charging Mongol soldiers like a hammer. The flirtatious woman spat blood, sustaining injuries so severe that she couldn’t fight anymore.","“Bai Sun, His Highness may be in danger if we let the lass to continue take us down one by one. Why don’t we join hands to subdue her?” The Red Sun Reverend was intimidated by what he was seeing. He dared not charge in alone, but it would be a different story if he could secure the help of Daoist Bai Sun and the others.","Even if the lass started training in her mother’s womb, there was no way she could withstand the combined prowess of both him and Daoist Bai Sun.","Daoist Bai Sun’s initial thought was to turn down the offer, thinking it was beneath him to gang up on a lass. But considering he had yet to accrue any merit ever since joining Prince Zhenjin, and Prince Zhenjin was clearly interested in the woman, this could be a good chance for him to score some points.","So, he snickered and said, “Alright.”","After securing Daoist Bai Sun’s help, the Red Sun Reverend got a huge boost of morale. He leaped into the air, his puffed-up red kasaya robe making him resemble a red sun.","“Someone who has already lost to me still dares challenge me?”","It didn’t take long for Firework to force the Red Sun Reverend back, but a green figure suddenly flashed toward her from the side to ambush her. She felt a cold aura even before the enemy arrived before her.","Firework was startled. This was hardly the strongest ice skill she had faced, but she'd had her almighty powers then. Stripped of her overwhelming power in this world, she could still overcome most attacks with her ingenious moves, but in a pure clash of energy, she was at a disadvantage.","She twisted to dodge the attack, but she was still forced to meet palms with Daoist Bai Sun. Both parties retreated several steps.","Firework shuddered. A tinge of gray appeared on her palms, slowly creeping up her arms. She frowned. His ice palm also contains lethal poison?","“Hahaha! The Xuanming Divine Palm lives up to its reputation!” The Red Sun Reverend was overjoyed. There was no way he would let Firework catch a breather. He charged in and rained attacks down on her.","Daoist Bai Sun snuck attacks in from the side, pressuring Firework with his Xuanming Divine Palm.","Firework channeled her inner energy to expel the ice poison while coping with the aggression of two top experts. She was no longer as domineering as before, but her composure remained.","Prince Zhenjin remarked, “What incredible martial arts and disposition. It’s my first time seeing a woman like that.”","“Your Highness, you can put your heart at ease. Your martial arts are formidable, but she is limited by her age. We can subdue her if we use our inner energy instead of our martial arts against her,” a monk observing the battle said.","Unlike other monks, his hair wasn't shaved. His hairstyle resembled that of the Western Xia[1] people, where the center was shaved and the sides were braided.","“I’m awed by your sharp insight, master. Once we conquer Great Song, I’ll assign you as Jiangnan’s Chief of Religious Affairs[2],” Prince Zhenjin said in delight.","“Thank you, Your Highness.”","The situation suddenly went awry. A Mongol soldier suddenly charged at Prince Zhenjin and took him hostage.","While Firework was distracting everyone else, Zu An had snuck into the Mongol soldiers’ ranks, holding his position and biding his time for a chance to strike Prince Zhenjin.","“You’re courting death!” the monk from Western Xia sneered as he thrust his palm at Zu An’s head. It’s rare for anyone to be as powerful as that lass. There can’t be another expert of that caliber in this world!","1. Also known as the Tangut Empire. ☜","2. ]The monk is Yang Lianzhenjia, a famous monk in the subsequent Yuan Dynasty, known for propagating Tibetan Buddhism further. ☜"]},{"number":2834,"title":"Chapter 2834: Chapter 2786: Assault","paragraphs":["Chapter 2786: Assault","Prince Zhenjin was of lofty stature. There was no lack of experts protecting him.","The de facto leader of his entourage of experts was a Western Xia monk named Yang Lianzhenjia. He'd defected to Mongolia after Mongolia conquered Western Xia.","He was a prodigy in Buddhist studies and martial arts. He was from Esoteric Buddhism, but he belonged to a different school than the Red Sun Reverend. He didn’t bother vying over the position of Esoteric Buddhism’s number one expert with the Red Sun Reverend, for he was already known as the Southern Desert’s number one expert.","As such, he had the highest position among the experts protecting Prince Zhenjin. That was also why he could address the prince in a casual tone as if they were friends.","He hadn’t made a move despite Firework’s incredible show of power, as he knew his primary mission was to protect Prince Zhenjin.","He was initially unfazed when another figure suddenly charged out of nowhere at the prince. He thought that it was ridiculous enough for a woman so young to be so skilled in martial arts—there couldn’t be a second one in this world—but his eyes nearly popped out of their sockets the next moment.","That figure easily subdued all the Mongol soldiers standing in his path, arriving before Prince Zhenjin in the blink of an eye.","Yang Lianzhenjia couldn’t remain still anymore. He thrust his palm forth to jolt the figure aside.","To his astonishment, however, the figure easily neutralized his palm strike. Then, a bizarre force hurled him backward, causing him to crash into the Mongol soldiers rushing in to reinforce them.","The figure continued charging at Prince Zhenjin.","Alarmed, Yang Lianzhenjia shouted, “Master of the Vajra School, protect His Highness!”","“Alright!”","An unseemly monk stepped forward to protect Prince Zhenjin. He formed a simple palm seal that caused his body to glow with a golden light.","The figure seeking to reach Prince Zhenjin was Zu An. He couldn’t stop Firework from making a move, so he could only sneak into the midst of the Mongol soldiers while she was distracting the others. As soon as a chance emerged, he hadn’t hesitated to make a move.","While he didn’t agree with Firework’s recklessness, he had the same idea in mind. As long as they could hold Prince Zhenjin hostage, they could disregard the dangerous Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan.","Everything proceeded smoothly.","He barged through the Mongol soldiers before they had time to react. He successfully launched a sneak attack against the lama protecting Prince Zhenjin, knocking the latter aside. He also didn’t think the monk with discolored patches on his head could stand in his way. With his prowess, he should have been able to send the monk flying within a couple of moves.","But much to his surprise, the monk was unfazed by his attacks. It was as if he were a mountain that couldn’t be moved.","He was referred to as the Master of the Vajra School earlier. Could it be the Indestructible Vajra Divine Art?","Zu An finally realized he had made a miscalculation, but it was all too late. Yang Lianzhenjia had already recovered from the earlier shove and was rushing in with other experts to protect Prince Zhenjin. This left Zu An with no choice but to retreat to Firework’s side.","“You waited so long just for this farce?” Firework scoffed.","Zu An replied bitterly, “I missed my chance. I didn’t expect there to be such a hardy guy beside the prince.”","It wouldn’t have been difficult for him to overcome the Indestructible Vajra Divine Art if he could do it all over again, but everything had happened so quickly earlier that he had no time to react. Clearly, the Mongols wouldn’t slip up a second time either.","A Mongol soldier whispered into Prince Zhenjin’s ear. The prince was startled. “You’re the Guo third master. The Golden Saber Prince Consort is amazing indeed. His children are all top-notch martial artists.”","Even the Red Sun Reverend remarked, “I doubt that Guo Jing and the so-called Five Greats are any stronger than these two.”","The others knew that the Red Sun Reverend was merely salvaging his reputation, but they had to agree with him. Several of them had met Guo Jing, and they agreed with those words. It was baffling to them how two youngsters could be so strong.","Prince Zhenjin continued, “I’ve treated you with courtesy. Don’t you think you should return the etiquette?”","Zu An sighed. “Pleasantries are meaningless when our paths diverge.”","Defecting to the Mongols can’t possibly be the way to clear this trial.","“Very well, I won’t hold back either. Once I hold you two hostage, breaching Xiangyang won’t be a problem.” Prince Zhenjin’s eyes heated up. Xiangyang was the biggest hurdle standing in the Mongol campaign against the Song. If he could contribute toward that, he would have a much greater stake on the throne.","“I’ll confer on anyone who captures those two the title of Mongolia’s Number One Hero!”","The eyes of the Mongol soldiers lit up.","Zu An and Firework were powerful, but even ferocious tigers feared wolf packs. Not to mention they had powerful experts on their side as well. There was no need to fear these two.","Mongolia was well on its way to conquering the world. Claiming the title of Mongolia’s Number One Hero would grant tremendous honor and riches not just for them, but also for their next few generations to come.","Even the Quanzhen Sect’s disciples were revved up. This was an opportunity for them to revitalize the Quanzhen Sect.","Sensing the ravenous gazes, Zu An and Firework pressed their backs against each other.","“Shall we break out of the encirclement?”","They had the upper hand in solo duels, but the Mongols had them far outnumbered. They had only been able to hold their ground thus far because they caught the Mongols by surprise, but now that they were encircled, the situation had become very difficult for them.","Needless to say, the Mongols wouldn’t grant them a second chance to approach Prince Zhenjin. On top of that, Firework had greatly depleted her inner energy from the earlier fight.","As powerful as Zu An and Firework were, they were constrained by this trial world’s laws.","“You stall the others. Give me ten seconds to kill him before we leave.” Firework eyed the Red Sun Reverend with cold eyes. How dare a mere ant covet my body?","Zu An understood her temperament. “Alright.”","He charged at Prince Zhenjin. Unsurprisingly, most experts rushed to stop him.","The more they fought, the more alarmed the experts became. Since they had the numerical advantage and at least five of them had inner energy on par with the two assailants, they initially thought they could subdue Zu An with ease, yet they struggled to breach his defense!","The way Zu An channeled his inner energy and moved was shockingly ingenious.","Meanwhile, Firework found an opening to charge at the Red Sun Reverend.","After witnessing Daoist Bai Sun injuring Firework earlier, the Red Sun Reverend had regained his composure. This woman is nowhere as powerful as I thought. Our inner energy is on the same level; she only has the advantage in terms of moves.","So, he decided to leverage his strengths and abandon the battle of skill for one of inner energy, knowing Firework wouldn’t dare to face him like that. Otherwise, she could be stuck in place and left vulnerable, to the extent that even a simple Mongol soldier could claim her life.","But his eyes soon narrowed. Much to his astonishment, Firework decided to face his palm.","“You’re courting death!”","The Red Sun Reverend felt slighted. Does she think she can defeat me instantly in a clash of inner energy? She has greatly exhausted herself; I have no need to fear her. Others will tear her apart if I can just stall her for even a moment.","As they met palms, the Red Sun Reverend poured out all his inner energy right from the start, hoping to catch Firework off guard and inflict severe injuries on her right away. To his surprise, however, Firework’s palm felt soft like cotton; there was no force whatsoever.","The next second, he felt a tremendous force rebounding onto him. It contained not just Firework’s inner energy, but the inner energy he'd unleashed earlier as well.","How did she do it?!","The Red Sun Reverend was horrified. He quickly used his Death Seal to retreat from the clash, but it was all too late. The terrifying force tore through his veins, causing him to die on the spot.","Zu An was awed. As expected of Firework. She really only took ten breaths to execute a top expert whose inner energy was on her level.","But his eyes quickly narrowed.","A Mongol soldier suddenly emerged from the crowd and unleashed a palm strike on Firework’s back just as she was inflicting the killing blow on the Red Sun Reverend. The impeccable timing and the immense force of the attack made it clear he was no ordinary Mongol soldier.","He was an expert on par with the other Mongol experts.","Zu An had never expected the enemy to copy his maneuver. It was unbelievable how neither Zu An nor Firework noticed the anomaly until that Mongol soldier made a move. The other party must have been a top-notch assassin who had been lying in wait all this time.","Firework realized what was going on, but the limitations imposed on her made it impossible for her to dodge this attack. She spurted fresh blood and crashed forward."]},{"number":2835,"title":"Chapter 2835: Chapter 2787: Betrayal and Defense","paragraphs":["Firework sensed someone holding onto her and instinctively launched an attack, but she quickly stopped when she realized the other party was Zu An.","She breathed a sigh of relief, only to be assaulted by fiery pain right after. It felt as if her meridians had all been ripped apart.","The Mongol soldier who ambushed her didn’t give chase. He cautiously retreated and eyed them from afar.","Zu An finally saw the other party’s appearance. The latter had a tall nose and distant eyes, an appearance that resembled Hu Feng[1]. He was clearly not from the Central Plains.","“You live up to your title as Persia’s Assassin King, Old Man Shanzhong. I’m impressed,” Prince Zhenjin complimented the man.","The other experts grunted in indignation, but they were awed by Old Man Shanzhong as well. They had all seen what Firework was capable of; the latter had even killed the Red Sun Reverend with ease. Yet Old Man Shanzhong had inflicted severe damage on her by dealing a timely blow.","With Firework’s injuries, the Mongols’ victory was sealed, but they chose to temporarily pause their assault lest Firework attempt a desperate counterattack—the last thing they wanted was to die in vain when victory was already theirs. Instead, the Mongols chose to encircle them from afar.","Brief silence settled upon the battlefield.","Zu An stared at Old Man Shanzhong. He hadn’t expected to meet Persia’s Assassin King here, though it all made sense considering how Mongolia had conquered Persia as well.","Prince Zhenjin said, “Young master Guo, your big sister is severely injured. Her life will be in danger if she isn’t treated right away. Why don’t you consider my proposal? I’ll make sure your big sister receives proper treatment.”","He had remained calm thus far because he knew about the experts hidden around him. With his victory certain, he tried to recruit Zu An and Firework once more. He understood how the carrot and the stick worked.","“Young master Guo, I suggest you think things through before answering. You’re alone now. If we continue this fight, not only will you be unable to save your big sister, you’ll also be going up against all of us alone. You are a smart person. I’m sure you know what to choose.”","Zu An’s expression darkened. Prince Zhenjin was right.","If Firework hadn’t sustained injuries, they could have broken out of this encirclement with ease. Now that he was alone, the chances of him breaking out of this encirclement alone were 50% at most. If he carried the wounded Firework with him, the odds would be even lower.","Firework understood that and coldly said, “Escape by yourself.”","Having survived by herself thus far, she didn’t expect anyone to protect her. Besides, they weren’t on close terms, either. It would be a stretch to call them friends; they had merely been making use of each other. There was no reason for Zu An to risk his life to save her.","There would be no disappointment if there was no expectation.","But Zu An smiled and said, “We’re comrades. I won’t abandon you.”","Firework frowned. “We aren’t comrades. You can even say that I’m your competitor.”","Zu An calmly replied, “Since we came here together, we ought to leave together as well. As I’ve said, I’ll find a way for the four of us to leave this place together. I won’t abandon you here. If our roles were reversed, I’m sure you wouldn’t abandon me either.”","Firework sneered, “You overestimate yourself. I’d toss you aside in a heartbeat.”","“What a pity,” Zu An remarked, though he continued standing his ground.","Firework looked at him in contempt. Is he so obsessed with playing the hero that he doesn’t recognize reality anymore? I bet he’ll leave without hesitation the moment his life is in danger.","She had seen such scenes play out far too many times. Even the closest friends and lovers eventually betray each other in times of desperation.","She focused on circulating her inner energy to heat up, but she soon frowned. Old Man Shanzhong’s earlier blow had crushed most of her meridians, making it impossible for her to properly channel her inner energy to recuperate.","I dominated the universe for so many years. To think I’d end up dying here.","The lack of response from Zu An made Prince Zhenjin’s expression darken. He waved his hand and ordered, “Attack!”","The Mongol soldiers nocked their bows and unleashed a rain of arrows.","Zu An kicked up two spears on the ground and wielded them. He twirled the spears around, deflecting the arrow rain.","He knew it wouldn’t do for him to passively defend against the arrows, or else it was only a matter of time before he was turned into a porcupine. Thus, he stomped the ground, jolting the arrows up into the sky, and flung them out with his spear.","While the archers were dealing with his abrupt counterattack, he quickly grabbed Firework’s waist and dashed into the Mongol soldiers.","Firework frowned. The heat on her waist made her uncomfortable. It wasn't the first time Zu An had hugged her in such a manner, but back then, she was a cat teasing a mouse. This was her first time being protected in such a helpless position.","But what’s the point? He’ll still abandon me in the end. He might as well just dump me now and spare me the misery.","As these thoughts surfaced in her mind, her expression grew increasingly colder.","The Mongol soldiers and Quanzhen daoists attacked Zu An, but with the combat experience he had accrued, the latter dealt with them easily.","Daoist Bai Sun and the other Mongol experts exchanged shocked looks.","Firework had already astounded them earlier, and they hadn't thought she would have an ally whose strength was on par with her. Just watching the pair's moves evoked an epiphany in them. They felt as if they could make a breakthrough if they went into closed-door training.","All of them had already reached a bottleneck in their martial arts, such that they had hardly made any advancement in the last few decades. Yet these two youths inspired them so much that they thought they could push toward higher ground.","That was how shocking the situation was.","Seeing over half of the Mongol soldiers and Quanzhen daoists crumbling in defeat, Prince Zhenjin turned to the Mongol experts and said, “I request you to join hands with my people and capture that man.”","He knew that these people were lofty grandmasters in their respective territories, and the only way they would join hands with one another was for him to make the request in person.","But he was wrong this time.","After witnessing Zu An and Firework’s tremendous fighting prowess, these experts wouldn’t dare to put on airs. They had only held still thus far because they wanted the Mongol soldiers and Quanzhen daoists to wear down Zu An’s inner energy.","Zu An and Firework’s moves surpassed their wildest imagination. Their only shortcoming was their comparatively weaker inner energy due to their young age. Their odds at victory went up the more Zu An expended his inner energy.","Those Mongol soldiers and Quanzhen daoists weren’t dying in vain; their deaths had expended at least half of Zu An’s inner energy. Since Prince Zhenjin was making the request in person, the experts decided to make their moves now.","The Master of the Vajra School dashed forth, confident in the defensive prowess of his Indestructible Vajra Divine Art.","Daoist Bai Sun exerted his Xuanming Divine Palm to inflict Zu An with his ice poison.","Yang Lianzhenjia revealed inner energy stronger than the Red Sun Reverend's.","The biggest headache of all was Old Man Shanzhong, who prowled in the shadows like a venomous viper, ready to dish out a lethal blow whenever Zu An let his guard down. Zu An had to continuously keep an eye out for the latter.","These four experts were highly experienced in combat, but Zu An calmly stood his ground against their joint offense. Thus, they quickly adjusted their strategy and focused on attacking the injured Firework instead.","Under normal circumstances, such a fighting style would have been beneath them, but no one faulted their actions here.","It worked. Zu An’s initial composure eroded away, and he began to struggle. It didn’t take long for wounds to appear on his body.","Firework’s expression turned even colder. “Enough. You have already shown enough camaraderie. You can scram now.”","Zu An smiled. “I’m not in the habit of abandoning my comrades, let alone a beautiful lady.”","Another injury was inflicted on his shoulder.","Firework closed her eyes. “A licentious pervert is bound to lose his life to a woman.”","1. A Chinese poet in the 1900s ☜"]},{"number":2836,"title":"Chapter 2836: Chapter 2788: Dead Meat","paragraphs":["The Mongols were confused by their conversation. What’s going on between those two?","“Are they really siblings?” Yang Lianzhenjia laughed eerily.","“They sound more like a couple,” Daoist Bai Sun scoffed.","“Heh! Everyone says Guo Jing is a hero, yet his children engage in such a depraved act,” the Master of the Vajra School said with an excited glint in his eyes.","Old Man Shanzhong didn’t utter a word, but he continued lurking around Zu An and Firework, occasionally dishing out blows at their blind spots.","Firework frowned, but she didn’t respond. She wasn’t truly Zu An’s sibling anyway.","The same went for Zu An. He was more worried about the current crisis they were in. In order to protect Firework, he needed to expend himself more than usual, causing his inner energy to deplete swiftly. At this rate, he was going to empty his tank.","The Mongol experts were well aware of that. Everything they did was with the intention of sapping his inner energy dry.","Zu An tried to expose some openings to bait the Mongol experts into overcommitting, so he could kill off some of them and reduce the pressure on him. However, the Mongol experts were all wily old foxes. None of them fell for his trick.","If only there were a way for me to replenish my inner energy...","Firework suddenly asked, “Didn’t you have a skill to absorb energy?”","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up, knowing she was referring to the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra. She’s right. This world may ban supernatural powers, but the concept behind the skill holds true. This world has skills like the North Sea Divine Art and Cosmos Absorption Art [1] that can suck out other people’s inner energy. They might not be anywhere as powerful as the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra, but they prove that such skills are feasible in this world.","Thus, he began altering the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra so he could use it in this world.","He had used the Heaven-Devouring Sutra for many years now and was extremely familiar with it, so it wasn’t tough for him to alter it. It didn’t take him long to come up with a skill similar to the North Sea Divine Art and Cosmos Absorption Art.","It wasn't stronger than the Nine Yin Manual he had learned from Guo Jing and Huang Rong, but it would greatly increase his endurance in a prolonged fight. He could absorb the might exerted by his enemies into his inner energy, thus replenishing it.","Yang Lianzhenjia and the others quickly noticed the anomaly. “I feel like my inner energy is being siphoned away whenever I execute a move.”","“I feel the same way, too.”","“Is that fellow using some kind of sorcery?”","...","The overwhelming power displayed by Firework and Zu An earlier had already piqued their vigilance. Upon realizing Zu An was using some kind of weird power, they hurriedly backed off to a safe distance away lest they fall for his tricks.","The Master of the Vajra School was less cunning than his peers and was a step too slow in his retreat. Zu An managed to grab him by his shoulder.","But the Master of the Vajra School wasn't worried. He channeled his Indestructible Vajra Divine Art, causing his body to glow with a brilliant golden light and his monk robe to puff outward. With his defenses raised to the maximum, he was confident that not even Old Man Shanzhong’s full-powered attack could hurt him.","But Zu An had already come up with a countermeasure after suffering a setback from that.","The Indestructible Vajra Divine Art, despite its grandiose name, wasn't particularly profound. Put in simple terms, the skill involved the compression of one’s inner energy around one’s body to an extreme degree, forming an invisible energy barrier.","At the same time, the compression also increased the density of one’s bones and muscles, achieving an effect reminiscent of ki. With all external attacks spread evenly across the energy barrier, it created an illusion of indestructibility.","It wasn't too hard to overcome this skill. Zu An had already come up with seven solutions against it. But with powerful enemies lurking around, he opted for the fastest and simplest method.","A peculiar light glowed from his eyes. It was the Nine Yin Manual’s Soul Transference Method. It was a skill used to attack a person’s mind.","“Huogong Toutuo! Despite being a Shaolin disciple, you killed the Dharma Hall’s abbot and massacred dozens of your peers. Do you plead guilty?”","Zu An’s mind was stronger than anyone else in this world, and he was talking about the Master of the Vajra School’s greatest grudge.","The Master of the Vajra School was initially dazed, but his eyes quickly narrowed in hatred as he roared, “They deserved to die! They humiliated and beat me up back then...”","“Be careful, Master of the Vajra School!” the other experts shouted as they rushed over to rescue him.","It was too late.","The Master of the Vajra School’s mind had already been compromised by the Soul Transference Method, and the Indestructible Vajra Divine Art required continuous channeling to maintain the energy barrier. This brief opening resulted in gaps appearing in his defense.","His inner energy began flowing toward Zu An’s hand as if it were water leaking out of a breached dam.","“NO!”","The Master of the Vajra School screamed in misery. He tried his best to stop the outflow of his inner energy, but it was to no avail. His eyes lost their spirit, and his body became withered. In no time, he looked no different from an ordinary old man.","There was a cold flash of light. In an attempt to save him from Zu An’s suction skill, Yang Lianzhenjia severed the Master of the Vajra School’s arm, but it was already too late.","The Master of the Vajra School had been reduced to a dried-up husk, with his inner energy all sucked away. As a result, the severing of his arm only worsened his condition. His breathing became incredibly shallow.","Zu An chuckled. “Tastes good. Who’s next?”","The experts felt goosebumps.","Fuck! Who’s the antagonist here?","Seeing that he had successfully intimidated the Mongol experts, Zu An made use of this opening to carry Firework out of the encirclement. The two of them swiftly disappeared behind the mountain.","With his inner energy suction skill, Zu An could have easily stood his ground against all these experts alone. But he needed to protect the severely wounded Firework from their enemies too. If the fight continued, Firework could very well lose her life.","So, he didn’t hesitate to flee the moment an opportunity arose. It wouldn’t be too late to settle the score with these people after rescuing Firework.","He flitted across the mountain before abruptly stopping in front of an ancient tomb.","An ancient tomb on the mountain behind the Quanzhen Sect. This should be the entrance to the Ancient Tomb Sect.","By now, Zu An had already noticed that Firework’s meridians had been severed. It would be unwise to continue traveling with her severe injuries. Thus, he shouted, “Hero Yang, Miss Long, my second sister has been injured by the Mongols. Can we seek refuge at your home?”","To his bewilderment, there was no response.","Even though Yang Guo was avoiding Guo Xiang to sever her feelings for him, upon seeing her life in danger, he should have shown up by now.","Worried about Firework’s critical condition, Zu An decided to push the entrance open and enter the ancient tomb.","The place had been armed with many defensive mechanisms that would have doomed most people, but Zu An had been through far more. These traps were child’s play in contrast.","He soon arrived at a quiet stone chamber. He placed Firework down and began treating her.","Firework spurted another mouthful of blood. She shook her head and said, “My meridians have been completely severed. My fate is sealed. You can’t save me. You’re wasting your energy.”","She was well aware of her physical condition. Such injuries would have meant nothing to her outside; she had countless ways to heal up. Unfortunately, there were no supernatural powers and miraculous pills here. She racked her brains, but it felt as if her only fate was death.","1. These are all inner energy suction skills in Jin Yong’s wuxiaverse ☜"]},{"number":2837,"title":"Chapter 2837: Chapter 2789: Someone I Know","paragraphs":["Zu An fell into deep thought. He knew that much as well.","Old Man Shanzhong lived up to his reputation as the Assassin King. His blow was fast, accurate, and precise. He could have saved the Red Sun Reverend, but he'd chosen to trade the latter’s life for a chance to ambush Firework.","His bet had paid off.","Were it not for Firework’s sturdy body and high inner energy, she would have died on the spot. Even so, she'd only delayed her death. It looked like there was no way to turn things around for her.","Zu An racked his brains. He was sufficiently knowledgeable about medicine to concoct some pills, but this ki-lacking world was lacking in potent herbs. The strongest herbs he could get here were at most ginseng and lingzhi, which were nowhere near enough to treat such severe injuries.","He pondered harder and asked, “Should I channel my inner energy into your body and help you connect your meridians?”","Firework coldly replied, “That might work for other meridians, but the ones around my heart are very fragile. You might have been useful with your previous cultivation, but now that we've both lost our supernatural powers, the slightest lapse in your control will only further damage my meridians and hasten my death.”","Zu An huffed impatiently, “I’m looking for ways to save you. Can’t you be less grumpy?”","“Did I ask you to do this for me?” Firework scoffed.","Zu An frowned. Firework had displayed a wide range of emotions thus far, even as the demon spider, but this was the first time she was venting her emotions. Her current condition had to be affecting her a lot.","So, Zu An consoled her. “Don’t worry. This world might lack supernatural powers, but there is quite a bit that can be achieved through martial arts. There’s hope for your injuries. Dali’s Duan Family[1] specializes in the Yiyang Finger, which can heal all injuries, no matter how severe.”","Firework had been treating Zu An coldly thus far, but the latter didn’t lose his temper and even talked to her gently. This calmed her down a little, and she replied, “Dali is too far away. I won’t last the journey. You don’t need to be too bothered by this.”","Zu An knew she was speaking the truth. Firework was in no condition to make the journey.","All of a sudden, he heard light footsteps and put his finger up to his lips, signaling for her to remain quiet. He snuck behind the door and waited vigilantly.","The door suddenly opened, and a cold gleam flashed.","Zu An swiftly flicked it away. It turned out to be a sword, which swiftly changed its trajectory to strike back at him, unleashing over a dozen stabs at once.","Zu An had thought that given his vast combat experience, deep comprehension of energy, and sharp judgment, he was pretty much unrivaled in this world. He hadn't thought that someone in this world was capable of employing such profound swordsmanship. There were several close calls that he had to fumble to overcome.","Then, he suddenly exclaimed aloud. He finally got a good glimpse of his aggressor.","The sword also came to a halt. A beautiful pair of eyes gleamed in the dark environment.","“Tingxue!” Zu An called out in delight.","The other party had flowing long hair and wore a snowy robe. She exuded an ethereal air that sharply distinguished her from the secular world.","A hint of emotion rippled in the white-robed woman’s usually nonchalant eyes. “It’s you...”","She also noticed Firework lying on the bed, and her eyes narrowed. A man and a woman staying alone in such dim lighting...","Zu An was exceptionally excited to meet a familiar face in a distant land. “Tingxue, what brings you here? What’s your relationship with the Ancient Tomb Sect? Are you... Xiaolongnu?”","His tone became peculiar. For some reason, he was very averse to the idea of her being Xiaolongnu, even if it was beneficial to the completion of her mission.","Tingxue shook her head and replied, “No, Xiaolongnu is my mother.”","Zu An and Firework were both stunned.","Tingxue replied with a rare hint of awkwardness. “It’s just this world’s setting.”","Zu An replied with a smile, “It’s the same for us, too...”","He proceeded to share his and Firework’s identity in this world.","“Guo Jing, Huang Rong... I’ve heard their names.” Tingxue took a good look at Firework. “So, you’re Guo Xiang. I heard from Xiaolongnu that you were courting Yang Guo.”","She was uncomfortable with calling those two ‘father’ and ‘mother’, especially since this was merely a temporary identity in a trial.","Firework’s face reddened. “That’s the original Guo Xiang! I have nothing to do with... Cough cough...” She spoke with such agitation that it triggered her injuries, causing her to go into a coughing fit. Blood splattered over the floor.","Tingxue was perplexed. “How did you sustain such severe injuries?”","While this world forbade supernatural powers, someone of Firework’s caliber wouldn’t be weak at martial arts.","“You still dare speak. Aren’t you the one who drew those guys here?” It had become clear to Firework that Tingxue was the gorgeous woman whom those Mongols outside had mentioned.","Tingxue blinked in confusion. Zu An explained the situation to her.","“Ah, I didn’t know they were calling out to me. They have been very noisy, so I left the ancient tomb half a month ago to look for you. I didn’t expect to bump into you here.” Tingxue nodded in realization.","If he learns that his half a month of sweet-talking has been in vain, Prince Zhenjin might just pop a vein out of sheer frustration.","“Speaking of which, we're here to fulfill the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan. We wish to borrow the Xuan Metal Sword from Yang Guo.” Zu An briefly shared the plan before asking out of curiosity, “Where are Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu?”","Considering the earlier commotion outside and their entry into the ancient tomb, those two should have appeared by now.","“They have gone out to explore the world,” Tingxue replied. “Yang Guo said something about how they had to overcome many tribulations before they finally got together, and that he wanted to cherish their every moment together. He didn’t want others to disturb them.”","“And that includes you as well?” Zu An retorted.","Tingxue shook her head. “They see their daughter as a third party.”","“...” Well, this kind of fits Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu’s lovebird persona. They only have each other in their eyes. Zu An thought about their agenda here and was worried. “That’s a shame. Looks like it won’t be easy for us to obtain the Xuan Metal Sword.”","Tingxue replied, “You don’t have to worry about that. The Xuan Metal Sword is stored in the ancient tomb. Come, I’ll bring you to it.”","Zu An was surprised by how smoothly everything was going, but he turned her down and said, “We’ll fetch it later. Firework is severely injured. I need to find a way to save her first.”","Baffled, Tingxue whispered, “Aren’t you two enemies? Why are you saving her?”","Zu An knew she meant no ill will. It was a question voiced out of sheer rationality. “I promised her that I’d find a way to bring the four of us out of this trial world safely.”","Due to her severe injuries, Firework had closed her eyes to rest, but her eyelashes fluttered a little after Zu An said those words.","“If you truly wish to save her, I do have a way.” Tingxue said.","1. The Duan Family is the royal family of Dali. Their previous patriarch is the Southern Monk, one of the Five Greats. ☜"]},{"number":2838,"title":"Chapter 2838: Chapter 2790: Strip","paragraphs":["“What is it?” Zu An was both overjoyed and confused.","Even someone as knowledgeable about this world as he couldn’t find a solution, but Tingxue, despite having only arrived here not long ago, knew a way out?","“The ancient tomb has a Cold Jade Bed that was passed down from my ancestor. A daoist named Wang Chongyang got it for her to treat her severe injuries. It’s still in the tomb now. Come with me.” Tingxue turned around and left the room.","Zu An hoisted Firework up his arms and followed Tingxue.","Firework usually put on a lofty attitude, but now that she was lying quietly in his arms like a little chick, he found it hard to relate her to that domineering demon spider.","They soon arrived at a room. As soon as they stepped in, a surge of cold air rushed at them. Zu An felt Firework tremble, so he gently channeled a surge of energy into her body.","The warm energy coursing through Firework’s body made her feel comfortable. She opened her eyes to look at the man carrying her. This angle feels familiar. This was how he held me back at the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation, too.","Oblivious to her thoughts, Zu An was focused on the pristine bed not too far away. The bed looked like an amalgamation of ice and jade, and there was a layer of frigid white air above it. He could feel its chill even from a distance.","“I know this bed helps to hasten the growth of one’s inner energy, but shouldn’t someone injured steer clear of this bed? Otherwise, the cold energy might worsen their injury.”","When resting on a Cold Jade Bed, martial artists could instinctively circulate their inner energy, even when asleep. This greatly enhanced their training efficiency, potentially reaping a week’s worth of gains within a single day.","But those who were injured couldn’t channel their inner energy to protect their bodies. Approaching the Cold Jade Bed in such a state would only result in cold energy seeping into their bodies, thus worsening their affliction.","Return of the Condor Heroes had mentioned that the Cold Jade Bed could be used for recuperation, but it had failed to save Xiaolongnu. That was why Zu An hadn't thought of it right away.","“In order to tap into the Cold Jade Bed’s healing property, you might have to cultivate the Ancient Tomb Sect’s signature skill, the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra,” Tingxue replied.","Zu An anxiously said, “Please save her, Miss Tingxue.”","But Tingxue shook her head and replied, “I can’t do it.”","Zu An was startled. Firework harrumphed. “Don’t beg her! Bring me out, lest I dirty her place.”","Tingxue knew Firework had misunderstood her words, so she explained, “It’s not that I don’t want to save you, but that I’m unable to do so. Cultivating the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra requires two people of opposing inner energy attributes. My inner energy carries the yin attribute, and so does Firework’s. I’d only worsen her injuries if I made a move.”","Firework realized she had misunderstood Tingxue and felt apologetic, but she was too embarrassed to admit it. “Since that’s the case, why don’t you let Zu An learn it? His inner energy carries the yang attribute.”","Zu An had channeled his inner energy into Firework many times now, and the warm feeling it evoked in her was extremely comfortable. With his vast knowledge, it shouldn’t be too difficult for him to learn a martial art in this world.","Tingxue frowned. “But there’s a problem with cultivating this martial art.”","“How hard can the martial arts of this world be?” Firework was confused.","“Well...” Tingxue’s cheeks reddened.","Zu An suddenly interjected, “Does the cultivation of the martial art require both parties to be naked?”","Tingxue looked at Zu An in astonishment. “How do you know?”","The Jade Maiden Heart Sutra was the Ancient Tomb Sect’s most prized martial art, and it had never been leaked to outsiders.","“This fellow is very familiar with this world’s setting.” Firework harrumphed. “So, does the cultivation of this martial art really require its practitioners to strip naked?”","Tingxue nodded. “Cultivating this martial art will cause one’s body to heat up and release steam, so it has to be done naked in an empty area, so the steam can swiftly dissipate without any blockages. If the steam accumulates, it can potentially be fatal.","“The Jade Maiden Heart Sutra is divided into nine stages. The odd-numbered stages are called ‘Advancing Yin’ and the even-numbered stages are called ‘Retreating Yang’.","“The Retreating Yang stages can be paused whenever needed, but the Advancing Yin stages have to be completed in a single breath. Pausing in the middle of an Advancing Yin stage will result in a severe backlash. It’s a highly risky process. That’s why both parties have to channel their inner energies for protection.”","Firework harrumphed. “That’s obviously an unorthodox martial art.”","Tingxue didn’t argue against that. “Our ancestor developed this martial art to deal with the orthodox sects’ number one expert, Wang Chongyang. She made many trade-offs to maximize its prowess, making mastering the skill much riskier. The original host of this body learned the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra under Xiaolongnu’s tutelage.”","She then turned to Zu An and continued, “Firework is severely injured. You’ll have to train the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra to a level where you can treat her. I can guide you in learning the martial art, but we’re of different sexes. How can we train together without clothes?”","Her fair complexion reddened, adding a touch of color to the dull room.","Firework teased, “I thought Nebula worshipers abandoned their emotions. It’s just stripping clothes. Are you embarrassed?”","Tingxue lowered her head. “Perhaps I’m still lacking.”","Firework was choked by her honesty.","Zu An chuckled. “That’s not an issue. There should be a camellia field outside the ancient tomb. We can cultivate there—the flowers will conceal our bodies from each other.”","He couldn’t believe he was using the method Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu had used back then. Tingxue probably didn’t know about that, as that was a secret between the couple, and they were too embarrassed to tell their daughter.","Tingxue blinked. “That sounds feasible.”","Firework rolled her eyes. Is that fellow dumb? Tingxue was already hesitating. If I played the pity card, she might have agreed to strip before him. Yet he’s not making full use of this opportunity.","Zu An and Tingxue made their way to the camellia field outside the ancient tomb. He made sure to survey the area to check if there were any Mongols around.","In truth, Zu An and Firework’s sudden appearance had intimidated the Mongols. Prince Zhenjin had felt threatened and hurriedly retreated with his subordinates.","Firework was awestruck by the vibrant camellias that covered the mountain. There are actually so many beautiful scenes in the world. My obsession with exacting vengeance has caused me to miss out on a lot...","Tingxue shared the formula and the things to look out for when cultivating the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra with Zu An. “Have you gotten everything down?”","“Yes, I’ve gotten it down.” With Zu An’s strong mind, it was a piece of cake for him to remember and grasp this world’s martial arts.","Tingxue glanced at Firework. “Aren’t you going to rest in the ancient tomb?”","Firework shook her head. “I hate dark places. I was sealed in one for too long.” You must be kidding me! They’re going to take off their clothes to cultivate. How can I miss such a show?","A tinge of redness touched Tingxue’s face. She sat down in the flowers and said, “Let’s begin.”","Zu An looked uncomfortable as well. No man could remain composed in such a situation, especially with Firework staring at him teasingly.","“Strip!” Firework exclaimed."]},{"number":2839,"title":"Chapter 2839: Chapter 2791: Turning Tables","paragraphs":["Tingxue’s eyebrows shot up. She picked up something amiss about Firework’s voice, as if she were some perverted auntie. She placed her finger on her robe, but she couldn’t bring herself to take off her clothes.","Firework scoffed, “You’re still lacking in the path of Nebula.”","Zu An seemed to have guessed Tingxue’s worry as he said, “Don’t worry, our divine senses don’t work in this world. It’s impossible to see through the flowers and bushes with our eyes.”","Their normal selves could see through trees with divine sense easily, which was why Tingxue was so awkward.","Tingxue nodded before unraveling her waistband. Her robe slid down.","Even through the flowers, Zu An could still see her smooth and radiant skin. His breathing became unnatural. He quickly reined himself in and undid his clothes.","“Come...” A pair of fair hands was extended toward him.","Zu An raised his hands and met her palms. It felt like touching a piece of ice or fine jade, and it stirred an urge to pull her into his embrace. He was shocked that, despite his mental fortitude, he could still harbor such thoughts. In a way, it showed how alluring Tingxue was.","“Calm your mind. Circulate your inner energy using the formula I imparted to you,” Tingxue instructed. Her quivering voice revealed that she was nowhere as calm as she appeared.","Zu An felt ashamed. He quickly reined himself in and did as he was told. Under her guidance, he was able to grasp the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra quickly. Steam soon rose from their bodies as if they were in a sauna.","Firework had come out to watch the show, but her severe injuries weighed her down. It didn’t feel like much at first, but even craning her neck over to take a better look was a challenge now. This made her feel frustrated.","That fellow Zu An does have a nice figure. Tingxue’s skin is also fairer and smoother than snow.","Firework became groggy due to her injuries, and it looked as if she had fallen asleep.","It would have taken even a talented martial artist months to learn the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra, but Zu An’s knowledge far surpassed this world’s level, and Tingxue was aiding him. It took him around half a day to master the technique.","Tingxue opened her eyes. “You have mastered the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra. That’s probably as far as the Ancient Tomb Sect’s founder reached.”","Zu An was about to answer when he heard a crashing sound. Firework had collapsed to the ground. Shocked, he rushed over to support her.","Tingxue’s face reddened. Due to Zu An’s abrupt movement, she caught sight of something she shouldn’t have in her peripheral vision.","But Zu An couldn’t bother with that now. He hurriedly inspected Firework’s condition—her severe injuries had induced extreme weakness in her. Her body was burning up in a high fever.","Tingxue had already put on her robe by this point, and while tidying herself up, she asked, “How is she doing?”","Zu An was in no mood to enjoy the sight. He quickly shared Firework’s condition.","“Bring her to the Cold Jade Bed for treatment,” Tingxue instructed.","“Alright!” Zu An belatedly realized he was still naked, and that made him feel awkward.","While he was searching for clothes, Tingxue passed a robe over and said, “Wrap yourself up.”","Zu An quickly draped the robe over himself before carrying Firework and sprinting back to the Cold Jade Bed.","The cold of the chamber caused the feverish Firework to snuggle closer to Zu An, as if only his body warmth could comfort her.","“You have to channel the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra to treat her right away,” Tingxue said grimly.","“Miss, may I trouble you to start a fire by the side?” Zu An asked.","Tingxue did as she was told. By now, all three of them understood how the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra could be synergized with the Cold Jade Bed to treat severe internal injuries. The crux was to nourish Firework’s meridians with a flow of pure yang energy before neutralizing that energy with the Cold Jade Bed.","The Cold Jade Bed served to dispel the heat and prevent any clots, lest the injuries worsen.","But there was a limit to a martial artist’s inner energy in this world. It would be tough for an individual to overcome the Cold Jade Bed’s chill with inner energy alone, so it would be ideal to start a fire next to the bed. Zu An could draw the pure yang energy from the fire and amplify it with his innate yang inner energy to heal Firework’s injuries continuously.","It was theoretically similar to how Master Yideng healed others with his[1] Yiyang Finger. It was slower, but it came without the downside of temporarily losing one’s inner energy and being unable to move one’s hands for several years.","Tingxue quickly gathered some dry branches and started a fire.","Zu An carefully placed Firework down on the Cold Jade Bed, but the cold made her embrace Zu An more tightly. She was shivering so much that even her teeth were chattering.","Zu An quickly infused some energy into her body to alleviate her chill. He was about to begin the treatment when Tingxue hurriedly stopped him.","“Do you intend to begin treatment just like that?”","Zu An was startled. “We can’t drag out her treatment any longer.”","Tingxue huffed. “I’m not stopping you from treating her, but no heat should be retained in your bodies during the crucial phase of the treatment. The two of you need to strip, just as you did when cultivating the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra.”","Zu An was stunned.","It dawned on him why Tingxue had told him to just drape a robe around himself earlier. He didn't have to put on clothes when he needed to strip very soon for the treatment. However, if he were to strip Firework, she would obliterate all of them when she regained her powers.","Firework sensed what was going on and murmured, “No...”","Unfortunately, her feeble words carried little persuasiveness.","Zu An looked at Tingxue for help, but the latter calmly replied, “Why are you looking at me? You can decide whether you want to save her or not.”","“Alright, I’ll do it.”","On the one hand, Zu An didn’t wish to see Firework’s death despite everything that had happened. On the other hand, he was unsure what the conditions to clear the Deity of Death’s trial were. It was possible that Firework’s character could play a crucial role.","So, he requested Tingxue to strip Firework, but she looked at him quizzically and asked, “Isn’t that unnecessary? You’ll still be baring your bodies to each other even if I strip her.”","Unlike in the shrubs, there was no cover on the Cold Jade Bed to shield their bare bodies from each other. They would only be more intimate, especially with the cold-averse Firework hugging him so tightly.","“May I trouble you to excuse yourself?” Zu An asked awkwardly.","“I need to be here to ensure the fire continues burning sufficiently. The slightest problem here may endanger both of you,” Tingxue replied with a straight face.","Zu An was speechless.","1. The Southern Monk, the abdicated emperor of Dali’s Duan Family. ☜"]},{"number":2840,"title":"Chapter 2840: Chapter 2792: Another Step Forward","paragraphs":["It’s awkward enough to have to strip Firework, but I have to do it with Tingxue watching by the side? Is she doing this to exact vengeance on Firework?","But the reason she gave makes perfect sense. I do need to tap into the fire’s heat lest the Cold Jade Bed’s cold energy get the better of me.","“Alright.” Zu An was reluctant to do this, but Firework was already in a critical state.","“Firework, I’m doing this to save you. Please pardon me if I offend you in any way,” he murmured in Firework’s ear.","Firework’s mouth moved, but she was too feeble to speak.","Zu An quickly stripped her robe. It was as if the dim chamber suddenly got brighter. Even the Cold Jade Bed looked dull in comparison to Firework’s fair skin.","Zu An quickly pulled himself together and treated her using the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra.","Firework, fearing the cold, instinctively snuggled up to Zu An like a koala hugging a tree.","Zu An had a hand placed above the fire and the other holding her both hands, pressing down on a key acupoint of her ‘Ren Du’ meridians and gently transferring his yang energy over.","Firework's meridians were so damaged that Zu An dared not exert any force. Her delirious condition also made it impossible for her to cooperate with him in the treatment. If he accidentally used too much force when transferring the yang energy, it could shatter her meridians and kill her.","Such precise control was much more tiring than fighting. It didn’t take long for sweat to seep down his forehead.","Tingxue looked at the duo with a bizarre look. Somehow, their posture felt strange to her. Her cheeks began to heat up.","This fire is too hot...","She was starting to regret staying here. She was averse to fire as her cultivation skills all leaned toward the ice element, but she could only quell her discomfort and focus on maintaining the fire.","Under Zu An’s patient treatment, Firework finally regained consciousness. When she realized she was naked in Zu An’s arms, she immediately fell silent.","Feeling her trembling body, Zu An quickly explained, “It was an emergency. Hold yourself together. Don’t let everything go to waste.”","Firework coldly replied, “Do you take me to be some foolish woman who would cause a huge fuss over such trivialities at this critical moment?”","Zu An was surprised by how composed Firework was, but on second thought, she was a powerful entity far surpassing the likes of him. He should never have thought of her as an immature child who had never seen the world.","He did think their current position was a little awkward, however. “Why don’t you turn over now that you’re awake?”","Neither of them was clothed, and they were hugging each other. This was grueling for Zu An. He was sweating not just because he had to be exceptionally careful treating her meridians, but also because it was exhausting having to control his lewd thoughts.","Little did he expect Firework to turn down his request. “I refuse. I’m too injured to sit directly on the Cold Jade Bed and withstand its bone-piercing chill. It’ll only worsen my condition.”","Zu An was speechless. You’re going to continue sitting on my lap? Have you considered my condition? Though there was no way he would say those words aloud. Besides, Firework was indeed in a weakened state.","“Since you’re awake, channel your inner energy based on the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra imparted to us by Tingxue. Cooperate with me in circulating my inner energy around your meridians.”","Given the severity of Firework’s injuries, it would be ideal for both parties to channel the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra together to ensure a precise flow of energy. Zu An had transferred his inner energy earlier to awaken her, so she could actively cooperate with him.","“Alright.” Firework nodded.","She had gained a good grasp of the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra from listening to Tingxue’s explanation. She began cooperating with Zu An in channeling his inner energy around her body to nourish her meridians.","It was tough at first. Firework’s meridians were so severely injured that it was difficult for her to channel her inner energy, but Zu An patiently unblocked her acupoints one by one before slowly expanding her blocked meridians.","Firework, with her deep understanding of energy and laws, was able to cooperate with him impeccably. It didn’t take long for the two of them to get into the flow of things.","Surges of warm energy flowed into Firework’s body and nourished her injured meridians before they were dispelled into the Cold Jade Bed, such that they wouldn’t hurt her brittle meridians.","Firework’s pale face regained some color.","“I've recovered some inner energy now. Put me opposite of you,” Firework suddenly said. They were in extremely close proximity, so much so that she could feel Zu An knocking at her gate, ready to enter at any time. That stirred some feelings in her.","And the greatest taboo while undergoing treatment was to get distracted. That could potentially lead to cultivation deviation.","Zu An’s face reddened. He understood the reason behind her request, so he wouldn’t turn her down. He gently put her down on the other side.","Firework closed her eyes and focused on circulating Zu An’s inner energy to heal her injuries, but her fluttering eyelids hinted that she was nowhere as calm as she appeared.","Zu An felt awkward as well, knowing Tingxue was watching off to the side. That said, he had weathered enough storms to have the mental fortitude to adjust his state of mind and focus on the task at hand.","Tingxue quietly averted her gaze. There was a red tinge to her fair skin. She deeply regretted choosing to stay in the chamber. She felt like a maid tending to the fire while the other two flirted with each other.","She had chosen to stay as vengeance for the shame she felt earlier, but she suddenly felt as if her presence here was extraneous. The thoughts in her mind alarmed her.","What’s going on? I should have lost most of my emotions after embarking on the path of Nebula. It’s rare for me to feel anything or harbor such thoughts. So why do I have so many miscellaneous thoughts in my head?","Is it because this trial world restricts my nebula power?","A bizarre silence settled upon the room. The only sounds that could be heard were the occasional crackling of the flame and the steam puffing from Zu An and Firework’s bodies.","Some time later, Firework suddenly opened her eyes and said, “The Jade Maiden Heart Sutra can be further refined.”","“You noticed it, too?” Zu An had also found the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra extremely familiar, since he had a cultivation skill similar to it.","“How can I not notice when you have?” Firework rolled her eyes at him. “Since this skill requires two people to grasp it, why not make it a dual cultivation martial art? It will come very close to the level of a cultivation skill. Its prowess should surpass the Nine Yin Manual and the Scripture of Tendon Transformation[1].”","She suddenly asked excitedly, “Shall we give it a try?”","Zu An exclaimed, “Ah?”","1. Known as Yijin Jing, it’s a real daoist text containing mental and physical exercises to cultivate one’s ‘essence’. In Jin Yong’s wuxiaverse, it is a Shaolin martial art created by Dharma. ☜"]},{"number":2841,"title":"Chapter 2841: Chapter 2793: Goes Against the Natural Order","paragraphs":["Tingxue raised her head. Her usually cold face carried a hint of astonishment.","Zu An was taken aback. “How do we test that?”","Firework looked at him with a devious smile. “I believe you have a lot of lovers. Are you pretending to be innocent now?”","Zu An’s face reddened. “I just find your words inconceivable.”","“Inconceivable? We’re too weak right now. We need to grasp every chance we can to become stronger.” Firework harrumphed. She was too used to being strong, to the point that her current vulnerability pricked at her nerves.","She'd thought that with her current body’s martial arts foundation, paired with her vast knowledge, she was unrivaled in this world. But her recent injury knocked some sense into her. There were many formidable experts in this world. Perhaps they wouldn't be a match for her in a 1-on-1, but they still posed a threat when ganging up on her.","She had to resolve this problem!","Seeing how Zu An was looking at her weirdly, Firework coldly pointed out, “Have you not wondered why no one has cleared this trial in so many years? You saw those long stairs of white bones, right? Some of them might have been stronger than us. Do you think their strength or wits were inferior to ours?”","Zu An fell silent. That was indeed the concern he harbored. To this moment, he still had no idea what this trial was about.","Firework continued, “Since we aren’t strong enough at the moment, we should do everything within our means to become stronger. If there’s a way to do so via dual cultivation, is there any reason why we shouldn’t do so?”","She turned to Tingxue and said, “It just so happens she knows the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra. You can also dual cultivate with her and raise her fighting prowess as well. That would put us in a better position to deal with whatever crisis we face ahead.”","Tingxue shot to her feet. “You can do it yourselves.”","She turned around and left, not bothering to tend to the fire anymore.","Zu An and Firework exchanged looks. Firework looked at Zu An in confusion. “Isn’t she a Nebula worshiper? She’s supposed to evaluate the world with a completely impartial mind, devoid of emotions. Is she still bothered by her physical form?”","Zu An sighed. “You’re the libertine here.”","Firework harrumphed. “Are you doing it or not? If not for the special nature of this place, I wouldn’t have made this offer. You should know that you’re the only man whom I could barely stand in all these years.”","Zu An retorted, “Isn’t it because you didn’t have a chance to meet other men because you were trapped in the forbidden land?”","“You’re asking for it!” Firework angrily lunged forward and bit Zu An’s shoulder.","“Ah! Be careful, we’re still in the midst of treatment!” Zu An was alarmed.","The Jade Maiden Heart Sutra was an unorthodox martial art in the first place; those who practiced it were prone to cultivation deviation. That was why there had to be no disturbances when channeling it. Yet Firework was still messing around.","“Don’t worry, my inner injuries have healed up considerably. I can channel a bit of my inner energy now.” Firework coyly lay on Zu An’s chest. “Big brother Zu, am I really not attractive to you?”","Zu An was so accustomed to her domineering tone that her suddenly reverting to the sweet, coy tone she'd used when they first met sent shivers down his spine. He quickly pushed her aside and said, “Stop it. This is improper...”","Touching her supple skin made his heart skip a beat. Given their current situation, it felt inappropriate to touch her anywhere.","“What’s the matter? We’re both willing parties. Or do you not want to?” Firework gently propped up Zu An’s chin while looking at him.","“Of course not.” Zu An pushed her hand aside. “You shouldn’t be talking about this now. I’m still treating your injuries.”","“Indeed, you’re treating my injuries.” Firework chuckled. “I’m sure you know my inner injuries would recover faster if we performed dual cultivation instead.”","Zu An was aware of that as well, but how could he conflate those two things?","“Now that you can channel your inner energy, you can treat yourself. I’ll be leaving first.” Having such a gorgeous beauty in his arms, at this rate, Zu An felt as if he would succumb.","But Firework grabbed his hand and stopped him. “You aren’t allowed to leave.”","Zu An sighed. “I don’t do it with just anyone.”","Firework widened her eyes in anger. “Are you implying that I’d do it with anyone?”","“That’s not what I mean. I just think that we shouldn’t be doing this...” Zu An would have never thought a day would come when he would struggle to guard his chastity against someone else.","Firework suddenly laughed. “You say you don’t want to, but your body is honest.”","Zu An was stunned. He suddenly felt as if he had jumped genres to the romance section. Sis, did you accidentally take my script?","Firework was starting to get impatient. “You’re so wishy-washy. Are you a man or not?!”","Her look of contempt stoked Zu An’s anger. “Don’t regret uttering those words!”","“What do I have to regret?” Upon seeing that she had provoked his competitive spirit, Firework’s eyes curled in glee. “I’ll be on top.”","Zu An was stunned. “Impossible. It goes against the natural order of the world.”","Pah pah...","The two of them came to blows.","“Brat, are you taking advantage of my injuries now?”","“Are you telling me to wait for you to recover before fighting you? Do I look like a fool to you?”","Upon seeing that she was at a disadvantage, Firework reverted to her coy tone. “Aiya~ Big brother Zu, please go easy on me.”","That sent shivers down Zu An’s spine. “Which is your true self?”","“They're all my real personalities,” Firework replied. “Or should I say that they're the personalities I had in different stages of my life? This was how I was in my younger years.”","“Cute...” Zu An was reminded of the young lady he met on the spaceship—she was eccentric but extremely endearing.","“I didn’t expect you to be a lolicon.” Firework glared at him.","Zu An nearly spurted blood. “Don’t talk rubbish! You’re obviously an adult. No, if we go by your real age...”","“Shut up!” Firework roared. Her hands had been restrained, so she could only lurch forward to seal his mouth.","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected their first kiss to happen like that.","Embarrassment flashed across Firework’s face. As their lips parted, she gently murmured, “You’re hurting me. I haven’t fully recovered yet.”","Zu An hurriedly freed her out of concern of her injuries.","But Firework used this opportunity to flip him over, seal his acupoints, and claim the initiative. She looked at him gleefully. “It’s my victory.”","She leaned toward his ear and whispered a formula, her hair naturally cascading on his chest in the process. “Remember this formula. You’ll have to cooperate with me later.”","Zu An was speechless."]},{"number":2842,"title":"Chapter 2842: Chapter 2794: I Am Not That Kind of Person","paragraphs":["Zu An hadn’t expected her to ambush him like that. He could only glare at her in anger.","Firework grinned triumphantly. “I like those eyes. Continue looking at me like that.”","Zu An was stunned. This woman is insane!","“Lie down. I’ll do it myself,” Firework smiled.","She frowned upon seeing her adversary, but she was a headstrong person. How could she admit defeat at a time like that?","Zu An inhaled sharply. She’s such a tenacious person. Even I'm feeling pain, let alone her.","Firework leaned toward his ear and whispered, “Be glad. If not for this world limiting my body, you would never have been able to get inside me, no matter what you did.”","Zu An looked resigned. “To think I was taken by a spider demoness...”","Before he could finish speaking, Firework bit him and hissed, “Are you insulting me? I used to be a human, too!”","Zu An remembered what the Deity of Death spoke about her past. Curious, he asked, “What made you turn into a demon?”","Firework’s gaze turned cold, but she quickly reverted to her gentle demeanor and asked, “Can we not talk about unhappy matters at a time like this?”","Her overflowing charm and tenderness made it plenty clear that this wasn’t the time to be touching on mood-ruining topics, but Zu An didn’t forget about her injuries. “Let’s treat your injuries first.”","“I’m healing much faster than before now.” Firework smiled sweetly.","The two of them interlocked their fingers and fully channeled the modified Jade Maiden Heart Sutra. Even so, her inner injuries were so severe that all her meridians were either shattered or clogged. Zu An struggled to channel his inner energy into her body.","While her meridians had recovered a little after their earlier treatment, it would still take a long time to open up all of them.","It was a good thing Zu An wasn’t in a rush, so they could take their time. It also helped that Firework could channel her inner energy to some extent. Through their cooperation, they could precisely channel Zu An’s energy into her body to ensure a thorough recovery.","Occasionally, they would encounter a meridian that was closed tightly. Zu An would first patiently probe the meridian with a small surge of inner energy, gradually expand it, then reinforce it.","As Firework’s meridians reconnected, her previously stuck inner energy converged like tributaries returning into a river, allowing her to better tap into her inner energy. She proactively channeled her inner energy to coordinate with Zu An.","At the same time, Zu An didn’t need to tread as carefully now that Firework was in a better condition. Even so, he didn’t dare make a reckless move. Like a small stream flowing into a river, he patiently inspected every bit of her body for injured meridians to repair.","When he was almost done healing most of her meridians, his inner energy could finally flow openly through her body to expand and reinforce all her meridians, thus pushing her martial arts cultivation up another level.","This raging flow of inner energy eventually returned to the vast sea. The vast sea evaporated into clouds, converged in the mountains, and returned as rain to replenish the river.","Just like that, the two of them formed a continuous cycle between themselves.","Firework’s complexion grew increasingly red, a sign that she had recovered fully.","The continuous flow of inner energy naturally unlocked Zu An’s acupoints, allowing him to regain control of the situation. Firework was initially reluctant to relinquish control, but her rejection was so weak that he got his way.","Their martial arts cultivation rose to another height.","Firework tightly embraced Zu An. Her domineering demeanor had softened considerably. “It’s a pity my powers are sealed, or else I could have pulled out Yani and Diodora to play with you. If you wanted, I could do Tingxue and Isabella as well.”","The thought of that made Zu An’s heart skip a beat, but he quickly put on a straight face and replied, “I’m not that kind of person. Don’t even think about tempting me with that.”","“Is that so? I don’t think your body is fooling anyone.” Firework laughed.","Zu An was so embarrassed that he harrumphed. “You don’t know what you’re messing with now...”","“Ahhh! I was wrong. Don’t...”","The two of them bickered. The cold chamber was filled with laughter.","Sometime later, Zu An and Firework stepped out of the chamber. They spent a long time searching the ancient tomb before they found the frosty Tingxue sitting in the forest outside.","“What are you doing here? We were looking for you,” Firework asked.","Tingxue looked at the energetic Firework and remarked in surprise, “You’re all healed up?”","“That goes without saying. I personally modified that martial art, and I had the help of the Cold Jade Bed as well,” Firework replied with a smile.","Zu An was stifled. Even though I got all sweaty and exhausted for you, you’re not giving me any credit?","Firework seemed to have sensed his frustration, and her eyes twinkled. “It’s also thanks to this lad. He has good stamina. You should give him a try. I guarantee he’ll bring you to new heights in your martial arts.”","Tingxue turned around. “I don’t need it.”","“There’s no need to be shy. You becoming stronger benefits all of us. Who knows what the clearing condition of this accursed Deity of Death trial is?” Firework suddenly grinned in mischief. “If you don’t become stronger while you can, you might regret it if I turn on you guys, if it turns out that only one of us can survive this trial.”","Tingxue’s face turned cold. “I’d have no regrets. That would be heaven’s will.”","“Tsk. How boring.” Firework wanted to see the Nebula worshiper succumbing to lust, but Tingxue remained unfazed.","Tingxue looked at Zu An with frigid eyes. She resembled Yan Xuehen so much that Zu An felt guilt-ridden, as if he had been caught cheating by Yan Xuehen herself. He wanted to say he'd been forced into it, but he couldn’t bring himself to say that.","Tingxue suddenly asked, “If I’m not mistaken, the two of you are siblings in this world?”","Zu An was speechless.","Firework retorted, “...What nonsense are you spouting?! We were transported in here with our real bodies. We’re merely borrowing their identities. It’s not as if we’re really siblings.”","Tingxue nodded nonchalantly, but she appeared unconvinced. Firework was so frustrated that she nearly spurted blood.","Zu An interjected with a cough and hurriedly changed the subject. “Where’s the Xuan Metal Sword? Shall we obtain it first?”","Tingxue nodded before leading them on a convoluted path through the ancient tomb. “Yang Guo placed that sword here. Go ahead and take it.”","Inside a giant boulder, a heavy black sword sat silently, as if awaiting its fated owner."]},{"number":2843,"title":"Chapter 2843: Chapter 2795: Dilemma","paragraphs":["“There’s something off about that sword...” Firework murmured.","Zu An walked over to draw the sword from the boulder, but it was shockingly heavy.[1]","“You’re right. It’s made out of a special material that contrasts with other weapons in this world.” Zu An remarked.","They had seen many weapons along the way, but the Xuan Metal Sword was made out of an unusual material.","Firework stroked the weapon and soon concluded, “Its material seems to be from another world. No wonder it became a godly weapon in this world.”","“Is it possible for the other universal deities to have tampered with this sword?” Zu An had previously discussed with her why no one had cleared this trial in so many years.","“Unlikely. It’s part of the main storyline of this trial. The Deity of Death would never have become a universal deity if he couldn’t even sense such blatant tampering.” Firework spent a moment in thought before shaking her head.","Zu An was awed. Given her stature, her judgment is much more reliable.","“Let’s take the sword out first. It’s part of our mission anyway,” Firework said. She clenched her fist and snorted, “That Mongol prince is lucky he escaped fast. Otherwise, I’d have settled the score with him.”","It had been a long time since she last suffered such severe injuries. If not for Zu An, she would have been dead by now. His determination to rescue her, even though it put him in grave danger as well, was part of the reason she was willing to dual cultivate with him.","She suddenly remembered how he had protected her from the Eight Barren Netherworld Suppression Formation, and that spurred some thoughts in her. She looked at him with tender eyes, only to see him whispering intimately with Tingxue. Her expression immediately soured.","Tingxue pulled out two swords from a wooden crate and passed them to Zu An. “Take the Gentleman Sword and Maiden Sword too. These two swords are made out of extraordinary materials as well. Just the Xuan Metal Sword might not be enough for you to craft the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber.”","The Gentleman Sword and the Maiden Sword were godly weapons Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu had obtained from the Loveless Valley, but the two of them had grown so strong that they didn’t need such weapons anymore.","Judging from her words, Zu An understood that she wasn’t planning to travel with them and was startled. “Tingxue, come to Xiangyang as well. This trial is too dangerous. We have to stick together for a better chance to overcome this crisis.”","Tingxue shook her head. “There’s no need for that. I’m accustomed to being alone. This ancient tomb suits me well.”","Firework walked over and asked, “Are you feeling uncomfortable because of what happened earlier?”","Tingxue ignored her and turned away.","Zu An was worried that they would bicker, so he quickly continued, “Our divine senses are sealed in this world, and there’s no effective way for us to communicate over a long distance, either. Let’s head to Xiangyang together and discuss a way to clear this trial.”","Firework harrumphed. “This brat insists on saving everyone from this trial despite its futility. I wouldn’t have wasted my time otherwise.”","Tingxue frowned in hesitation.","Zu An added, “There’s still Isabella. We don’t know her current whereabouts. It’d be easier to gather information about her in a city like Xiangyang. The Xuan Metal Sword belongs to the Ancient Tomb Sect, so it makes sense for you to join us as a representative of the Ancient Tomb Sect.”","“Fine. Let’s find Isabella as soon as possible.” Tingxue finally gave in.","Zu An was overjoyed. It would be easier for them to overcome this trial if they joined forces.","The three of them left the ancient tomb. Firework found a chance to sneak up to Tingxue and asked, “What’s your opinion of our circumstances? Do you think it’s possible for the four of us to survive this trial?”","Tingxue nonchalantly replied, “I don’t like to think about such stuff.”","“It doesn’t matter to you even if you die in the trial?”","“Everything in the universe eventually returns as dust to the nebula. Dying is merely a natural passage of life.”","Tingxue’s calm response made Firework feel as if she had punched cotton. I nearly forgot this woman is a Nebula worshiper. Of course she doesn’t care!","To get back at Tingxue, Firework intentionally acted intimately with Zu An for the rest of the journey. Even when they stayed at inns at night, she would sneak into his room and cause a huge ruckus.","Zu An initially indulged in it, thinking that Firework was hooked on him. However, he soon realized her intention and was rendered speechless. She’s trying to cuckold Tingxue by getting together with me? But there’s nothing between me and Tingxue!","But Firework had a reason for doing so. She had heard from Zu An that Tingxue resembled one of his lovers, and she keenly sensed something peculiar between the two of them. That was why she was so enthusiastic about this.","This put Tingxue in a tough spot. I shouldn’t have agreed to accompany them to Xiangyang.","Zu An also faced a dilemma. Tingxue was clearly irritated with him, but the more he tried to console her, the louder the ruckus Firework made at night.","His ‘days of suffering’ only ended when they returned to Xiangyang.","Guo Jing and Huang Rong were overjoyed when they learned that their children had brought back not just the Xuan Metal Sword, but the Gentleman Sword and the Maiden Sword as well. They were also amazed when they saw Tingxue.","Huang Rong grabbed Tingxue’s hand and exclaimed, “Big brother Jing, they look so alike. Doesn’t this remind you of the first time we met Miss Long?”","“Indeed.” Guo Jing looked wistful, as if he had returned back in time.","Even Guo Fu rushed over to peek at Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu’s daughter. Her lower jaw dropped when she saw Tingxue’s face. There were many words at the tip of her tongue, but they dissipated with an air of melancholy.","Tingxue felt uncomfortable by their amicability. She instinctively shuffled toward Zu An.","Huang Rong noticed her subtle movements and was initially startled before she revealed a heartened smile.","Guo Jing suddenly said, “Tingxue, Polu and Xiang’er can be considered your uncle and aunt.”","Zu An, Firework, and Tingxue were all speechless.","Even Huang Rong rolled her eyes at her husband. “Guo’er called Miss Long ‘little aunt’ back then as well, but there isn’t a big disparity in their ages. There’s no need for such formalities.”","Guo Jing smiled sheepishly as he realized he had misspoken.","Firework couldn’t care less about this farce, so she quickly pulled the topic back on track.","Huang Rong instructed Guo Fu to call her maternal grandfather[2] over, using that as an excuse to send her away. Then, she explained, “We invited your maternal grandfather over. He’s highly knowledgeable, and he has been researching how to forge a godly weapon. He has experimented with other weapons and found two chokepoints.","“One, it’ll take more than an ordinary flame to melt the Xuan Metal Sword. He heard that there’s a mystical man residing near Sichuan’s E’mei Mountain who specializes in crafting Thunderbolt Bombs. That man might have a solution to this issue.","“Two, a fire strong enough to melt the Xuan Metal Sword would easily melt any metal clamps used to hold the weapon in place. We’ll need special tools to craft the godly weapon. The Ming Cult’s Sacred Fire Token is the only thing in the world capable of withstanding such heat.","“Thus, I’ll need you two to make a trip to E’mei Mountain and the Ming Cult. Xiang’er can visit E’mei Mountain, but the trip to the Ming Cult will be treacherous. Cult Leader Shi is a formidable martial artist, and he has many powerful subordinates. The Sacred Fire Token is the Ming Cult’s holy treasure; there’s no way he’ll give it to us, even if it’s a request from us. We’ll have to find a way to steal it.","“Unfortunately, your father and I cannot leave Xiangyang at this juncture, and your grandfather is not young anymore. If only Guo’er were around... I don’t know who I can entrust this task to.”","1. In Return of the Condor Heroes, the Xuan Metal Sword was known to be extremely heavy, weighing 41 kilograms—even top martial artists in this world struggled to effectively wield it as a weapon. ☜","2. Guo Fu’s maternal grandfather is one of the Five Greats, East Heretic Huang Yaoshi. ☜"]},{"number":2844,"title":"Chapter 2844: Chapter 2796: Deepening Ties","paragraphs":["Firework was bewildered. She pointed to Zu An and asked, “Can’t you just send him?”","Given Zu An’s skills and wits, there was no better candidate than him.","Huang Rong was taken aback. “Polu’s skills are still lacking.”","Guo Polu’s aptitude was at the same level as his father[1], and he was nowhere as focused as his father. His martial arts were subpar at best.","“He’s not weak by any means. He might have even surpassed the two of you,” Firework replied candidly.","“Oh?” Guo Jing was overjoyed to hear that. He thrust his palm to attack Zu An, hoping to test the latter’s martial arts.","Zu An sensed the incoming attack and instinctively thrust his palm in retaliation.","Huang Rong was horrified. Big brother Jing, you shouldn’t use so much inner energy just because Xiang’er made a passing remark! How can Polu withstand that attack?","Her eyes soon bulged in shock. The two men had exchanged over a dozen blows by now, but Guo Polu was standing his ground against Guo Jing. From time to time, Guo Polu would make an ingenious maneuver that astonished even Huang Rong.","Guo Jing burst into laughter. “Polu has grown at a rapid pace. He’s almost on par with me now.”","Firework smiled. Zu An obviously held back earlier.","Huang Rong frowned. She stared intently at Zu An. “Polu, how did your martial arts advance so much within this short span of time?”","Zu An was stunned. He had revealed too much earlier because he was worried Huang Rong would send someone other than him.","Huang Rong was an intelligent and skeptical person. She knew that the real Guo Polu would have never achieved such a level of mastery in his martial arts in his lifetime, let alone within this short span. It would be disastrous if she realized that he wasn’t the real Guo Polu.","Just then, Firework interjected, “He just dual-cultivated with Tingxue not long ago.”","Tingxue, who was nonchalantly watching the spectacle from the sidelines, was stunned.","Zu An was speechless.","Firework shot the two of them a glance. It’d be disastrous if Guo Jing and Huang Rong learned that she'd dual cultivated with Zu An.","Zu An could only awkwardly nod in acknowledgment.","Tingxue was speechless. So this is how it feels to be angry. Her inability to explain the situation only further stoked her frustration.","Huang Rong’s skepticism gave way to delight. “Ah, so it’s Tingxue’s credit. Polu is really too much...”","She grabbed Tingxue’s hand and began trading pleasantries once more.","To think that my son would bring not just the Xuan Metal Sword, the Gentleman Sword, and the Maiden Sword back, but also a daughter-in-law as well! I’m surprised an oaf like him knows how to win a woman’s fancy.","She hadn't shown anything earlier, but she'd initially felt a tinge of dislike toward Tingxue upon seeing that she resembled Xiaolongnu. Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu had left her with many traumas back then. But now, she was growing more and more fond of Tingxue.","The Ancient Tomb Sect’s martial arts are indeed unorthodox. To think that the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra was a dual cultivation skill. No wonder Xiaolongnu, despite being Guo’er’s master, insisted on marrying him.","Tingxue’s face turned bright red. She didn’t know what to do.","Huang Yaoshi, who had just arrived, was also overjoyed to hear the news. “Yang Guo’s daughter? Wonderful!”","He was more fond of Yang Guo than his slow-witted son-in-law.","Zu An couldn’t help noticing that the legendary grandmaster’s hair had turned white, and his vitality had greatly declined. His days were numbered. The lifespan of a mortal is short indeed.","The room buzzed for a while before they returned to the main topic at hand. “Rong’er and Jing’er were thinking of hiding the manuals in the weapons, but my experiments show that it’s not feasible—the manuals won’t be able to withstand the heat of the forging. I think it’s better to hide the manuals elsewhere and leave clues about their locations in the weapons.”","Huang Rong smiled. “Father, you’re more thoughtful. With the Mongols’ influence spreading all over the Central Plains, there’s nowhere safe to hide the manuals here. No matter how I look at it, it’s safer to hide the manuals across the sea, where the Mongols can’t reach it.”","“The Peach Blossom Island is located in the middle of the sea. It is tough for outsiders to find it, and the island is protected by formations constructed according to the principles of Qi Men Dun Jia[2]. Even if someone chances upon the island, they'll be trapped by the formations.”","“Thus, we’re planning to hide the Nine Yin Sutra and the Book of Wumu on the Peach Blossom Island, and we’ll leave the map and the solutions to the formations in the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber.”","Zu An was amazed. Guo Jing and Huang Rong had put a great deal of effort into this plan.","Huang Rong then turned to Tingxue and continued, “Someone has to supervise the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan to ensure the weapons do not fall into the wrong hands. There’s no one more suited for that role than the Ancient Tomb Sect. Your sect steers clear of the secular world, making it hard for the Mongols to find you. On top of that, your sect members are highly skilled and cold in nature.","“We currently aren’t able to find Guo’er and Miss Long, but your presence works as well. You can consult them about this when you return. I’m sure the righteous Guo’er and Miss Long will not turn away from this responsibility.”","Having Tingxue as her future daughter-in-law only made her more confident of her plan.","Tingxue had no choice but to accept the request.","Huang Yaoshi said, “Xiang’er, you’ll head to E’mei Mountain to find the Thunderbolt Bombs. Polu, you’ll sneak into the Ming Cult and steal the Sacred Fire Token. Miss Tingxue, you can accompany my disciple, Cheng Ying, to the Peach Blossom Island to familiarize yourself with the route to the Peach Blossom Island and the formations there. This serves as an additional layer of insurance.","“The Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan spans a century; there’s bound to be hiccups along the way. They could go missing or fall into the wrong hands. So, if you find someone suitable in the meantime, you can guide them straight to the Peach Blossom Island without bothering with the Heavenly Sword or the Dragon Slaying Saber.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. Huang Rong and the others had considered so many different possibilities that it seemed nigh-impossible for the plan to fail.","Tingxue frowned. She instinctively looked at Zu An. It was only after seeing the latter nod that she finally gave her consent.","Huang Rong’s smile widened.","Huang Yaoshi proceeded to brief Firework about E’mei Mountain’s mystical man, while Huang Rong briefed Zu An about the Ming Cult.","Zu An was familiar with the Ming Cult a hundred years from now, but he he knew nothing about this era’s Ming Cult[r]The Ming Cult only appears in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’, which is set a hundred years from ‘Return of the Condor Heroes’[/ref].","He learned from Huang Rong that the Ming Cult’s current leader had the surname of ‘Shi’, and that it was only active in the Western Regions. Their limited activity in the Central Plains meant that little was known about them. Only the Beggar Sect, who had a past conflict with them, had more information.","The Ming Cult originated from the Persian religion of Manichaeism. Many considered them to be an unorthodox cult, but it would be unwise to judge their morality solely from that. It was rumored that they had a formidable martial art known as the Great Cosmic Shift.","Zu An jotted down all the Ming Cult’s experts that Huang Rong mentioned in his mind. At the same time, he wondered if the Ming Cult had already made contact with its main Persian sect, given that Old Man Shanzhong had come to the Central Plains.","It was getting late, so the group retired to their rooms for the time being. They would set off tomorrow morning.","Much to Zu An and Tingxue’s bewilderment, they were assigned the same bedroom.","Xiangyang was severely lacking in resources from many years of war. To lead by example, the Guo Clan had dismantled their mansion’s pillars to repair the city walls, so there were already fewer rooms than before. The simultaneous arrival of Huang Yaoshi, Cheng Ying, and the others only worsened the shortage.","Huang Rong, taking into consideration that Zu And and Tingxue had already dual cultivated, chose to assign them the same room. This would have been considered rude in the past, but etiquette was a luxury when their country’s downfall was imminent.","In fact, she thought it would be ideal if they could speed things up and leave some descendants for the Guo Clan.","This put Zu An and Tingxue in a tight spot. They stared at the only bed in the room, at a loss for words.","1. Guo Jing, despite being one of the strongest experts in the world, is known to be slow-witted and untalented. Huang Rong helped him a lot by convincing top martial artists to teach him. ☜","2. Qi Men Dun Jia is a divination book, but in the context of Return of the Condor Heroes, it is a set of principles that allows you to construct elaborate labyrinths that can confuse, trap, and even injure others. ☜"]},{"number":2845,"title":"Chapter 2845: Chapter 2797: Holy Maiden","paragraphs":["“You take the bed. I’ll sleep on the floor.” Zu An reacted fast to the situation. It would appear suspicious if he requested another blanket from Huang Rong, but it was no big deal for a martial artist of his level to do without a blanket.","Tingxue shook her head. “There’s no need for that. I have an idea.”","White silk shot out from her sleeve and pierced the wall, forming a hammock. She gracefully leaped into it. “Xiaolongnu taught me this. I thought it was interesting.”","Seeing her rest on the silk hammock, Zu An was briefly dazed. He felt as if he was looking at the legendary Xiaolongnu in person.","Just then, the window opened. Zu An and Tingxue looked over and saw Firework sneaking in.","Tingxue nearly slipped off her silk hammock. “What are you doing here?”","Firework laughed. “It wasn’t easy for me to create an opportunity for you two, but you’re squandering it just like that?”","Tingxue huffed, “Look at the mess you have made!”","While covering up for Firework, she'd suddenly become the Guo Clan’s daughter-in-law. Somehow, she found herself unable to return to her usual composure. Emotions swayed her much more easily. She had never felt like this before.","“We’re friends. Shouldn’t we help each other out?” Firework replied with a grin.","Tingxue coldly replied, “What are you doing here so late at night? Are you here to mess around with him again?”","“It’s called training,” Firework corrected her.","Tingxue was speechless.","She wasn't so dense as to be unable to tell that Firework was intentionally getting intimate with Zu An in front of her to provoke her. What kind of perverted inclination is that? She wasn’t about to play along with this nonsense, so she got up and went to the neighboring room.","But Firework grabbed her hand and exclaimed, “Where are you going? I won’t be able to explain it if others see me sharing a room alone with him.”","It would invite controversy if Zu An and Firework, who were siblings in this world, were spotted spending the night together. However, they could still explain it if Tingxue was here as well.","Tingxue’s eyelids twitched. “You want me to stay here to watch you?”","It was one thing back when we were in different rooms, but you’re going too far now. She wrapped her hand around her sword sheath.","“I’m just teasing you.” Firework laughed. “Since we’re about to part ways, I’m here to discuss things with you two.”","Zu An burst into laughter. Since our time in the ancient tomb, Firework has reverted to the bubbly girl I met on the spaceship. Could she be suffering from dissociative personality disorder?","“Do you find their plan feasible?”","Zu An replied, “I have to say that they've thought things through. I don’t think we could have done it any better.”","Firework frowned. “But none of the countless challengers before us has cleared this trial. Is there an intrinsic flaw in the plan itself, or is the difficulty in accomplishing the plan greater than expected?”","Tingxue finally expressed her view. “There’s no point thinking so much right now. All we can do right now is to do as we were told and attempt to craft the Heavenly Sword and the Dragon Slaying Saber first.”","“What if it’s a trap?” Unable to be as nonchalant as the Nebula worshiper, Firework turned to Zu An and asked, “You’re familiar with this world’s background, right? Did the plan succeed or not?”","“There were some twists and turns, but in the end, the plan succeeded.” Zu An summarized the story of ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’ for the two of them.","“What could the problem be?” Firework was perplexed. “Based on what you have shared, I am the future founder of the E’mei Sect, so it makes sense for me to head to E’mei Mountain right now. That seems to be an inevitability of fate.”","“It doesn’t seem likely that you’ll face significant danger during your journey to E’mei Mountain, but you mustn’t let your guard down. Anything involving fate has to be taken seriously.”","“Don’t worry, Tingxue and I should be fine. What’s more worrying is your journey to the Ming Cult.” Firework had already learned about the Ming Cult’s association with Old Man Shanzhong, and the latter had proven himself to be a formidable assassin.","“I’ll tread carefully,” Zu An replied.","They continued their discussion through the night, but they still had no clue how to tackle this trial.","The following day, when Guo Fu called them out for breakfast, she saw them sleeping on the same bed and shouted in shock. That jolted Zu An and the others awake.","Tingxue shot to her feet, whereas Firework was unfazed.","“We chatted too late into the night, got tired, and fell asleep like that.”","The three of them were bound to mortal bodies in this world. Consecutive days of traveling had caused fatigue to build up in them. When the sky darkened, they fell asleep before they realized it. Needless to say, nothing happened among them.","Guo Fu huffed, “Xiang’er, you aren’t young anymore. You shouldn’t be fooling around like that.”","She didn’t suspect anything because Tingxue was around as well. Her little sister had always been eccentric from a young age, so it was normal for her to not maintain the usual boundaries between men and women.","Before embarking on their journey, the three of them first paid a visit to Guo Jing and Huang Rong.","As Zu An rushed northwest to Kunlun Mountain, he couldn’t help replaying the conversation they had the night before parting ways. Based on what I remember, the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan succeeded in the end, so why has no one succeeded in the trial to date?","He didn’t think that those who had come before them wouldn’t be able to obtain the Sacred Fire Token and the Thunderbolt Bombs.","Is the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan not the crux of the trial? Or has this world’s future changed, making the plan doomed to fail? How did the other universal deities tamper with this world?","Zu An had several conjectures in mind, but they needed confirmation. He continued heading toward the Western Regions.","Around a month later, he finally arrived at the foot of Kunlun Mountain. The long journey made him realize how accustomed he was to flying around. It felt frustrating for him to have to travel by foot like that.","Soon, he found the Ming Cult’s home at the vast Kunlun Mountain.","The Ming Cult of the present era was nowhere as powerful as they would be in the future. He encountered some guards along the way, but none of them could stop him. He snuck his way toward the Radiant Peak, only to find fewer guards around. Huh? Shouldn’t there be more guards as I approach the Radiant Peak?","He soon learned the reason by eavesdropping on the cult members’ conversations. A holy maiden from the Persian headquarters had graced the Ming Cult, so Cult Leader Shi had gathered all important figures at the main hall to welcome her.","Zu An was surprised.","A holy maiden from the headquarters? Could it be Purple Dress Dragon King Daiqisi? But that can’t be. That’s a character from ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’, so she hasn’t even been born yet.","He secretly knocked out a cult member, changed into his clothes, and snuck into the main hall.","A crowd was gathered in the main hall—they were likely all in the Ming Cult’s upper echelons. Seated on the highest chair was a brawny old man. Judging from his clothes and the respect accorded to him, he was Cult Leader Shi.","Cult Leader Shi coldly said, “Treasure Tree King, the Central Plains Ming Cult may have descended from the Persian Ming Cult, but it has been centuries since we have laid our roots here. The Mongols seek to conquer the Central Plains, and we have sworn to fight them to the bitter end. So, how can we obey the Persian headquarters’ unreasonable order to serve the Mongols?”","Zu An swiftly understood the situation.","The Persian headquarters must have sent an envoy down to persuade the Central Plains Ming Cult to surrender to the Mongols, but Cult Leader Shi refuses to obey the order. He’s a righteous person.","Zu An was initially worried for the Central Plains Ming Cult for defying the Mongols, but on second thought, they were located in the middle of the remote Kunlun Mountain. The Mongols’ army of hundreds of thousands wouldn’t be of much use here. It was no wonder they were fearless.","A Persian with a sharp nose and distant eyes replied, “We have different aspirations. We won’t force you to comply since you aren’t willing to do so. I just hope this matter doesn’t impair the goodwill between us.”","The Persian was so understanding that Cult Leader Shi felt embarrassed. The Central Plains Ming Cult did have deep ties with the Persian Ming Cult, after all.","The Persian continued, “Actually, we have another objective here. A respected elder from our Persian headquarters passed away a year ago. He was from the Central Plains, but he migrated to Persia and joined our Ming Cult. He contributed greatly to our Ming Cult and married a Persian lady, and the two of them had a daughter.","“That respected elder missed his homeland even on his deathbed, and he wished for his daughter to return to the Central Plains. Our cult leader respects his will and commanded me to escort his daughter to the Radiant Peak, hoping that the Central Plains Ming Cult would take good care of her.","“Isabella, come here and pay respects to Cult Leader Shi.”"]},{"number":2846,"title":"Chapter 2846: Chapter 2798: A Clue","paragraphs":["The Persian envoy stepped aside for a young woman to make her entrance. She was so gorgeous that her presence lit up the room.","The Ming Cult’s main hall should have been a solemn place where important decisions were made, but the young woman’s entrance invited gasps of astonishment. Her beauty felt out of this world.","Zu An was both surprised and delighted. Despite tapping into the Beggar Sect’s vast information network, he hadn’t been able to find any clues on Isabella all this time. He hadn’t expected to reunite with her here.","Isabella was dressed in Persian clothes, giving her an exotic touch. She stepped forward and gracefully bowed to Cult Leader Shi. Her manners were flawless, as one would have expected from the Acadias’ esteemed big miss.","Upon seeing her, Cult Leader Shi’s heart softened. “Holy maiden, since your father was from the Central Plains, you should treat this place like your home, too. From now on, you’re the Central Plains Ming Cult’s holy maiden. Heed my order, cult members. You are to show utmost respect to the holy maiden from this day onward!”","“Yes, cult leader!” the cult members replied in unison.","Isabella’s appearance alleviated the tense atmosphere.","The members of the Ming Cult warmly welcomed the envoys from the Persian headquarters with a banquet. To avoid alarming the esteemed holy maiden, Cult Leader Shi instructed a maid to settle her in a quiet residence.","Zu An snuck out of the main hall and followed the maid to the courtyard. It looks like the Ming Cult regards the headquarters’ holy maiden highly. This residence is almost on par with the cult leader’s residence.","While the maids got busy tidying up the place, Isabella sat down alone in the room and sighed. She gazed at the distant mountains outside the window, but she was in no mood to admire this majestic scenery. Instead, she pouted as if she had suffered a grievance.","“Why is our holy maiden brooding alone here?” a teasing voice echoed.","Isabella was frightened, but the voice sounded oddly familiar. “Am I dreaming? Why do I hear his voice?”","“I didn’t expect to bump into you here. It feels like a dream to me as well.” A figure slipped into the room.","Isabella quickly clasped her about-to-gasp mouth. “Big brother Zu, it really is you!” She was so excited that she immediately leaped into his embrace.","Feeling her trembling body, Zu An also embraced her tightly. “I’ve finally found you.”","He suddenly narrowed his eyes. “Shh, someone’s coming.”","He nimbly leaped out of the window. It would surely cause a huge uproar if the cult members were to see their pure holy maiden embracing a man.","Several maids entered the room. “Paying respects to the holy maiden. Our cult leader has commanded us to serve the holy maiden from this day onward. Please instruct us if there’s anything you require here.”","Has the holy maiden... been crying? Well, she did leave the place where she grew up and traveled a long distance to get here, so she might be feeling homesick.","Isabella traded some pleasantries with them before anxiously sending them out.","“Big brother Zu! Big brother Zu~” She rushed to the windowsill and called out with a quivering voice, afraid that their earlier reunion was merely an illusion.","“Why are you sniffling?”","Zu An's gentle smile pierced through Isabella’s defenses, and she began sobbing in his arms, venting the fear and horror she had been accumulating all this time.","Zu An patted her shoulder and gently consoled her.","Some time later, Isabella, now feeling a little embarrassed, raised her head and wiped off her tears. “I made a fool of myself, big brother Zu.”","“Not at all. If you didn’t react after seeing me, I’d be the one crying.”","“You’re teasing me~”","The two of them spent a while reminiscing about the past before Zu An asked her about what she had been through ever since entering the trial.","After entering the trial, Isabella had assumed the identity of the Persian Ming Cult’s holy maiden. She was respected within the cult, but due to the foreign environment, all the scheming individuals who approached her with ulterior motives, and her failure to find any clues about Zu An despite secretly searching for him, she couldn’t shake off her anxiety.","On top of that, she'd suddenly been forced to leave Persia and travel to a distant place called the Central Plains. She'd thought there was no way she could find Zu An and the others anymore, but little had she expected to reunite with him here.","“What’s the Persian Ming Cult’s motive for visiting the Central Plains Ming Cult?” Zu An didn’t believe their bullshit story about sending their holy maiden back to her motherland.","“Their foremost agenda was to persuade the Central Plains Ming Cult to surrender to the Mongols, but Cult Leader Shi refused to do so,” Isabella replied. “Their secondary goal is to obtain the secret manual, Great Cosmic Shift.”","“Great Cosmic Shift?” Zu An was confused. “Didn’t the Central Plains Ming Cult inherit the Great Cosmic Shift from the Persian headquarters? Why are they looking for it here?”","Isabella explained, “Persia has been ravaged by war for many years now, resulting in the original manual of the Great Cosmic Shift going missing. That’s why the Persian headquarters covets the copy in the Central Plains Ming Cult. There’s no way the Central Plains Ming Cult would relinquish a martial art as powerful as the Great Cosmic Shift to them, so they instructed me to settle down here and find a chance to steal it.”","She paused for a second before adding, “At all costs.” Her face reddened in embarrassment and anger.","Zu An understood what that meant for a young, beautiful maiden. He secretly berated the Persian headquarters for being despicable and shameless in his mind before further asking, “Do you know the conditions to clear this trial? Could it be to steal the Great Cosmic Shift?”","Isabella spent a moment in thought before replying, “I don’t think it’s that simple. Stealing the Great Cosmic Shift is merely a part of it. The final goal should be to become the leader of the Persian headquarters.","“There are a total of three holy maidens in the Persian headquarters, including me, and the cult leader of every generation has always been chosen from the three holy maidens. The other two have been dispatched to Eastern Europe and Western Europe, and they have been entrusted with arduous tasks as well.","“The cult leader position will be passed on to the one who contributes the most to the sect. I suspect that stealing the Great Cosmic Shift won’t be enough; I’ll have to persuade the Central Plains Ming Cult to surrender to stand a chance at victory.”","Isabella noticed Zu An’s prolonged silence and was intrigued. “Big brother Zu, do you have different conditions for clearing the trial?”","“I’m afraid that my conditions for clearing the trial might be contrary to yours...” Zu An replied with a bitter smile before sharing the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan.","Isabella was horrified. “How can this be?!”","To think they were in opposite camps! Didn’t this mean that one of them had to die here?","Zu An consoled Isabella, “It might not be that bad. I’ll find a way for all of us to survive.”","He'd still been confused a moment ago, but learning about Isabella’s mission gave him some peace of mind. Even though they were in opposite camps, there could still be a way for both of them to win.","He was more concerned about Firework and Tingxue’s missions now.","Firework’s mission is probably about the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan, or the founding of the E’mei Sect, but what about Tingxue? Is her mission to supervise the plan? Isn’t that too simple?"]},{"number":2847,"title":"Chapter 2847: Chapter 2799: Secret Tunnel","paragraphs":["“Do you know about the Sacred Fire Token?” Zu An asked after some thought.","Isabella nodded. “The Sacred Fire Token is a sacred treasure of the Persian Ming Cult. It’s made from platinum mixed with xuan metal and diamond sand. It’s about 60 centimeters long, has a texture resembling jade, and is extremely hard. You’ll recognize it at a glance.","“Six Sacred Fire Tokens were crafted and passed down to the Central Plains Ming Cult back then. Such sacred treasures are wielded only by the cult leader, so you might have to work on Cult Leader Shi.”","Zu An said, “I don’t think Cult Leader Shi was carrying the Sacred Fire Token earlier. He must have placed it elsewhere.”","“It could be in his room, but I have no idea where it is.”","“It could also be in the secret tunnel. The Radiant Peak has a secret tunnel that only the cult leader can access. Anyone else who enters will be executed. It’s the perfect place to store the Sacred Fire Token.”","“Hm? Big brother Zu, how do you know about that?” Isabella was surprised. Not even the Persian Ming Cult knew about the Radiant Peak’s secret tunnel.","Zu An briefly shared why he was knowledgeable about this world with her.","Isabella widened her eyes in surprise. “Big brother Zu, you have such a profound connection with the Deity of Death’s trial. It looks like you’re the most likely candidate to clear the trial.”","“No matter what, I’ll find a way to save everyone.”","“I believe you can do it, big brother Zu.”","Zu An was surprised. He'd thought it would take him more effort to convince Isabella, but the latter believed him right away.","Isabella noticed his expression and smiled. “I've seen you pulling off the impossible many times in Dreamland. I trust you.”","In truth, Zu An wasn't very confident despite his declaration. This was a universal deity’s trial, after all. But looking at Isabella’s gleaming eyes, he suddenly felt a surge of courage.","The two of them continued chatting about what had happened to them respectively after they parted ways, before Zu An took his leave to scout the Radiant Peak.","By the time he returned, it was already nightfall. “Isabella, I found the entrance to the secret tunnel. Let’s investigate it together. We might find the manual for Great Cosmic Shift there.”","“Alright.” Isabella’s eyes lit up. She felt more at ease being with Zu An than staying in her room alone.","Firework and Tingxue had spent their lives in combat, but Isabella, being born into a powerful background, rarely had to fight. Her combat style revolved around her overpowered treasures, but that put her at a disadvantage in this trial world, where supernatural powers were banned.","Isabella wasn't weak compared to the majority of the martial artists, but it would be a stretch to consider her a top-notch expert. On their way to the secret tunnel, Zu An often had to carry her and employ his movement skills to avoid being discovered by guards along the way.","But Isabella enjoyed it. Her grandfather had built many amusement parks for her across the universes, but even those didn’t bring her this much joy.","The thrill of possibly being discovered at any moment and the security she felt from Zu An’s embrace felt overwhelming. If not for the inappropriate circumstances, she might have been shrieking by now.","The two of them soon arrived at the secret tunnel. There were no guards stationed here, as it was a forbidden area.","They pushed open the stone door and entered it. A winding path appeared before their eyes. They advanced carefully, but contrary to their expectations, it wasn't booby-trapped.","They traveled around a hundred meters before reaching the end. Isabella examined their surroundings and remarked in surprise, “We seem to have reached a dead end. It doesn’t look like there are any mechanisms installed here.”","Zu An probingly touched the wall before saying, “Please step aside for a moment.”","He channeled his inner energy into the wall and pushed it aside by twenty centimeters, revealing another passageway. Then, he said, “I’d have expected no less from the Ming Cult’s forbidden area. The other mechanisms in the tunnel are delicate, but this stone door has to be opened with brute force. No matter how smart an intruder is, unless their inner energy is strong enough, they won’t be able to enter.”","Isabella was awed. “I hadn’t expected these people from a lower world to be so cunning. We mustn’t let our guard down here.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. Knowing that universal deities could have tampered with this trial world, he'd never treated the people of this world as countryside bumpkins.","The two of them entered the passageway.","Isabella surveyed their surroundings as she remarked, “There are many forks here. It seems to be a labyrinth.”","“It’s a basic labyrinth,” Zu An replied. Having witnessed major formations in the Myriad Worlds, this labyrinth was indeed nothing in comparison. It didn’t take long for them to find the right path to advance deeper.","Soon, they arrived at a wide room. Its layout hinted that it was the cult leader’s private training room.","Zu An searched the room, but much to his disappointment, he didn’t find the Sacred Flame Token or Great Cosmic Shift manual.","Come to think of it, in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’, one of the later cult leaders, Yang Dingtian, died in this secret chamber while carrying the Great Cosmic Shift manual. If I’m not mistaken, the manual is a piece of goatskin leather. I’m many years too early to be finding the manual here.","I bet Cult Leader Shi carries the manual on him everywhere he goes.","Zu An shared his deduction with Isabella. While the two of them were planning their next move, they suddenly heard voices and hurriedly darted into the neighboring stone chamber to hide.","Footsteps approached. There appeared to be two people.","“Cult leader, those Persians are definitely up to something. We should take this chance to deal with them once and for all!”","“That won’t do. They are from the headquarters, and they have come as representatives for the Mongols. The Mongols will retaliate against the killing of their envoys. Back then, Khwarazm was a considerable power in Central Asia, but they killed a Mongol envoy, and that provoked an all-out attack from Mongolia, resulting in their country’s downfall.”","Isabella and Zu An exchanged gazes. One of them had to be Cult Leader Shi, and the other had to be among the Ming Cult’s upper echelon, though his exact identity eluded them.","“Cult leader, the killing of the envoy was an excuse. The Mongols would have conquered Khwarazm regardless. The Persians are clearly here as scouts. If we allow them to return, the Mongols will have information about our location and geographical terrain. By the time the Mongolian army reaches our base, it’ll be too late for regrets!”","“Things have not come to that point yet. We’re so remotely located that it isn’t worthwhile for the Mongols to invade us. They sent a holy maiden here to serve as a hostage to ease our minds.”","“That holy maiden harbors ulterior motives. I sent someone to check her residence, and she isn’t there! Who knows where she has gone to wreak havoc!”","Hearing those words, Isabella stuck out her tongue. She was in quite a predicament.","“I need to think things through.” Cult Leader Shi sounded vexed.","“Cult leader, it’ll be too late if you continue hesitating!”","A sinister laugh suddenly echoed. “It’s already too late.”"]},{"number":2848,"title":"Chapter 2848: Chapter 2800: Stealing Treasure","paragraphs":["Zu An had secretly taken a look.","The person who was conversing with Cult Leader Shi was a middle-aged man. He was likely the Ming Cult’s Radiant Left Envoy, judging from his position earlier in the main hall. I think his family name is Yi or something.","In the organization, the Radiant Left Envoy was second only to the cult leader. It made sense for Cult Leader Shi to bring him into this secret tunnel.","But who could the other person be?","Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi were astounded as well. “Who is it?”","Several figures stepped in.","Zu An glanced at Isabella. The intruders were the Persians who had escorted her here.","Isabella was stunned as well. She had no idea what those Persians were doing here, but regardless, it was bad news for her. Whether those Persians succeeded or not, it would put her in a spot, especially since she had to settle down here.","“Treasure Tree King, the Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon, what are you doing here?” Cult Leader Shi’s eyes were cold. It wasn't a joke that anyone who barged into the secret tunnel without the cult leader’s permission would be executed.","Zu An eyed the Persians. The Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon were two men and one woman. The two men had vicious eyes, whereas the woman wore a veil and had a figure that was more voluptuous than the women of the Central Plains.","Since their ages don’t match, they can’t be the same Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber'. They must have always been two men and one woman.","“We would never have known about your secret ploy against us if we hadn’t come here,” the Treasure Tree King sneered in halting Chinese.","Left Envoy Yi roared in anger, “Don’t you know that those who barge into the forbidden area will be executed without mercy?”","The Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon suddenly launched an attack.","Left Envoy Yi was a top expert; he couldn’t have climbed to his current position otherwise.","He quickly defended himself, but the three envoys used unorthodox martial arts that were hard to read, and their teamwork was impeccable. One swept his legs. One grabbed his hand. One attacked his acupoints. There was no chance for him to counterattack at all.","It didn’t take long for the three envoys to defeat Left Envoy Yi. It happened so abruptly that Cult Leader Shi couldn’t make it in time to support him.","Left Envoy Yi felt so ashamed that he would have dug a hole and buried himself on the spot. He had always been proud of his strength, believing himself to only be second to Cult Leader Shi in the Ming Cult. Yet he was swiftly curbed by these enemies.","He felt icy-cold inner energy gush into his acupoints, assaulting him with excruciating pain and preventing him from channeling his inner energy.","Zu An clearly saw what had happened. The Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon’s martial arts were so unorthodox that they could easily curb most enemies unless one was significantly stronger than them.","Cult Leader Shi’s expression turned grim. He was shocked by the three envoys’ martial arts as well. “What do you mean by this?”","The Treasure Tree King laughed. “Cult Leader Shi, we’re doing this out of self-defense, lest you join forces to kill us. You don’t have to worry about Left Envoy Yi’s safety. All you have to do is to defect to the Mongols. That’d make you my superior in the future. I wouldn’t dare offend you.”","Cult Leader Shi’s expression darkened. “I believe I made myself clear earlier.”","“You’re putting me in a difficult spot.” The Treasure Tree King shook his head. “There are voices in the headquarters who want to slowly advance our goals and buy time for the holy maiden to find the Great Cosmic Shift, but I don’t see the need to play the long game here.”","Zu An and Isabella exchanged looks. Looks like there are diverging opinions in the Persian Ming Cult. The Treasure Tree King might be a supporter of another holy maiden, and he’s doing this to foil Isabella’s mission.","Cult Leader Shi harrumphed. “I knew you harbored ulterior motives. I should have made a move earlier.”","He secretly retreated while lamenting. This was the Central Plains Ming Cult, his home turf. No matter how powerful the Treasure Tree King and the Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon were, they would be doomed with everyone charging at them at once.","The only problem was that the other cult members were forbidden from stepping into the secret tunnel. If he died here, no one would find him for a long time.","But the Persians saw through his intention. The Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon quickly spread out to block his path of retreat.","“Does the great Cult Leader Shi plan to escape like a downtrodden dog?” the Treasure Tree King sneered.","Cult Leader Shi harrumphed.","All of a sudden, he lunged at the veiled woman. He was planning to take down the weakest Radiant Moon Envoy as quickly as possible to unravel the Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon’s collaboration formation.","But the Radiant Moon envoy was guarded against his assault. She dodged his attack with an unorthodox movement skill while scoffing, “Tsk tsk tsk. Is Cult Leader Shi interested in me? But I’m not sure if an old man like you has the stamina to take me on.”","Cult Leader Shi’s face darkened, and his attacks became even more ferocious. Faced with great pressure, the Radiant Moon Envoy couldn’t maintain her smile anymore.","The Flowing Cloud Envoy and the Profound Wind Envoy quickly reinforced her. The three envoys had been working together for such a long time that they could read each other’s intentions. Their teamwork was impeccable.","Cult Leader Shi was able to stand his ground despite simultaneously fighting three opponents, though.","“Is that the legendary Great Cosmic Shift? It’s unfathomable indeed.” The Wind, Cloud, and Moon Envoys keenly sensed their inner energies being directed against their own comrades, which made it seem as if they were fighting among themselves instead.","Cult Leader Shi harrumphed. Their martial arts are too unorthodox. I can’t read their moves. Somehow, they're always able to dodge my attacks from unbelievable angles, causing my fatal blows to miss. And that Treasure Tree King is eyeing me like a hawk from the side.","As the fight dragged on, he grew increasingly agitated.","Meanwhile, Zu An watched the battle with a frown.","Cult Leader Shi is in a terrible position, but for some reason, the only top martial art he's using is the Great Cosmic Shift. His other moves are strong in their own right, but they aren’t top-notch.","Why isn’t he using the Nine Heavens Palm? That’s the move that skyrocketed Cult Leader Yang Dingtian to the top of the martial world in the future—though he failed to best Zhang Sanfeng.","Even the head of the Shaolin Temple’s Three Elders lost an eye to the Nine Heavens Palm! His two juniors spent decades developing the Vajra Evil Subduing Ring, but they dared not confront Yang Dingtian to avenge their senior.","So, why is Cult Leader Shi not using the Nine Heavens Palm? Does he plan on catching the Treasure Tree King by surprise?","But Zu An soon rejected that conjecture.","The Treasure Tree King found an opening and hurled his fist into Cult Leader Shi’s back.","Cult Leader Shi had planned to use Great Cosmic Shift to transfer the force behind the fist to the Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon, but he found himself unable to move. The four Persians took advantage of that opening to strike Cult Leader Shi’s acupoint.","Pu!","Cult Leader Shi spat blood. He crumpled to the ground, unable to fight anymore.","“Cult leader!” Left Envoy Yi was enraged, but he was unable to do anything about it.","Sensing Cult Leader Shi’s confusion, the Treasure Tree King explained with a smile, “Great Cosmic Shift originates from our Persian headquarters. We might have lost the main manual, but we still have texts to understand its unique traits. You have only reached the third layer of Great Cosmic Shift; there’s no way you could have transferred my attack.”","Cult Leader Shi’s face turned pale. To think that I’d die here due to a moment of carelessness.","“I reckon he’s carrying the Great Cosmic Shift manual with him. Radiant Moon Envoy, search his body.” The Treasure Tree King was worried Cult Leader Shi had a final ace up his sleeve and dared not risk his life.","“Yes!” The Radiant Moon Envoy rushed forward to search Cult Leader Shi’s body. “Oh? I didn’t expect someone as old as you to have a decent figure.”","Soon, her eyes lit up. She lifted a piece of lambskin and exclaimed, “Found it!”","The Treasure Tree King was overjoyed. He was about to take it when a shadow flashed across the room and snatched the lambskin.","Only then did the crowd realize there was another young man in the room.","“Who are you?!” the Treasure Tree King roared in anger. Does the Central Plains Ming Cult still have other hidden experts? He must have been hiding here for some time now, but to think that none of us noticed him!","Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi traded perplexed looks. That guy isn’t a member of our Ming Cult. What is he doing in the secret tunnel?"]},{"number":2849,"title":"Chapter 2849: Chapter 2801: A Forced Compromise","paragraphs":["Zu An couldn’t be bothered to waste his breath. “Did you bring the Sacred Fire Tokens here?”","Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi were taken aback. We thought he was here to reinforce us, but it looks like he’s after the Sacred Fire Tokens.","The Treasure Tree King and the Three Envoys of Wind, Cloud, and Moon were enraged. How dare this fellow covet our Sacred Fire Tokens? The former yelled, “Hand that goatskin to me, and I’ll spare your life!”","Even the great leader of the Ming Cult and its Radiant Left Envoy had been subdued by them. He didn’t think a young man in his twenties could be stronger than them.","Zu An shook his head. “That won’t do. My friend needs the Great Cosmic Shift manual.”","Isabella chuckled from the shadows, her laughter bringing a tinge of sweetness to the dull secret chamber.","“You’re courting death!” The Treasure Tree King thrust his palm at Zu An.","Zu An stood his ground and confronted the palm head-on.","“Be careful! There’s something peculiar about his inner energy!” Cult Leader Shi warned them. While this mysterious fellow didn’t appear to be an ally, he harbored greater animosity toward the Persians. The Treasure Tree King’s peculiar inner energy had overwhelmed him with pain earlier, resulting in his eventual incapacitation.","“It’s too late!” the Treasure Tree King sneered. His inner energy morphed into thin needles to pierce Zu An’s palm acupoints.","It was their signature skill, Bone Penetrating Needles. It involved manifesting one's inner yin energy into needles as thin as a hair, transmitting it into an enemy’s body and repeatedly piercing the enemy from within. The pain inflicted was so great that it would briefly stun anyone. They also had another skill called the Yin Gale Knife. They could manifest their inner energy as invisible blades to pierce the enemy’s hand acupoints to inflict considerable damage.","It was with these attacks that they'd subdued Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi with ease. Their unorthodox martial arts played a part, but these skills were the ones that had allowed them to catch their enemies by surprise.","But Zu An took his palm without flinching in the slightest.","“Impossible!” The Treasure Tree King was certain he'd hurled out a few Bone Penetrating Needles, but they seemed to be ineffective against Zu An.","Bewildered, he quickly manifested more Bone Penetrating Needles, but the moment he channeled his inner energy, it began gushing out toward Zu An’s palm like a breached dam.","To his relief, the Three Envoys attacked at that moment, forcing Zu An to release him.","Sheesh, the simplified version of the Heaven-Devouring Sutra I modified for this world is nothing compared to the real deal. Otherwise, I could have sucked the Treasure Tree King dry there and then.","Even so, that brief contact left the Treasure Tree King sweating profusely. He anxiously shouted a warning, “Be careful, he’s capable of sorcery! Avoid physical contact with him!”","The Three Envoys were startled. Their attacks required physical contact to send their Bone Penetrating Needles and Yin Gale Knives into their enemy’s body. Otherwise, their power would be greatly decreased. But they had also seen what happened to the Treasure Tree King earlier, so they obediently changed their moves.","The Three Envoys employed bizarre martial arts that martial artists of the Central Plains struggled to deal with, but with his sharp eyes, Zu An easily deciphered them.","The trio hurriedly changed their moves, but in the midst of doing so, they revealed a huge opening for a brief instant. Zu An unhesitatingly charged in and struck the Wind Envoy and Cloud Envoy, causing the two of them to collapse like sacks of mud.","Horrified, the Radiant Moon Envoy immediately turned around to flee, only to find herself immobilized. To her horror, Zu An’s palm was already on her shoulder.","Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi gasped in shock. Having crossed blows with the Persians, they knew that they were difficult opponents. Yet Zu An had made quick work of them.","“Spare me, young master. I’m willing to serve you...” The Radiant Moon Envoy attempted to seduce Zu An. Her beauty had never failed her. She had even charmed the Flowing Cloud Envoy and Profound Wind Envoy, which was why the other two died first even though she was the weakest in the group.","“My women are a hundred times better than you.”","Zu An was about to end her when a voice suddenly spoke up, “Please have mercy!”","Isabella held up her skirt and rushed out. Faced with Zu An’s questioning gaze, she quickly explained, “Big sister Radiant Moon took good care of me at the Persian headquarters.”","Zu An recalled that there were two other holy maidens in the Persian Ming Cult. Isabella will need helpers to become the cult leader. So, he nodded. “I’ll spare you for Isabella’s sake.”","“Thank you, great hero! Thank you, holy maiden!” The Radiant Moon Envoy was extremely relieved to have survived this crisis.","The Treasure Tree King was infuriated. “Isabella, you traitor! How dare you collude with outsiders against us?”","Isabella’s expression turned cold. “Our cult leader ordered me to infiltrate the Central Plains Ming Cult to obtain the Great Cosmic Shift, but your actions have compromised my position in the Central Plains Ming Cult. Who is the traitor here?”","Zu An was impressed by Isabella’s air of majesty. He was so accustomed to her little sister vibes that he nearly forgot that she was the Acadias’ big miss, a powerhouse in the Universal Conglomerate.","The Treasure Tree King sweated profusely. He could tell that Zu An was on close terms with Isabella, and he happened to be the supporter of another holy maiden. Seeing that he had lost the upper hand, he roared and feigned an attack, only to abruptly turn around and flee. After seeing what the latter was capable of, he didn’t dare to confront Zu An.","But when he realized he was being dragged back into the chamber, fear swiftly gripped him.","Zu An wasn’t about to let him escape. He pulled the Treasure Tree King into his grasp with the simplified Heaven-Devouring Sutra and siphoned his inner energy dry.","Earlier, he had chosen not to siphon the inner energies of the Three Envoys, as it would risk revealing an opening for his enemies to exploit, but since the battle had already ended, there was no harm absorbing the Treasure Tree King’s inner energy to bulk up. The stronger he was, the more prepared he would be for future crises.","When they saw the brawny Treasure Tree King withering in an instant, Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi felt shivers run down their spine.","Zu An looked at the duo. “Where are the Sacred Fire Tokens?”","Cult Leader Shi raised his head and declared, “Go ahead and kill me. I’ll never hand you our cult’s sacred treasure!”","Isabella interjected, “He just saved your lives. Isn’t that worth the Sacred Fire Tokens?”","Cult Leader Shi snorted, “How can I trade the Sacred Fire Tokend for my life? I wouldn’t be able to face my predecessors when I die!”","Left Envoy Yi nodded in agreement. “Our cult leader is right. Kill us if you want to. We don’t need your pity!”","Isabella wanted to continue persuading them, but Zu An stopped her and said, “It’s also fine by me if you don’t want to hand over the Sacred Fire Tokend. I’ll just kill the two of you, strip your bodies, and tell your people that you were messing around in the cult’s sacred land. How does that sound?”","Both Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi were horrified. “How dare you!”","“You despicable scum!”","The more they berated Zu An, the colder his expression became. In the end, Cult Leader Shi had no choice but to surrender. “I’m powerless to stop you from stealing the Sacred Fire Tokend. Do you dare leave your name behind?”","“Me?” A thought suddenly popped into Zu An’s mind. “I am from the Beggar Sect.”","He remembered that in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’, the Beggar Sect had obtained the Ming Cult’s Sacred Fire Tokens from their 31st Cult Leader Shi."]},{"number":2850,"title":"Chapter 2850: Chapter 2802: A Ray of Hope","paragraphs":["Upon mentioning the Beggar Sect, Zu An felt as if he had had an epiphany, but that feeling passed him by before he could grasp it.","“The Sacred Fire Tokens are in my bedroom,” Cult Leader Shi suddenly said.","“Bring me there.” To stop them from playing any tricks, Zu An layered more restrictions on Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi.","Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi traded helpless and fearful gazes. They weren’t afraid of death, but this fellow was too despicable.","So, they left the secret tunnel and made their way to Cult Leader Shi’s room. Despite bumping into several cult members along the way, both Cult Leader Shi and Left Envoy Yi knew they would only be dragging their cult members down by asking for help, so they didn’t bother putting up any resistance.","The cult members thought that Cult Leader Shi was bringing the Radiant Left Envoy, the holy maiden, and the Persian envoys to his room for a private conversation, so they didn’t probe into it.","Cult Leader Shi opened a hidden compartment built into his room and took out six Sacred Fire Tokens.","Zu An took the tokens. They felt heavy, and they had a peculiar texture that felt like an amalgamation of metal and jade. There was no way to fabricate such a material.","“I’ll borrow your cult’s Sacred Fire Tokens. You can be assured I’ll return them to the Radiant Peak once I’m done with them.” Zu An stowed away the Sacred Fire Tokens. He didn’t explain further as he didn’t want to reveal the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan.","Cult Leader Shi harrumphed. “I only have myself to blame for my weakness. Should a cult member surpass me in the future, you can be certain he’ll knock on the Beggar Sect’s doors.”","Zu An simply smiled, not bothering to argue. He took the goatskin containing the Great Cosmic Shift manual and handed it to Isabella.","Isabella stared at the blank goatskin in a daze. The sharp-witted Radiant Moon Envoy bit her finger and scattered her blood on it. Only then did pictures and words surface on the goatskin.","Isabella passed the goatskin to Zu An. “Big brother, why don’t you practice it too? This is the Ming Cult’s highest martial art. It should prove to be useful in this world.”","Indeed, the Great Cosmic Shift likely wouldn't be much in the Myriad Worlds, but it was definitely one of the strongest martial arts within the restrictions of this trial world. So, Zu An didn’t turn down her offer.","“You should study it, too.”","Isabella leaned on his shoulder, and the two of them studied the manual together. Moments later, their expressions darkened.","Zu An leaped away and knocked out the Radiant Moon Envoy and Left Envoy Yi. Then, he glared coldly at Cult Leader Shi and asked, “Where’s the real Great Cosmic Shift manual?”","Cult Leader Shi laughed. “That’s the real one.”","“Impossible! This manual only contains the first three layers!”","The parts detailing the subsequent layers were so badly damaged that there were only bits and pieces left, and the choice of words was so obscure that it was impossible to comprehend them without context.","Cult Leader Shi sneered, “Did the Persian Ming Cult, despite being the creators of the Great Cosmic Shift, lose their manual too? In the history of the Central Plains Ming Cult, only the powerful Cult Leader Zhong has been able to reach the fifth layer. Only a small handful of cult leaders had been able to reach the fourth layer. Furthermore, we have faced a great deal of infighting over the years. We only have the first three layers now.”","Isabella believed his words, but Zu An’s expressiom darkened. “Impossible. There has to be a complete Great Cosmic Shift manual. Where did you hide it? Don’t force me to resort to violence!”","Cult Leader Shi’s face reddened in anger. “I’d have practiced it if I had the complete manual; then I wouldn’t have been captured by the likes of you people!”","Isabella pulled Zu An aside and whispered, “I don’t think he’s lying. Big brother Zu, you don’t have to worry about me. It looks like I’m fated to fail my mission.”","Zu An patted her head. “It’s still too early to give up, Isabella. There has to be a complete Great Cosmic Shift manual in this world. Have you forgotten the plotline of the ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’ I shared with you?”","Isabella was startled. “Ah, you’re right. Could there be another copy of the Great Cosmic Shift hiding somewhere?”","“Impossible. The Great Cosmic Shift manual is strictly passed down only through the line of cult leaders. There can’t be a copy of it.” Cult Leader Shi refuted that conjecture.","Zu An pondered for a long while. “Cult Leader Shi, I’ll be staying at your Ming Cult’s Radiant Peak for a while. I hope you don’t mind.”","Cult Leader Shi was speechless. Will you leave if I say that I mind you staying?","Obviously, that was impossible. Zu An stayed behind, taking up residence beside Isabella.","In Isabella’s room, Isabella worriedly asked, “Big brother Zu, do you think Cult Leader Shi will rally the experts of the Ming Cult to encircle us?”","“You don’t need to worry about that. Cult Leader Shi is a smart man. He knows it’s futile to send his cult members at us, and there’s no need to take such a risk since we don’t plan to destroy the Ming Cult. He’ll weigh the pros and cons and decide on the optimal course of action.”","“Then why did you choose to stay behind?”","“I need time to think things through. I have an idea what the goal of the trial is.”","“Oh? What is it?”","“It won’t work if I say it aloud.”","“You’re terrible, big brother Zu.”","Just like that, Zu An stayed on the Radiant Peak for half a month.","...","“Impossible!” Cult Leader Shi exclaimed while staring at the goatskin presented to him.","It contained the subsequent layers of the Great Cosmic Shift manual, which should have been lost to time.","“There’s nothing impossible about it. I found the full manual,” Zu An said.","Cult Leader Shi was skeptical. Who knows if you fabricated it?","He browsed the manual and found that the subsequent layers were aligned with the first three layers he had grasped. He had spent many years studying the Great Cosmic Shift, and he couldn’t confidently say that this manual was fake.","He wanted to study the goatskin more, but Zu An sucked it back into his palm. “I’m not giving you the full manual for free. There is a condition.”","“What is it?” Cult Leader Shi’s eyes heated up. He would even step down as the cult leader if it meant completing the lost layers of the Great Cosmic Shift.","“Join the Mongols.”","“Dream on!” Cult Leader Shi was infuriated. “I thought the Beggar Sect was persistently holding the line against the Mongols thus far, but to think you people are already thinking about surrendering.”","“Calm down, Cult Leader Shi. I’m merely asking you to surrender in name.”","“Surrender in name?”","“How much longer do you think Southern Song can hold on against the Mongolian invasion?”","Cult Leader Shi pondered. “At most a few years more.”","“Once Southern Song is destroyed, the Mongols will have the manpower to clear away surrounding flies. How long do you think the Ming Cult can last against the Mongol army?”","“Hmph! Kunlun is a vast mountain. The Mongols will suffer huge casualties if they invade our Radiant Peak. The Mongol Khan won’t be so foolish.”","“What if they execute the surrendered soldiers of Southern Song instead?”","Cult Leader Shi was startled. Cold sweat rained down his back. He had turned down the Persian envoy because he knew it simply wasn't worthwhile for the Mongolians to send their troops to attack the Ming Cult.","But it was very possible for the Mongols to execute the surrendered Song soldiers instead. That was an effective way to reduce the size of the Song army, thus making it less likely for the Han to overthrow them in the future.","“But if we surrender to the Mongols, we’ll become a laughingstock.”","“Only a coward dies in vain. A hero stands firm amid criticisms to accomplish their goal,” Zu An argued. “Besides, you’d just be feigning surrender. You have a holy maiden here to help you strike diplomatic relations with the Mongols; there would be no reason for the Mongols to interfere in the distant Radiant Peak. The barbarians won’t be so lucky as to last beyond a century. Who knows? The Ming Cult might just play a critical role in overthrowing the Yuan Mongols.”"]},{"number":2851,"title":"Chapter 2851: Chapter 2803: Tingxue Needs to Have a Child","paragraphs":["Cult Leader Shi thought Zu An had come here for the Sacred Fire Tokens, but somehow, the latter was now strategizing for the Ming Cult against the Mongols. He couldn’t fathom what Zu An’s true goal was.","“It doesn’t matter who I am. The important thing is for you to choose what’s beneficial to the Ming Cult.” Zu An briefly hesitated but chose against revealing his identity. Guo Polu was an unknown figure in this world. Leaving his name here could affect the trajectory of events.","“You snatch our Ming Cult’s Sacred Fire Tokens and Great Cosmic Shift manual, yet you claim to be working in our interest?” Cult Leader Shi was bubbling with anger.","“You would have been killed by the Persians if not for me. I saved your life. Once you were dead, the Persians would have taken over the Ming Cult and brought it under the Mongols’ rule. The Ming Cult would have become nothing but a shell of its former self.","“I'm not only pointing out a road for the Ming Cult’s survival, but also offering to return the lost Great Cosmic Shift to you. Shouldn’t you be thankful to me?”","Cult Leader Shi fell silent. He couldn’t refute what Zu An had said, and he slowly calmed down from his initial anger.","“Don’t worry, the Sacred Fire Tokens will be returned to the Ming Cult in the future,” Zu An spoke so confidently that his words felt prophetic.","Cult Leader Shi wondered if Zu An was an immortal who'd descended to the mortal world. On top of wielding martial arts surpassing that of the legendary Five Greats, Zu An had also filled up the incomplete portions of the Great Cosmic Shift manual, and he spoke compellingly as if he could see the future.","“How can you ensure that our Ming Cult won’t be annexed by the Mongols?”","Seeing that Cult Leader Shi had finally loosened his stance, Zu An called Isabella over to discuss the finer details.","Following that, he bade Isabella farewell. “I have to bring the Sacred Fire Tokens to Xiangyang, so I can’t accompany you to Persia. Can you handle those matters by yourself?”","Isabella replied with a sweet smile, “Rest assured, big brother Zu. You've settled the matters of the Great Cosmic Shift manual and the Central Plains Ming Cult’s surrender to the Mongols for me, and I have the Radiant Moon Envoy to aid me now. If I still can’t become the cult leader, I might as well buy a slab of tofu and smash my head into it.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. Isabella was the Acadias’ big miss, and he had witnessed her socializing prowess from how she'd easily dealt with the experts coming from all over the Myriad Worlds. There was indeed no need to worry about her.","“Remember, you have to withhold the Great Cosmic Shift manual from the Persians. They can’t know about it.” Zu An knew how the plotline progressed. Decades later, the Persian Ming Cult would dispatch the Purple Robe Dragon King over to the Central Plains Ming Cult to steal the Great Cosmic Shift again.","“You can put your mind at ease. I know how to deal with it.” Isabella bit her lips and embraced Zu An tightly. “Big brother Zu, I don’t know if this will be our final meeting.”","Zu An fell silent. It was one thing for them to be separated, but if they couldn’t clear this trial, all of them would die.","“Don’t worry. I’m confident things will work out.”","“Mm! I trust you, big brother Zu.”","...","Zu An rushed back to Xiangyang. Firework and Tingxue were already waiting for him. Both E’mei and the Peach Blossom Island were closer than Kunlun Mountain, not to mention he had spent an entire month there.","Guo Jing and Huang Rong looked visibly relieved when they saw him. Even Firework and Tingxue felt as if a boulder weighing on their hearts had been released. Despite knowing that few in this world could pose a threat to him, they'd still been worried by his late return.","Zu An entrusted the Sacred Fire Tokens to Guo Jing and Huang Rong for the forging of the Heavenly Sword and the Dragon Slaying Saber. “I promised Cult Leader Shi I would return the Sacred Fire Tokens to them after we’re done.”","Guo Jing was overjoyed. “That goes without saying! Cult Leader Shi is magnanimous to lend us the Ming Cult’s sacred treasure!”","Huang Rong was perplexed. She hadn't thought Cult Leader Shi would lend out the Sacred Fire Tokens, but the proof was right before their eyes. She didn’t dwell on it too much since they were in a rush to forge the sword and saber, though.","Firework pulled Zu An and Tingxue to her room and asked him for updates.","“Tell me what happened on your side first.”","“Tingxue went to the Peach Blossom Island and familiarized herself with the route and formation. Nothing noteworthy happened, other than her pummeling perverts along the way. E’mei Mountain’s Thunderbolt Bomb was tricky, but something of that caliber can’t stump me.” Firework had a wistful look on her face. “But E’mei Mountain’s cloud sea left me with a deep impression. It was as mesmerizing as the fireworks I saw when I was sixteen.”","Firework snapped out of her daze and groaned, “Ugh, that’s a memory from this body’s original owner. How annoying!”","Zu An was surprised to hear that.","“Quick, tell us what happened on your side,” Firework urged. Tingxue also looked at him with curious eyes.","Zu An briefly shared what he'd been through with them. Firework exclaimed in surprise, “To think you actually met Isabella! I have to say you have quite the luck!”","“Why didn’t Isabella return with you?” Tingxue was confused.","Zu An told them about her mission.","Firework frowned. “Her mission is at odds with ours?”","“Not necessarily.” Zu An smiled. “Her mission was to obtain the Great Cosmic Shift and convince the Central Plains Ming Cult to surrender to the Mongols, so she could become the leader of the Persian headquarters. That’s not at odds with our mission, and I resolved it for her...”","He shared the details with them.","Firework frowned. “Won’t we be goners if she clears her mission first?”","“It isn’t that easy to clear the trial,” Zu An said. “I had an epiphany while I was at Kunlun Mountain. Perhaps those who challenged this trial before us failed because they refused to work together, thus resulting in their failure. Think about it. Each of us was assigned a different mission, with varying levels of difficulty. How is this a fair assessment?”","Firework frowned. “I see where you’re coming from, but how can the trial decide who is worthy to succeed the Deity of Death? No one wants to become a foil to another person.”","Zu An shook his head. “I’m unsure of the details right now. We can only take it a step at a time.”","There was no lack of smart people who'd challenged this trial before them, and some of them must have thought about cooperating with one another. Yet no one had succeeded to date. That suggested there was another crucial factor leading to their failure.","“What’s your plan?” Firework asked.","“Your mission is easy. On top of ensuring the successful forging of the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber, your other mission should be the establishment of the E’mei Sect. But things are a bit trickier for her.” Zu An looked at Tingxue with worried eyes.","“Isn’t her mission just to supervise the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan? That’s the easiest mission of all. I don’t see how that can be tricky.”","“There’s a huge gap in the timeline. The Yuan Mongols will only be overthrown eighty years later, but given her mortal body, she won’t survive that long in this trial world.” Zu An paused before hesitantly adding. “She needs to have a child.”","Tingxue was stunned."]},{"number":2852,"title":"Chapter 2852: Chapter 2804: A Crucial Figure","paragraphs":["Firework widened her eyes in bewilderment. She glanced at Tingxue, followed by Zu An, before finally asking, “Are you saying that because you covet her body?”","“Of course not! The Ancient Tomb Sect needs to have a successor for us to close the loop decades from now,” Zu An exclaimed indignantly. He turned to Tingxue and asked, “Do you have any siblings, or rather, do Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu have other children?”","“Not at all.” Tingue’s face darkened.","Zu An was put in a spot. They needed to have successors to ensure the plan went smoothly.","Firework laughed. “Now I know why the powerhouses who came before us failed the trial. Cooperation is tough for them, and they are too proud to leave offspring with the natives of this backward world. To make things worse, this world limits their lifespan, so there’s no way they could last eighty years.”","She turned to Tingxue and suggested, “Why don’t you get your parents to grind out a handful of siblings for you? I heard Xiaolongnu was the number one beauty of the martial world in her era. Is that Yang Guo still a man if he doesn’t make her pop out a dozen kids?”","Dark streaks appeared on Tingxue’s face. “According to my body’s memories, those two spend their days immersed in each other as if they exist in their own world. They think I’m merely an accident, a third party who disturbs their peace. They've been traveling around the world ever since I was very young.”","Zu An was speechless.","Firework said, “...No wonder my Guo Xiang couldn’t find Yang Guo.”","Zu An was worried. “I’m not sure they could have kids even if they wanted to. They should be in their fifties now.”","Those two had faced so many tribulations along the way that they were no longer young by the time they finally got together, and many years had passed since then. Even top martial artists had to obey the rules of the world.","Firework remarked with an enigmatic smile, “Since those two can’t do it, I guess you’ll have to do it with Tingxue.”","Tingxue was speechless.","Zu An huffed. “Can you stop stirring chaos at a time like this?”","Firework laughed. “Founding the E’mei Sect and becoming a nun doesn’t sound too bad now.”","Tingxue placed her hand on her sword. Firework finally changed the topic and asked, “Are there any other difficulties aside from this?”","“There is. We have to find someone called Yang Dingtian.”","“That shouldn’t be too hard if we use the Beggar Sect’s information network. How old is he? What are his unique traits?” Firework had gained a deeper insight into this world from Huang Rong in recent days.","“Let me see. I don’t think he’s been born yet.”","“Are you messing with me?”","“Of course not. He might not have much screentime, but he plays a pivotal role in the ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’-verse.” Zu An proceeded to share Yang Dingtian’s background in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’ with Firework and Tingxue.","“Can’t you just tell me everything in a single shot? You’re telling me things a droplet at a time like a leaky tap.” Firework clenched her jaws in anger.","“The worldbuilding is too deep. I only remember certain details when I encounter them,” Zu An replied with a sigh.","Tingxue, who had been quiet all this while, spoke up, “You mentioned that this world is a mix of historical events and the contents of several novels. Why don’t you tell us everything you know about this world while we’re staying here?”","She wasn’t about to blindly believe everything Zu An told her. The suggestions he had been randomly dropping were almost enough to give her a heart attack. Who knew what else he would suggest in the future?","Firework nodded in agreement. “That’s right. Tell us everything you know. We might be able to spot details you have overlooked and fill in the gaps.”","She felt nervous making that proposal. Zu An’s greatest edge over them in this trial world was the information he wielded, and that made him the most likely one to clear this trial. If he refused to divulge the information he knew, it would mean all his talk about them clearing the trial together was lip service, and he still prioritized himself above all things else. Despite having lived long enough to grow skeptical of others, she still felt nervous, as if she was afraid that she would be disappointed by his response.","Zu An answered without hesitation, “You’re right. We should brainstorm to check for gaps.”","Firework laughed. He’s looking cuter and cuter.","Zu An was oblivious to the changes in her state of mind. He shared the wuxiaverse created by Jin Yong with them, going from book to book in chronological order. He raked up details from the novels from the dredges of his mind and shared them in elaboration. His mind was much stronger than before he transmigrated, allowing him to recall most details.","Time passed swiftly.","Halfway through, Guo Fu dropped by to check on them and saw them chatting together on the bed. She was amazed by how close they were, but at the same time, she was also perplexed as Guo Xiang and Guo Polu had never been this close before. Even I’m feeling envious now.","Also, hasn’t Xiang’er been searching for Yang Guo all these years? Why is she getting close with his daughter?","The situation didn’t make sense to her.","It went without saying that the trio noticed Guo Fu’s arrival, but they were too busy brainstorming the possibilities in the plotline, so they couldn’t be bothered with her. Fortunately, Guo Fu got bored shortly after and left.","The following day, they realized that they'd fallen asleep on the same bed again, but they didn’t feel as awkward as they did on the first time. On the contrary, they were becoming used to it.","“Other than Yang Dingtian, the Ming Cult’s future Radiant Left Envoy, Yang Xiao, is also a problematic one. How did he learn Peach Blossom Island’s Divine Flick? Is he Yang Guo’s descendant?” Firework asked with a frown while tidying herself up.","“That’s unlikely. The age doesn’t match, and Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu don’t have a son. Even if...” Tingxue paused as her face reddened. “Even if I have a child, I doubt his surname will be Yang.”","Firework looked at Zu An.","Zu An replied with a frown, “That’s weird. The Yellow Dress Maiden in Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber definitely goes by the surname of Yang.”","“Then there’s no way to explain it. It’s unlikely Xiaolongnu can have more children. Could it be a child between Yang Guo and another woman? If so, who could it be?” Firework quickly racked her brains. It was unlikely to be her, since she became a nun in this world’s timeline.","A beautiful face suddenly popped into her mind, and she asked with a frown, “Could it be Guo Fu? She’s a bit younger, and she's maintained herself well. I think she can still have a child. Last night, you mentioned that Yang Guo and Guo Fu were betrothed to each other, right?”","“But Guo Fu and Yelu Qi haven't had a child even though so many years have passed.” Tingxue nonchalantly voiced her disagreement as if they weren’t talking about her father.","“Tsk. They either don’t love each other enough, or that Yelu Qi is lacking as a man. I think Guo Fu has the right figure to have a child,” Firework casually remarked.","Zu An was rendered speechless. “I doubt it. There are theories floating around, like Yelu Qi surrendering to the Mongols when Xiangyang finally fell, but Guo Fu refused to follow him and was eventually rescued by Yang Guo. But those are just guesses. I don’t think someone like Yang Guo would betray Xiaolongnu.”","“What if Xiaolongnu dies prematurely? She was inflicted with severe injuries and lethal poison several times, so her body could already be at its limit. That could be why Yang Guo abandoned his daughter in favor of taking Xiaolongnu around the world,” Firework said.","Tingxue blinked. Those words seem to make sense.","Zu An pondered the suggestion. “We’ll have to find Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu to confirm that.”","“Indeed. Yang Guo is a key character,” Firework said. “Yang Dingtian is likely related to him, possibly his illegitimate son or disciple. Also, the Huashan Sect is quite the peculiar one. You mentioned that the Sect was founded by Quanzhen Sect’s Hao Datong, but why would someone from the Quanzhen Sect be well-versed in the Jade Maiden Swordsmanship?","“And those Nine Swords of Dugu are an enigma as well. There’s no such thing in this world. Yang Guo was the only one who had any connection with Dugu Qiubai, so he might be behind the Nine Swords of Dugu.”"]},{"number":2853,"title":"Chapter 2853: Chapter 2805: Dying For Love","paragraphs":["Zu An was impressed. You can totally tell she’s a powerhouse who's lived through the ages. I did consider these issues, but I couldn’t pinpoint the heart of the problem the way she did. Yes, the main issue does lie with Yang Guo.","He asked Tingxue, “Do you have any idea where the two of them went?”","Tingxue shook her head. “I've never seen them since arriving in this world. All I know about them comes from my memories.”","Zu An was speechless. What kind of parents are those two?!","So, they turned to Huang Rong[1], hoping to tap into the Beggar Sect’s information network to find Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu.","Huang Rong was astonished. She eyed Firework with suspicion.","Zu An knew that Huang Rong must have thought that her daughter was still pining over Yang Guo, so he explained, “Tingxue has something urgent she needs to consult her parents about.”","Huang Rong chuckled. These two lovebirds must be looking for Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu to receive their approval for their relationship. This would complicate our family ties. Yang Guo can be considered a nephew to me, but now he’s going to become our in-law.","Even so, since the world was already in chaos, she couldn’t care less, and she was very satisfied with Tingxue as her daughter-in-law, too. Thus, she summoned the disciple in charge of maintaining the Beggar Sect’s information network.","Unfortunately, Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu were very elusive. The Beggar Sect could only identify a couple of places where the couple had appeared a while back.","Still, Zu An was relieved. This was better than having no clues. Considering how iconic the couple was, they'd likely be able to follow the pair's trail if they headed down in person and asked the locals. So, he bade farewell to Huang Rong.","Firework wanted to tag along, but Huang Rong stopped her and said, “Xiang’er, there are more details regarding the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan that we need to discuss.”","She was worried her daughter still hadn’t forgotten Yang Guo.","That relationship was never going to work out in the first place. What if Guo Xiang somehow wins Yang Guo over? That would be a catastrophe! The older sister marries the father, while the younger brother marries the daughter? That’s completely unacceptable!","Firework saw through Huang Rong’s thoughts. She considered outright ignoring Huang Rong, but on second thought, they needed someone to stay here to keep an eye on the progress of the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan.","On top of that, she needed to prepare for the establishment of the E’mei Sect as well. In light of all these things, she agreed to stay behind.","Before Zu An left, she secretly pulled him to one side and whispered, “Make full use of this opportunity to knock up Tingxue.”","Zu An was stunned.","Firework was irritated by Zu An’s startled expression. “Why are you acting innocent with me?”","“That’s not what I mean. Don’t you feel jealous in the slightest?”","“Don’t worry, I’m a magnanimous woman. Besides, we need her child to clear this trial. I’m sure you don’t want her to bear another man’s child, right?”","That thought pricked Zu An’s heart. Somehow, he was extremely averse to that idea.","Firework laughed at his reaction. “You two are fated to be, and Tingxue harbors goodwill toward you. It all comes down to your charisma.”","...","After leaving Xianyang, Tingxue kept looking at Zu An as if she had something to say but was hesitant. In the end, she mustered her courage and asked, “What did Firework ask you before we left Xianyang?”","Zu An smiled. “You used to not care about such matters.”","Tingxue was momentarily stunned before she slowly nodded. “You’re right. I have gotten emotional since coming to this world.”","“You're a human at the end of the day. The path of Nebula demands you to abandon all feelings, but that goes against nature’s will. Why don’t you take this opportunity to relinquish it now?”","“I don’t know why I chose this path back then, but there must be a reason behind that.” Tingxue wasn’t distracted by his abrupt question. “You haven’t answered me yet.”","“Promise me you won’t get angry.”","“Why would I be angry? I forgot anger before coming to this trial world.”","“She told me to take this chance to knock you up.”","“!!!”","“You promised me you won’t get angry! Aiya, stop hitting me!”","...","Despite the trail of clues provided by the Beggar Sect, Zu An and Tingxue struggled to gather information about Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu. Nevertheless, they could tell that the two lovebirds had only stayed at each area briefly, and their traveling became increasingly rushed.","In the end, the trail of clues ended at a town.","Zu An and Tingxue had to take out a map to discuss their next step.","While studying the routes, Tingxue suddenly exclaimed, “Doesn’t it look like they’re heading toward Mount Zhongnan’s Ancient Tomb Sect?”","Zu An’s eyes lit up. It did look as if Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu were heading for the Ancient Tomb Sect. “Perhaps they got tired of traveling, so they decided to return and look for you.”","“That’s not how they were in my memories. I have a bad feeling about this. Let’s quickly return to the Ancient Tomb Sect to take a look.”","“All right.” Zu An reined in his smile. He also felt unnerved by Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu’s rushed travel—it felt like an ominous premonition.","So, the two of them traveled day and night in a hurry, but it still took them half a month to arrive at the Ancient Tomb Sect.","To their disappointment, there was no one there.","“No, someone has been here.” Tingxue sensed an anomaly. She made her way to her room and found a letter there. She tore it apart, and her expression darkened.","“What’s wrong?” Zu An asked, feeling concerned.","Tingxue handed the letter to him. Zu An took a look and his heart sank.","It was Yang Guo’s will.","It turned out that Xiaolongnu’s body had taken a toll from all the lethal poisons she had been inflicted with, and it didn’t help that her foundation was already impaired due to her cultivating on the Cold Jade Bed at a young age. She could initially shrug it off due to her strong inner energy, but as soon as she gave birth, her condition had dropped off a cliff.","Yang Guo had been taking her around the world to search for medicine to treat her and to find warm places for her to recuperate. Unfortunately, he couldn’t stop the inevitable. Judging from the rapid deterioration of her condition, Xiaolongnu knew that her days were numbered, so she'd wanted to return to her roots. Her ancestor grandmother, master, and the others were all resting in the ancient tomb too.","Yang Guo had pushed down his sorrow and hurriedly took her back to the ancient tomb.","Xiaolongnu had gritted her teeth and held on, but to her regret, she failed to see Tingxue when she returned. With her wish of returning to the ancient tomb fulfilled, she breathed her last.","Yang Guo had succumbed to his pain and ended his life in the same coffin as his wife. Before he died, he left a will expressing his apology to Tingxue. At the same time, he left behind his martial arts insights in recent years, hoping that Tingxue could learn them and protect herself.","Zu An and Tingxue rushed to the coffin room. Only when they saw the lovebirds, who continued to embrace each other even upon death, did it register to them that this was all real.","Zu An felt as if his head had been struck by a hammer. What’s going on? Why did they die? What’s going to happen to the plotline now? Are our theories all wrong? Or have other universal deities tampered with the trial so much so that it’s no longer possible to clear it?","Tingxue was stunned. Despite only being their daughter in name in this trial world, she couldn’t stop sorrow from engulfing her. Two streams of tears flowed from her eyes.","So, this is what sorrow feels like.","She was so shaken up that she spurted blood and fainted.","1. The ex-leader of the Beggar Sect. ☜"]},{"number":2854,"title":"Chapter 2854: Chapter 2806: The Nine Swords of Dugu and the Nine Heavens Palm","paragraphs":["Alarmed, Zu An rushed forward to support her. Her hands were icy cold.","He immediately realized this was the backlash from cultivating the Ancient Tomb Sect’s Jade Maiden Heart Sutra. The Ancient Tomb Sect had a unique cultivation skill, but it came with a huge downside—the practitioner couldn’t feel extreme bouts of emotions. Otherwise, they risked cultivation deviation.","Zu An quickly supported Tingxue back to her room and channeled his inner energy to heal her.","Moments later, Tingxue regained consciousness. “Thank you.”","“There’s no need for thanks between us.”","Tingxue flashed him a faint smile before her eyelids drooped. “They might not be my real parents, but I couldn’t hold back my sorrow after witnessing their death.”","“Unlike plants, we’re born with hearts,” Zu An said wistfully. “Anyone would be shaken when witnessing a love that transcends even death.”","Tingxue looked dazed. “I may have been alone all this time, but I have never felt lonely. But now that they are dead, I don’t have anyone else in this world.”","“What do you mean by that? You still have friends like me, Firework, and Isabella,” Zu An hurriedly interjected.","Tingxue sighed. “I’d already be thankful if Firework didn’t provoke me.”","Zu An suddenly felt uncomfortable as he remembered what Firework had told him before they left Xianyang. He quickly changed the topic and said, “This will be tricky. Their deaths prove that our previous guesses are off.”","Most of their plans had been banking on Yang Guo. His death meant that there was no way for them to accomplish those plans anymore.","“That’s not necessarily so.” Tingxue picked up Yang Guo’s will. “Look at this...”","Zu An was so shaken up by Yang Guo’s death that he hadn’t read the latter half of the letter, which contained the martial arts Yang Guo left for his daughter. Other than the Ancient Tomb Sect’s martial arts, there were also the Nine Yin Manual, the Toad Skill, and most important of all, the Melancholic Palm.","Yang Guo was well aware that his Melancholic Palm was a unique martial art built on his yearning for his wife, so there was no way for him to impart it to others. Thus, he sought to create a new set of martial arts.","He was a unique individual who had inherited the skills of the Five Greats and grasped Dugu Qiubai and the Ancient Tomb Sect’s essences. His understanding of martial arts far surpassed that of any of the other Five Greats.","He'd thus put together the strengths of different experts to create a sword skill and a palm skill. He then named the sword skill the ‘Nine Swords of Dugu’ because the greatest influence behind the sword skill was Dugu Qiubai, and he didn’t want his invincible predecessor buried deep in the mountains to remain unknown. As for the palm strike, he'd named it the ‘Nine Heavens Palm’.","Unfortunately, due to Xiaolongnu’s abrupt death, he hadn’t completed the sword skill and the palm skill. However, he had completed a finger skill.","The finger skill had been inspired by Reverend Yideng’s Yiyang Finger, but Yang Guo had tapped into the unique traits of the Nine Yin Manual and the Ancient Tomb Sect’s soft inner energy to create the ‘Yiyin Finger’. It was nowhere as profound as the Nine Swords of Dugu and Nine Heavens Palm, but it would be enough for his daughter to protect herself.","Zu An was shocked beyond words. He absolutely hadn’t expected Yang Guo to be the creator of these martial arts. He'd thought it was a coincidence at first, but everything made sense. There had been much discussion about the origins of these martial arts, but indeed, Yang Guo was the most likely person to have created them.","That explained how Yang Dingtian had become unrivaled in the martial world, pummeling the Three Elders of Shaolin Temple until they didn’t dare to leave, even though his inner energy was only strong enough to grasp the fourth layer of the Great Cosmic Shift.","It was because the Nine Heavens Palm had the same origin as the Nine Swords of Dugu. It wasn’t reliant on one’s inner energy.","Tingxue spoke up. “There’s still a problem. These martial arts should have appeared in the future, but Yang Guo passed away before he could complete them. We’ll have to find a way around that.”","Zu An burst into laughter. “That isn’t a problem. Yes, Yang Guo might be the only one in this world who could have created these martial arts, but neither you nor I are from this world. How can we be stumped by something like this?”","Tingxue thought that made sense. With their vast knowledge, they could fill up the missing bits in the martial arts, and the final products would be more potent than what Yang Guo could have ever created.","“We can also easily circumvent Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu’s deaths—we just have to create another Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu.” Zu An’s eyes gleamed brightly as he thought of another plan.","“How do we do that?” Tingxue was confused.","“The Condor Hero was traveling around the world with a mask on, so most people don’t know what he looks like. All I have to do is to put on the same mask. You greatly resemble Xiaolongnu, so it shouldn’t be tough for you to impersonate her,” Zu An said as he dug out Yang Guo’s mask.","Tingxue blinked. He wants to be my father, and I have to play my mother? “This feels weird. Do we have to do this?”","“We have to. We transmigrated into this world assuming the identities of people who exist here. But there was next to no information about Guo Polu even in the original plotline. He vanished after Xianyang collapsed, with rumors that he had died in battle. It’d break the plotline if I continued my activities as Guo Polu, and that could lead to us failing the trial.","“It’s the same for you, too. We’re the only ones who know about Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu’s deaths. This is the perfect situation for us to assume their identities,” Zu An replied.","“All right.” Tingxue didn’t oppose this course of action.","The two of them began studying the incomplete Nine Swords of Dugu and Nine Heavens Palm. They had to concede that Yang Guo was extraordinarily talented to have created such profound martial arts in this world. These two martial arts had already surpassed this world’s ceiling.","It was fortunate that Zu An and Tingxue were experts from the Myriad Worlds, and they were both adept in swordsmanship. After days of studying, they eventually completed the Nine Swords of Dugu.","Tingxue remarked, “If someone intelligent learns this swordsmanship, they can exert formidable prowess even if they lack inner energy.”","Zu An was also satisfied with their work. However, he said, “The Nine Heavens Palm is slightly lacking. We specialize in swordsmanship, after all. If Firework were here, she could have done more with it.”","“You miss her?”","Zu An was startled by that question. He couldn’t believe such words could have come from that icy beauty.","Tingxue’s face reddened. She quickly changed the subject. “Don’t worry, the Nine Heavens Palm is only slightly inferior to the Nine Swords of Dugu. It’s more than enough for one to reign supreme in the martial world.”","Zu An agreed with her judgment. Unlike the more influential Nine Swords of Dugu, the only person known to wield the Nine Heavens Palm was Yang Dingtian. There was no need for them to fuss too much over it.","Zu An’s ears suddenly twitched. “Hm? I hear fighting sounds coming from the Quanzhen Sect. That’s weird.”","“Let’s take a look.”","The two of them snuck out of the ancient tomb and soon discovered members of the Quanzhen Sect pursuing fifteen daoists who were dressed in Quanzhen uniforms.","Is it infighting?","The ones being chased were at a huge numerical disadvantage. They would have been dead by now if not for a youth, who looked to be in his twenties, protecting them with his outstanding martial arts.","“Zhang Baojun, this is our Quanzhen Sect’s internal affair. Are you sure you want to get involved?” one of the pursuers roared in anger.","The youth calmly replied, “I’m only here to aid a friend. Not all Quanzhen disciples wish to pledge allegiance to the Mongols. You don’t need to go this far.”","Zu An was surprised. This youth is a future legend of the martial world—Zhang Sanfeng [1] !","1. In real life, Zhang Sanfeng is known as a legendary daoist credited with creating Tai Chi. In Jin Yong’s wuxiaverse, he appears in Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber as a head of the Wudang Sect. ☜"]},{"number":2855,"title":"Chapter 2855: Chapter 2807: The Plan to Close the World’s Loop","paragraphs":["“We’re merely following fate. It’s foolish to stand against the tides of change.” The pursuing Quanzhen disciples had no plans on continuing the debate and soon continued their assault.","Zhang Baojun had yet to master his martial arts and struggled to simultaneously deal with multiple opponents. Just as they were about to be captured, several rocks suddenly flew out and struck the Quanzhen disciples’ weapons.","The Quanzhen disciples were stunned. Who is capable of using such small pebbles to knock away all our weapons from a far distance? Is it East Heretic Huang Yaoshi?","Two figures stepped out. The man wore a withered mask, whereas the woman looked pure and ravishing.","“Yang Guo, Xiaolongnu...” Some Quanzhen disciples had met Xiaolongnu back then and recognized her at a glance. They were perplexed how she hadn’t aged despite years passing, but it was normal for fairies to remain perpetually youthful.","Zhang Baojun exclaimed, “Big brother Yang!”","He'd received pointers from Yang Guo back then and benefited greatly from it.","Zu An nodded. It’s a good thing I have the mask with me. As long as I hide an arm, it shouldn’t be too difficult for me to impersonate Yang Guo [1] .","“Quanzhen’s values have regressed so much that its disciples are ganging up on others now. Scram now before I change my mind!” Zu An growled with an intentionally deeper voice. His imitation of Yang Guo wasn't necessarily accurate, but most people wouldn’t know better, except for a small handful of people who knew him well.","Relieved, the Quanzhen disciples immediately turned tail and fled. The Condor Hero’s reputation had grown resounding over the years, not to mention that the Quanzhen disciples had witnessed his prowess in person during the battle at Chongyang Palace then.","Zhang Baojun and his friends from the Quanzhen Sect stepped forward and thanked Zu An for saving their lives. Zu An traded some pleasantries with them while asking about the situation.","It turned out that the Quanzhen Sect’s defection to the Mongols had been extremely controversial within the sect. Most disciples were averse to siding with the Mongols, though they were also worried that rejecting the Mongols would bring a crisis upon them.","This move had prompted the remaining Quanzhen Seven Masters to leave and establish their own sects. For instance, Hao Datong’s line founded the Huashan Sect, while Sun Bu’er founded the Tranquil Sect.","The current Quanzhen Sect was run by the third-generation disciples. There were many hot-blooded ones among the young disciples who didn’t want to serve the Mongols and wanted to break free of the Quanzhen Sect as well.","Naturally, the Quanzhen Sect’s leadership wouldn’t permit such movements. They didn't have the influence and the power to stop the Quanzhen Seven Masters, but they could definitely curb the younger disciples.","As a result, an internal conflict had broken out in the Quanzhen Sect.","It was also then that Zhang Baojun had received a request from his friends to help them leave the Quanzhen Sect. Unfortunately, the Quanzhen Sect’s leadership caught wind of their plans and sent people after them.","No wonder they say the Wudang Sect was an offshoot of the Quanzhen Sect. Zu An uttered some words of motivation before asking, “What are your plans?”","Zhang Baojun looked confused. “I don’t know, but surely there must be a place for us in this huge world.”","Zu An smiled. “Why don’t you go to Mount Wudang?”","Zhang Baojun blinked before replying heartily, “All right.”","Zu An imparted the Quanzhen Sect’s swordsmanship and inner energy methods to them, so they could preserve their roots. That would serve as the Wudang Sect’s foundation for their rise in prominence in the future.","The young disciples were extremely grateful to Zu An. Most of the Quanzhen Sect’s martial arts had become incomplete by their generation, and it didn’t help that their leadership were hoarding the key martial arts. As a result, they had hardly learned any of the Quanzhen Sect’s martial arts.","Zu An pulled Zhang Baojun aside for a private conversation. “I have a portion of Wang Chongyang’s Innate Energy Art, which is highly compatible with you. Do you want to learn it?”","Wang Chongyang had inscribed not just the Nine Yin Manual, but also a portion of his Innate Energy Art in the ancient tomb.","Zhang Baojun was more than happy to learn the martial art of someone who had been the world’s strongest martial artist, but he was also concerned that it was unethical to secretly learn another sect’s martial art.","Zu An reassured him with a smile, “Rest assured. Given its current state, Wang Chongyang wouldn’t want his martial art to be passed down within the Quanzhen Sect. He would be happier if you could bring glory to his martial art. However, there’s a flaw in the technique. You’ll have to remain chaste for your life. You won’t be able to have a wife or children.”","Wang Chongyang hadn't gotten together with Lin Chaoying[2] not just because of their pride, but also because of his Innate Energy Art.","South Emperor Duan Zhixing of the Five Greats had once had many concubines in his imperial harem, but it was because he'd begun practicing this skill that he began to distance himself from women. That led to Ying Gu cheating on him and him becoming a monk.","Zhang Baojun was stunned to hear those words. A beautiful woman flashed across his mind. But Heroine Guo only fancies big brother Yang. She wouldn’t care about someone like me. So, he replied, “My heart is fully committed to the dao. I don’t plan to marry or have children.”","Whether in real history or Jin Yong’s wuxiaverse, Zhang Sanfeng had remained chaste his entire life. So, Zu An imparted the Innate Energy Art’s sutra to him.","Zu An didn’t complete the Innate Energy Art for Zhang Baojun, knowing that the latter could comprehend something deeper from it. The inspiration from that would spur him to create even more martial arts.","Zhang Baojun quickly memorized the sutra. While feeling thankful to Zu An, he couldn’t help but ask, “Big brother Yang, second miss Guo has been looking for you all these years.”","He'd met Guo Xiang more than a decade ago in the Shaolin Temple, when she was still traveling around in search of Yang Guo. It was then that she'd given him an arhat doll. While he had learned some Shaolin martial arts from the arhat doll, it was her radiant smile that was imprinted in his mind.","“I know.” Zu An looked at Zhang Baojun and sighed.","In the original story, Guo Xiang had conceded defeat to Xiaolongnu. She'd lamented not having met Yang Guo earlier, or else she could have protected him as a sugar mommy[3], and that could have led to them getting together instead.","But in truth, Guo Xiang had met another ‘Yang Guo’, but failed to realize it and lost her opportunity to be a sugar mommy.","Zhang Baojun glanced at the gorgeous Tingxue and thought Yang Guo’s decision was understandable. Once again, he thanked Zu An before setting off to Mount Wudang with his Quanzhen friends.","The current him probably couldn’t have imagined that he would build on the Innate Energy Art and Nine Yin Manual to create the Pure Yang Infinite Art and become a true grandmaster.","“Why do you treat him so well?” Tingxue asked after Zhang Baojun and the others left.","Zu An replied, “There’s an eighty-year gap between the end of ‘Return of the Condor Heroes’ and ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’. In this period, the old Five Greats passed away one after another, and the Mongols took over the world. The martial world inevitably descended into chaos.","“There’s a famous saying in the future that Zhang Sanfeng devoted sixty years of his life to quelling demons. Naturally, we can’t let him remain weak.”","He had already deciphered the crux of this trial. The world was incomplete, and his job was to pick up the missing pieces, stitch them together, and ensure this world’s trajectory proceeded in the direction that was intended.","No matter how intelligent or powerful the previous challengers were, there was no way they could have accomplished this feat without knowing about the trial world’s background.","—","Brief History of Wang Chongyang and Lin Chaoying","Both are characters who died before Return of the Condor Heroes.","The two of them were martial arts prodigies who were in love with each other, but they were rivals as well, and refused to get together because of their immense pride.","Lin Chaoying thought Wang Chongyang scorned her, so she created the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra to counter the Quanzhen Sect’s moves.","When Lin Chaoying died, Wang Chongyang paid her a visit in the ancient tomb and was shocked to see the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra inscribed on the wall. He tried to devise a counter against the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra but was unable to do so, forcing him to acknowledge Lin Chaoying’s talents.","Later, Wang Chongyang came into possession of the Nine Yin Manual and realized it was highly compatible with the Quanzhen Sect’s skills. He finally came up with a counter against the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra, so he returned to the ancient tomb and inscribed his solution against it (which contains bits of the Nine Yin Manual and the Innate Energy Art).","1. Yang Guo only has one arm. His other arm was chopped off by Guo Fu. ☜","2. She’s the founder of the Ancient Tomb Sect. ☜","3. Xiaolongnu was responsible for training Yang Guo when he was weak, and could be considered responsible for his success, hence ‘sugar mommy’. ☜"]},{"number":2856,"title":"Chapter 2856: Chapter 2808: Xianyang Collapses","paragraphs":["Tingxue nodded, though it was unclear if she understood what Zu An was getting at. “Where should we head next?”","She wasn't fond of thinking too much into things—Nebula worshipers were emotionless machines in the first place. She liked how she didn’t have to speculate too deeply when with him.","“Mount Hua!”","Mount Hua wasn't too far away from Mount Zhongnan. It only took them three days to arrive there.","Looking at Mount Hua’s treacherous cliffs, which looked as if someone had hacked cleanly through them, Tingxue remarked, “It is a little short, but there are few mountains as steep as this in the Myriad Worlds.”","Zu An chuckled. The mountains in this world were short compared to those in the Myriad Worlds, which easily reached tens of kilometers tall. This was a world where supernatural powers were forbidden, after all. It would be hard for such tall mountains to grow without the nourishment of ki or spirit energy.","The two of them made their way up Mount Hua. Unlike the modern-day mountain, which had paved routes, the trial world’s version was dangerous to climb. It was fortunate that Zu An and Tingxue were strong enough to overcome most obstacles, so it didn’t take them long to reach the top of Mount Hua, where the Huashan Sect was located.","The current era’s Huashan Sect was still shabby. Hao Datong had long passed away, and there were only young disciples left in the sect.","When they saw Zu An and Tingxue, these young disciples put up their guard, having deduced that they were Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu from the duo’s appearances. Clearly, they knew about Hao Datong accidentally hurting Grandma Sun[1], which resulted in the latter’s death.","They thought Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu had come to the Huashan Sect to exact vengeance for Grandma Sun.","But that wasn't Zu An’s intention.","He explained that he hadn’t come to exact vengeance. Rather, he had great respect for Wang Chongyang and didn’t want his martial arts to disappear with time, so he'd journeyed to Mount Hua to offer them some martial art manuals.","The Condor Hero had built up a good reputation over the years, and Zu An told them about Zhang Baojun rescuing a line of Quanzhen disciples as well. These details helped to dispel the Huashan disciples’ doubts, and they welcomed the pair as honored guests.","Zu An soon learned that the Huashan Sect had already developed the Purple Haze Divine Skill.","It turned out that Hao Datong had felt helpless after encountering so many top-notch experts. While the Quanzhen Sect’s inner energy method was calm and righteous, it lacked power. Thus, he put his heart into developing a new inner energy method to amplify the power of Quanzhen inner energy.","However, the Purple Haze Divine Skill had side effects. Those who overexerted themselves in the long run would find their skin turning purple.","The Quanzhen Seven Masters are still quite capable. Each of them found their own path and developed unique martial arts. Their martial arts might not be top-notch, but they're easily high-grade.","Since the Huashan Sect’s inner energy problem had been resolved, Zu An imparted to them the Quanzhen Sect’s swordsmanship, whereas Tingxue imparted to them the Ancient Tomb Sect’s Jade Maiden Swordsmanship.","The future Huashan Sect did have the Jade Maiden Swordsmanship and the Virtuous Lady Swordsmanship, after all. Zu An was certain that those had been passed down from the Ancient Tomb Sect.","That day, the Huashan disciples witnessed a white-robed fairy executing indescribably beautiful swordplay. That was a sight they would never forget in their lives. They unanimously agreed to name the Huashan Sect’s main peak Jade Maiden Peak.","After they passed down their respective sword skills to the Huashan disciples, Zu An asked if they had a disciple named Feng Qingyang[2], but unfortunately, everyone shook their heads.","Zu An figured that Feng Qingyang hadn't been born yet. I might have to return to Mount Hua again decades from now.","The two of them bade the Huashan disciples farewell and began wandering Mount Hua.","While walking past a cliff, Tingxue suddenly exclaimed. She walked up to a boulder and saw the words ‘Cliff of Remembrance’ inscribed on it. “This handwriting looks familiar.”","Zu An inspected the handwriting and said, “It’s likely from Guo Xiang. She traveled the world searching for Yang Guo. She might have heard about Yang Guo witnessing the showdown between Hong Qigong and Ouyang Feng on Mount Hua’s peak, so she came here to try her luck. She didn’t find Yang Guo here, so while watching the scenery in a daze, she suddenly felt sentimental and left these words behind.”","Tingxue sighed. “Miss Guo is truly a sentimental woman. Yang Guo is a heartless man.”","Zu An laughed. “Is it fine for you to speak about your father like that? He would have been cheating on your mother if he'd accepted Guo Xiang.”","Tingxue rolled her eyes. “You know they aren’t my parents.”","“Your expressions are more animated than before. You look better now.”","“...Where do we go next?”","“We’ll head to the imperial palace. We have to find a eunuch.”","“???”","“It’s about time to create the Sunflower Manual. That skill should be inspired by the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra as well. We have to close that loop as well.”","“Is it that demonic skill that requires practitioners to castrate themselves?” Tingxue frowned. “How did the Ancient Tomb Sect’s martial arts get distorted like that?”","“The Ancient Tomb Sect’s martial arts are unorthodox. Practitioners of the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra are vulnerable to cultivation deviation, especially if they didn’t have a mentor to guide them. Those who obtain an incomplete copy are prone to be misled,” Zu An replied with a smile.","“Practicing the Innate Energy Art requires one to consume all kinds of pills, which may lead to unbearable heat building up within one's body. Similarly, cultivating the Jade Maiden Heart Sutra can easily stoke one’s lust. If the Sunflower Manual originates from those two, it’s not that surprising that it demands its practitioners to castrate themselves. Let’s look into it on the way.”","“Alright...”","So, Zu An and Tingxue traveled during the day and discussed the creation of the Sunflower Manual in the inns at night. Neither of them had ever learned such a bizarre skill, so it wasn't as easy for them to create it.","At the start, the two of them still stayed in separate rooms, but they often stayed up late to discuss the details of their plans, so they eventually just booked a single room and slept on the same bed when they were exhausted. They'd already shared a bed in Xianyang anyway.","Of course, the two of them slept with their clothes on.","Some time later, they arrived at Lin’an. When they saw how the capital was still merry despite the ongoing war, the two of them sighed. This explained why the Song Dynasty was ailing.","That said, neither of them was in the mood to worry about the country. They slipped into the imperial palace and looked around, but they couldn’t find a suitable eunuch.","Later, it struck Zu An that even the humblest eunuch would have become a master after decades of training, and such a character would have undoubtedly left his mark in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’. That didn’t check out.","Most likely, he would have to find a suitable successor for the Sunflower Manual later on, similar to the case of the Nine Swords of Dugu.[3]","Just then, they heard news on the street, saying that the Mongols had encircled Xianyang, and the reinforcements dispatched by the imperial court had been crushed. Xianyang was on the verge of collapse.","Without hesitation, Zu An and Tingxue hurried back to Xianyang. But by the time they returned, the place had already collapsed.","Guo Jing and Huang Rong had realized that there was no way to turn the tables anymore, so they urged Lu Wenhuan, the general guarding Xianyang, to surrender to the Mongols and open the city gates in exchange for the people’s safety.","Then, they'd ended their lives because they didn’t want to bow to the Mongols. The Guo manor was set ablaze.","This was aligned with the world’s intended trajectory. Zu An had planned it with Firework beforehand—she would leave with the Heavenly Sword ahead of time, while the Dragon Slaying Saber would fall into the hands of the masses and be fought over by different factions.","In addition, Guo Polu also vanished after the battle in Xianyang, with rumors that he had died fighting against the Mongols.","These things were all planned out beforehand, but Zu An still felt melancholic witnessing it in person. Huang Rong and Guo Jing must have been disappointed that I didn’t return...","Just then, there was a ruckus in the city. A lady carrying something in her arms was being chased by the Mongols. A few members of the Beggar Sect fought to their dying breath to escort her out of Xianyang, but it didn’t take long before they were massacred by the Mongol soldiers.","The Mongols slowly approached the lady, their faces twisted into perverse smiles. What a gorgeous lady. We've struck gold this time!","The lady was Guo Fu, and the item she was carrying was the Dragon Slaying Saber!","1. Grandma Sun took care of Xiaolongnu while she was growing up. ☜","2. Feng Qingyang appeared in ‘The Smiling, Proud Wanderer’ as a swordmaster wielding the Nine Swords of Dugu. ☜","3. In Jin Yong’s wuxiaverse, the Sunflower Manual was created by a eunuch. To close that loop, Zu An is seeking to create a Sunflower Manual and pass it on to the eunuch. But if he passed on the Sunflower Manual now, the eunuch would have become an expert by the start of ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’ and would have played a huge role in that story. ☜"]},{"number":2857,"title":"Chapter 2857: Chapter 2809: You’re Going to Use Her To Give Birth?","paragraphs":["Zu An was taken aback. Why is the Dragon Slaying Saber in her hands?","But he had no time to think deeper into it. Guo Fu was already surrounded by the Mongol soldiers. To avoid being humiliated, she raised her dagger and thrust it toward her chest.","Zu An hurriedly flicked his finger to knock away her dagger.","Guo Fu turned around and saw the iconic masked man with a single arm. For a brief moment, she was stunned. “Big brother Yang...”","Zu An had made sure to disguise himself to avoid others from recognizing him as Guo Polu, but he hadn’t expected even Guo Fu to fail to recognize him.","The Mongol soldiers were infuriated at someone getting in their way, but their eyes lit up in delight when they noticed Tingxue. What amazing luck we have today! First that beautiful lady, and now another gorgeous babe!","Some Mongol soldiers cheered. They rushed at Tingxue, fearing that their peers would get to her before them.","Tingxue’s face turned cold. She drew her sword and slew her way through the soldiers.","Zu An made his way to Guo Fu’s side and asked, “Are you all right?”","“Big brother Yang!” Guo Fu stared at him in a daze. All her grievances and fear she had suppressed in recent days gushed up in her heart, and tears began streaming down her cheeks. She lunged into his embrace and started crying.","Yang Guo had already saved her and Yelu Qi once in the great battle of Xianyang back then. She hadn’t expected to bump into him again now that Xianyang had been breached, and she was cornered.","She thought about how she had wrongly placed her trust in Yelu Qi, and complicated emotions swirled in her mind. Why did I treat him like that in the past? Things could have been different otherwise.","Zu An was speechless.","Even Tingxue also looked over, intrigued by the situation on their side.","Zu An shrugged. He was confused as well.","Tingxue’s expression became increasingly colder as her blows grew sharper. It didn’t take her long to massacre the soldiers around her and return to their side.","“Miss... Long...” Guo Fu looked awkward. It suddenly struck her how inappropriate it was for her to be hugging Yang Guo in front of Xiaolongnu. “Miss Long, why do you look so young... Tingxue?”","Zu An gently tapped Guo Fu’s neck, and the latter fainted. “We can’t reveal our identities here. Let’s take her away with us first.”","More Mongol soldiers were rushing over after hearing the news, and there was no lack of experts among them. Even with their current level of martial arts, it would be disastrous if Yang Guo and Tingxue would be encircled by them.","Tingxue nodded. She glanced at the Dragon Slaying Saber and asked, “What about that?”","Zu An grabbed the Dragon Slaying Saber and flitted some distance across the city before casually tossing it into a hut to hide it. According to the world’s trajectory, the Dragon Slaying Saber fell into enemy hands.","He couldn’t simply hand it over, as the Mongols would have suspected that something was wrong with it. It would be more believable if they searched the city and chanced upon it.","During the chaos, the two took Guo Fu out of Xianyang and temporarily settled down in a cavern in the mountains.","Tingxue eyed Zu An. “How do you intend to deal with her?”","“We need to figure out what happened to her first.” Zu An recalled how she was carrying the Dragon Slaying Saber earlier. Something must have happened.","“But she already recognized me. She might figure out your identity from that.” Tingxue was worried. According to their plan, Guo Polu should have died when Xianyang was breached, as there was no other record of him in history. If Guo Fu recognized him, it could lead to unexpected complications.","“That’s simple.”","Zu An released Guo Fu’s acupoint, causing the latter to slowly regain consciousness. When she met Zu An’s gaze, he quickly used the Nine Yin Sutra’s Soul Transference Method.","Guo Fu looked completely dazed, but her eyes swiftly regained their clarity. By then, she was already convinced that the duo before her were Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu.","Zu An asked, “What happened? Why were you fleeing with the Dragon Slaying Saber? Where’s Yelu Qi?”","Guo Fu shouldn’t have known about the Heavenly Saber and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan.","Guo Fu’s eyes reddened. “Big brother Yang, I have severed ties with that fellow. He... He defected to the Mongols!”","Zu An and Tingxue exchanged looks, though they weren’t surprised. They had anticipated such a possibility.","Guo Fu continued with tears flowing down her cheeks. “I recently learned that he had been leaking information from Xianyang to the Mongols. If not for him, Xianyang wouldn’t have been breached so quickly.”","“He would have been of considerable status even if he had joined the Mongols. The two of you have been on good terms all these years. How did you end up like that?” Zu An was perplexed.","He wasn't surprised that Yelu Qi had defected to the Mongols. He was surprised that the latter hadn’t taken Guo Fu with him, though.","“He wanted to take me with him, but how could I be with a traitor? Our parents guarded Xianyang for many years!” Guo Fu spat hatefully.","Zu An was surprised. He'd always thought Guo Fu was a bumpkin who only cared about herself, but who could have thought she had such spirit in her?","“Did he cause your parents’ death?”","Guo Fu shook her head. “He didn’t. He used another name, Yelu Zhu, when dealing with the Mongols to avoid staining my parents’ reputation, especially since he’s the leader of the Beggar Sect. He even tried persuading my parents to surrender, promising to ensure their safety. But my parents refused to join the Mongols and chose to end their lives instead.”","“When I learned that he was planning to hand the Dragon Slaying Saber, which my parents and grandfather painstakingly crafted, to the Mongols, I immediately stole and escaped with it. However, the Mongols quickly noticed it and pursued me. That’s when you appeared and saved me.”","Zu An was stunned. It was recorded in history that Yelu Zhu was Yelu Chucai’s oldest son, but who could have known that Yelu Qi was actually Yelu Zhu?","Yelu Qi did have a conscience after all. He and his father were Mongol officials, so it wasn’t surprising for them to support their homeland. Guo Jing and Huang Rong had already guessed as much, or else they wouldn’t have excluded Yelu Qi and Guo Fu from the Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber Plan.","But news would still have eventually gotten out.","There had to be people in the Beggar Sect who knew about Yelu Qi’s betrayal. In the first place, Yelu Qi was a distinguished young master, whose disposition was at odds with the Beggar Sect. This could be where the conflict between the Beggar Sect’s Clean Clothes Faction and Dirty Clothes Faction started from...","“Speaking of which, where is the Dragon Slaying Saber?” Guo Fu suddenly recalled this matter and searched the area.","Zu An explained, “There were Mongol soldiers all around Xianyang. We had to fend them off while retreating; there was no way we could have carried such a heavy saber with us then. So, we hid it in one of the residences.”","Guo Fu sighed. “Big brother Yang, you should have left me there and taken the saber instead.”","Zu An was surprised. This was unlike Guo Fu’s personality. But on second thought, she had gone through a lot within such a short time—her parents’ deaths, her siblings’ disappearance, and her husband defecting to the enemy side. It was normal for her to seek death.","Knowing that, Zu An dared not leave her alone here. “What do you plan to do from now on?”","“I don’t know.”","“You can travel with us in the meantime.”","...","The group made their way to E’mei Mountain.","Firework was initially delighted to see them, but upon seeing Guo Fu, she looked at Zu An with a perplexed gaze. “So, you've made up your mind to have her bear your child?”","Zu An was stunned."]},{"number":2858,"title":"Chapter 2858: Chapter 2810: Firework’s Plan","paragraphs":["“What nonsense are you spouting?” Zu An was dumbfounded.","Firework tilted her head in confusion. “Why else did you bring her here? She’s completely useless except for her beauty... though I have to say, even though she’s no longer a young lady, she is still ravishing. She fully inherited her mother’s beauty. Is that why you saved her?”","Zu An huffed. “She’s our big sister in this world. Am I to turn a blind eye to her plight?”","“But rescuing her complicates things. What do you intend to do with her? And how are you going to explain your identity to her?” Firework frowned. It would be inconvenient for them to discuss matters if they had to constantly bring an outsider with them.","“I’ll bring her around for now, lest she suddenly decides to end her life. You don’t have to worry about my identity. I used the Soul Transference Method to implant a belief that we're Yang Guo and Xiaolongnu in her,” Zu An explained.","Firework looked at him with a crooked smile. “You aren’t planning to take responsibility for her?”","Zu An was speechless.","Firework eventually said, “Fine. You can keep her for the time being.”","“How are preparations going on your side?” Zu An asked.","“I’m almost done. I’m ready to establish the E’mei Sect whenever required. I've also created the E’mei Sect’s martial arts.” Firework remarked with a sigh, “Guo Xiang is such a sentimental woman. It feels like every bit of the E’mei Sect has Yang Guo’s shadow in it.”","Be it the Spirit Fox of the Black Marsh or Guo Xiang’s future disciple, Abbess Fengling, they were all named after Guo Xiang’s experiences with Yang Guo back then.","With this thought in mind, she glared at Zu An and snorted, “That Yang fellow is too much. He wouldn’t have let down so many women if he was a philanderer like you!”","Zu An was speechless. Actually, I respect Yang Guo’s devotion to Xiaolongnu, although it is also true that he held up the lives of many women. But then again, it is this feeling of regret that makes the characters memorable to the readers.","“What’s the situation with Zhu Ziliu, Dawu, and Xiaowu?”","“Zhu Ziliu and Xiaowu traveled to the Western Regions and established the Red Plum Blossom Mansion there,” Firework replied. “But Dawu’s wife is Yelu Yan, and the Yelu Clan refuses to leave the Central Plains. It’s for the same reason I couldn’t send Guo Fu off ahead of time, either.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. Everything was going according to plan. They weren’t worried about Dawu and the Yelu Clan’s fate, since this was only a trial world.","Firework suddenly nudged Zu An and asked, “How are things on your side?”","“I've settled Wudang and Huashan. As for the Nine Swords of Dugu and Sunflower Manual, I might have to wait a few more decades before passing them down...”","“That’s not what I’m asking. How are things between you and Tingxue? Is she pregnant yet?”","Zu An’s face reddened. “You’re thinking too much.”","Firework’s face grew stern. “Stop being so wishy-washy. This concerns whether we clear the trial or not. Settle it as soon as possible.”","Zu An was stunned.","In the days to come, the three of them kept an eye on the movements across the world.","Great Song lost its momentum after Xianyang was breached. The Mongols traveled down the river and defeated Southern Song’s final stronghold at Dingjiazhou. After that, they marched straight toward Lin’an, easily crushing everything along the way.","Southern Song’s empress dowager led the majority of the officials to surrender to the Mongols. Some loyal officials tried to escape with the little emperor, but they were wiped out in the Battle of Yamen. An official named Lu Xiufu jumped into the sea with the little emperor in his arms, and the two of them died...","Over at Persia, Isabella was promoted to the leader of the Persian Ming Cult for retrieving the Great Cosmic Shift and persuading the Central Plains Ming Cult to surrender to the Mongols.","In the Central Plains, the martial world moved in the direction they'd designed. Many foreign experts settled in the Central Plains after the Mongols conquered the world. Many of the world’s original experts died in battle or of old age. It was truly an age of chaos, and the people suffered greatly.","Soon, however, a Wudang youth stepped forward to quell the evildoers with his supreme sword, upholding justice in the world.","The Ming Cult’s Cult Leader Shi passed away, and the Radiant Left Envoy took over his position.","The E’mei Sect was established and took in female disciples.","Huashan Sect slowly grew from a minor sect with just a few members into a powerhouse...","Everything progressed smoothly, except...","“What are the two of you doing? Why aren’t you sleeping with each other?” Firework glared at Zu An and Tingxue.","Tingxue kept her silence. Zu An sighed. “Such things require building up to the moment. How can you make a child just because you want to?”","“That wouldn’t have been a problem in the past, but we’re in mortal bodies now. Waiting is a luxury we can’t afford!” Firework gritted her teeth in anger.","Zu An looked at the embarrassed Tingxue and said, “Why don’t we adopt a child and nurture her into the Ancient Tomb Sect’s successor?”","His current relationship with Tingxue was above that of friends, but beneath that of lovers. They still lacked impetus.","“That won’t do.” Firework turned down his proposal. “Our survival is at stake here. Who knows if there will be a problem if the Ancient Tomb Sect’s successor has no blood ties to you? We can’t take this risk.”","“So be it. Death is nothing scary anyway.” Tingxue stood up and left.","The three of them had more or less completed their missions. The Ancient Tomb Sect’s successor fell under Tingxue’s jurisdiction.","Zu An shrugged.","Firework clenched her teeth. If it had been in the past, she would have already knocked out Tingxue, stripped her naked, and delivered her onto Zu An’s bed. She was irked by how the two of them were roleplaying innocent youths here.","But this world had sealed her supernatural powers, resulting in her being roughly equally matched with Tingxue. It also annoyed her that Zu An refused to cooperate with her in subduing Tingxue. This left her with no way to proceed.","She knew it could be disastrous if they continued dilly-dallying. Just then, though, a thought popped into her mind, and she smiled cunningly.","That night was a sleepless one for Zu An. He rolled around his bed, tugging his clothes, feeling unbearably hot. “What’s going on? Is this cultivation deviation?”","Just then, he heard light footsteps. He could tell it was Firework, and it made him chuckle a little. She really likes to sneak around.","His blanket was suddenly lifted. A warm and smooth body slipped in and hugged him tightly.","“It’s cold...” a gentle voice murmured.","Zu An immediately realized something was amiss. She's...","Just then, Firework suddenly appeared like a specter to seal his acupoint.","“Again?” Zu An was both infuriated and horrified.","Firework stood by the windowsill with a gleeful smile. “It’s finally done. You and Tingxue insisted on roleplaying innocent youths. I couldn’t stand it anymore, so I had no choice but to help you out.”","Zu An was speechless. You aren’t helping anyone here. You should have at least delivered Tingxue in! Why did you bring Guo Fu in instead?"]},{"number":2859,"title":"Chapter 2859: Chapter 2811: The End","paragraphs":["“Don’t worry. I've checked her body—it’s definitely good for childbirth. Have a pleasant night, the two of you.” Firework chuckled before leaping out the window.","Zu An was speechless.","“Big brother Yang, I’m cold...” Guo Fu embraced him tightly with her feverishly hot body. Perhaps due to her inner energy, her skin remained as supple as a youth.","Zu An narrowed his eyes. She isn’t thinking rationally. Someone must have drugged her. It has to be Firework’s doing as well. She’s truly a demoness; she doesn’t think things through before doing them.","He clenched his teeth in anger. In his current state, he couldn’t even get up and push away Guo Fu. All he could do was to channel his inner energy to unseal his acupoint as soon as possible.","But Guo Fu was already wrapping herself around him. Perhaps due to the drug or the series of blows she'd suffered, she murmured, “Big brother Yang, did you know that I fell in love with you at first sight back then? But I was young and didn’t know better. You weren’t as attentive to me as Dawu and Xiaowu, so we often fought.","“I was thrilled when I met you again in the Hero Tournament. I reacted angrily when I heard my father was going to betroth me to you, but in truth, I was secretly overjoyed. Yet you said that you were going to marry your master instead. I felt humiliated in front of everyone else. Since then, I've hated you.","“Everything that happened afterward was a result of that. I’m sorry. I know I’m letting Miss Long down, but I can’t hold myself back. Please don’t reject me...”","...","Hearing a beauty pour out her feelings left Zu An dazed.","She'll be inconsolable if she learns that Yang Guo is dead too. Her parents are dead. Her siblings are scattered around. Her husband betrayed her. Yang Guo’s death might be the last straw that causes her to crumble for good. It might be better for her to live blissfully in an illusion than to cruelly reveal the truth to her.","Guo Fu displayed her feminine charms and tenderly took in his everything. Tears of joy streamed down her eyes.","...","In a distant forest, Tingxue coldly eyed Firework. “Aren’t you being too cruel to her?”","Firework was unfazed. “I had no other choice. You refused to get off your high horse, so I had to resort to another measure.”","Tingxue was speechless.","Firework leaned in and asked, “Why? Does it hurt you to see the man you love sleep with another woman?”","Tingxue turned away. She couldn’t be bothered to respond.","Firework continued, “Her original fate was to fall into the hands of the Mongol soldiers. We saved her life and offered her a sanctuary for her soul when she was in despair. How are we being cruel to her? If anything, we're her benefactors.”","Tingxue frowned. She didn’t agree with that, but she couldn’t find the words to retort against it.","Firework continued, “Besides, do you think that the Soul Transference Method is really that effective in this world, which forbids supernatural powers?”","Tingxue widened her eyes in astonishment. Indeed, their old selves could have easily controlled the mind of a mortal, but it would be hard to pull it off impeccably in this world.","“No matter how dumb Guo Fu is, she’s bound to notice something over time. Yet the effects of the Soul Transference Method remain even after so long. This can only mean one thing—this is what she wants. She’s subconsciously keeping herself hypnotized because she doesn’t want to wake up from this lovely dream and face the hell known as reality,” Firework coldly replied.","Tingxue harrumphed. “I shouldn’t have expected anything less from the demoness who controlled Dreamland for many years. You’re skilled at weaving dreams for others.”","“Thanks for your compliment.”","“What do you intend to do next?”","“Have them work overtime to bear a baby.”","“...”","“You’ll raise the child as her mother.”","“???” Tingxue couldn’t maintain her nonchalance anymore. “You intend to kill her?”","Firework coldly pointed out, “Your mission is to leave behind a successor for the Ancient Tomb Sect, so that child has to be a descendant of the Condor Heroes. The world needs a Yellow Dress Maiden who believes that she’s the descendant of the Condor Heroes, not the offspring of Yang Guo and Guo Fu.”","“I’ll raise the child, but don’t you dare kill her,” Tingxue said before taking her leave. Her cold voice carried unwavering conviction.","Firework looked at Tingxue’s departing silhouette with a smile.","...","In order to ensure that her childbearing plan went smoothly, Firework closely supervised Zu An and Guo Fu for the next few months.","Fortunately, Guo Fu did have a constitution that was good for childbearing.","Zu An had been perplexed as to why Guo Fu and Yelu Qi had no offspring despite being married for so long, but the truth was now apparent to him. Guo Fu was in love with someone else, which had made her instinctively reject Yelu Qi.","The Yelu Clan had been on the decline, so Yelu Qi desperately needed Guo Jing and Huang Rong’s influence. Thus, he'd played along with Guo Fu and put on the appearance of a model couple before the world.","No wonder he defected to the Mongols. The situation must have been incredibly stifling to him.","After suffering a series of major setbacks, Guo Fu had grown more mature. She was even willing to lower herself before Tingxue, fearing that the latter harbored a grudge against her for all the hurt she had caused them in their earlier years that would tear them apart.","She didn’t have her parents’ protection anymore, and she was no match for ‘Xiaolongnu’. She was well aware that if a conflict broke out between them, ‘Yang Guo’ would side with his beloved ‘Xiaolongnu’.","So, she kept an extremely humble posture and finally convinced 'Xiaolongnu' to accept her.","While living in the ancient tomb, Guo Fu swiftly discovered that ‘Yang Guo’ and ‘Xiaolongnu’ were nowhere as close as the world thought. More often than not, the two of them spent their time alone in their respective rooms.","Soon, she began straightening her back again, as she came to believe that she was the one whom ‘Yang Guo’ was truly in love with. She even tried picking a fight with ‘Xiaolongnu’, only for the latter to beat her up. She reverted to her humble attitude afterward.","Nevertheless, she still felt indignant.","I might be no match for Xiaolongnu alone, but I should be able to deal with her if I have my little sister’s help. I heard that Xiang’er became a grandmaster and founded the E’mei Sect.","On that note, she did feel apologetic to her little sister. She knew that her little sister harbored deep feelings for Yang Guo, having devoted more than a decade of her life to scouring the world in search of Yang Guo, yet she'd slipped in and gotten together with Yang Guo before her.","When she received Guo Fu’s letter requesting help, Firework rolled on the floor in laughter.","But she did miss Zu An, and she'd already taken in Abbess Fengling as her disciple anyway. So, she used the pretext of looking for a remote place to train to leave E’mei Mountain and visit Mount Zhongnan’s ancient tomb.","Guo Fu was initially overjoyed to have found an ally. She proactively tried to matchmake her little sister with ‘Yang Guo’, not knowing that the two of them were already together.","To her dismay, her little sister was closer to ‘Xiaolongnu’ and refused to help her. To make things worse, after her little sister joined them, ‘Yang Guo’ stayed in her room less often. This filled her with regret.","On the whole, though, the four of them lived in harmony.","Seasons came and went. Decades passed. Guo Fu passed away after living a fulfilling life. Zu An and the others had also grown old and ailing.","Over the years, Zu An had been steadily completing his missions.","He'd found the young Yang Dingtian and imparted the Nine Heavens Palm to him.","He'd secretly taken in Cheng Kun as his disciple and imparted to him the Yiyin Finger.","He'd found a youth named Feng Qingyang in the Huashan Sect and imparted the Nine Swords of Dugu to him.","He'd also found an oppressed eunuch in the imperial palace and imparted the Sunflower Manual to him.","He'd also secretly arranged for the old Cheng Ying to take in a disciple named Yang Xiao and impart to him Plum Blossom Island’s Divine Finger Flick.","Meanwhile, Lu Wushuang quietly honed the Five Poison Art she'd learned from Li Mochou back then at the southern border and eventually founded the Five Poisons Sect.","...","Everything had gone according to plan, but Zu An felt increasingly uneasy.","He felt as if he had overlooked something, but that was impossible. The three of them had been constantly discussing their plans, and they had already considered everything.","Shortly after, however, they received news that Isabella had died in Persia. Perhaps struck by that revelation, Firework and Tingxue passed away shortly after as well.","Zu An sat on a chair in a courtyard, watching the setting sun. He could feel his life force slowly seeping away. He was at his limit as well.","But why? Why can’t I see any signs of us clearing the trial even at this point?"]},{"number":2860,"title":"Chapter 2860: Chapter 2812: Overthrowing Everything","paragraphs":["Will the trial only end when we''re all dead?","But what if the trial remains uncleared even after I close my eyes and pass away? That would spell all our deaths.","Zu An’s unease deepened at that thought.","No, I must recall what I've overlooked. Otherwise, the decades we've spent planning everything out would have been in vain.","He thought about his encounter with the Deity of Death, as well as everything that had happened after they entered the trial. Not a single challenger had cleared this trial to date, and he didn’t think he was smarter than the powerhouses of the Myriad Worlds.","Granted that he had a huge advantage, knowing the trial world’s background, there was no guarantee that his interpretation of the trial was accurate.","Above all, he still had no idea how the other universal deities had tampered with this world.","Memories flashed across his head before finally settling on the duel with the Mongolian Prince Zhenjin on the mountain behind Chongyang Palace. He had finally figured out what was amiss.","The timeline is wrong!","It’s one thing for us to encounter Daoist Bai Sun and the Master of the Vajra School, but why did the Red Sun Reverend appear in this world as well? Not only is he not a character in Jin Yong’s wuxiaverse, but the timeline doesn’t fit as well.","The Red Sun Reverend is a powerhouse who appeared in the final years of the Yuan Dynasty, so how could he have been Prince Zhenjin’s vassal? Heck, the Yuan Dynasty wasn't even formed then!","There’s also that white-haired man with the flute and that seductive woman. They should be ‘White Hair’ and ‘Ravishing Beauty’ from Huang Yi’s novel. Those are characters who appear in the final years of the Yuan Dynasty as well!","Their appearance here suggests that this world’s timeline has been plunged into chaos.","My solution assumed that this world would follow the normal timeline. If the other universal deities hadn’t tampered with the trial world, it would have been the right answer. But if other universal deities have truly tampered with things here, it won’t be surprising if we fail this trial.","That must have been that being’s doing—the Deity of Chaos and Enigma Mi Li!","She must have tampered with this trial world because she doesn’t want someone to inherit Death’s legacy. She did it so discreetly that there would be no way for one to realize that something was amiss unless one was familiar with its background.","The Deity of Annihilation probably tampered with the Mongols. Their act of killing and plundering is perfectly aligned with the deity's beliefs. With the Mongols strengthened by Annihilation's divine power, Zhang Wuji and Zhu Yuanzhang won’t be able to overthrow the Yuan Dynasty like they did in ‘Heavenly Sword and Dragon Slaying Saber’.","I wonder how the other universal deities tampered with this trial world...","It’s a pity I discovered it too late. I’m already on my last legs. What else can I do?","Zu An’s eyes, which had grown turbid with age, suddenly regained their clarity.","No, there’s still time. I can still do something about it. I have the perfect tool for that. I am the envoy of not just the Deity of Chaos and Enigma, but the Deity of Memory as well!","Since the other universal deities were able to tamper with this trial world, it stands to reason that I can tap into their powers here as well.","Along with this realization, a mysterious surge of power flowed into Zu An’s body, temporarily delaying his death. He took out the Spring Autumn Brush and the Time Annal.","Since this world is already in chaos, I might as well stir the pot more!","He activated his divine sense, and the Brush of Spring and Autumn began furiously scribbling in the Time Annal.","“This is a world of distorted spacetime, where the Mongols, the Jin, the Qing, the Liao, Western Xia, Southern Song, Dali, the Tibetans, the Oirats, Tshongkha, the Karakhanids, the Persian Ming Cult, Goguryeo, Fusang... all simultaneously exist.","“It is primarily based on Jin Yong’s 14 novels...","“ Ouch! It hurts terribly! Song Qingshu slowly roused from his sleep, feeling as if all his bones had shattered...","“ In the end, Song Qingshu united all factions together to defeat the Mongols and rebuild his homeland... ”","“What should I call it? Under the Madam's... No, that won’t do. I’ll call it The Master Player instead!”[1]","This book’s content is even more chaotic than this trial world. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Chaos and Enigma.","This book records everything that happens here. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Memory.","This book stirs the desires of those who read it. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Bliss and Desire.","This book encourages a proclivity for reproduction. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Reproduction.","This book quells chaos to re-establish order. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Order.","This book records the annihilation of countless nations. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Annihilation.","This book describes beauty beyond measure. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Love and Beauty.","This book’s emperor displays a tenacious desire for longevity. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Longevity.","This book contains ingenious schemes and politicking. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Knowledge.","This book’s protagonist resolutely protects his loved ones and the Divine Continent. I shall offer this as tribute to the great Deity of Protection.","Last but not least, I shall offer the countless souls who have died in war in this book to the great Deity of Death!","...","Zu An had no idea which universal deities had participated in the crusade against the Deity of Death, so he showed his respect to all of them except for the Deity of Nebula. Considering how they had little interest in everything, it was unlikely that the Deity of Nebula would participate in the crusade against the Deity of Death anyway.","There’s nothing I can offer that would interest the Deity of Nebula anyway.","Several surges of divine light flowed into Zu An’s body. Everything began to collapse until the trial world was reduced to a single white dot.","Zu An found himself standing in the middle of a monotonously white world. His previously aged body had reverted to its youthful form, and he'd regained his supernatural powers as well.","The skull stairway appeared before his eyes once more.","“Come up!” a divine voice boomed.","Zu An slowly climbed the stairway a step at a time. He soon reached the end and was met with a pair of gigantic red eyes.","“You’re fated with death. I didn’t think those fellows would tamper with my trial. That explains why no one has been able to clear my trial in such a long time.” The Deity of Death was both infuriated and heartened. “Good. You were born to be the Deity of Death. Are you willing to inherit Death’s authority?”","“Where are my companions?” Zu An asked.","“They’re dead. They didn’t clear the trial.”","Zu An narrowed his eyes. “That’s not true. They played a crucial role in the completion of the trial. I couldn’t have cleared this trial without their assistance. Going by the rules you set, they should be qualified to inherit Death’s authority as well.”","The Deity of Death coldly replied, “Only one person can inherit Death’s authority.”","“Do you truly believe I’d be able to inherit Death’s authority?”","“What do you mean?”","“The universal deities tampered with your trial because they don’t want to see a new Deity of Death. I might have cleared your trial, but my actions must have drawn their attention. I wouldn’t be surprised if some of them are listening in on our conversation.”","“...” A long while later, the Deity of Death said with a resigned tone, “I have lost too much of my powers to tell if they are watching us or not, but your words make sense.”","Zu An finally continued, “Entrusting Death’s authority to a single person is no different from a child carrying gold into a busy market—it’ll only lead to death. You might as well split Death’s authority into multiple pieces and entrust them to those who have contributed to the clearance of the trial.","“That would allow Death’s authority to be passed down. At the same time, the other universal deities would view the situation more favorably, as it would ensure that Death’s authority remained under their surveillance, since my companions are worshipers of other universal deities.”","The Deity of Death was silent for a long while. “This means Death’s authority might never become whole ever again. There might never be another Deity of Death.”","“At least hope will be preserved.” Zu An smiled. “I don’t think you have the strength to protect me from the other universal deities in your current state.”","1. This is a webnovel on Qidian. Its original name was Under the Madam's Skirt, then it was later renamed to The Master Player. ☜"]},{"number":2861,"title":"Chapter 2861: Chapter 2813: The Universal Deities’ Reactions","paragraphs":["The gigantic red eyes flickered with hesitation. It took some time before the Deity of Death finally made up his mind. “You must truly love those women.”","“Why do you say that?”","“No one else in the Myriad Worlds could reject the allure of a universal deity’s authority and instead request that it be split into pieces just to save a few women,” the Deity of Death replied with a sigh.","“This has nothing to do with love. I promised them that we'd overcome the trial together, and they put their utmost trust in me. I don’t want to break my promise,” Zu An replied calmly.","Of course, the threat posed by other universal deities also played a huge part, or else he couldn’t have withstood the temptation so easily.","“Forget it. You’re the only promising candidate I've met in so many years. Maybe you’re right,” the Deity of Death said. The gigantic red eyes split into four rays of white light, with the biggest ray flowing into Zu An’s body.","Zu An’s body shuddered. He was gripped by an unprecedented sensation that was far more profound than what he'd felt when he obtained the Cultivation World’s World Law Beacon. It felt as if he had the Myriad Worlds in his grasp, but this authority was obscured by a veil.","It must be because my piece of Death’s authority is incomplete.","The remaining three rays of white light descended to other areas. Moments later, Firework, Tingxue, and Isabella appeared before his eyes. They experienced similar sensations as well.","Firework stared intently at Zu An with a furiously beating heart that refused to calm down. After everything she'd been through, she had lost all her trust in others . It was only because she knew that it was nigh impossible for her to survive the Deity of Death’s trial, and that Zu An had proven himself to be trustworthy so far, that she'd chosen to make an exception and trust him this once.","That said, she'd already been prepared to be backstabbed once more. Zu An had promised to save all of them, but she was skeptical about it.","She had gained some grasp of Zu An’s character by this point. If there were no competing interests at stake, Zu An could still choose to save all of them. But the same couldn't be said if there were competing interests.","For instance, if only one of them could survive this trial, she hadn't thought Zu An would give up his life to save the others.","Little had she expected Zu An to go this far just to score some chicks! He'd actually given up Death’s authority!","Other powerhouses wouldn’t have hesitated to massacre entire universes to obtain Death’s authority, but he'd chosen to share it with them!","Tingxue had a complicated expression as well. She'd already returned to being a Nebula envoy and had regained her usual impassiveness, but this was a universal deity’s authority they were talking about here...","That man fulfilled his promise to save all of us and even gave something this precious to me.","She recalled how they had lived together as a couple for the past few decades, and that left ripples in her heart, which should have long become still like an old well.","Isabella was nowhere as subtle as Tingxue. She excitedly dove over to embrace Zu An. “Big brother Zu, I knew you’d succeed!”","Zu An dotingly patted her head. “It's been tough on you, having to stay alone in Persia all those years.”","“It was lonely, but thinking about you gave me strength.” Isabella hugged Zu An’s arm while radiating a blissful smile. She didn't mention Death’s authority, but there was no way the Acadias’ big miss wouldn’t know about its value.","Suddenly, the world shook. The winding skull staircase began to crumble. The skulls shrieked miserably as they desperately tried to reassemble the staircase, but they still dropped to the ground and shattered into dust.","The gigantic red eyes in the sky vanished. The Deity of Death’s aura could no longer be felt. Everyone present understood that the Deity of Death was gone for good.","The group was transported back to the forbidden land’s earth vein.","Zu An was about to speak when a divine light suddenly flashed, and he found himself transported into a special space. Sensing a familiar aura, he hurriedly bowed. “Paying respect to the exalted Deity of Chaos and Enigma.”","Countless stars in the sky twinkled as if depicting the Deity of Chaos and Enigma’s expression. “You have done well this time. Your book, ‘The Master Player’, has been written to my liking. The world setting and timeline are beautifully chaotic. But don’t you think you’re being too greedy, trying to please all the universal deities?”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He hurriedly said, “I’m overwhelmed by your magnanimity in protecting someone as humble as me. I’d have been reduced to nothing otherwise.”","“You need not put yourself down. Your unique take has pleased quite a few of them. At least the Deity of Bliss and Desire and Deity of Reproduction are happy with you. However, if the Deity of Love and Beauty were still around, they would have smashed your head in. You made so many beautiful women follow the same man.”","Zu An smiled sheepishly in response. Looks like I buttered her up the wrong way.","“The others can’t be bothered. How can the shallow schemes of your book’s characters catch the interest of the Deity of Knowledge? It’s the same for the others, too.”","“What about the Deity of Annihilation?” Zu An asked. The Deity of Annihilation had supported the Mongols in this trial world, but Zu An had written the Mongols as antagonists who were defeated in the end. He'd offered the demise of countless countries as tribute to the other party, but that wouldn't necessarily be enough to placate them.","“They were infuriated, of course. They want to destroy you. Don’t worry, I stopped them.” The Deity of Chaos and Enigma suddenly changed her tone and asked, “But what surprised me is that Meng actually stood up for you as well. Can you tell me why?”","The question was asked in a nonchalant tone, but it made Zu An sweat profusely.","“I beg your pardon, exalted Deity of Chaos and Enigma. The Deity of Memory summoned me and conferred me as her envoy. I didn’t dare reject her.” Zu An didn’t hide anything, knowing that the other party could uncover the truth if she investigated it. It would be wiser to be honest to show his loyalty.","“Interesting. I’d have never expected a Time Scribe to become a Mirror Scribe as well.” The stars in the sky twinkled, as if reflecting Mi Li’s good mood, but she proceeded to calmly drop a dangerous question right after. “Who do you prefer between the two of us?”","Zu An instinctively sought to flatter Mi Li, but a thought popped into his mind, and he quickly changed his words. “You are both exalted entities whom I admire greatly, but a humble ant like me truly dares not comment about the universal deities.”","“You are a cunning one. Now that you possess half of Death’s authority, you aren’t an ant anymore.”","“I am first and foremost your envoy.”","“Hahaha! You are a Chaos and Enigma envoy, but you are also a Memory envoy. On top of that, you possess Death’s authority. What remarkable chaos this is. You’re indeed suited for my path. Fine, I shan’t make things hard for you.”","The countless stars in the sky vanished. Mi Li had left.","Zu An barely managed to breathe a sigh of relief when his surroundings morphed once more. This time, he was transported into a peculiar space filled with waterfalls of numbers. Taking a closer look, the flowing numbers were unusual, resembling a combination of 0s and 1s, yet not exactly so either.","It was the Deity of Memory!"]},{"number":2862,"title":"Chapter 2862: Chapter 2814: A New Skill","paragraphs":["“Paying respects to the exalted Deity of Memory!” Zu An was starting to get used to this.","The surrounding numbers flickered as if assessing Zu An. “Why didn’t you say that you liked Mi Li more earlier?”","Cold sweat rained down Zu An’s back. She was listening in. He quickly replied, “I am the envoy of not just the exalted Deity of Chaos and Enigma, but the Deity of Memory as well.”","“I see. Then why don’t you like me more?”","Zu An sweated profusely. These two universal deities are... He quickly reined himself in and replied, “It’s the utmost honor of a humble ant like me to receive the grace of a universal deity. I’d be stepping out of line to dare evaluate supreme beings of your stature.”","“Mi Li is right. You’re a cunning one.” The numbers flickered. “You are the envoy of two universal deities and the wielder of half of Death’s authority. You aren’t an ant anymore.”","Zu An carefully replied, “Exalted universal deity, please be assured that I have no intention of resurrecting Death. That is why I opted to divide its authority.”","You must be kidding me! Even the Deity of Death was killed by the universal deities. I'm nothing in comparison!","“You don’t need to be nervous. If not for our tacit approval, you couldn’t have retained half of Death’s authority,” the Deity of Memory replied.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. “Allow me to express my utmost gratitude to you for saving me from the Deity of Annihilation.”","“I protect my worshipers. You have done well, recording so many important events. I am very satisfied.” The Deity of Memory was in a good mood.","Zu An took the chance to ask, “May I ask how I should deal with Death’s authority? I don’t feel any different from before.”","“Possessing half of a universal deity’s authority elevates your stature. Just as there are countless civilizations in the Myriad Worlds, there are countless power level systems as well. Those power level systems mark a difference in quantity, such as the difference between 100 and 1. There is no fundamental change in its meaning. A change in stature, however, can give rise to a fundamental change from 0 to 1.","“It is extremely difficult for those of a lower stature to hurt those of a higher stature, and you now possess the highest stature in the Myriad Worlds. You might have only inherited half of Death’s authority, but you’ll still benefit greatly from it,” the Deity of Memory patiently explained.","“Thank you for your guidance, exalted universal deity!”","Zu An had gained some insight into power and laws when he obtained the Cultivation World’s World Law Beacon and became its god. Cultivators were divided into tiers, ranging from first rank to earth immortal. But to a higher being, there was no fundamental difference among those cultivation levels.","The concept of stature was likely related to one’s ability to control, alter, and even create laws. No matter how powerful a cultivator was, they were still reliant on the energies around them and had to obey the laws of physics in each world. A higher entity could render a powerful cultivator helpless just by altering a law.","The stream of numbers suddenly flickered, and a book fell from the sky and floated into Zu An’s hands. The Deity of Memory said, “That trial world was created by the Deity of Death before his demise. He left a secret manual for his successor. It should have been impossible for anyone to clear the trial, and I also withheld the manual.","“However, I have browsed the manual; it has nothing to do with Death’s path. He must have had a plan in mind, but now that he has completely fallen, it’s no longer worth dwelling on that. I’ll give you the manual.”","But Zu An didn’t dare take it. “I dare not casually browse through something left by the Deity of Death.”","The numbers in the surroundings flickered. “There’s nothing for you to fear. The Deity of Annihilation was the one who wanted to bring down the Deity of Death. The rest of us had only just attained our deityhood and still harbored fear toward Death, so we tacitly permitted and even aided Annihilation. We are not the same entities we were back then. Death can no longer faze us. Of course, I wouldn’t have handed this manual to you if you weren’t my worshiper.”","Zu An quickly understood what was going on.","The other universal deities no longer feared Death, but they still wouldn’t permit the rise of another Deity of Death. Had it been anyone else, they would have never been permitted to clear the trial, or inherit the Deity of Death’s legacy.","Thanks to him being fortunate enough to become both Memory and Chaos and Enigma’s envoy, Zu An was the only exception. At the same time, the others who participated in the trial were highly regarded worshipers of the other paths. That was why the universal deities had let them off.","Zu An took the manual and saw three words written on its cover—Song of Righteousness. He was taken aback.","“Yes, it’s the one you’re thinking about. Following Southern Song’s collapse, Prime Minister Wen Tianxiang rejected the Yuan Mongols’ invitation and wrote the Song of Righteousness. Despite being a mortal, Wen Tianxiang’s Song of Righteousness resonated with the world. Even I have a high opinion of it. The current Song of Righteousness is elevated from its previous state, and it’s compatible with you.”","“Compatible with me?” Zu An was confused.","“I sense that you have an ability resembling Soulspeak, but using it incurs a hefty price, so you can’t use it under normal circumstances. The Song of Righteousness nurtures a righteous energy, which can be used to offset the cost of your ability. Now that you possess half of Death’s authority, you should be able to use it.”","Zu An was overjoyed to hear that. “Thank you for your bestowment, exalted Deity of Memory!”","This was indeed invaluable to him.","“Allright. Remember to record more important events like this...”","Hearing that the Deity of Memory was about to leave, Zu An hurriedly asked, “Exalted Deity of Memory, may I know how I can travel through spacetime to reunite with someone whom I have lost touch with?”","He'd visited Dreamland in search of a solution, but Dreamland turned out to be a sham. That left him at a loss. But thinking about it, there was no one better to pose this question to than the universal deities of the Myriad Worlds.","The stream of numbers froze. “Who do you want to meet?”","“An old friend.”","“A lover, I see.”","Zu An was speechless. I forgot she can read my thoughts.","“Why didn’t you ask Mi Li?”","Zu An dared not to speak ill of the Deity of Chaos and Enigma, so he replied, “You are the exalted Deity of Memory. You must possess all kinds of records about the Myriad World.”","“There’s no use bootlicking me. I do know the answer, but I am not obliged to answer your questions. It makes me wonder who is the universal deity here.”","Cold sweat rained down from Zu An. “Exalted Deity of Memory, please pardon my brashness.”","“I’ll tell you how you can find the person you want to meet when you find something better to offer to me.” With that, the stream of numbers vanished, and Zu An returned to the forbidden land’s earth vein."]},{"number":2863,"title":"Chapter 2863: Chapter 2815: Love Sage","paragraphs":["Zu An wiped off his cold sweat. The universal deities sure are capricious. He quickly put a halt to those thoughts lest those entities overhear them.","He flipped open the Song of Righteousness.","“In Heaven and Earth there exists righteous energy, pervasive in all forms and things. Below, it manifests as rivers and mountains; above, as the sun and stars. Within mankind, it is called the noble spirit, vast and mighty, filling the universe. When the imperial path is pure and peaceful, it harmonizes all in the imperial court...”","Zu An heard a voice echoing in his ears, bringing him enlightenment. Righteous energy began to sprout within him.","New secret manual detected: Song of Righteousness. Do you want to absorb it?","Zu An was overjoyed to hear the long-awaited voice. According to prior experience, the Keyboard System absorbing the manual wouldn’t cause the latter to lose its original function, so he chose to absorb it.","The Song of Righteousness transformed into a stream of light and embedded itself onto the Keyboard’s F9 key.","New secret manual collection. New function unlocked: Title System.","The system will select the most suitable title for you based on your performance in major events.","In this dungeon, you have staked everything to protect your female friends, going to the extent of relinquishing the indescribably invaluable authority of Death to rescue them. The extent you’re willing to go to score a girl is no different from a Love Sage.","Love Sage: You can more easily earn a woman’s goodwill. Damage inflicted on women is reduced by 50%. Damage received from women is reduced by 70%.","Zu An was initially overjoyed to have unlocked a new keyboard skill, only to be flabbergasted by the title he obtained. What kind of title is that?! More easily earn a woman’s goodwill? How is that even measured?","At least there are numbers on the damage reduction, but that only means I’ll deal half as much damage to women in the future. As for being hurt by women...","Zu An suddenly thought about the Heiress’ Ball of Delight, which made him immune to damage from women richer than him. This 70% damage reduction appeared humble in comparison, but if used well, it could prove to be an invaluable asset.","Will the damage reduction apply to the bedroom as well, though? That would be a gigantic nerf for me!","“Big brother Zu? Big brother Zu?” Isabella called out.","Zu An snapped out of his daze and noticed the three women staring at him with weird eyes.","“Big brother Zu, you were standing in a daze earlier, smiling to yourself. You mumbled something about a nerf. What do you mean by that?” Isabella’s clear eyes were brimming with overflowing curiosity.","Faced with such clear eyes, Zu An’s face reddened. “It’s nothing...”","Firework clicked her tongue. “Isn’t it just being summoned by a universal deity? There’s nothing to hide here.”","The flow of time inside a universal deity’s domain was different from that of the real world. During Zu An’s conversations with the Deity of Chaos and Enigma and the Deity of Memory, an instant had only passed in the real world.","Zu An smiled. “I was indeed summoned by a universal deity...”","“You’re amazing, big brother Zu. You were summoned by a universal deity multiple times within such a short span!” Isabella’s voice was filled with admiration. The people of the Myriad Worlds viewed it as an honor to be summoned by a universal deity. It symbolized greater strength and potential.","“You have a portion of a universal deity’s authority inside you now. That lad must be out of his mind to share something like that,” Firework grumbled, though her twinkling eyes reflected her excitement.","“I don’t know how I can repay you, big brother Zu...”","“Stop. Are you going to betroth yourself to him next?” Firework interjected.","“Don’t talk nonsense!” Isabella stomped her feet. She looked adorable.","Zu An smiled. “We've braved life and death situations together now. Saying such words only makes us look distant.”","Isabella nodded. She bit her lip, not knowing what to say.","“Big brother Zu, why don’t you follow me back to the Universal Conglomerate? I remember you were looking for something. We have branches all over the Myriad Worlds. I’m sure we can help you find what you’re searching for.” Isabella looked at Zu An with expectant eyes before adding, “Big sister Firework and big sister Tingxue, you should come along as well. I’ll make sure to host you all well.”","Firework sneered, “Tsk, your invitation is obviously only directed at that fellow. We’re just add-ons. I’m not interested.”","Isabella felt indignant. “Big sister Firework, I have no such intention.”","Tingxue replied, “I’ll pass. There’s something I need to investigate.”","Zu An was surprised. It was no surprise for a Nebula envoy like Tingxue to be uninterested in the Universal Conglomerate, but to think she would be so concerned about a certain matter.","Just then, Firework suddenly spoke up. “It’s getting late. Why don’t you rest in my territory first? Dreamland’s accommodations are quite well-known across the Myriad Worlds.”","The others looked at Firework with weird eyes, knowing that Dreamland was a dead city, with practically its entire populace being her clones.","Firework harrumphed. “Relax. I’m in a good mood after finally being freed. I no longer need their souls. I’ll return them.”","“Didn’t you say they were dead?” Zu An was surprised.","“You believed that? It was merely part of my background setting as Dreamland’s big miss,” Firework replied with a gleeful grin. “I merely extracted their souls and infused mine into their bodies. That’s much easier than creating them from scratch.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. Despite his intimate relationship with Firework, he'd still been jarred by her lack of hesitation to massacre entire worlds. Her willingness to spare Dreamland’s people is a good start. I need to advise her more.","“Big sister Firework, can you free Uncle Alfred?” Isabella looked at Firework with teary eyes.","“Don’t worry, he’s alive. I have no interest in such old souls.”","“You’re the best, big sister Firework!” Isabella was glad that Zu An had dealt with Firework, or else she had no idea how she could deal with such a terrifying enemy.","Firework casually waved her hand and pulled out countless cocoons from the darkness using silk threads. These cocoons contained the guests who had been on board the frigate.","The guests remained on edge even after they were freed.","“Where’s that demon spider?”","“Did big miss Isabella save us?”","“We have to leave this place right away. We’ll be dead meat if that demon spider finds us.”","...","Those people looked as if they were scared out of their wits.","Isabella noticed Firework’s twitching eyelids and quickly spoke up. “It’s big sister Firework, big brother Zu, and big sister Tingxue who saved us all. You have nothing to worry about anymore. That demon... Cough cough , I mean, we’re out of danger now.”","Isabella had noticed that Firework had conjured Yani and took it as a sign that she wasn't planning to reveal her true identity to the guests, so she played along with that.","The guests thanked Firework, but they still left in a hurry as they couldn’t shake off their fear.","The frigate they'd traveled on had been destroyed, so Isabella pulled out a tiny ship model from her bag and tossed it into the water. It swiftly expanded into a gigantic ship.","Everyone boarded the ship and embarked on their journey back to Dreamland.","While the guests remained fearful for their lives, Zu An began conversing with a beautiful woman wearing a red dress. It was Mi Li, who had been absent for a long time.","“You've been gone for so long that I thought you were dead.”","“It’s a good thing you didn’t ask them for the materials to reforge my body, or else I might have really died.”"]},{"number":2864,"title":"Chapter 2864: Chapter 2816: Turning Tables","paragraphs":["“I’m not a fool. I've noticed how you disappear each time a universal deity appears. There’s no way I’d talk about you in front of them.” Zu An looked at Mi Li with confusion. “Are you on bad terms with the universal deities? Otherwise, why are you afraid of catching their notice?”","Mi Li harrumphed. “How can I defy the universal deities? I just wanted to avoid trouble.”","“Considering how they can read my mind and memories, I’m surprised that the universal deities never noticed you or the Keyboard System.”","“You have to thank that Keyboard System of yours. It partially shielded you from the universal deities’ probing, allowing you to retain some secrets before them.”","Zu An was surprised. The Keyboard System can even fool universal deities? I wonder who created it.","“Where did you hide in the Deity of Death’s trial world? I was worried that you’d get killed by the laws.”","“I was hiding in the Tai’e Sword. Many universal deities were observing that trial world, so even the Keyboard System dared not make an appearance. Otherwise, they might have detected its existence while collecting Rage points. Rage points are soul pulsations, after all.”","Zu An narrowed his eyes. “You’re very familiar with the Keyboard System.”","“Of course. I'm contracted with you.” Mi Li yawned. “You’re smart to have divided Death’s authority into multiple parts. Otherwise, the other universal deities would have killed you, even if you had the backing of Chaos and Enigma, as well as Memory.”","“Come to think of it, I'm quite fated with Death.” Zu An thought about how he had become the master of the Netherworld across different timelines. “Now that Death’s authority is fragmented, does it mean there will never be a new Deity of Death?”","“Once you grow strong enough, you can recollect the other pieces of Death’s authority and become the new Deity of Death,” Mi Li replied with a smile. “It just so happens that the other three pieces are with those women, and they're on good terms with you. On that note, I can’t believe you didn’t score Tingxue despite spending so much time with her in the trial world. The Keyboard System must be blind to label you ‘Love Sage’.”","Zu An was speechless. He hadn’t expected Mi Li to even know about his title. He really had no secrets in front of her.","“Tingxue appears to lack emotions, but she has a strong will. We might be on good terms, but we’re lacking something. It feels like our relationship may unravel if I take a step forward.”","“Tsk. You were just too busy indulging in Firework and Guo Fu’s bodies. That Guo Fu looked a lot like Huang Rong when she was younger. No wonder you worked so hard plowing her.”","“...”","“There’s Isabella as well. It can’t be more obvious that she has maxed out goodwill for you. You can practically see hearts in her eyes. Yet you didn’t take the opportunity to push her down.”","Zu An was annoyed. “It was already a struggle to find a way out of that godforsaken trial. I didn’t have the energy to be thinking about all these things.”","“Was it?” Mi Li looked at him with an ambiguous smile, her feet shaking provocatively. It was so irritating that Zu An wanted to pull her feet down. “Back to the topic. Instead of recombining Death’s authority, you can also use your half of Death’s authority to forge your own path. You might just become a new universal deity.”","Zu An was surprised. “I can become a new universal deity that isn’t the Deity of Death?”","“Of course. Each authority symbolizes a divine jurisdiction. It’s like a ticket to the dining table, though in your current state, you’re only qualified to stand next to the table. Whether you can secure a seat and which seat you’ll get depends on how you grow in the future,” Mi Li replied.","Zu An fell silent. He began pondering his path for the first time. Are there still incomplete paths in the Myriad Worlds that no universal deities have reached the end of?","Mi Li suddenly yawned. “That’s all for now. Your little girlfriend is here. I’ll go back to sleep, lest I hear annoying clapping sounds.”","She vanished into thin air.","Right after, someone knocked on the door before gently pushing it open. A woman with voluptuous legs strutted in. “Sir, I’m here to thank you for saving my life.”","Zu An’s jaws dropped. The one who had entered the room wasn’t Firework but Dreamland’s guard captain, Yani. He still remembered how Yani had valiantly struck down a Death envoy and blasted a hole in the sky.","However, he quickly snapped out of his daze and asked, “Firework, what are you doing?”","Yani was confused. “Sir, what are you saying? I’m Yani.”","“Stop playing.” Zu An harrumphed.","Yani chuckled. “Tsk, how boring. Do you not like me in this form? I guess you prefer smaller girls. Lolicon!”","“That’s slander!” Zu An was irritated. “What are you up to?”","Yani casually sat down beside him and wrapped her hand around his neck. “I wasn’t able to show you the real me because my supernatural powers were sealed in the trial world. Now that I've regained my powers, it’s only right for me to let you have a taste of it.”","Zu An was speechless.","Before he could process what was going on, Yani grabbed his shoulder and pushed him down onto the bed. She towered over him, her beautiful face exuding valiance and charisma. Her shirt button began to groan due to her movements, and it looked as if it could snap at any moment. “Do you prefer the coy Firework, or the valiant Yani?”","“Aren’t they both you?” Zu An found this situation utterly ridiculous. Those two women felt completely unrelated to each other, yet he knew that they were both the same person.","“If you like Yani more, I’ll accompany you more as her in the future,” Yani whispered into his ear, teasing him.","Zu An was mesmerized. Unlike the bubbly Firework, Yani resembled a general who had conquered the battlefield. Her disposition, the sensations from her body, and even her fragrance felt completely different.","He felt an urge to protect Firework, but when it came to Yani, he felt a desire to conquer her.","“I can feel it. You’re moved.” Yani looked at him with a mischievous grin.","Zu An flipped over and pinned her beneath him. “You aren’t going to be on top of me.”","“Hmph. The trial world is one thing, but do you think you can defeat me here?” Yani’s eyes gleamed with pride. She wrapped her legs tightly around Zu An and flipped him over, pinning him down beneath her.","“???”","“...”","Fighting sounds filled the room as they competed for supremacy.","Some time later, Yani suddenly exclaimed, “Hold on! How did you suddenly become so strong?”","Zu An looked down on Yani from above in glee. His Love Sage title surprisingly came in handy here— reduces 70% damage from women ! Furthermore, Yani had held back to avoid hurting him, so that gave him a chance to stage a comeback."]},{"number":2865,"title":"Chapter 2865: Chapter 2817: The Real Firework","paragraphs":["Yani tried to fight back, but Zu An was no pushover, either.","He wouldn't even get into the ranks of top experts in the Myriad Worlds when fighting in a proper battle, but it was a different story when the battle was in bed. Yani had been dominant in the earlier phase, but little did she know Zu An had many tricks up his sleeve.","“How many women did you go through to learn this instant unbuttoning technique?”","“Hold on for a moment.”","“Hm?”","...","Zu An felt as if he had returned to the Fiend races’ grassland. Back then, a vassal state had handed over a ferocious mare that no one in the imperial family could subjugate as tribute. The Little Fiend Empress had given it to Zu An, and he'd spent a great deal of effort before taming it.","Zu An faced a greater challenge today. This time, he felt as if he was trying to tame a great stallion which had a temperament and stamina far greater than the mare.","...","Some time later, Zu An stroked a beautiful back that looked as if it had been carefully sculpted by the heavens. He was glad that such things didn’t count as dealing damage, or else his Love Sage title would have been too much.","Yani suddenly got up and grinned at him. Before Zu An could admire her beauty, her hair suddenly grew thicker and curlier. Her fiery red lips also became more seductive. In the blink of an eye, she transformed from a valiant general into the charismatic elder Diodora, the most stunning woman in Dreamland.","When Diodora had briefly made an appearance in the hotel, most experts could hardly keep themselves together.","Zu An was startled, but it quickly occurred to him that the other party was still Firework. “You should give me a heads up first so I can mentally prepare myself.”","“What would you like to tell me, hero?” Diodora spoke in a voice different from that of Yani. It carried a tinge of sweetness, which stirred yearning in men.","Zu An frowned. She’s truly an actress. I wouldn’t have seen through her if I hadn’t known about her ability. “What if I fail to recognize you in the future if you keep transforming from one person to another?”","“So be it. Let mistakes be made.”","“...”","“I’m here to thank our great hero for rescuing Dreamland. You are our great benefactor. Name anything you want from our Dreamland, and it shall belong to you,” Diodora declared.","Zu An had to admit that Firework was a succubus. Her acting skills were ridiculous—no, this transcended acting. It felt as if the real Diodora was really standing before him. This stoked his interest. “Your guard captain, Yani, came over to relay her gratitude to me earlier.”","“Great hero, what do you think of Yani?”","“She’s fine. It’s just a bit tiring to subjugate her because she keeps trying to one up me.”","“Yani has always been a bit rough. Don’t you worry, great hero. Just give me the word, and I’ll alleviate your exhaustion.” Diodora’s hair gently tickled Zu An’s chest.","Zu An’s lust was stoked. “Since you’re here to thank me, shouldn’t you be the one making the moves?”","“You’re right, great hero. I should be the one to make a move.” Diodora smiled seductively as she lowered herself.","“Ssss~”","...","Meanwhile, Isabella was in her room telling her loyal butler everything that had happened in the meantime.","Alfred was shocked. “To think our big miss has acquired a portion of Death’s authority. Even our patriarch would be shocked by your fortuitous encounter!”","Isabella excitedly replied, “It’s all thanks to big brother Zu. That trial was a deathtrap. We would have all died if not for him.”","Alfred looked at Isabella dotingly. “Big miss, are you thinking of bringing young master Zu in as the Acadias’ son-in-law?”","“Uncle Alfred, you’re making fun of me!” Isabella shyly stomped her feet.","Alfred chuckled a little more before his expression turned grim. “Young master Zu is indeed an outstanding man, but his strength and background are still lacking. I’m afraid the Conglomerate will not accept him as the Acadias’ son-in-law. There are simply too many outstanding candidates.”","Isabella’s expression turned cold. “Not only does big brother Zu possess half of Death’s authority and a Wonderpoint World, but he also has exceptional wits and a sincere heart. That should easily put him above the other candidates.”","Alfred replied bitterly, “Big miss, there’s no point telling me that. The ones calling the shots are those above. Our patriarch and the others are in a difficult position as well. The other candidates are from distinguished backgrounds. The Conglomerate needs to show them some respect.”","“They can marry those candidates if they want to. As for me...” Isabella’s face reddened, and she cut her words short. “Forget it, I’ll go chat with big brother Zu.”","Isabella was about to head out when Alfred stopped her. “Big miss, there are other guests onboard. It’s already nightfall. Rumors might spread if you enter a young man’s room at this time.”","“Big brother Zu saved them! How dare they gossip about him?”","“Not everyone knows to show gratitude. Besides, Dreamland’s guard captain Yani went to look for young master Zu earlier and is still in his room. It might be awkward if you were to head there right now,” Alfred kindly reminded her.","“Yani?” Isabella frowned.","“Yes. Yani is a formidable expert, even by the standards of the Conglomerate. She boasts incredible beauty as well. Even I might have fallen for her in my younger years,” Alfred remarked wistfully.","You wouldn’t be thinking that if you knew she was the demon spider. Big sister Firework has regained her powers now. Will she bully big brother Zu?","...","Cough cough!","Diodora raised her head and gracefully wiped her lips before glaring at Zu An resentfully.","No one in this world could resist this silent invitation. It was the same for Zu An as well. He pounced over without any hesitation. Soon, he let out a surprised exclamation.","Diodora’s body was fresh!","He'd always thought that Firework’s ability was to transform into different people, but even when she transformed into Diodora, her physical condition would still remain the same. He had just ravaged Yani, so he would surely have left his mark.","Yet there were no marks on Diodora’s body whatsoever. It was as if she was a completely different person than before.","In the trial world, when Firework told him that having her was equivalent to having the entire world, he had snorted in disdain; but he was finally seeing the marvel in it. Indeed, no man could resist a woman like that.","Some time later, Diodora leaned into Zu An’s ear and whispered, “Do you want to try something more exciting?”","Zu An watched in confusion as the seductive elder vanished. She was replaced by an icy beauty—Tingxue!"]},{"number":2866,"title":"Chapter 2866: Chapter 2818: Dreamstar","paragraphs":["Zu An was startled. He was about to explain himself out of sheer instinct when it occurred to him that the woman before him wasn’t Tingxue, but rather Firework.","“Stop messing around- wu ...”","His lips were sealed before he could finish his sentence. Tingxue wrapped her arms around him as she asked, “Do you hate me that much?”","“Tingxue isn’t like that.” Zu An sighed.","Firework had impeccably captured Tingxue’s tone and expression, but the latter would never initiate intimacy with him on her own accord.","“It looks like you’re into icy beauties.” Tingxue’s voice turned cold and distant.","Zu An felt goosebumps. He had to admit that he was moved, but this was simply too weird. While he was hesitating, the window suddenly shattered, and a cold gleam flashed through the air.","Zu An was initially startled. When he saw it was Tingxue, he breathed a sigh of relief, but moments later, he began worrying yet again.","The ‘Tingxue’ on the bed laughed as she casually knocked away the incoming sword. “Why are you so angry? In the trial world, the two of you spent decades as a couple.”","“You are forbidden from taking on my appearance!” Tingxue had thought that when she regained her identity as a Nebula envoy, she would also regain her previous voidlike state of mind, thus freeing her from being disturbed by emotions.","She had come to speak with Zu An, only to see Firework flirting with Zu An in her form. How could she tolerate that? She immediately blew up.","The two of them fought ferociously in the cabin. Zu An trembled fearfully under his blanket.","How embarrassing! It was just a little kink play with Firework, but we got caught red-handed by the person in question.","Isabella and the others rushed to the scene and were shocked to see two Tingxues.","Firework started the fight smiling gleefully, but anger began to build up in her when Tingxue unleashed killing blow after killing blow. The shockwaves from their clash were so great that the other experts on the ship were forced to retreat.","Even the ship couldn’t withstand their fight and was sliced in half by sword ki.","Isabella and the other guests were speechless.","The guests flew into the sky as they watched the two women fight from the ocean to the sky. Even the world seemed to shudder before their might. What terrifying women they are. Anyone who marries them in the future will be in for a world of suffering.","“Big brother Zu, why are they fighting?” Isabella looked at Zu An with wide eyes. It feels like there’s some tea in here.","Zu An clutched the blanket tightly around his body. His legs were feeling chilly from the sea breeze. “It might have been because Firework impersonated Tingxue.”","Isabella was pure, but she wasn't naive. She could deduce what had happened from Zu An’s unkempt state. Big brother Zu and big sister Firework sure are wild.","All of a sudden, her face reddened. When doing it with big brother Zu, did big sister Firework turn into me as well...","Moments later, Firework backed out from the battle and said, “Enough, enough. There’s no point continuing this fight. I have no interest in putting on a show for these people.”","Tingxue sheathed her sword as well, knowing that Firework was stronger than her. It would be difficult for her to defeat Firework.","Isabella took this chance to step in and mediate between them. At the same time, she reached into her bag and tossed another tiny ship model out. She looked at the two women worriedly, as if pleading with them to not destroy this ship too.","Tingxue coldly turned around and returned to her room.","Zu An had planned to ask her if she had something to talk about with him, but he knew better than to approach her while she was still angry.","Alfred calmed the crowd down, and the guests returned to their rooms. Firework also took Zu An back into their room.","Isabella thought of telling the two not to use her appearance, but saying something like that proved to be too challenging for a maiden like her. She was also worried that the mischievous Firework would feel more inclined to use her appearance if she asked her not to do it.","In the end, she dragged her feet back to her room with a worried heart. Even as she lay on the bed, she couldn’t help but wonder what was happening between Zu An and Firework...","“AHHHH! It’s so embarrassing!” Isabella buried her head under her blanket while her legs kicked vigorously in mid-air.","...","The following morning, Zu An made his way to Tingxue’s room to ask her about the reason behind her visit yesterday. To his astonishment, she was nowhere to be found, but there was a note left on the table.","Zu An stared at the note—’ I’m leaving ’—with a sense of loss.","“Do you miss her that much? Should I conjure her for you?” Firework leaned against the window with an unreadable smile. In the blink of an eye, she had already transformed into a white-robed woman.","Zu An hurriedly stopped her. The thought of what happened yesterday made his face redden. No wonder Tingxue wants to leave. Playing like that is a bit too much.","“It’s not just Tingxue. I’m leaving too.”","“Ah?”","“I have some business to resolve.” Firework reined in her smile, giving rise to a solemn mood.","“Are you seeking vengeance?” Zu An was worried. “I can help you.”","“Don’t worry, I know what I’m doing. I won’t act recklessly.” Firework looked at Zu An as her expression softened. “I already know your world’s coordinates. I’ll look for you afterward.”","She leaned in and kissed him. By the time he snapped out of it, she was nowhere to be seen.","...","Days later, the ship returned to Dreamland’s hotel.","The people of Dreamland were already waiting to welcome Zu An. They were aware of how they'd been saved. No wonder Firework had to leave ahead of time. It would be uncomfortable for both sides if they met under such circumstances.","After the banquet, Zu An paid a visit to the real master of Dreamland to ask if their renowned foretelling ability could help him achieve the agenda of his trip.","Dreamland’s master replied apologetically, “Our prophecies consume karma. We have been under the control of that woman for so many years that we have expended all our karma. I’m afraid we won’t be able to accrue enough karma to fulfill your wish any time soon.”","Despite having expected as much, Zu An still couldn’t help but be disappointed.","Feeling apologetic, Dreamland’s master took out a rainbow jewel and gave it to Zu An. “Benefactor, you have saved all our lives. I don’t know how else I can repay you. This is the Dreamstar, a sacred treasure that has been passed down within Dreamland. It can be activated once per day to increase your luck. It might help you fulfill your wish faster.”","Zu An was astonished to hear about the Dreamstar’s effect.","Be it from his previous life’s games or everything that had happened after he had transmigrated to this world, he was well aware of how rare the ‘Luck’ stat was. To think that this treasure could raise a person’s luck! It was an invaluable item even if it could only be used once per day.","Knowing that the Dreamstar would be useful to him, he thanked Dreamland’s master and accepted the gift.","While he was returning to his room, he bumped into an excited Isabella, who said, “Big brother Zu, my father wishes to meet you.”","She grabbed his hand and dragged him to her room.","Zu An was speechless."]},{"number":2867,"title":"Chapter 2867: Chapter 2819: The Method to Rescue Her","paragraphs":["Zu An was confused as to what was going on. Isn’t it too early for me to meet her parents?","Isabella realized that she had gotten ahead of herself, so she hurriedly explained with a furious blush, “I asked my father about the items you needed, and my father replied that he might have a solution.”","Zu An was overjoyed to hear that. The Universal Conglomerate commands untold wealth and influence across the Myriad Worlds. It might just have a way to do that.","The two of them soon arrived in Isabella’s room.","Isabella had a watch on her wrist. She tapped on it a few times, and a hologram appeared. It showed a middle-aged man standing in a study room. He wore a collared robe embroidered with profound runes. He had electrifying eyes that gave him an air of sharpness and authority.","“Father, this is big brother Zu. Big brother Zu, this is my father.” Isabella gently tapped on the ground with the tip of her right foot. Her expression showed her excitement, but there was also a tinge of embarrassment.","Even through the hologram, the middle-aged man’s gaze was so piercing that it could bore a hole through Zu An.","Zu An had been through too much to be shaken up by that, though. “Pleased to meet you, uncle.”","A hint of approval flashed through the middle-aged man’s eyes. “Pleased to meet you. I am Aragorn Acadia. You have my gratitude for saving my cherished Isabella.”","Zu An smiled. “That was the result of our combined effort. Isabella helped me a lot as well.”","“It’s rare for a young man as accomplished as you to remain humble.” Aragorn smiled. He proceeded to ask a few questions about Zu An’s background, such as his background and his homeland, only stopping short of asking about his eight characters[1].","Zu An was perplexed, but he still politely replied to the questions. Of course, he made sure to leave out sensitive information.","“Father, we’re here to request your help. Why are you asking so many questions?” Isabella grumbled, unable to take it anymore.","Aragorn laughed. “I nearly forgot about our main agenda. Isabella has told me about your circumstances. Only a handful of extremely unique artifacts in the Myriad Worlds will allow you to access ancient spacetime fragments to search for your old friends. One of them is known as the Nature Jade.”","Zu An replied, “I have chanced upon a Nature Jade, and I successfully traveled back in time with it. But it turned into a stone after one use, and it’ll take a long time to regain its functions. Do you know of any other artifacts like it?”","Aragorn was surprised. “Artifacts used to travel through spacetime are rare. Even with our vast information network, we only know about the Nature Jade. In the first place, spacetime is a jurisdiction exclusive to universal deities. That said, the fact that you obtained such an artifact proves that you’re blessed with great fortune. I’m sure you’ll find another way in the future.”","Zu An couldn’t help but be disappointed. Is there no way except to request a universal deity’s help? The Deity of Memory said that she knows a way, but I don’t know what tribute I have to offer to satisfy her.","Isabella anxiously interjected, “Father, didn’t you say that you have solutions for the other two matters as well?”","Aragorn quietly sighed. My daughter, you’re favoring him over your own father. “Isabella told me you require the Agate of Enlightenment and One Life Water. Our Conglomerate has the Agate of Enlightenment; I’ll give it to you when you visit our headquarters. I’ve browsed through our records for One Life Water, and there is some information on it. Let me verify the authenticity of the information first before sharing it.”","Zu An was overjoyed. “I don’t know how I can thank you, uncle.” To think that my unexpected meeting with Isabella would resolve Mi Li’s quandary.","“Those things are valuable, but they are nothing compared to Isabella’s life,” Aragorn replied. “The third matter is a bit more troublesome.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. The third matter concerned Chu Chuyan staying in the Oblivion River for a thousand years.","“I thought of a few ideas, but only one of them is apt for your circumstances.” Aragorn didn’t beat around the bush. He opened a box beside him and retrieved an emerald card from within. He flicked his finger, and the card flew toward Zu An.","Zu An sensed a distortion in space before the card appeared before him. Astonished, he grabbed the card. Aragorn should be in the Universal Conglomerate’s headquarters, a long distance away from where we are. Yet he’s instantly transported an item over.","“Big brother Zu, that is the spatial transportation technology we have been developing. Unfortunately, it can only transport non-living items at the moment,” Isabella secretly explained to Zu An.","Aragorn’s expression darkened. Daughter, at this rate, you’re going to give away all our secrets!","Zu An smiled at Isabella before examining the card. It was extremely thin and had an emerald, jade-like color. It resembled collector’s edition cards in his previous life, though it was made of a far more valuable material.","Aragorn spoke up, “This is a super rare Emerald Card that wields the power to turn a living entity into a card. If you use it on your little sister, you can circumvent the rules of the Oblivion River and rescue her from it.”","“Little sister?” Zu An glanced at Isabella, and the latter averted her gaze. He figured that she dared not tell her father the truth. However, there was a more pressing question on his mind. “What does it mean to turn someone into a card? Do you mean it literally?”","“Yes, it literally turns a person into a card. Don’t worry, it won’t affect her day-to-day life. She can still function like a normal being.” Aragorn briefly paused before continuing his explanation, “Let me put it this way. Many entities might not necessarily be living beings. For instance, some beings are a stream of numbers in a supercomputer. We might also just be a simulation created by a higher-order being.”","Zu An understood what Aragorn was driving at. “What are the downsides of being turned into a card?”","“She’ll automatically be contracted to you, but that shouldn’t be a problem since you won’t hurt her. You can summon her to fight for you, though it’ll expend your energy. Also, the method for her to raise her strength will be different. She’ll have to consume special materials and cards to evolve...”","Zu An frowned. There were quite a few limitations.","Aragorn consoled, “You don’t have to worry. This card is one of the most precious ones, even within our Universal Conglomerate. It has a high power ceiling, so it won’t hinder your little sister from growing stronger. Personally, I think the downsides are a small price to pay to escape a thousand year imprisonment.”","“Thank you for your generosity.” No matter what, Zu An was glad he had found a way to save Chu Chuyan.","Aragorn laughed. “You saved Isabella and shared Death’s authority with her. What I gave you is nothing in comparison. I’ll need time to prepare the Agate of Enlightenment, so I’ll give it to you when you visit our headquarters. Hopefully, I will have confirmed the information about the One Life Water by then.”","1. Basically his birth date and time in the context of Chinese astrology. ☜"]},{"number":2868,"title":"Chapter 2868: Chapter 2820: A New Lease on Life","paragraphs":["After the call ended, Isabella turned to Zu An with an apologetic look. “Big brother Zu, I was planning to invite you to the Conglomerate as a guest, but you’re going to rescue big sister Chu, so I won’t hold you up.”","“It’s all thanks to you. You did me a huge favor. After I rescue Chuyan, I’ll pay a visit to the Conglomerate to express my gratitude.” Zu An was thrilled. He had resolved half of the three problems that had been troubling him.","Isabella nodded with a strained smile. She had hoped to visit Zu An’s world, but her father issued a strict order for her to return right away. Her father was worried about her after the dangers she had been through, and he wanted to inspect the Death authority in her as well.","She'd tried to buy some time, saying that she would return after visiting Zu An’s world, but Alfred stopped her. It was demeaning for someone of her standing to visit Zu An’s world when their relationship hadn’t been confirmed. Furthermore, she would be at a disadvantage against Zu An’s many lovers.","It would be wiser to wait for Zu An to first visit the Universal Conglomerate and confirm their relationship with her father before visiting his world.","Isabella was young, but offspring of major clans knew the importance of doing things the right way. It was just that her emotions had gotten the better of her. After Alfred’s reminder, she gradually calmed down and decided to return to the Conglomerate to wait for Zu An.","She pulled a starship model out of her bag and handed it to Zu An. “Big brother Zu, your world is too far away from Dreamland. You should take this starship instead. It might be smaller than a typical starship, but it’s a smart vehicle equipped with an auto navigation system. Our headquarters’ coordinates have also been entered into the system, so you can come visit me whenever you want.”","Zu An was completely flabbergasted by the insanity of her casually pulling out a starship and giving it away. “Alright, I’ll look for you after I’m done handling things on my side.”","“I’ll be waiting for you.” Isabella pursed her lips. Redness tinged her cheeks.","Zu An could already tell what was going on from her shy and expectant look.","Aragorn had said that he would hand him the Agate of Enlightenment when he visited their headquarters, but that was clearly an excuse. He could have delivered the item using their spatial transportation technology.","Ultimately, Aragorn wanted him to visit the Conglomerate to give his daughter greater leverage. Zu An wasn't averse to that. He thought that it was only right for a father to do that for his daughter.","That night, Zu An and Isabella chatted about the Conglomerate and the Cultivation World. The Myriad Worlds was a huge place, so neither of them knew when they would reunite after parting ways.","Isabella had been worried about Firework disguising as her to fool around with Zu An, so she hadn’t been sleeping well in the past few nights. Now that Zu An was beside her, she felt calmer than ever. At some point while chatting, she lay on his shoulder and fell asleep.","Looking at Isabella’s long eyelashes and delicate features, Zu An felt a rush of fondness for her. He took off his outerwear and draped it around her.","Initially, Alfred was still worried about them, using the pretext of delivering tea and snacks to check up on them. His heart was finally put at ease when he confirmed that Zu An had been maintaining propriety all this time.","Just like that, Zu An sat with Isabella by the beach, taking in her scent while gazing at the beautiful sky and serene ocean. His heart was tranquil and warm.","The following day, Isabella woke up and immediately blushed furiously. She wiped off her drool while feeling so embarrassed that she could almost cry. “I’m sorry, big brother Zu...”","How embarrassing! I fell asleep while chatting. Sleeping on a lover’s shoulder should have been something romantic, but I ended up getting drool all over big brother Zu’s shoulder!","She even wondered if she should hang herself to atone.","“It’s fine. I find it adorable. Hahaha.” Zu An chuckled.","“Big brother Zu~”","After Zu An consoled Isabella, it was finally time for the two of them to part ways. Isabella reluctantly waved her hand as Zu An boarded the starship and left Dreamland.","This starship was nowhere near as big as the one he had arrived on, but it was much faster. It leaped straight into a wormhole and traversed through folds in space. All Zu An needed to do was key in the Cultivation World’s coordinates, and the starship would automatically navigate its way over.","The starship also had all kinds of robots to service him. He could simply issue an order to the AI for them to get moving.","While traversing through a wormhole, a monster tried to attack the starship. Zu An didn’t even need to lift a finger for its self-defense system to obliterate the monster. Meanwhile, if a monster appeared that was exceptionally strong, the starship would go into stealth mode and make a detour.","Zu An was amazed by how advanced the Universal Conglomerate’s technology was. No wonder they are able to do business in so many worlds.","Little did Zu An know that Isabella had handed him a state-of-the-art starship equipped with the crystallization of the Universal Conglomerate’s most advanced technologies. Aragorn had given it to his daughter for her protection, but the latter had given it away just like that.","Months later, the starship finally reached the Cultivation World.","Zu An stopped the starship some distance away and stowed it away before discreetly entering the Netherworld. He didn’t want to deal with anyone else right now; he simply wanted to save Chu Chuyan as soon as possible.","When he reached the Bridge of Forgetfulness and saw the silhouette wrapped in a lotus, his heart quivered. “Chuyan...”","Chu Chuyan sensed his arrival and woke from her rest. She was delighted as well. “Ah Zu, you’re back?”","“Mm, I’m back!” Zu An flew onto the lotus pad and embraced her tightly.","Chu Chuyan tenderly embraced him back. “How was your trip? Did you encounter danger?”","“We can talk about that later. I have found a way to save you.” Zu An took out the Emerald Card and explained its use to her.","“Turning into a card?” Chu Chuyan was hesitant. These concepts were much too futuristic for her.","Zu An summarized the pros and cons for her. “I’ll leave it to you to decide whether you want to use this card or not.”","Chu Chuyan smiled. “Using it spares me from a thousand years of suffering, and I can be with you all the time. There’s no reason for me not to.”","Those words dispelled the final slivers of Zu An’s hesitation. He activated the Emerald Card using the method Aragorn had taught him. Soon, a gentle ray of light shrouded Chu Chuyan’s body.","Chu Chuyan quickly examined her body, but she didn’t sense any anomaly. Moments later, she morphed into a ray of light and entered the card.","The Oblivion River began to rage. Countless vengeful spirits stretched their hands forth to pull Chu Chuyan back.","Zu An’s expression turned cold. He exerted his authority as the Netherworld’s master to quell the vengeful spirits. However, the Oblivion River appeared to have gained a will of its own as it tried to re-imprison Chu Chuyan.","Zu An’s expression darkened. He couldn’t stop this phenomenon as the Netherworld’s master, as it was one of the fundamental laws governing the Netherworld.","The will scanned the Emerald Card, but it was unable to find its target. A long time later, it reluctantly dissipated.","Zu An was stunned. What’s this Emerald Card? It bypassed the Oblivion River’s influence! No wonder it’s one of the rarest cards in the Universal Conglomerate’s collection!","A beautiful woman wearing a light blue dress appeared in the previously empty card.","Zu An was so mesmerized that he gently stroked the card. I can see why there were so many card collectors in my previous life.","He suddenly felt a ripple in his heart. He quickly used the card’s summoning method. The card lit up before transforming into a beautiful lady.","But Chu Chuyan’s face was a little red. “Ah Zu, your touch made me feel itchy...”"]},{"number":2869,"title":"Chapter 2869: Chapter 2821: Their Disappearance","paragraphs":["Zu An felt both awkward and heartened. He pulled Chuyan into an embrace. “Chuyan, I’m glad that you’re fine!”","Chu Chuyan also hugged him tight. Even though the two of them occasionally met under the Oblivion Bridge, it didn’t change the fact that they had been apart for a long time now.","They had been a young couple, but they'd gone their different ways.","Chu Chuyan had become the Snow Lady in a distant spacetime and lost her memories. When she finally regained her memories, she'd sacrificed herself to save Zu An, resulting in her being trapped under the Oblivion Bridge for a thousand years.","She'd watched him search for a way to save her, and now, he'd finally succeeded. She understood how much he had to have gone through to achieve this feat.","The two of them embraced tightly as they shared their feelings of yearning.","Zu An told Chu Chuyan about what he had gone through in Dreamland. The latter remarked, “Ah Zu, you always have such mystical encounters. I doubt anyone else could have survived that crisis.”","“I was lucky.” The experience had been frightening for Zu An. A single misstep could have spelled their deaths.","“It wasn't just luck.” Chu Chuyan looked at him with tender eyes. “You mentioned that Miss Tingxue resembles my master a lot?”","“That’s right. I was shocked. I thought she was Xue... Cough cough , I mean, your master.”","Chu Chuyan noticed Zu An’s slip of the tongue, but she didn’t expose him. “Ah Zu, I wish to meet my master.”","“Alright. We ought to tell her that you’re free now.” Zu An missed Yan Xuehen as well. He did a quick scan of the Netherworld and sensed something amiss, but he was so overwhelmed with joy that he didn’t think deeper into it.","He wrapped his hand around Chu Chuyan’s slender waist and teleported to the White Jade Sect.","Now that he was back in the Cultivation World, he was finally a god once more. He could perform many unbelievable feats that would otherwise be impossible for him.","The White Jade Sect’s disciples stared at Zu An with curious eyes. There was hardly anyone in the world who hadn’t heard about Zu An, not to mention that he'd had a scandal with their sect leader not too long ago.","Most people were curious to know the truth.","Chu Chuyan was astonished. “To think that the White Jade Sect has developed this much!”","The disciples they encountered were much stronger than back when she was still in the sect. However, she attributed it to her prolonged absence and didn’t think too much about it.","Zu An, on the other hand, knew something was amiss. These disciples were growing too quickly. Did Yan Xuehen go all out training them in recent days? Also, I can’t help but notice that there are fewer disciples in the White Jade Sect than before.","He revealed his intention to meet Yan Xuehen.","The disciple who stepped forward to welcome him replied, “Sect Master Yan has gone to a Divine Palace.”","“Divine Palace?” Zu An was perplexed. Chu Chuyan was confused as well.","After further probing, Zu An finally understood what was going on.","Shortly after he left for Dreamland, mysterious powers had begun to appear. People had learned about the universal deities, who had projected their powers into the Cultivation World and founded their respective Divine Palaces.","Those who entered a Divine Palace and received recognition could be bestowed with a universal deity’s power.","These Divine Palaces had initially been met with skepticism, but the Shadow Group’s movements had already exposed the existence of the Deity of Annihilation. Countless coveted the incredible power wielded by the Annihilation worshipers.","Thus, people had begun entering the Divine Palace.","When someone finally emerged from the Divine Palace, wielding powers far surpassing their previous self, the world went crazy. The ultimate goal of all cultivators was to attain immortality. However, they had stagnated at the Earth Immortal rank for a long time.","Now that a higher level was within sight, how could they not be moved?","As a result, more and more people had entered the Divine Palaces. Cultivators had begun growing stronger at a rapid pace.","Yan Xuehen, as the leader of the orthodox faction, had investigated the Divine Palaces to get to the bottom of what was going on; but in the process of doing so, she'd been recognized by a universal deity and become an envoy. Her fortuitous encounter piqued the envy of many.","Zu An was startled. “Which universal deity did she become an envoy of?”","“The Deity of Nebula. It’s rumored that the Deity of Nebula is the strongest one of all. Hardly anyone has cleared the Nebula Divine Palace’s trial, let alone become an envoy,” the disciple replied with a tinge of pride and envy.","Zu An and Chu Chuyan exchanged shocked looks.","Zu An hurriedly asked, “Where is Sect Leader Yan now? Is she still in the Divine Palace?”","The disciple shook his head. “I’m not sure, but it’s rumored that the respective Divine Palaces send their most outstanding worshipers out into the Myriad Worlds for training. Perhaps our sect leader has gone out for training.”","Zu An and Chu Chuyan searched the White Jade Sect, and Yan Xuehen was indeed nowhere to be found.","After they left the White Jade Sect, Chu Chuyan said, “My master became a Nebula envoy. Ah Zu, do you think she’s Tingxue?”","Zu An replied with a bitter smile, “That’s very likely.”","That explains their identical appearance and the inexplicable intimacy I felt toward her. It turns out she was Yan Xuehen!","Becoming a Nebula envoy must have impaired her memories. She might have also been through other experiences in other times or worlds, similar to how Chuyan became the Snow Lady back then and forgot about herself and me.","“Do you know how to contact Miss Tingxue?” Chu Chuyan anxiously asked.","Zu An shook his head. Tingxue had left because she was furious about Firework using her appearance to mess around with him. Of course, there was no need to share such details with Chu Chuyan.","He calmed down, closed his eyes, and scanned the Cultivation World with his divine sense. Soon, he found ten Divine Palaces. They emanated formidable divine powers that belonged to their respective universal deities.","All the cultivators in the world were busy selecting the Divine Palace that aligned the most with their path. It was as if the Cultivation World had entered a golden era.","Zu An sighed. I merely took a trip, and my homeland got invaded.","Wonderpoint Worlds could isolate themselves to prevent intruders, but this time, the intruders were the universal deities, the strongest entities in the Myriad Worlds. On top of that, they didn’t resort to violent measures.","The people of the Cultivation World had embraced them willingly, which made it hard for the will of the world to stop them.","Zu An’s expression suddenly darkened. If Yan Xuehen is gone, what about the others?","He quickly scanned the places he had been to and discovered that his lovers were all gone!"]},{"number":2870,"title":"Chapter 2870: Chapter 2822: Unknown Whereabouts","paragraphs":["No wonder I felt something was amiss. This world has been ‘invaded’ by the universal deities! It’s just that I was in such a rush to save Chu Chuyan that it flew across my head.","He grabbed Chu Chuyan’s hand and teleported to the Lake of Hatred.","Chu Chuyan, as the successor of the orthodox faction, had dreamt of stomping the Devil Sect’s headquarters many times before. The old her would have never imagined coming here in such a manner.","It was no longer her first time experiencing it, but she was still shocked by Zu An’s ability to teleport thousands of kilometers in the blink of an eye. He'd become an enigmatic being even to her now.","She suddenly understood why the others had chosen to enter the Divine Palaces. They didn’t want to lag behind Zu An and become a burden to him.","The members of the Devil Sect were appalled to see two people appearing out of nowhere, and they immediately put up their guard. Only when the guards noticed Zu An did they finally reveal welcoming smiles.","There was no one in the world who didn’t know about the regent. On top of that, he was their saintess’ lover, and it was rumored that he had an affair with Sect Leader Yun as well.","“Where’s Sect Leader Yun?” Zu An asked.","The upper echelons of the Devil Sect exchanged meaningful looks. You’re asking for our sect leader instead of our saintess? That confirms it. They definitely are having an affair!","“Sect Leader Yun has begun traveling in search of a higher realm.”","“Which Divine Palace did she choose?”","“I don’t think Sect Leader Yun chose any of those Divine Palaces.”","“She didn’t?” Zu An was taken aback.","“Indeed. She claimed that none of the Divine Palaces in this world were suited for her, and that she wanted to forge her own path,” a higher-up of the Devil Sect replied. “That’s what she told us to tell you when you returned.”","Zu An fell silent. He had scanned the ten Divine Palaces that had appeared in this world. They belonged to Memory, Chaos and Enigma, Annihilation, Nebula, Bliss and Desire, Order, Longevity, Reproduction, Knowledge, and Protection.","Death and Love and Beauty were conspicuously absent. I guess the Deity of Love and Beauty has died as well.","If Yun Jianyue didn’t think any of these ten paths were suited for her, what else could she have chosen?","“As expected of Sect Leader Yun. She wants to forge her own path.” Chu Chuyan was awed.","“That sounds like her, but it's easier said than done,” Zu An replied with a bitter smile.","The twelve universal deities were lofty entities towering over the Myriad Worlds; it wouldn’t be easy to forge another path outside of theirs. It was also uncertain how the existing universal deities would take to that. The Deity of Death had died because the other universal deities thought that his path threatened them.","“I believe that Sect Leader Yun will succeed.” Chu Chuyan turned to the Devil Sect’s members and asked, “Where’s Honglei?”","“Our saintess has been selected by the Longevity Divine Palace and is currently training there.” The members of the Devil Sect felt wistful. Chu Chuyan and Qiu Honglei had been the representatives of the orthodox faction and the Devil Sect, respectively. They were once fated to be rivals, yet they were now as close as sisters.","“The Longevity Divine Palace...” Zu An wasn’t surprised. Qiu Honglei had been revived by an immortal medicine. That fortuitous encounter could be the reason she'd been chosen by the Deity of Longevity.","As the two of them walked out of the Devil Sect, Chu Chuyan suddenly said, “Ah Zu, I’d like to head home to take a look. I wonder if my parents, Huanzhao, and Youzhao have visited any of the Divine Palaces.”","Zu An nodded. It’s about time to return to the capital.","In the blink of an eye, they teleported to the capital’s Chu manor. Thanks to Zu An, the entire Chu clan had moved to the capital. Only the second house and the third house remained in Brightmoon City to manage the family business.","But the Chu manor felt much colder than usual. Back then, one could hear Chu Huanzhao causing a commotion in the backyard even from a distance away.","Zu An scanned the Chu manor, but he couldn’t find Huanzhao or Youzhao. Even Murong Qinghe had disappeared. However, there was still a familiar face in the manor.","He led Chu Chuyan into the inner area. A shriek suddenly echoed.","Black streaks appeared on Chu Chuyan’s face. “Mother, it’s us.”","Qin Wanru, who had retreated to the wall, was both shocked and delighted. “That scared me! The two of you suddenly appeared out of nowhere!”","She quickly snapped out of it and asked with a quivering voice, “Chuyan, are you alright now?”","“Ah Zu saved me.”","Despite her cold personality, Chu Chuyan felt choked up. Too many things had happened ever since she went into closed-door training and somehow traveled across spacetime to become the Snow Lady. It felt like an eternity had passed since their last meeting.","“My good daughter!” Qin Wanru rushed forward to embrace Chu Chuyan.","The mother and daughter sobbed while embracing each other. It was a long time before they finally calmed down.","Chu Chuyan asked about what had happened to their household.","Qin Wanru replied while wiping her tears, “They have gone to the Divine Palaces to train. Your father went to the Order Divine Palace, whereas Youzhao and Huanzhao went to the Protection Divine Palace.”","“Why didn’t you go too?” Chu Chuyan asked out of curiosity.","Qin Wanru’s face reddened, but she quickly regained her confidence and replied, “This family needs someone to keep things together. Otherwise, there would have been no one to welcome you when you returned.”","Zu An and Chu Chuyan exchanged looks. They could see the amusement in each other’s eyes. Qin Wanru did have some aptitude for cultivation, but it was nowhere near enough to catch the eye of the universal deities.","“Where’s Qinghe?” Zu An asked.","Qin Wanru rolled her eyes. He must already know what happened that night for him to be so concerned about Murong Qinghe. “Qinghe suffered a blow when she failed the Divine Palace’s trial, so she began traveling the world to train herself up. I don’t know where she is currently.”","“She didn’t clear the trial?” Chu Chuyan was perplexed. Given Murong Qinghe’s aptitude, that didn’t seem too plausible.","Zu An was taken aback as well. He had scanned the world with his divine sense earlier but didn’t find Murong Qinghe. The only place his divine sense couldn’t penetrate were the Divine Palaces, so he thought that she was training in one of the Divine Palaces.","“We were perplexed as well. Only heaven knows what the criteria for those Divine Palaces are. Even I failed their trial,” Qin Wanru blurted out the truth.","But Chu Chuyan was in no mood to make fun of her. She noticed Zu An’s expression and asked, “Could Qinghe have gone down the same road as Sect Leader Yun?”","Zu An shook his head. “I didn’t sense Yun Jianyue in this world, either.”","If they aren’t in the Divine Palaces or in this world, could they have...","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He teleported to the Netherworld and opened the Netherworld Book of Life and Death. Only after confirming that their souls hadn’t entered the Netherworld did he finally breathe a sigh of relief.","He returned to the Chu manor and told Chu Chuyan what he'd just done.","Chu Chuyan consoled him, “Ah Zu, you don’t need to worry too much about them. They might have entered another world like me. There are many fortuitous encounters in this world.”","“I can only hope that’s the case.” This encounter made Zu An more anxious to investigate the whereabouts of his other lovers.","Chu Chuyan followed him.","Watching as the duo vanished into thin air, Qin Wanru murmured enviously, “Now that she has her lover, she doesn’t care about me. No wonder they say daughters can’t be counted on.”","Zu An and Chu Chuyan teleported to different places, only to realize that Yun Jianyue and Murong Qinghe weren’t the exceptions. Pei Mianman, Shang Liuyu, Shang Hongyu, Yu Yanluo, Bi Linglong, Snow, and Ji Xiaoxi hadn’t entered any of the Divine Palaces either.","Even Ji Dengtu and Xie Xiu were nowhere to be found."]},{"number":2871,"title":"Chapter 2871: Chapter 2823: Divine Palace","paragraphs":["Zu An scanned the world with his divine sense. He confirmed that the others had entered Divine Palaces aligned with their paths.","Qiu Honglei had entered the Longevity Divine Palace due to the immortal medicine.","Suolun Shi and Xie Daoyun had entered the Memory Divine Palace. Those two had become close, especially since the latter had taken on the identity of the ancient Fiend races’ saintess. Xie Daoyun specialized in the brush and runes, so her choice made sense.","Qi Yaoguang and Tang Tian’er had entered the Chaos and Enigma Divine Palace. Qi Yaoguang’s astrology was an offshoot of the Enigma path, so that was the most suitable path for her.","Sang Qien and Kong Nanwu had joined the Knowledge Divine Palace. They had always been sharp-witted, so it wasn’t surprising for them to have been chosen by the Deity of Knowledge.","Although, Zu An was surprised by Yun Yuqing and Zheng Dan joining the Order Divine Palace. Since she was the descendant of an ancient Celestial Emperor and sought to re-establish the Celestial Court’s order, Yun Yuqing could have chosen the Deity of Order, but what about Zheng Dan? What had prompted her onto the path of Order?","The Little Fiend Empress, Empress Dowager Liu Ning, and Bluefield Country’s leader Tushan Yu had joined the Bliss and Desire Divine Palace. That wasn’t a surprise, since all three had seduction inscribed in their very blood. Their strengths would be maximized on this path.","On that note, he'd thought that Yun Jianyue and Qiu Honglei would join the Bliss and Desire Divine Palace as well, since the two of them practiced the art of bewitching. He was bewildered that they'd gone down a different path instead.","Of course, the path of Bliss and Desire wasn't just about desire—there was bliss, too.","While showing little to no desire, Firework had pretended to be a Love and Beauty worshiper,. What stood out more was her bubbly personality, and it looked as if she could be happy without anything.","Though she'd turned out to be extremely lustful afterward, especially as Yani and Diodora...","Bai Rouxue and the Chu sisters had joined the Protection Divine Palace. Huanzhao and Youzhao had been protecting the Chu clan in their own ways, whereas Bai Rouxue had been protecting her child. They were indeed suited for that path.","It astonished Zu An that Little Blue and Little White had joined the Reproduction Divine Palace. He'd thought that it was mostly insects that gave birth to entire nests that joined the Reproduction Divine Palace. He still remembered how slender Little Blue and Little White were. They didn’t seem to be the childbearing type.","Zhao Xiaodie had joined the Annihilation Divine Palace.","Zu An instinctively disliked the Annihilation Divine Palace, possibly because he had fought with Annihilation worshipers several times now. Did she join the Annihilation Divine Palace to acquire power to avenge her father, King Qi?","The world had learned about the Shadow Group’s rebellion, as well as the astounding power Zhao Yuan and the others obtained from the Deity of Annihilation. Thus, many evildoers and the ambitious were drawn to the Annihilation Divine Palace, hoping to obtain power.","Apart from his lovers, many people whom Zu An knew had entered the Divine Palaces most suited for their paths. However, Zu An didn’t have the spare energy to consider the others. He was more worried about where Pei Mianman and the others had gone.","“Chuyan, if you have to choose, which Divine Palace will you go for?”","Chu Chuyan pondered for a moment before replying, “My first thought was to join the Nebula Divine Palace, since I practice the Unshakable Daoist Manual. But when I think about how my master, despite her cultivation, forgot about everything and even herself, I don’t think the Nebula Divine Palace is suited for me anymore.”","She gently touched her lover’s cheek. “I've already lost you once. I don’t want to lose you a second time.”","Just recalling how she had forgotten about everything as the Snow Lady filled her with fear.","Zu An pulled her into his arms, and the two of them shared their warmth. It was a while later before they began discussing the others.","“Don’t worry about them too much, Ah Zu. Their disappearance might not necessarily be detrimental to them. They might have stumbled upon other fortuitous encounters. There might be other paths in this world other than those twelve. Besides, aren’t there two Divine Palaces that didn’t appear here?”","Zu An knew that the Death Divine Palace would never appear, so the only mystery left was the Love and Beauty Divine Palace.","It was possible for the others to be summoned by the Deity of Love and Beauty, but Ji Dengtu? Impossible.","“I’ll go take a look at the Divine Palaces.” Zu An figured that he needed to take a trip there to gather answers.","Chu Chuyan was worried. “Ah Zu, you aren’t just a mortal now. If you enter their Divine Palaces carelessly, you may draw a universal deity’s gaze. This is too dangerous.”","Not only was Zu An the Cultivation World’s god, he was also the envoy of two universal deities. The other universal deities wouldn't necessarily welcome him visiting their Divine Palaces. If so, he could stand to lose his life.","“Don’t worry, I’ll visit the Memory Divine Palace and the Chaos and Enigma Divine Palace first. I won’t risk my life.” Zu An knew that some universal deities harbored a grudge against him for unraveling their plans in the Deity of Death’s trial, so he decided to first check out the ones he was on good terms with.","Chu Chuyan breathed a sigh of relief. She initially wanted to visit the Divine Palaces with Zu An, but the latter was concerned about the dangers, and instructed her to stay home and accompany their mother first.","Zu An bade farewell to the mother and daughter before teleporting to the Chaos and Enigma Divine Palace. Looking at the grand structure, he could see why the appearance of the universal deities had sent the entire world into a frenzy.","No human could have created such a grand structure. It had to be a divine vestige.","As he approached the Divine Palace, someone quickly stepped forward to stop him. “Only the most devout worshipers of Chaos and Enigma can enter.”","Not everyone in the world recognized Zu An.","Zu An didn’t make things difficult for the other party. He revealed his aura as the envoy, and everyone in the surroundings widened their eyes in astonishment. Only a universal deity can wield such pure divine power. Could he possibly be the great Deity of Chaos and Enigma?","Zu An strutted in. This time, no one dared to stop him.","The palace had a high ceiling. Two rows of enormous statues holding massive horns lined the paths. Upon sensing a guest, the statues blew a deep melody.","Zu An sensed interweaving laws in the palace. This appeared to be how the Divine Palaces tested if the guest was their worshiper, though just being a worshiper was insufficient. One had to be of sufficient aptitude before the Divine Palace would take one in.","An ordinary mortal would only feel an urge to grovel on the ground and worship whatever was inside the Divine Palace.","There were lofty figures in the Divine Palace who appeared to have assumed the role of cardinals. Upon seeing an intruder, they were about to shout at Zu An when they sensed the pure divine power flowing from him. They immediately lowered their heads while whispering among themselves to figure out his identity.","Zu An couldn’t be bothered with them. He walked straight up to the centermost divine idol. That was the highest area of the Divine Palace. Murals were inscribed on the walls and the ceiling, looking both chaotic yet enigmatic.","Zu An stared at the idol in astonishment. This was his first time seeing Mi Li’s appearance.","Her outline appeared to be feminine, but her facial features were obscured. Universal deities wouldn’t allow others to casually look at their faces. Ordinary beings couldn’t bear the karma of witnessing a universal deity’s appearance either.","“O great Deity of Chaos and Enigma, your envoy expresses his most sincere respect to you...” Zu An prayed in hopes of summoning the Deity of Chaos and Enigma, but to his surprise, he received no response, no matter how he called out to her."]},{"number":2872,"title":"Chapter 2872: Chapter 2824: Old Friend","paragraphs":["Zu An was perplexed. Were these Divine Palaces not constructed by the universal deities?","He quickly rejected that notion. Other beings couldn’t hope to replicate the grandeur of these Divine Palaces. Putting all things aside, he was extremely familiar with the aura in the Chaos and Enigma Divine Palace.","The auras coming from Memory, Chaos and Enigma, and Annihilation—powers he had come into contact with—were on the dot. There was no faking them.","“Did something happen to Mi Li?” Zu An halted that train of thought right away. It was blasphemous to harbor such thoughts in her Divine Palace. How could danger possibly befall a lofty universal deity?","He called the person who appeared to be the pope. The latter bowed to him respectfully. “May I know who you are?”","Someone had already recognized Zu An as the regent, but now that universal deities had descended upon this world, such secular power meant nothing. The regent was still the number one powerhouse in the Cultivation World, but he was nothing compared to the universal deities.","The pope was only showing respect to Zu An because of the pure Chaos and Enigma power flowing from him. He even wondered if Zu An was the universal deity himself.","Zu An saw through his thoughts. He revealed his Time Annal and replied, “I am an envoy chosen by the great Deity of Chaos and Enigma.”","After feeling the vast power radiating from the Time Annal, no one dared to doubt Zu An. They zealously fell to their knees and greeted, “Paying respect to the esteemed Lord Envoy!”","They were thrilled. This was the first time any envoy had emerged from the Divine Palaces. Doesn’t this signify that Chaos and Enigma is the strongest path of all, and that we have made the right decision?","Zu An sighed. No wonder everyone wants to become a god. I didn’t receive such earnest respect even when I was the almighty regent. He reined in his thoughts and asked about the situation. Soon, he got a good grasp of what was going on.","The Divine Palaces chose their own worshipers. Being able to enter the Divine Palace meant receiving the recognition of the respective universal deity.","The path Zu An had walked earlier was a test. It would have been an ordeal for mortals to take even a single step forward. The closer a worshiper could approach the universal deity’s idol, the more devoted and aligned they were to their respective path. That signified greater blessings and more divine power bestowed.","These people had become the de facto leaders of the Divine Palace because they came closest to the Deity of Chaos and Enigma’s divine idol. Even so, they had only been able to greet the divine idol from afar. None of them had been able to walk right up to the divine idol as Zu An did.","They had a deep impression of Qi Yaoguang and Tang Tian’er. Both had walked closer to the divine idol than the rest of them, but they'd showed no interest in managing the Divine Palace and had instead taken on a trial to obtain greater power.","They led Zu An toward an altar beside the divine idol. There was a spatial vortex on the altar. Most worshipers would choose to enter and undergo a trial in hopes of obtaining greater power.","This was the greatest benefit the ten Divine Palaces offered to their worshipers. Anyone who survived the trial would obtain world-changing power, though more often than not, they didn’t.","Those who returned said that the trials were so dangerous that one could die at any moment. Furthermore, each individual was transported to a different trial world, so it was impossible to tap into the experience of predecessors.","The survival rate was only 10%, but the allure of greater power still prompted many cultivators to dive in, especially the older ones who had reached a bottleneck. Those people were already on the verge of death anyway, so it was worthwhile to take this chance. If they succeeded, they could potentially extend their lifespan significantly.","Besides that, there were also ambitious ones like Qi Yaoguang and Tang Tian’er.","Zu An stepped into the spatial vortex without warning. None of the Divine Palace’s upper echelons had time to stop him at all. They exchanged shocked looks, knowing how dangerous the trial was. What if Lord Envoy dies in there...","Before they could begin worrying, the spatial vortex flickered, and Zu An returned from within. That awed all of them. “No wonder he’s the envoy...”","Zu An ignored the bootlicking and fell into deep thought. He had just inspected the spatial vortex in person—it was a mysterious portal that randomly teleported one into different dungeons. That explained why those who entered had different experiences.","Were it not for his deep comprehension of spatial transformation laws, he wouldn’t have been able to return that easily. Universal deities sure are amazing. They can link a single spatial vortex to countless dungeons. That makes it nigh impossible to find an individual in there.","Seeing that he wouldn’t be able to get more news here, Zu An took a step forward and appeared before the Memory Divine Palace next.","Tapping on his prior experience, he marched straight up to the Deity of Memory’s divine idol.","The Memory Divine Palace’s layout and murals were different from that of the Chaos and Enigma Divine Palace. It resembled the starry sky, and Meng’s divine idol held a book and a brush while observing the sky.","Just like before, Meng’s divine idol had no facial features, though her outline was on the feminine side. Zu An wasn't surprised by that, as he had accidentally caught a glimpse of her with the Eye of Insight. She was likely a female deity.","“O great Deity of Memory, your most faithful envoy has come to pay respects to you...” Zu An formulaically greeted the divine idol. He harbored no hope that Meng would respond, since that had been the case with Mi Li earlier.","A cold voice replied from the void, “Most faithful? I doubt that.”","Zu An was both surprised and overjoyed. He could tell it was Meng. He hurriedly bowed and said, “O great Deity of Memory, you have finally responded to me!”","“You came to look for me because Mi Li ignored you?” The starry sky in the ceiling flickered as if a supreme entity was gazing upon mortal beings.","Cold sweat gushed down Zu An’s back. “I went there to investigate my friends’ whereabouts. I seek the Deity of Memory’s pardon.”","The Deity of Memory seemed to accept that reason. “Speak. Why did you summon me?”","“I’d like to ask about the sudden appearance of the Divine Palaces in this world,” Zu An carefully asked.","“Are you dissatisfied that your territory has been invaded?”","“I dare not to harbor such thoughts. It’s my greatest honor to have the universal deities shower my homeland with their miracles.”","“Insincere words.”","“...”","“We currently require more power from worshipers. We have already scattered our radiance upon discovered worlds across the universes. Your world is a little unique, so there are more Divine Palaces than usual.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. The universal deities are already at the top of the Myriad Worlds. Why would they require more power? He knew that the other party wouldn’t explain this matter to him, so he asked, “May I know what’s special about my world?”","“A world born at the fringes of a universe should have never developed into such a rare Wonderpoint World. On top of that, I sense traces of an old friend in this world. The other fellows might have sensed it, too.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Who could that ‘old friend’ of the universal deities be?"]},{"number":2873,"title":"Chapter 2873: Chapter 2825: Fortune Palace","paragraphs":["Sensing Zu An’s thoughts, the Deity of Memory said, “You need not concern yourself with that.”","Zu An decided to change his strategy and asked from another direction. “May I know if there’s any way I can be of service to you?”","The stars in the ceiling flickered as if in contemplation. A while later, the Deity of Memory said, “The universal deities have bumped into some trouble recently. An apocalypse is approaching, and Annihilation has grown exceptionally powerful. Mi Li likely didn’t respond to you because she’s busy dealing with this matter.”","“Apocalypse?” Zu An struggled to understand the situation. “Universal deities are already at the pinnacle of the Myriad Worlds. Why would they fear an apocalypse?”","Speaking of which, he had encountered an apocalypse before, such as the destruction of the Monster World. However, he'd later learned that the so-called apocalypse was just Annihilation’s subordinates. That was nowhere near enough to threaten a universal deity.","“It’s different from the apocalypse you encountered. This is anapocalypse from behind the World Gate...” The Deity of Memory paused, reluctant to go into details with Zu An.","But Zu An wouldn’t let such a good opportunity slip through his fingers. “As your most faithful worshiper, I’m devoted to sharing Memory’s greatness across the Myriad Worlds and increasing your number of followers, so as to contribute whatever little I can.”","“My most faithful worshiper?” The stars in the ceiling flickered. “Not at all. You are my most cunning worshiper.”","Zu An was speechless.","“But I do have a task to entrust to you.”","“O great Deity of Memory, please ask anything of me. I won’t hesitate to dive into a sea of flames if you command me so!”","“Something huge is going to happen at the Universal Conglomerate soon. Head there in your capacity as Memory’s envoy and record this event.”","“May I know what that huge event is?”","“I wouldn’t need you to witness it if I knew.”","“...”","The Deity of Memory continued, “While universal deities can foresee the rough outline of an event, there are several universal deities in the Myriad Worlds. How the event will unfold and the eventual outcome remain as variables.”","“Using the terms of your Cultivation World, the great dao has fifty trajectories. 49 can be divined, but the last falls on human deeds.”","Zu An nodded in realization. Most events were set in stone, but there was still a single variable that simply couldn’t be grasped.","“O great Deity of Memory, it is my utmost honor to be able to serve you. However, I have lost contact with my friends, and I wish to know how they are faring.” Fearing that the other party would misunderstand, he quickly explained, “It is not my intention to talk terms. I just fear that I won’t be able to put my whole heart into fulfilling your task if I’m constantly worried about them.”","The stars in the ceiling flickered. “They are facing trials in their lives. You need not worry about them. They have their own pursuit as well, and they don’t want to remain under your protection permanently.”","Zu An’s heart initially skipped a beat when he heard they were facing trials, but his tension loosened up after hearing the following words. Indeed, they were the most outstanding women in their fields before becoming my lovers. I can’t think of them as flowers in a greenhouse.","“Thank you for your advice. I know what I should do now.”","“Good. If you accomplish this task, I’ll tell you how you can find your friends who are lost in spacetime.”","Zu An was delighted to hear that. “Thank you, o great Deity of Memory.”","He was glad to have found a clue. He would feel a prick in his heart whenever he thought about the ancient Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","“Don’t bother going to the other Divine Palaces, especially the Annihilation Divine Palace. Most of them aren’t favorable toward you. You might be killed if you show your face before them,” the Deity of Memory warned.","“Thank you for your reminder.” Zu An wiped off his cold sweat.","He had considered checking out the other Divine Palaces, thinking that this was a good chance to experience the other universal deities’ powers. Perhaps it wouldn't have been a good idea elsewhere, but this was his turf. Surely the danger level would be lowered, he'd thought.","But it seemed that he'd still been underestimating the universal deities.","Annihilation had to truly hate him. Were it not for the Memory’s and Chaos and Enigma’s protection, he could well have suffered divine retribution by now.","The other universal deities were aware of his affiliation, so they wouldn’t harbor goodwill toward ‘heretics’ like him.","Soon, the stars receded, leaving behind just the starry sky mural and the divine idol.","Before backing off, Zu An bowed to the divine idol once more. Then, he casually dealt with the upper echelons of the Memory Divine Temple before teleporting back to the Chu manor in the capital.","Chu Chuyan was busy chatting with her mother when she saw Zu An and excitedly rushed forward to welcome him back.","Qin Wanru felt stifled when she saw how naturally the two of them ignored her and walked away. It’s one thing for my daughter to side with someone else, but Ah Zu isn’t talking much with me nowadays anymore.","“How was it?” Chu Chuyan was oblivious to her mother’s grudge.","Zu An shared his findings with her. He filtered away information regarding the universal deities, lest it brought her danger.","“Do you intend to head to the Universal Conglomerate next?”","“Yes.”","Zu An felt wistful. He had just rejected Isabella’s invitation not too long ago in Dreamland. To think that they would reunite so quickly.","“I’ll come too.”","“???”","“Are you worried that I’ll stand between you and the big miss?” Chu Chuyan was still smiling, but Zu An felt a cold wind blowing at him.","“Of course not. I’m just worried about your safety,” Zu An replied awkwardly.","“Ah, I nearly forgot. You’re heading there to ask for their daughter’s hand in marriage. It isn’t apt for you to bring me along,” Chu Chuyan grumbled.","“Isabella knows about you...” Zu An replied sheepishly. Isabella’s father and the Universal Conglomerate could be displeased if Zu An brought Chu Chuyan along, and that could affect his relationship with Isabella and the gathering of the rare materials required to forge Mi Li’s body.","Above all, something that the Deity of Memory described as huge was going to happen to the Universal Conglomerate. Clearly, the trip would be fraught with danger.","“We've barely reunited after being apart for so long. I didn’t think that we would part ways so quickly.” Chu Chuyan’s expression darkened.","Zu An’s heart quivered. It might have only been a few years for him, but it had been ages for Chu Chuyan. With that thought in mind, he grabbed his lover’s hand and said, “Come with me.”","“Won’t I get in the way of your business?” Chu Chuyan was both surprised and delighted.","“Who knows? You might even be able to lend me a helping hand.” Zu An decided not to think too much. The Deity of Memory was right. He couldn’t be obsessed with thinking about how he could protect everyone. Chu Chuyan was a prodigy in her own right. Overcoming danger was also a fortuitous encounter to her.","Besides, the last thing he wanted was for her to disappear like the others when he returned. He couldn’t risk losing her again.","He went to the Sang manor to visit his daughter and made a series of arrangements before setting off to the Universal Conglomerate. He boarded Isabella’s starship and set the destination to be the Universal Conglomerate’s headquarters—the Contract Galaxy, Fortune Palace!"]},{"number":2874,"title":"Chapter 2874: Chapter 2826: Speak of the Devil","paragraphs":["Isabella had entered the location of the Universal Conglomerate’s headquarters into the spaceship’s system in hopes that Zu An could visit her soon. All he had to do was to give the order for the spaceship to transport him to the legendary Contract Galaxy.","Chu Chuyan was amazed. “That big miss sure is meticulous to have prepared this for you.”","Zu An pulled her into his embrace. “Are you jealous?”","“Why would I be jealous? I’m more than happy that someone treats you so well. I’d rather everyone in the world treats you this kindly.” Despite her words, Chu Chuyan struggled free from his embrace.","You have successfully trolled Chu Chuyan for +55... +55... +55...","And you say you aren’t angry.","To distract her, Zu An introduced the spaceship’s functions to her.","Chu Chuyan was initially annoyed at how Zu An was excitedly introducing a gift he'd received from another woman to her, but this was her first time coming into contact with something from a technological world. It didn’t take long for her curiosity to be piqued.","She strolled around the spaceship, examining everything that was new to her. Her movements were extremely careful, as she was worried of accidentally touching something that would cause the spaceship to go haywire.","Zu An couldn’t help but chuckle.","“Don’t worry, this spaceship is sentient. Feel free to ask anything of its AI, Aphrodite. You can also ask her to explain anything that confuses you,” he said while calling the spaceship’s AI.","A second later, a hologram of a beautiful woman dressed in professional clothes appeared. She had an amicable smile and a sweet voice. “Aphrodite. A pleasure to be at your service.”","Chu Chuyan jolted in shock. Zu An explained to her what kind of entity Aphrodite was. She remarked, “You’re truly beautiful.”","“I’m grateful for your compliment, miss. You’re gorgeous, too. According to the data from the Myriad Worlds, you're definitely within the top percentile in the looks department.”","Chu Chuyan had been complimented by countless people from a young age, so much so that such compliments rarely fazed her unless they were from Zu An. However, being complimented by a virtual assistant filled her up with joy. The other party was just a hologram devoid of human emotions, judging fairly solely by data.","Aphrodite led Chu Chuyan around the spaceship, explaining how the spaceship functioned. The two of them ended up leaving Zu An behind.","Chu Chuyan looked like a little girl who had found a new toy. Zu An looked at her with a gentle smile. She'd always assumed a cold demeanor, lacking the vibrancy that a young woman of her age ought to have. He thought this was a good thing for her.","All of a sudden, Zu An sensed something. His pendant glowed, and Jing Teng appeared on the spaceship.","“I nearly suffocated to death. You left me alone for so long. Did a dog eat your conscience?”","You have successfully trolled Jing Teng for +110... +110... +110...","Zu An looked at her black stockings. Yup, it’s the younger sister. He'd already gotten to the bottom of their maneuvers.","The big sister, White Jing Teng, was graceful and dignified. She cared a lot about her appearance and was often reluctant to voice her thoughts aloud. At times like this, she would send her little sister, the demoness, out. No matter what she says, it has nothing to do with me, the big sister.","Black Jing Teng jumped onto Zu An and bit his shoulder. “You promised to cultivate with us to help us recover, but you didn’t visit us once even though we've hibernated for so long. Where did your credibility go?”","Zu An responded with a bitter smile, “I was in a lot of danger up until recently. I didn’t have the time to visit you.”","Black Jing Teng looked around. “You look free to me now. Ten times. Make it up to me in a single shot.”","Zu An was stunned.","Before he could respond, Black Jing Teng was already clutching to him like an octopus. I feel like all they want is my body and not me.","Despite thinking that, it didn’t take him long to be riled up by the Jing Teng sisters. The little sister was passionate and daring, whereas the big sister was dignified and demure. Yet the two of them were the same entity. This contrast was fatally charming...","He started to get in the mood, but this wasn’t the right time for that!","While they were tugging at each other, Zu An sensed something and looked at the doorway. Chu Chuyan was looking at him with a frosty face.","“Looks like I came at the wrong time.”","While exploring the spaceship with Aphrodite, she'd come across interesting things and felt an urge to share them with her lover. Yet, when she returned, she saw Black Jing Teng riding him....","Granted, he was pushing her back, but if he was truly reluctant, given his strength, there was no way she could have climbed on him in the first place.","You’re going to have sexy time with other women even in this short interval?","You have successfully trolled Chu Chuyan for +66... +66... +66...","“Ah, it’s big sister Chuyan!” Black Jing Teng said with a grin.","Chu Chuyan raised her eyebrows. You’re old enough to be my great grandmother. Nevertheless, she was pleased that Black Jing Teng was willing to recognize her position by calling her big sister, and her cold expression loosened up a little.","“You continue,” she said before turning around to leave.","“Big sister Chuyan, why don’t you join us?” Black Jing Teng beckoned her over.","“???”","“I don’t mind. Good things are meant to be shared,” Black Jing Teng added.","Even if you don’t mind, I mind!","Unable to take it anymore, Chu Chuyan slammed the door shut.","You have successfully trolled Chu Chuyan for +211... +211... +211...","She went to the link bridge and looked at the vast space outside the window, feeling a little empty inside.","Just then, a gentle voice asked, “Are you angry?”","She turned around and saw her lover looking at her tenderly. Startled, she asked, “So fast?”","Then, her face reddened. What am I saying?","Black streaks appeared across Zu An’s face. “My Chuyan is angry. Of course I needed to come over right away to take a look.”","“What about Jing Teng?”","“Don’t worry, I’ve placated her. She’s an understanding person.” Despite Zu An’s words, he'd spent a great deal of effort and accepted a list of unfair conditions before she finally let it go.","“I guess I’m not as understanding,” Chu Chuyan blurted out, only to regret it right away.","She hadn't thought she would be such a childish person as to throw a tantrum over this, but they had been apart for so long. She'd thought that now that they had finally reunited, they could finally enjoy some private couple time, only to catch Zu An messing around with another woman. It was inevitable that she felt displeased.","While Chu Chuyan was in a daze, Zu An lifted her up.","“Hey, what are you doing? Put me down.”","Zu An would be a fool to listen to her right now. He lifted her and carried her back to their room.","Chu Chuyan could already guess what was going to happen. She felt embarrassed and flustered. “I don’t want to go there...”","He had just messed with Black Jing Teng there. It felt weird to do it there.","Zu An paused momentarily before chuckling. “You want to do it here? Fine by me.”","Chu Chuyan was startled. His movements caused her cheeks to swiftly redden. “That’s not what I mean... Ah....”","She bit her lips and rained her fists on her lover, expressing her dissatisfaction at his roughness. But as his movements got gentler, her body slowly relaxed. They had been apart for so long that every bit of intimacy meant a lot to them.","Looking at the spaceship’s transparent windows and the brilliant galaxy outside, Chu Chuyan covered her face. She hadn't thought he would mess around in a place like this. How is this any different from doing it in public?","It might have been due to their prolonged separation or the unique environment that Chu Chuyan felt extremely sensitive. She could only continuously console herself that no one could see them since they were in the middle of space.","But there was a famous saying called ‘speak of the devil’.","A hologram suddenly appeared before them, and a young woman's voice echoed, “Big brother Zu, have you finally decided to visit me... Ah?”"]},{"number":2875,"title":"Chapter 2875: Chapter 2827: Round Table Council","paragraphs":["Chu Chuyan had already been nervous because of those transparent glass windows, and the abrupt appearance of a hologram caused her body to tense up further. She was a conservative person, and she'd only agreed to this because they had been separated for too long.","Little had she expected someone else to catch them in the act!","It was only a young woman, but it nearly made her faint. What maddened her further was that Zu An was still moving slowly!","You have successfully trolled Chu Chuyan for +119... +119... +119...","Zu An gasped. He felt as if the world’s tectonic plates were furiously crushing against each other, causing the volcano to erupt furiously.","He hadn’t expected Isabella to contact him at a time like this. And why did the hologram call come on without my permission?!","Isabella was in an adorable pink room that appeared to be her bedroom.","It’s a relief she’s alone...","Isabella stared at the scene in shock. Naturally, she had set alerts and notifications in the spaceship she'd given to Zu An, so she was alerted when the spaceship began navigating toward the Contract Galaxy. She was so excited that she'd immediately contacted him to chat.","Who knew she would witness such a sight as soon as the call connected?","That big sister is gorgeous! Is she big brother Zu’s wife, who has been sealed under the Oblivion Bridge? But her current appearance looks nothing like the frosty mountain immortal that big brother Zu described her to be.","Big brother Zu is terrible. He fooled around with big sister Firework as well.","Her face swiftly reddened as various thoughts filled her mind.","Just like that, the three of them stared at one another, and the atmosphere grew increasingly bizarre.","Isabella was a scion from a powerful clan, after all. She reacted fast and remarked, “Hm? Why isn’t the call connecting properly? It must be because we’re too far away. Forget it. I’ll do it again later on. Maybe the signal will be better then.”","Zu An burst into laughter. Her acting is so terrible that anyone can see right through it. But this helps to preserve the dignity of those involved here.","Chu Chuyan’s face reddened like an apple. “It’s all your fault! I’m so embarrassed!”","“Don’t worry. I’m sure you looked beautiful.”","“???” Chu Chuyan was so angry that she wanted to turn around to bite him, but she was unable to do so in her current state. “You’re still doing it?!”","“We’re already doing it. It’d be more infuriating if we sullied our reputation over nothing.”","“...”","Chu Chuyan felt like she was losing her mind. Ah Zu is getting more audacious! But the earlier shock, embarrassment, and stimulation overwhelmed her with unprecedented sensations. In her daze, she ended up going along with him.","It was only when the storm passed that rationality took over. As soon as she snapped out of it, she dashed back to her room in embarrassment, refusing to respond to Zu An no matter how he called for her.","Zu An looked at the claw marks on his body and chuckled. He knew how easily embarrassed Chuyan was. The earlier situation was indeed too much for her to bear. She needed time to process and calm down from it.","So, Zu An tidied up his clothes, made his way to the link bridge, and instructed Aphrodite to make a hologram call to Isabella. Moments passed, but no one picked up. It was only on the third call that Isabella finally picked up.","“Oof, the signal is really bad.” Isabella looked around Zu An’s environment, fearing that she would see something she wasn't supposed to.","Zu An burst into laughter. Her acting skill is horrendous. She needs to take some lessons from Firework. But there was no reason to expose her here. He cleared the air with a cough and said, “Isabella, I didn’t think we would meet again so soon.”","“I also thought it would be a long time before we met again.” Isabella breathed a sigh of relief when Zu An skipped over what happened earlier. That’s weird. I’m not the one fooling around, so why am I feeling so jumpy?","“Did anything huge happen in the Universal Conglomerate recently?” Zu An asked vaguely. He couldn’t casually reveal the intelligence he had received from a universal deity.","“Hm?” Isabella was stunned. She racked her mind, and her expression grew unnatural. “There is indeed something huge. Big brother Zu, I’ll tell you about it when you arrive.”","Zu An nodded. Some secrets were too confidential to be revealed via a remote call. Who knew if someone else was eavesdropping on their conversation?","“Can you share the internal structure of the Universal Conglomerate with me? I tried asking Aphrodite, but she said that she doesn’t have the clearance to reveal confidential information.” Zu An believed in gathering information about where he was going to head to beforehand, or else a dangerous situation could easily become a hopeless one.","“What do you want to know, big brother Zu?”","“What is the current situation surrounding the members of the Round Table Council?”","The Universal Conglomerate operated across many universes, connecting countless worlds together. This behemoth was governed by the members of the Round Table Council, with each of them being top powerhouses in the Myriad Worlds.","Since Zu An was traveling to their headquarters, it was inevitable that he would bump into them.","“Ah, it would be difficult for someone on the outside to acquire such information.” Isabella smiled. Her expression slowly grew serious as she began sharing what she knew.","“The Round Table Council comprises seven people. First Elder Oberon is a stern figure known as the Hand of Order. He is a devout worshiper of the Deity of Order, and he believes that order is the foundation of all civilizations. He is a conservative and obstinate old man. I have been a bit afraid of him since I was a child.” Isabella stuck out her tongue as if recalling being lectured by him.","“Second Elder Hermes is a strong-willed, resilient, and proud man. He manages our Conglomerate’s commercial operations. He views anyone who undermines our commercial activities as an enemy.”","Zu An chuckled. “The Universal Conglomerate does need someone like that.”","“Big brother Zu, you need to be careful around him. The Second Elder is a devoted man. There’s nothing he hates more than people who aren’t devoted to their partner. You mustn’t provoke him,” Isabella warned.","Zu An was stunned. She must have been shaken up by the earlier sight...","Isabella continued, “Second Elder Hermes is very handsome, and he commands an incredible disposition despite his old age. Countless women have professed their adoration for him, but he remains unmarried to date. It’s rumored that he fell in love with a woman when he was younger, but that woman suddenly went missing, and he couldn’t let her go.","“He’s also the one who created Aphrodite. It’s rumored that he modeled it in the image of his old lover.”","Zu An nodded. “Aphrodite is indeed beautiful. I can see why he’s unable to forget her.”","“The Third Elder is my father. You have met him.” Isabella’s face suddenly reddened. “What’s your impression of him?”"]},{"number":2876,"title":"Chapter 2876: Chapter 2828: Contract Galaxy","paragraphs":["“He seems like a gentle, knowledgeable, and wise man, as well as a good father who dotes on his daughter.” Zu An thought about his encounter with Aragorn. “He wouldn’t have raised such an adorable daughter otherwise.”","Isabella’s face reddened. “He isn’t that good. He’s fierce at times.” She was happy that Zu An had such a good impression of her father.","Worried that he would see through her, she dared not linger too much on her father and quickly changed the topic, “Fourth Elder Mastema is also known as the Gold Avarice.”","Zu An was surprised. “That nickname doesn’t mean anything good.”","Isabella hesitantly replied, “The Fourth Elder doesn’t have a good reputation. He’s greedy, cunning, and lustful like you. He has a lot of concubines and children, so much so that he can’t even remember the names of many of his children.”","Zu An was speechless. I didn’t expect to get implicated.","Isabella suddenly realized what she had just said and tried to salvage the situation. “But the Fourth Elder is fat and ugly. The women he’s with are clearly not looking for romance, so it’s different from the situation big brother Zu is in.”","“You aren’t helping with your explanation.” Zu An didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. “It’s to be expected. As one of the Universal Conglomerate’s seven elders, he’s bound to have countless women throwing themselves at him. I’d say the Second Elder is in the minority.”","“You’re right. All the elders, except for the Second Elder, have many concubines. Even my father, despite loving my mother so much, has many mistresses.” Isabella’s face darkened.","Feeling guilt-ridden, Zu An quickly changed the topic. “What about the Fifth Elder?”","Displeasure flickered across Isabella’s face. “Fifth Elder Lilith has an extreme personality. She tends to act irrationally. Many say that she has lost her mind, but I know for certain that she hasn’t. It’s just her personality.","“Like the Fourth Elder, she is very lustful and has many male pets. Big brother Zu, you mustn’t get seduced by her. That woman will gobble you whole!”","Zu An burst into laughter. “Do you see me as someone who falls in love with every woman I see? Don’t worry, I have high standards. I only like kind and innocent ladies.”","Sensing Zu An’s gaze on her, Isabella lowered her head in embarrassment. She continued meekly, “Sixth Elder Naraka gives off a heavy and desolate atmosphere. Even machines are more animated than him. His presence strikes fear in me.”","Zu An was surprised. “Is he a Nebula worshiper?”","Isabella shook her head. “I don’t think so. The feeling he gives off is different from big sister Tingxue. Our Universal Conglomerate mostly worships the Deity of Order, with some worshiping the Deity of Protection as well. It’s unlikely for someone among us to worship a universal deity who strays too far from that.”","The mention of Tingxue made Zu An’s heart sink. Tingxue should be Yan Xuehen, but I wonder what happened to her that caused her to lose her memories. It’s a pity she's elusive, so I don’t know where I can look for her.","Isabella keenly noticed Zu An’s shift in emotions and consoled, “Does big brother Zu miss big sister Tingxue? Don’t worry. Big sister Tingxue is strong enough to overcome most trouble that appears in her way. I’m sure she’ll return to look for you once she’s done with whatever matter she has on hand.”","“You’re truly meticulous, Bella,” Zu An said. He was surprised that given her elevated background, she didn’t grow up to be an arrogant little princess.","“I’m just saying whatever comes to mind.” Isabella’s face reddened when Zu An called her by an intimate nickname—Bella. She did a light cough before continuing, “Seventh Elder Viktor is a very calm person, to the point of being emotionless. He manages the Conglomerate’s contracts. His impartiality is doubted by none.”","Zu An proceeded to ask more about the seven elders. Isabella told him everything she knew.","Following that, they chatted about what happened after they parted ways.","Zu An listened to her thoughts, while Isabella learned about the appearances of Divine Palaces in the Cultivation World and the disappearance of his lovers.","“My father looks worried as of late. Something huge might be happening to the Myriad Worlds,” Isabella remarked. “But big brother Zu, you don’t have to be too worried. It’s normal for universal deities to dispatch their Divine Palaces to different worlds. That’s how they propagate their greatness and expand their faith. Your friends will metamorphose after clearing their trials.”","“I can only hope that’s the case.”","“Big brother Zu, have you saved big sister Chuyan? Did my father’s card work?”","Zu An was speechless. Didn’t you already see her in person? He knew she was trying to confirm Chu Chuyan’s identity through this indirect questioning, but he wasn’t averse to it. If anything, he thought she was adorable.","“Yes, I’ve managed to save her. It’s all thanks to your father and Bella,” Zu An replied with a mischievous grin.","Isabella’s heart pounded furiously. Oh no, big brother Zu saw through my thoughts. “You’re too polite, big brother Zu. I think my father is looking for me. I’ll have to hang up first.”","She anxiously hung up her call.","Zu An suddenly noticed something. He got up and opened the door—Chu Chuyan was standing outside, her usually cold appearance still tinged with evening hues.","“It’s all your fault. I was so embarrassed.”","“Don’t worry, Bella is a kind lady. She won’t go around talking about it.”","“Is that the issue here? How am I supposed to face her in the future?”","“She has chosen to circumvent the topic. We can just continue that.”","“I’m about to go insane.”","...","While traveling through space, Zu An wanted to talk to Mi Li about the reforging of her body, but she didn’t appear. He noticed that Mi Li’s hibernations had been growing longer. Does this mean something?","In the meantime, he explored Chu Chuyan’s cultivation, hoping to raise her strength by borrowing the powers of a universal deity. To his surprise, she had no affinity with any of the universal deities' paths. In other words, she was rejected by all the paths.","Chu Chuyan wasn’t bothered by it. She had already cultivated for many years without relying on the universal deities; she was confident of finding a path herself.","Time flew by. While the two of them were cultivating, they received a notification from Aphrodite, telling them that they had arrived at the Contract Galaxy.","They made their way out to the link bridge and saw brilliant golden lights. Flowing through the Contract Galaxy were countless gold coins.","Zu An and Chu Chuyan possessed considerable wealth themselves, but they were still blinded by this extravagant display of wealth. The Universal Conglomerate was indeed loaded!"]},{"number":2877,"title":"Chapter 2877: Chapter 2829: The Holy Knight Order","paragraphs":["Zu An was blinded by the sheer wealth laid before him. In his two lifetimes, he'd never seen so many gold coins before. It felt as if the Universal Conglomerate had gathered gold from all over the Myriad Worlds to construct this gleaming galaxy.","As a behemoth that operated across many universes, the Universal Conglomerate had transcended the conventional notion of using gold and silver as currency. They had developed a new currency known as credit, and it was encrypted with state-of-the-art technology, ensuring that it couldn’t be forged.","Zu An could somewhat understand the concept thanks to the development of blockchain before he transmigrated to this world.","Even though gold wasn't the default currency used by the Universal Conglomerate, it remained a precious metal in many worlds. To think that the Universal Conglomerate would use it to make such an extravagant scene!","On one hand, it flaunted the Conglomerate’s prowess. On the other hand, it displayed the Conglomerate’s massive reserve, which encouraged trust in its distributed currency.","“What a bizarre galaxy. It’s nothing like the pitch-black space we traveled through along the way,” Chu Chuyan remarked. She had gained some knowledge of technological civilizations along the way.","Zu An looked at the vague runes visible in the galaxy and said, “Those must be the contracts the Universal Conglomerate sealed with the other worlds. These contracts bind and connect both parties.”","Chu Chuyan was awed. “No wonder it’s called the Contract Galaxy. I can also sense the countless contracts floating around us. How do they ensure that the contracts don't conflict with one another?”","“The Universal Conglomerate is predominantly a technological civilization, but their business spans countless worlds. They must have learned from the strengths of different civilizations to develop something like this. It’s incredible,” Zu An complimented them.","As the spaceship approached the interstellar river of gold coins, Chu Chuyan suddenly remarked with a frown, “Those gold coins might not appear to be moving quickly, but that’s only because we’re still a distance away from them. Won’t our spaceship be ruined if we crash into them like that?”","“Surely not...” Zu An figured that Isabella must have taken that into account when she set the coordinates in the spaceship’s flight computer.","He would step forward to block the gold coins if needed, but they were moving so quickly that they each harnessed destructive prowess comparable to a rocket. He wasn’t confident of blocking all of them.","“Please do not worry, esteemed guests. This interstellar golden river doubles as picturesque scenery and a protective measure for the Fortune Palace. Only those with the Conglomerate’s invitation letters or permission are allowed to pass through it. This spaceship belongs to Miss Isabella and has a high level of clearance, so you won’t be attacked,” Aphrodite explained.","Zu An and Chu Chuyan breathed a sigh of relief.","When the spaceship reached the golden river, the gold coins automatically parted to open a path for them.","Zu An and Chu Chuyan exchanged shocked looks.","The Universal Conglomerate was truly an unfathomable entity to them. Chu Chuyan sent a voice transmission over, “Ah Zu, I regret coming here with you.”","“Why?” Zu An asked.","“You’re here to ask for Isabella’s hand in marriage. My presence is bound to be jarring to the Conglomerate’s elders. I might bring trouble to you,” Chu Chuyan said worriedly.","Zu An held her hand and said, “Chuyan, you’re overthinking it. You’re my wife, and that’s a fact that will never change. If I conceal your existence just to marry another woman, that means that I might do the same to Isabella when I find someone more formidable in the future.”","Chu Chuyan shook her head. “I trust you, but the elders might not think the same. They might fly into a rage when they learn about my identity. Why don’t you tell them that I’m your little sister or maid instead?”","Zu An burst into laughter. “Don’t you think we’re too intimate to be siblings? Your disposition doesn’t suit that of a maid either. Don’t think too much about it. This journey is destined not to be smooth anyway. Soon, they might not have the energy to care about us.”","“What do you mean by that?”","“Do you remember me telling you that something huge might happen at the Universal Conglomerate?”","“That only makes me more worried.”","...","While the two of them were chatting, the spaceship approached a port. Countless vessels zoomed to and from the docks. Some were parked there, unloading their goods. Aphrodite explained that those were commercial spaceships used for trading with different worlds.","Zu An had visited the biggest port in his previous world, and seeing the jungle of metal containers then had filled him with awe. But that was nothing compared to what he was witnessing right now.","A patrol ship approached, wary of their abrupt appearance.","Their spaceship flickered as Aphrodite communicated with the patrol ship. Soon, the latter escorted them forth.","Aphrodite explained, “We’re at the Conglomerate’s headquarters, after all. There have been attempts to hold staff members hostage to breach this place, and those attempts have resulted in massive losses. For that reason, security is tightened whenever there’s a major event.”","“That’s understandable.” Zu An’s curiosity was piqued. “What major event is there now?”","“It’s rumored that a captain of the Holy Knight Order has come to visit.” Aphrodite proceeded to explain what the Holy Knight Order was.","The Universal Conglomerate worshiped the Deity of Order, but it wasn't the only power to do so. The Holy Knight Order was another comparable power in that regard.","If the Universal Conglomerate was Order’s money tree, the Holy Knight Order was Order’s sword. Their job was to deal with heretics, traitors, and blasphemers.","And the greatest blasphemers of the Deity of Order were none other than the Deity of Annihilation’s worshipers. They brought death and destruction wherever they went, which was why the Holy Knight Order devoted most of its energy to battling them.","Hearing that, Zu An suddenly felt a surge of goodwill toward them. He was also on bad terms with Annihilation worshipers, and not too long ago, he had offended the Deity of Annihilation in the Deity of Death’s trial.","An enemy’s enemy was a friend.","He'd been left wondering why a small fry like him needed to deal with an entity as terrifying as Annihilation. It comforted him to know that rival powers existed as well, and the weight on his shoulders suddenly felt much lighter.","“Let the radiance of Order suffuse every corner!” Aphrodite devoutly exclaimed as the spaceship landed at the port.","Much to Zu An’s surprise, he was only welcomed by Alfred. Isabella was nowhere to be seen."]},{"number":2878,"title":"Chapter 2878: Chapter 2830: Unease","paragraphs":["Alfred was shocked by Chu Chuyan’s beauty, but he quickly snapped out of it and performed an impeccable bow. “Young master Zu and Miss Chu, welcome to our Conglomerate.”","Chu Chuyan’s face reddened. The only way Alfred could have recognized her was if Isabella had also recognized her from the hologram call and given him a heads-up. This is embarrassing. It’s all Ah Zu’s fault!","You have successfully trolled Chu Chuyan for +55... +55... +55...","Zu An burst into laughter. Chuyan must be thinking of that incident. “It has been a while, but your complexion looks better than ever, Alfred.”","“It’s all thanks to you, young master Zu. Otherwise, I’d have died in that demon spider lair.” Alfred trembled in fear, thinking about what had happened then.","They traded some pleasantries before Zu An casually asked, “Speaking of which, where’s Isabella?”","Alfred explained, “An important matter that requires our big miss’ intervention has cropped up recently. She has her hands full at the moment, so she entrusted me to take good care of you. I hope you don’t mind it.”","Zu An replied with a smile, “Work comes first.”","But his heart sank. Isabella had already excitedly mentioned that she would receive him when he arrived several times, but it had been days since he last managed to contact her. Given their relationship, she would have squeezed in some time to welcome him before rushing off to handle her business.","Could something have happened to Isabella?","But since Alfred refused to speak, Zu An withheld his thoughts.","Alfred brought the two of them to a sedan which, considering the lack of wheels, appeared to be a low-altitude aircraft. The sedan was extravagant, installed with all sorts of high-technology items.","Chu Chuyan sat upright, showing none of the excitement and curiosity she had displayed on the spaceship. She didn’t want to appear like a bumpkin in front of Isabella’s subordinate.","Zu An quietly took in the scenery outside. The streets were lined with glowing travelators and towering skyscrapers that appeared to be alive. He had already seen the skyscrapers change their shapes and positions several times now.","Alfred explained, “They are made out of liquefied metal or Memory Crystals, which allows them to change their form when required. More often than not, they are used for advertisements.”","And indeed, the skyscrapers were projecting all kinds of immersive, holographic advertisements.","Zu An was rendered speechless. I guess ads can’t be avoided no matter where we go.","The streets were filled with beings from all over the Myriad Worlds. Zu An could spot a cultivator riding on an immortal crane bickering with an octopus-shaped mecha lifeform. At this rate, it looked as if they could get into a fight.","Colossal beasts of over fifty meters tall were patiently carrying mountainloads of goods on a specified pathway on the streets.","...","The sky was filled with low-altitude aircraft, cultivators riding on swords, and monsters with unfurled wings, inundating the sky with all sorts of lights. There were no traffic lights, but these beings still moved in a fast and orderly fashion with zero risk of collision.","Zu An looked up at the blue sky, where there was not only a majestic golden interstellar river visible, but also trade data that kept refreshing every second. He asked, “That isn’t the real sky, is it?”","Ever since entering the port, he'd noticed that there was an artificial ceiling above them.","“Young master Zu is indeed sharp-eyed. Most people fail to notice that. This information is confidential, but young master Zu is our Conglomerate’s benefactor, so it isn’t a problem to tell you.”","Alfred opened an interface. Zu An and Chu Chuyan saw something flicker across their eyes, then the blue sky abruptly vanished, replaced by three blazing fireballs that were much bigger than the sun.","The land beneath them wasn't true earth, either. It was an amalgamation of flowing digits, energy, and all kinds of materials. They continuously reconstructed and expanded at a pace visible to the naked eye, forming a massive ring around the three stars.","Zu An sensed that the massive ring world served to contain the three stars.","“The Conglomerate requires a colossal amount of energy for its daily operations, which is why the Fortune Palace is constructed around three stars to allow for easy harvesting of energy. The golden interstellar river you saw earlier doubles as a system of energy mirrors to prevent the stars’ energy from leaking out, thus maximizing our energy efficiency,” Alfred explained. “We only constructed an immersive hologram and an atmospheric layer to accommodate the habits of most living beings.”","Scientists in Zu An’s previous life had proposed the concept of a Dyson sphere[1], though their civilization had been nowhere close to achieving that feat. But the Universal Conglomerate had gone a step further to harness the power of not just a single star, but three stars.","Chu Chuyan widened her eyes in astonishment.","People of the Cultivation World were grateful to the sun’s bestowment, and there were even religions that worshiped it. Yet stars much larger than the sun were being treated like servants here. Is this the coldness of high-tech civilizations?","Zu An asked out of curiosity, “As large as these three stars are, their energy will eventually run out. What will you do then?”","Those three stars had to harness an unimaginable amount of energy, but judging from what he had seen along the way, the Fortune Palace was constantly expending an astronomical amount of energy as well. Surely the energy from the three stars would be depleted one day.","“We’ll just look for new stars to harvest from. The Fortune Palace is mobile. It can search for new stars when required,” Alfred replied casually. “But at the current pace, these three stars can still sustain us for at least ten thousand years.”","Zu An and Chu Chuyan fell silent. They felt a sense of powerlessness compared to the ridiculous feats performed by high-tech civilizations.","Looking at the three stars, a ridiculous notion suddenly emerged in Zu An’s head.","I wonder if my Sun Slaying Bow could shoot them down. But considering the Universal Conglomerate’s technological prowess, I’m sure countless defensive weapons would emerge to block my arrow as soon as I shot it.","Soon, the sky and the earth reverted to normal, and the extravagant sedan stopped at a quiet but luxurious manor.","“This is one of our old master’s favorite accommodations. Please stay here for the next few days. Feel free to request anything from the maids and the servants here,” Alfred said as he brought them on a tour around the manor.","“When can I meet Isabella and the Third Elder?” As beautiful as the manor was, Zu An wasn't here for a holiday.","Alfred looked troubled. “I’m afraid the old master and the big miss have their hands full at the moment. However, you can be assured that they will meet you as soon as they are done with their business.”","Zu An and Chu Chuyan exchanged looks. They could see unease in each other’s eyes.","1. A Dyson sphere is a hypothetical megastructure that encompasses a star and captures a large percentage of its power output ☜"]},{"number":2879,"title":"Chapter 2879: Chapter 2831: Like Planets Orbiting the Sun","paragraphs":["After Alfred left, Chu Chuyan went to Zu An’s room. The two of them were settled into neighboring rooms. Perhaps they'd been assigned different rooms as a gesture of hospitality, but Chu Chuyan still couldn’t help but wonder if there was another meaning behind this.","Chu Chuyan was about to speak when she warily eyed the surroundings. What happened on the spaceship had traumatized her. She now knew that advanced civilizations had discreet cameras capable of recording someone.","Seeing Chu Chuyan’s vigilant expression, Zu An chuckled and said, “Don’t worry, I’ve already scanned the room. It’s safe.”","To be sure, he constructed a barrier around them so that their images and voices couldn’t be recorded.","Chu Chuyan exhaled in relief, only to frown shortly after. “Something is amiss. Isabella has been very friendly to you along the way. It doesn’t make sense for her to suddenly disappear now that you've arrived.”","“I agree. Her father also extended his invitation to me, but he only dispatched an old butler to welcome me.” Zu An was satisfied with the hospitality he was receiving, but these little details revealed a lot about what was going on.","“Could it be because of the Holy Knight Order’s visit?”","“While that’s a major event, I doubt it would leave them so busy that they would have no time to meet us.”","“I know!” Chu Chuyan’s eyes lit up.","Zu An looked at her.","“Someone from the Holy Knight Order must be infatuated with Isabella and wants to propose to her,” Chu Chuyan deduced.","Zu An frowned. “There isn’t enough information to make that conjecture.”","“No, that’s the most likely explanation. It explains why Isabella is unable to find time for you,” Chu Chuyan replied. “I believe that little sister Bella isn't the type to fall for others easily. It’s more likely that the Conglomerate has restricted her freedom to avoid misunderstandings with the Holy Knight Order. I’m not sure what her father thinks though.”","Zu An initially didn’t think much of Chu Chuyan’s conjecture, but his expression soon turned grim. “What you have said sounds plausible. Her father is only one of the seven elders. If the other six elders support a bond of marriage with the Holy Knight Order, his hands will be tied.”","He asked out of curiosity, “What made you guess that?”","“Call it a woman’s intuition.” Chu Chuyan glared at Zu An. “I’ve been around you long enough to be familiar with such situations.”","Zu An laughed sheepishly. He quickly changed the topic and said, “There’s no point in theorizing here. Let’s take a stroll outside and see if we can gather any information.”","Chu Chuyan was also interested in exploring this new world. The two of them made their way out of the manor, only to be stopped right away. The guards claimed that the city was currently on high alert, and the two of them didn’t have passes. It would be troublesome if they bumped into the patrols.","So, the two of them returned to Zu An’s room.","Chu Chuyan angrily exclaimed, “Isn’t this house arrest?”","Zu An calmly remarked, “They might be protecting us. It wouldn’t be good to get into an argument with our hosts when we've only just arrived.”","He leisurely plopped down on a sofa, grabbed a beer from the fridge, and handed it to Chu Chuyan.","Chu Chuyan was surprised. “You’re different from before. You didn’t shy away from trouble in the past.”","“That’s because the best strategy right now is to wait.”","“Wait for what?”","“Wait for them to come knocking.”","Chu Chuyan was confused, but Zu An’s guess was soon proven to be on the dot.","A flamboyant woman dressed as a secretary soon visited them to deliver an invitation letter for a banquet the following day.","Zu An accepted the invitation letter. “Beautiful miss, may I ask who this invitation letter is from?”","“Young man, why don’t you make a guess?” the secretary replied with a chuckle.","“I’m guessing it’s Mister Gold Avarice.”","It was an easy guess, as Zu An had previously asked Isabella about the details of the Round Table Council’s seven elders. The only elder who would have such a flirtatious secretary was the lustful Fourth Elder, Gold Avarice Mastema.","The secretary was surprised. “I see why the Fourth Elder has such a high opinion of you. Tomorrow’s banquet will be interesting.”","She strutted off afterward.","Chu Chuyan remarked frostily, “I don’t like her.” That woman is too flirtatious. The women around Zu An are much more pleasant.","Zu An chuckled. “She’s only here to deliver the invitation letter.”","“How did you know someone would be coming?”","“Politics exist wherever people dwell. I doubt the seven elders are that tight-knit. If someone doesn’t want me to meet Isabella, there’s bound to be someone who wants me to meet her as well.”","Chu Chuyan was awed. “That’s true.”","Zu An spent a while examining the black-gold invitation letter before putting it away. “Since there’s nothing better to do now, let’s take a rest and recharge.”","Chu Chuyan’s face reddened. “Rest up if you want to. Why are you holding onto me?”","“Don’t you know my cultivation skill? I grow faster when I’m with you.”","“Hmph. I think it works with any woman.”","“Let’s not fuss over the details. You’re not like any other woman.”","...","The following evening, the flirtatious secretary drove them to the banquet location.","Even though the entire world was called ‘Fortune Palace’, the true Fortune Palace was the Universal Conglomerate’s headquarters. Its entrance wasn't a conventional door, but slowly revolving constellations that were drawn into orbit in this small space by some inexplicable force.","Zu An and Chu Chuyan exchanged looks. It’s a relief we didn’t try to barge in, or else we wouldn’t even be able to pass through this door.","A gentle surge of golden light drew their vehicle into the revolving constellations, and their surroundings suddenly turned brilliant.","“Sir and miss, we have arrived at our destination. Please!” The flirtatious secretary bowed with a smile.","Zu An and Chu Chuyan entered the premises.","Instead of a ceiling, the banquet hall had a starry sky adorned through divine power and technology. Light streams made out of stars flowed through the air, forming the Universal Conglomerate’s insignia—an ancient coin surrounding a star. On the face of the coin, the birth and the death of the universe appeared to play in a loop.","“The space appears to be folded,” Chu Chuyan told Zu An via voice transmission.","Zu An nodded. The floating platforms, corridors, and main hall were connected by streams of energy that resembled rainbow bridges.","Some platforms were serene gardens that cultivated trees with jade leaves and jewel fruits. Others had buildings of different styles, ranging from immortal palaces to mecha castles. They symbolized the different civilizations under the Conglomerate’s influence and their tribute.","These gardens and castles weren't built in this hall; they were connected to the hall through some mysterious means.","A subtle fragrance lingered in the air; it smelled like a scent that had matured over countless years, fused with the universe’s nebula. A light whiff left Zu An feeling energized, and his ki felt more active than ever.","“What extravagance. They've suffused this space with the purest universe ki. Just a brief moment here offsets months of diligent cultivation elsewhere,” Zu An remarked. He had been to many blessed lands, but none had ki as rich as this.","Chu Chuyan was stunned as well. It’s a pity Manman isn’t here. It’s too difficult for me to go up against a rival like this alone. She took a look around and discreetly murmured, “Those servants don’t appear to be humans.”","Zu An had also noticed the light entities dressed in dignified clothes. There was always an impeccable smile hanging on their lips, and they never failed to perfectly fulfill the requests of any guests.","“That must be the manifestation of some law. Anyone who causes trouble here would be in for a terrible time.”","The guests had already begun gathering in small groups.","A massive lava entity clinked cups with another entity that was shrouded in flowing data. The fluids in their cups resembled liquid galaxies.","Several dignified old men stood before a prized tree capable of nurturing treasures from different worlds as they discussed it.","Some entities alternated between tangible and intangible, as if they were projections from a higher dimension.","But the most eye-catching figure in the hall was a golden-haired man dressed in white, knightly garments. A huge crowd was gathered around him like planets orbiting a star.","He was speaking to a beautiful woman beside him with an impeccable smile. Anyone could tell that he was courting the beautiful woman at a glance.","And the woman was none other than Isabella. Not only was she not smiling, there was even a hint of ire to be seen in her eyes. She impatiently looked away, only to notice Zu An, who had just entered the room.","Her eyes immediately lit up."]},{"number":2880,"title":"Chapter 2880: Chapter 2832: Radiant Son","paragraphs":["Isabella was both overjoyed and embarrassed to see Zu An. Her earlier impatience melted away like a blossoming flower. She quickly addressed the people around her before raising her skirt and joyously skipping over to Zu An’s side.","Chu Chuyan breathed a sigh of relief. She had been worried about Isabella’s attitude. Zu An would have been put in a bad position if she were more inclined toward the Holy Knight Order.","She suddenly froze up. Why am I helping Zu An get together with other women? Am I into cuckolding myself, just as Manman told me?","A shiver ran down her spine. She quickly shook off those miscellaneous thoughts.","Isabella was the brightest pearl in the Universal Conglomerate, commanding the center of attention no matter where she stood. Her presence drew gazes to Zu An and Chu Chuyan, and the spectators were awed by what they saw.","It was a dashing man and a beautiful woman—they were truly a perfect couple.","The crowd whispered among themselves, discussing the couple’s background. The more well-informed ones divulged the news they'd heard about Isabella and Zu An a while back. Some glanced at the golden-eyed man with an amused look.","The golden-haired man’s smile stiffened. Isabella’s earnest joy when approaching Zu An contrasted starkly with her disinterest when talking to him earlier, and that sparked anger in his heart.","You have successfully trolled Adrian for +444... +444... +444...","Zu An looked at the young man on the platform. Is he already provoked by this?","In the meantime, Isabella went up to him and sweetly called out, “Big brother Zu!”","She turned to Chu Chuyan and greeted her as well, “Big sister Chu.”","“Nice to meet you, little sister Bella.” Chu Chuyan was reminded of the hologram incident and felt incredibly uncomfortable. If there was a hole in the ground, she might have dove into it there and then, but she didn’t want to make an embarrassment out of herself in public, either.","Isabella also recalled the incident, and her face reddened in embarrassment. An awkward silence settled between them as they struggled to continue the conversation.","Zu An quickly interjected, “Little sister Bella, I hope you won’t blame me for coming uninvited.”","Isabella anxiously replied, “Of course not! I would have already visited you if not for my father stopping me. Big brother Zu, I hope you aren’t offended. My father has his difficulties as well...”","Before she could finish her sentence, the golden-haired man walked over with his entourage. “Bella, aren’t you going to introduce your friends?”","Isabella frowned. “Adrian, please address me by my full name. Only my family members and elders can address me by that nickname.”","The corners of Chu Chuyan’s lips curled up. This lass has double standards. She didn’t show the slightest impatience when we called her by that nickname. She must truly fancy Zu An.","Adrian looked uncomfortable. Being snubbed in public pricked his ego, though he quickly shrugged it off to Isabella throwing princess tantrums. It wasn’t to the extent where he would lose himself in public. He performed a knight’s bow and said, “Miss Isabella, please pardon me for my discourtesy.”","The spectators nodded. As expected of the Holy Knight Order’s Radiant Son. His personality is flawless.","Only then did Isabella explain, “This is my good friend, big brother Zu. This is big sister Chu. This young man over here is a vice captain of the Holy Knight Order, Radiant Son Adrian.”","Adrian’s eyelids twitched. While Isabella had introduced him properly, her words clearly put distance between them. So, he turned to Zu An and asked, “May I know which galaxy Mister Zu is from? Which clan are you from?”","Zu An replied with a smile, “I am from a remote planet. My clan is nothing noteworthy.”","Adrian consoled him, “Please do not be dismayed, Mister Zu. Those gathered in the Fortune Palace are renowned figures in the Myriad Worlds. With their help, I’m sure you and your clan can prosper.”","Isabella’s face darkened. Adrian’s words appeared kind on the surface, but he was implying that Zu An had come to the Fortune Palace in search of a golden goose, as if he had an ulterior motive.","Zu An shrugged it off with a smile. “With little sister Bella here, I wouldn’t need to find anyone else.”","Isabella’s face reddened. Big brother Zu is terrible! He’s obviously saying that in public to provoke Adrian.","Unsurprisingly, Adrian’s dashing face twisted out of jealousy, especially when he noticed that Isabella didn’t refute those words but instead reacted shyly.","She had corrected him when he addressed her by her nickname, yet she reacted coyly when this fellow was implying an even more intimate relationship than that.","This is preposterous!","You have successfully trolled Adrian for +666... +666... +666...","Adrian decided not to tolerate it anymore. He glanced at Chu Chuyan, and despite having met his fair share of beauties, he still found himself enchanted by her. Looking at a beauty dispelled his anger by a fair bit.","“Are you Mister Zu’s little sister?”","Chu Chuyan hesitated. She didn’t think it was appropriate to reveal their relationship publicly and was about to nod when Zu An grabbed her hand and said, “No, she’s my wife.”","Those words sparked a commotion.","Those qualified to attend this banquet were powerhouses with powerful information networks. They might not have known at the start, but by now, their subordinates had already submitted a comprehensive report about Zu An to them.","They knew that Zu An had won Isabella’s heart. Who could have imagined that he would bring his wife with him to the Fortune Palace to ask for Isabella’s hand in marriage? Was he asking the esteemed Isabella to be a concubine?","Isabella lowered her head gloomily.","She looked so pitiful that it sparked Adrian’s desire to protect her. He felt that it was time to make a move.","“I believe I have heard about you. If I’m not mistaken, you are here to ask Mister Aragorn for Isabella’s hand in marriage. Don’t you think it’s inappropriate for you to bring your wife to the Fortune Palace for that? You’re being offensive to both Isabella and the Fortune Palace.”","Adrian felt gleeful at having played his hand well. He had cornered Zu An in a single move.","Zu An looked at the triumphant Adrian and calmly remarked, “You asked about me despite already knowing my identity. Don’t you think that’s rather hypocritical?”","Adrian’s expression stiffened up. He noticed the amused looks from the surroundings and understood that his behavior was indeed unbefitting of a knight. But that wasn't important right now.","“Don’t change the topic. You’re insulting the Fortune Palace by bringing your wife along when asking for Isabella’s hand in marriage. The other elders are not saying anything because you’re a guest, so I’ll speak on Isabella’s behalf instead. Please leave this palace right now.”","Isabella was startled. She was about to stop him when Zu An suddenly splashed the wine in the glass he was holding in Adrian’s face.","“Who do you think you are?”","The entire hall fell unnervingly silent."]},{"number":2881,"title":"Chapter 2881: Chapter 2833: You Want to Compare Our Status?","paragraphs":["Everyone was stunned.","Adrian was a vice captain from the Holy Knight Order, someone who had unlimited potential in him. Many powers were doing everything they could to win him over.","In contrast, none of them had heard about Zu An. If not for Miss Isabella fancying him, a bumpkin like him wouldn’t have been qualified to even step into the Fortune Palace. Yet he dared to pour wine on Adrian’s face?","He’s not going to walk out of here alive today.","Even Chu Chuyan and Isabella were stunned.","Chu Chuyan hadn’t expected Zu An to be so rash, but she was already prepared for battle. If it comes down to that, we’ll die together.","Isabella turned to her father for help. She didn’t wield sufficient influence to save big brother Zu from the consequences of his actions.","Adrian’s eyes reddened. He clenched his teeth and roared, “You’re courting death!”","He hurled a punch forth without any hesitation. Sparks flew as his punch surged toward Zu An’s head like a falling comet, almost arriving at its target in the blink of an eye.","You have successfully trolled Adrian for +999... +999... +999...","Just when everyone thought Zu An’s head was going to explode, Adrian’s fist suddenly softened, and he made a weird noise. “Ikuu ikuu!”","Ikuu Experience Card: If your back hurts, it might not be because of a blade. If you are screaming your heart and lungs out, it might not be because of pain. What rests on your shoulders might not necessarily be responsibility. Things you are forced to learn might not be a lesson!","Only effective on men. Once a target is selected, it will force them to experience a woman’s perspective. They will feel as if they were being powerfully filled by a strong and robust man. One of the four scenarios above will be chosen, and they will continue to scream ‘Ikuu ikuu~’.","Adrian had been angrily hurling out a punch just a second ago when, in his mind, he suddenly saw a black bull crushing and furiously ramming into him. He should have been strong enough to throw off the black bull, yet he found himself powerless to do so.","The sheer humiliation he felt, coupled with the tremors running through his body and the screams that came right from the soul, evoked “ Ikuu ikuu~ ” sounds from him.","He knew he was done for immediately. The persona he had painstakingly built up over many years was ruined, but he couldn’t suppress the urge to cry out as if it was coming from the depths of his soul.","Hearing the surrounding whispers, he felt ashamed and humiliated.","Isabella’s lower jaw fell agape. How did big brother Zu do that?","Chu Chuyan was aware of Zu An’s ability, and her lips curled into a smirk. He’s crushing that fellow not just physically, but mentally as well.","Zu An looked at Adrian calmly. He had faced universal deities before, and he'd even turned the Deity of Annihilation against him. What kind of storms had he never weathered before? He might have lowered his head to universal deities, but never to a brat like that.","His mind is clearly not as strong as he looks if he can’t withstand the Ikuu Experience Card.","Just then, a furious roar echoed, “Who dares cast such evil sorcery?”","A divine light illuminated the hall as a golden-haired, middle-aged man raised his finger and pointed it at Zu An. He didn’t make a move, but his little finger seemed to look over Zu An. Immense pressure squeezed away the surrounding ki, making it hard for anyone targeted by his finger to even breathe, let alone retaliate.","He was the captain of the Holy Knight Order, Augustus.","Thus far, he had ignored the situation between his son and Isabella, thinking that the young Isabella had merely misjudged others and misplaced her feelings. Once she marries my son, she’ll forget about everything else.","That was why he'd continued chatting with the elders. Little had he expected such a mishap to happen. His son had ended up tarnishing his reputation here.","In a fit of anger, he made a move to kill Zu An.","“Please spare him!” Aragorn shouted in astonishment.","But First Elder Oberon stepped forward and blocked Aragorn. “Calm down, Third. Augustus won’t go overboard and hurt Isabella.”","Aragorn was speechless. I know that he won’t hurt Isabella, but the one I’m trying to rescue is Zu An!","With the First Elder blocking him, Aragorn couldn’t do anything else to save Zu An even if he wanted to. He looked at Zu An with worried eyes. Isabella will hate me for life if he dies here.","Chu Chuyan drew her sword. Her hair turned snowy white, and a snowstorm brewed around her. She was planning to withstand this attack together with Zu An. She wasn't going to stand still and die just because the enemy was much more powerful.","The crowd was startled. That beautiful woman has such a unique disposition. I can’t tell which universal deity she falls under. Did she become that strong just based on her own capability?","But that wasn't the most startling thing yet.","Zu An grabbed Chu Chuyan’s hand and pulled her back as if telling her not to make a move.","Has he given up on fighting because he knows he’s doomed?","The crowd couldn’t be blamed for thinking that. Augustus, as the captain of the Holy Knight Order, had slain many powerful demons and had many face-offs with the experts under the Deity of Annihilation. He was a renowned figure in the Myriad Worlds.","In contrast, Zu An didn’t look strong at all. Surely Augustus could crush Zu An as easily as crushing an ant?","But what happened next stunned everyone.","A beautiful river of stars appeared before Zu An. Augustus’s destructive finger fell into the river and was silenced for good.","“The River of History! It’s the Deity of Memory’s River of History!” Some of the experts who had been watching the drama stood up in shock.","It was only then that Zu An smiled. “Are you saying that Memory worshipers are demons?”","Augustus’s expression stiffened up. Perhaps he was a powerhouse in the Order faction, but he dared not blaspheme another universal deity.","Isabella was worried that someone could act recklessly despite that revelation, so she quickly added, “Big brother Zu is the Deity of Memory’s envoy.”","A commotion broke out in the hall.","The gap between the noble Adrian and the little-known Zu An had been like the gap between heaven and earth before, but now that it had been revealed that Zu An was a universal deity’s envoy, all of a sudden, Augustus’s halo suddenly appeared insufficient.","Adrian was the vice-captain of the Holy Knight Order, but being a universal deity’s envoy immediately put Zu An on equal standing with his father. Conventional etiquette demanded for him to respect Zu An as an elder.","It was one thing if Zu An was merely a Memory worshiper—Augustus’s standing was elevated enough to bear the consequences of killing a Memory worshiper—but it would be a completely different story if Zu An was a Memory envoy.","Other than the lunatics under Annihilation, no one wanted to risk drawing a universal deity’s ire by killing their envoy. That was no joking matter.","Unsurprisingly, Augustus hesitated to make a second move.","First Elder Oberon’s voice boomed, “The Fortune Palace is an Order domain. This is no place for someone under Memory to flaunt their stature.”","He stamped his staff on the ground, and a pulse of light rippled outward. The trembling Adrian finally recovered from his abnormal state. He hurriedly crawled to his feet, feeling both humiliated and furious. He glared at Zu An with venomous eyes.","You have successfully trolled Adrian for +1024... +1024... +1024..."]},{"number":2882,"title":"Chapter 2882: Chapter 2834: Tension In the Air","paragraphs":["Zu An replied with a calm smile, “Memory worshipers only seek to record everything faithfully. We don’t flaunt our stature.”","The First Elder is a devout worshiper of Order, which is why he favors the Holy Knight Order, which is also in the Order faction, over me. He hopes for Isabella to marry Adrian. With that, the Universal Conglomerate and the Holy Knight Order can deepen their cooperation.","That’s why he tried to isolate me inside that manor.","But another elder reached out to me and invited me to this banquet. The seven elders are indeed not that united in will.","The crowd had the weirdest look on their faces. You just fought with the Holy Knight Order’s captain and made a fool out of its vice captain, and yet you say that you aren’t flaunting?","But again, there was nothing wrong with that. A universal deity’s envoy was bound to have some temper, not to mention that Adrian was the one who'd provoked him first.","That was how the world worked.","The same matter would be viewed in a different light if the individual involved was of a lower stature. If Zu An had been a bumpkin from a minor world, no one would have thought there was an issue when he was trampled under Adrian’s foot.","Oberon’s face darkened, but that was indeed the nature of Memory worshipers. They didn’t interfere in matters, and that was why they had a good relationship with the other factions of universal deities.","In fact, Memory worshipers often concealed themselves in the shadows, so that others couldn’t even sense their presence.","But this fellow doesn’t feel like a Memory worshiper. His behavior is more aligned with a Chaos and Enigma worshiper.","“We have not sent any invitation out to any Memory worshipers, so I’ll have to ask you to...”","A plump figure stepped forward and interjected, “Big brother, we need a Memory worshiper to witness this event anyway. Besides, that man saved Isabella and carries our Conglomerate’s golden friendship emblem. We will appear ungrateful if we chase him out.”","Zu An looked at the plump man. He must be Fourth Elder Mastema, the one who sent me the invitation letter.","I ought to thank him for his intervention, but it’s hard to feel any goodwill toward him when he keeps looking around with eyes filled with desire.","Third Elder Aragorn immediately built on that, “He’s right, big brother. That event takes priority. We mustn’t lose sight of what’s important over trivial affairs.”","With two elders dissuading him against it, the First Elder could only let this matter rest, though he harrumphed in displeasure. He turned to Adrian and asked, “Are you injured? We have all kinds of medicine in our Conglomerate.”","Adrian was too ashamed to speak, so Augustus replied on his behalf, “Thank you for your concern, First Elder, but my son has only fallen for that fellow’s evil sorcery. Fortunately, he didn’t sustain any injuries.”","The mention of that prompted Augustus and Oberon to assess Zu An. What was that power earlier? I didn’t sense any energy pulsation. Is it a law-level ability? But Memory shouldn’t have that kind of ability.","Fourth Elder Mastema moved his plump body as he spoke cheerily, “We need a Memory worshiper to record the great Order Ceremony, so that we can propagate Order’s greatness across the Myriad Worlds. No one is more suited to the task than Memory’s envoy.”","Order Ceremony?","Isabella explained, “The Conglomerate is the most devoted group of Order worshipers. Every era, we invite devoted Order worshipers over to hold the Order Ceremony to sing praises of the Deity of Order and propagate their greatness. Each time, we invite important figures from other paths to witness the ceremony.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief.","The events at Dreamland had traumatized him. Surely something like that won’t happen again, given the sheer number of powerhouses gathered here.","Augustus protested, “I object. It was just moments ago he had a conflict with Adrian. I don’t think he can be an impartial witness.”","Zu An replied with a smile, “Lord Augustus, are you doubting the Deity of Memory’s judgment? The Deity of Memory chose me to be their envoy because they believe in my competency.”","Augustus choked. No matter how formidable he was, he wouldn’t dare to blaspheme a universal deity. Can you stop mentioning the Deity of Memory at every turn? Argh!","You have successfully trolled Augustus for +444... +444... +444...","I’d have torn him into shreds if he wasn’t a Memory envoy!","“The Deity of Memory’s judgment can’t be wrong, but I can’t find it within me to harbor any goodwill toward an infidel like you.” A dashing man dressed in a magnificent robe walked out. Time had hardly left its mark on him; if anything, it only made him more dignified. He must have charmed many women in his younger years.","Many female guests squealed in excitement. Stars twinkled in their eyes, and it looked like they would faint from excitement.","Looking at his elder robe and dashing looks, Zu An knew right away that he had to be the Second Elder, Hermes.","Hermes looked at Zu An and Chu Chuyan in contempt. “If you already have a wife, you should be faithful to her and avoid other women. The last thing you should do is to bring her here when asking for Isabella’s hand of marriage. You’re the worst scum there is out there.”","Zu An was speechless. This is annoying. I forgot about his devoted lover character setting.","Hermes’s words made many female guests clutch their chests and swoon.","“Hermes is so devoted to his lover!”","“This is a true man!”","“How wonderful if I could marry him.”","“Dream on! If he’s going to marry anyone, it would be me.”","“That Zu fellow is a scoundrel. Pui! What a waste of his good skin.”","...","Hearing the insults directed at her lover, Chu Chuyan interjected, “Sir, you aren’t me. How do you know I’m not happy? I fully support Ah Zu proposing to Miss Isabella. The two of them have gone through a huge ordeal and forged a tight bond through it. It’d instead pain me if they had to part ways over me.”","Hermes sneered, “You love him and don’t want to see him unhappy, but he ignores your feelings and pursues other women. Doesn’t that show that your love for him is unrequited?”","Chu Chuyan looked at Zu An with a tender smile. “We have been through a lot. Our feelings have transcended words and form. We don’t have to prove our relationship to others.”","The esteemed guests gathered in this palatial banquet hall watched in awe as a beautiful lady stood steadfast to protect her lover.","Fourth Elder Mastema stared intently at Chu Chuyan. “Miss Chu, do you have any sisters?”","“I have two younger sisters.” Chu Chuyan was perplexed by the abrupt question.","“I dare not dream of someone like Miss Chu. Can you introduce your sisters to me? I’d be content if they are half as gentle as you,” Mastema looked at her with lustful eyes.","Chu Chuyan said, “...I’m afraid they are already married.”","“What a pity.” Mastema sighed as he reluctantly tore his eyes away from her.","“Stop changing the topic, fourth brother. Her words don’t make any sense.” Hermes frowned.","He was about to continue speaking when a bewitching voice echoed, “Second brother, I think this fellow isn't bad. I like him.”"]},{"number":2883,"title":"Chapter 2883: Chapter 2835: Is It a Coincidence?","paragraphs":["Fragrance wafted through the air as a woman wearing a low-cut dress strutted over. All of the men present couldn’t help but be drawn to the way her hips moved rhythmically along with her footsteps.","There was no need for introductions; she was the Conglomerate’s Fifth Elder Lilith. Indeed, the first thought that appeared in anyone’s head upon seeing her was of bed.","She walked to Zu An’s side and gently tidied his clothes. “What a dashing one you are. I can see how you won the fancy of so many ladies.”","Her voice was coy like that of a young lady. Her touch was so light that it induced goosebumps all over Zu An’s body.","Chu Chuyan was displeased. How can she walk right up and touch him? But since Lilith was speaking up for Zu An, she held herself back from blowing up.","“You’re very beautiful as well, madam.” Zu An quickly recovered and returned the compliment.","“Call me big sister. I’m still single,” Lilith replied coyly, rolling her eyes.","Zu An was speechless. He'd learned that Lilith had many boy toys from Isabella. It was hard to associate her with the word ‘single’.","Lilith turned to the Second Elder and said with teary eyes, “Second brother, you can’t impose your principles on others. There aren’t many people who can fulfill such a virtuous stance when it comes to romance. Since the two people in question are fine with it, there’s no need for us to point fingers at them.”","The plump Fourth Elder chuckled. “What do you think, fifth sister? Should we let this fellow participate in our Order Ceremony?”","Lilith averted her gaze in disgust. Her choice of lovers consisted of either beautiful men or brawny hunks. She wasn't into pigs. “I don’t have any qualms with this dashing lad.”","“Let’s hold a vote then,” First Elder Oberon proposed. A huge red ‘X’ appeared above his head.","This was how the Conglomerate’s Round Table Council made decisions. Whenever they reached an impasse, they held a vote to decide on the course of action.","Without any hesitation, Oberon cast an ‘object’ vote.","The second ‘X’ soon appeared, as Second Elder Hermes also cast an ‘object’ vote.","Third Elder Aragorn hesitated for a moment, but faced with his daughter’s pleading eyes, he cast an ‘approve’ vote.","Fourth Elder Mastema looked around with an innocent smile. A green tick soon appeared above his head. He had also cast an ‘approve’ vote.","Fifth Elder Lilith cast a bewitching glance at Zu An. Needless to say, she cast an ‘approve’ vote as well.","Sixth Elder Naraka had been present all along, but being the gloomy man he was, hardly anyone noticed his presence before this vote was held. He cast an ‘object’ vote.","It was 3v3. The tiebreaker fell on Seventh Elder Viktor.","Isabella looked nervous. Viktor was an impartial man who staunchly followed his principles, never bending to anyone. To her surprise, however, Viktor cast an ‘approve’ vote.","Oberon’s face darkened. He could use his authority as the First Elder to veto the motion, but such abuse of power could fracture the relations among the seven elders. Unless absolutely necessary, he was reluctant to resort to this move.","“The majority approves of him participating in the Order Ceremony. We shall follow the result of the vote,” First Elder Oberon calmly declared. His voice was no longer as stiff as before.","Isabella’s eyes twinkled in happiness. The Order Ceremony was just a symbolic ritual, but participating in this major event would still help to build Zu An’s credentials. Big brother Zu will benefit from participating in this, and that will make it easier for us to...","Meanwhile, Zu An was nowhere near as relaxed. He hadn’t forgotten that he had come here under the Deity of Memory’s order. Is the major event related to the Order Ceremony? An event that catches a universal deity’s attention is anything but normal. I have to remain vigilant.","He was also surprised that so many elders had spoken up against the First Elder on his behalf, considering how he was only acquainted with Aragorn before this.","The Universal Conglomerate isn’t as peaceful as it looks.","When he learned that Zu An would be joining the Order Ceremony, Adrian’s expression darkened.","Just then, he heard his father’s voice. “Your life has been too easy so far. It’s not a bad thing for you to face some setbacks.”","Adrian’s face reddened in shame. “Yes, I’ll learn from this lesson.”","“Don’t take it to heart. There’ll be chances for you to exact vengeance in the Order Ceremony.”","Adrian was rendered speechless. You’re asking me not to take it to heart while telling me to exact vengeance?","It was also then that First Elder Oberon turned to Adrian and calmly said, “You should stand up where you have stumbled. When your father finally drags that orderless fellow under Order’s radiance, your heart will become impeccable once more.”","Adrian hesitantly asked, “But he’s a Memory envoy...”","“In the Order ceremony, everything is bathed in Order’s radiance. Not even other universal deities can peer into it.”","Adrian was overjoyed to hear that. “Yes! May Order’s radiance envelop the Myriad Worlds!”","Meanwhile, Isabella dragged Zu An up to Aragorn.","“Pleased to meet you, uncle.” Zu An bowed. Chu Chuyan greeted Aragorn with a nod, though she couldn’t help but feel a little uncomfortable.","“I hope you don’t blame me for settling you in another manor,” Aragorn said.","“I know that you have your considerations.” Zu An didn’t mind it. He was probably also trying to probe the stances of the other elders before deciding on his next move. Or maybe he thought that Adrian was a more suitable candidate. Regardless, it doesn’t matter.","All that matters to me is Isabella’s attitude.","“It’s good that you’re mature. Isabella is still much too young and childish. I can rest at ease entrusting her to your care.”","“Daddy~” Isabella complained coyly.","Aragorn looked at his daughter dotingly before turning to Zu An. “You must prepare yourself. We’ll be holding the Order Ceremony very soon. Miss Chu, you should join us as well.”","Zu An took the opportunity to ask, “May I know what the Order Ceremony entails?”","Aragorn explained, “To showcase Order’s radiance to the Myriad Worlds, every century we pick a world that has descended into chaos, restore order to it, and offer it as tribute to the great Deity of Order.","“This happens to be the tenth century, so we’ll be holding it at a larger scale. Other elders will participate in the event, and we have invited important figures from all over the Myriad Worlds to join us as well.”","Zu An asked, “Are we entering with our bodies? Will it be dangerous?”","“Yes, we will be entering with our bodies, but we will take the identities of people who exist in that world. It’s quite similar to the Deity of Death’s trial. As Memory’s envoy, you only have to record the events that unfold in the ceremony. I don’t think you’ll face any danger.","“Besides, the seven elders, including me, will be participating as well. Unless a universal deity descends, we should be able to overcome any danger.”","How many flags are you planning to raise? Zu An thought.","“Right. You should familiarize yourself with the world first. Everyone attending the Order Ceremony will be entering the world tomorrow morning. It is a cliched story about a feudal dynasty that is being invaded by enemies while facing uprising from its people.” Aragorn whipped out something resembling a tablet and handed it over.","An introduction video played on the tablet.","The subtlest look crept onto Zu An’s face as he watched the introduction video. Isn’t this the chaos that unfolded in the final years of the Ming Dynasty... How is it coincidentally another world I’m familiar with?"]},{"number":2884,"title":"Chapter 2884: Chapter 2836: How Did I Become Hong Chengchou?","paragraphs":["Zu An had been to larger dungeons before, and they were often related to the world he had been in before his transmigration. They were usually modeled after ancient dynasties.","If it had been once or twice, he could still shrug it off as a coincidence. But it had happened so many times that he would have to be a fool to brush it off.","He felt as if an invisible hand was secretly controlling everything. Could it be a universal deity?","Just then, Aragorn’s voice dragged him back to reality. “The identity you take on inside that world will be related to your path. Those of us from the Conglomerate are Order worshipers, so we’ll likely become members of the Ming Dynasty’s imperial court. Our mission will be to protect the imperial court and uphold order.","“You are a Memory envoy, so it’s unlikely that you’ll take on a dangerous position. It should either be that of a historian or a Western missionary.”","Chu Chuyan interjected, “The Conglomerate is filled with experts. Any one of them should be more than enough to turn the tides of an ancient feudal dynasty. Is there a need for so many people to enter the world at once?”","“That’s a great question, Miss Chu,” Aragorn said. “That world is a spacetime fragment replicated using a universal deity’s divine power. The cosmos has its way of finding equilibrium in all things. Indeed, our entrance will greatly strengthen the Ming Empire, but consequently, other worshipers will enter that world as its enemies as well.","“But there’s nothing to fear. The First Elder is personally leading the team, and the Holy Knight Order will be joining us as well. We’ll be able to surmount even the biggest waves.”","Stop planting flags! Zu An couldn’t help thinking.","Shortly after, the First Elder gathered everyone who would be participating in the Order Ceremony and briefed them on things they ought to look out for.","Zu An noted that other than the Third Elder and the Seventh Elder, the other elders were also participating in the Order Ceremony. Also, the Holy Knight Order and the other invited parties were mainly sending youths in for the ceremony.","They’re hoping to build the younger generation’s credentials through this. It can serve as a stepping stone for them to reach greater heights. That’s also the reason Isabella is participating in the Order Ceremony.","If not for Fourth Elder Mastema’s invitation, I’d have probably missed this Order Ceremony.","But what is Aragorn planning? Did he plan to stop me from attending, or is he waiting for other elders to make a move before intervening?","Meanwhile, Adrian recovered from the earlier setback. He smiled at Isabella and said, “Miss Bella, you can be assured that I’ll protect you inside the world, so you don’t need to be afraid.”","Isabella glanced at Zu An and said, “I have been through greater danger with big brother Zu, and he has protected me well. I’m sure this time will be no exception.”","Adrian’s eyebrows shot up. No wonder Isabella is so infatuated with that fellow. I didn’t know there was such a nuance to their relationship. Doesn’t that mean that if I protect her well in the dungeon, she’ll fall in love with me too?","“He’s participating as a Mirror Scribe to record everything. I’m afraid he might not be able to take good care of you. There are many talented prodigies from the Myriad Worlds here. I’m sure they surpass him in terms of strength and experience.”","His father had already counseled him. He knew that Zu An wasn’t truly strong; he merely had a set of unusual abilities that made him tricky to deal with. His father had just given him an artifact, so Zu An’s tricks wouldn’t work on him anymore. With my strength, I should be able to crush him easily.","The spectators agreed with him. Despite Zu An’s incredible stature as a Memory envoy, the aura he emanated was honestly weak.","Besides, Memory worshipers steered clear of secular affairs. They hardly had any sense of presence. It was truly an unusual turn of events for Zu An to have won Isabella’s heart.","Isabella looked at Zu An apologetically. “Big brother Zu, you mustn’t take those remarks to heart.”","Zu An shook his head. “I wouldn’t get angry at a bunch of dead people.”","An event that caught the attention of a universal deity had to be treated with utmost caution. Even a shockwave from it could easily claim countless lives.","“Ah?” Isabella was confused. She didn’t understand what Zu An was driving at.","Zu An didn’t bother explaining his remark. He merely reminded her, “It’s unlikely that the Order Ceremony will go smoothly. Once we arrive in that world, no matter our identities, let’s meet at the Forbidden Palace’s west gate[1].”","Having learned from his previous experience, he knew that they would likely be scattered across different places. They were fortunate to have crossed paths in the Deity of Death’s trial, but there was no guarantee they would have the same luck here.","He didn’t want to suffer the pain of parting ways with Chu Chuyan again.","Isabella nodded, whereas Chu Chuyan revealed a slight smile. The latter appeared to have understood Zu An’s sentiments.","The other youths clenched their jaws in anger. What sorcery has that fellow cast on Miss Isabella? He came with his wife to propose to Miss Isabella, but not only is Miss Isabella not angry, they’re even getting along well!","The elders opened a spacetime passageway that resembled a stargate and entered it. Augustus, Adrian, and the Holy Knight Order’s elites marched toward the stargate with their heads held up high.","Zu An grabbed Isabella and Chu Chuyan’s hands and made his way over as well. Despite knowing that they would likely be separated in the world, he felt more at ease doing this.","That sparked another wave of fury from the youths.","Those who entered the stargate morphed into stars and descended toward the unique world, which was set in the final years of the Ming Dynasty. They would assume identities of historical figures to restore the collapsed order.","Just then, a finger appeared in the sky and gently touched one of the stars, altering its trajectory. No one participating in the Order Ceremony noticed this anomaly.","When Zu An woke up, he found himself sitting in a classical study room. He exhaled in relief. Looks like I’ve taken on the role of a historian. I wonder what my identity is here.","Just then, he heard someone running toward the study room. “Milord, bad news! The Red Madame[2] has brought her subordinates to raid our prison!”","Zu An was startled. Memories flashed through his mind, and he suddenly understood what his identity in this world was. He had the weirdest expression on his face.","Hold on. How did I end up as Hong Chengchou?","Hong Chengchou was a famous Han[3] traitor in history. He held an important military post in Great Ming, wielding military power across several provinces. He quelled the peasants’ uprising, which had great momentum at that time.","Later, the Chongzhen Emperor dispatched him to the borders to deal with the invading Manchus. However, he was captured and eventually defected to the Qing Dynasty. The strategies he contributed played a huge role in the Qing Dynasty’s swift capture of the Central Plains.","But this was the Order Ceremony!","The Universal Conglomerate, the Holy Knight Order, and Isabella were all on the Ming Dynasty’s side, and they were seeking to rebuild the Ming Dynasty’s imperial power to bring stability to the world.","Doesn’t that make me the antagonist here?","Not only am I a traitor in the eyes of the Ming Dynasty, but the Qing Dynasty will also view me as a defector and discriminate against me.","More importantly, aren’t I supposed to be a neutral Mirror Scribe who records the events here? How did I end up with such an influential position here?","1. The Forbidden Palace is where the emperor’s consorts and concubines live. ☜","2. Red Madame, or Hong Niangzi , was a famous female rebel leader in the final years of the Ming Dynasty. She was born in a small village and led a local militia to fight against officials who sought to exploit them. ☜","3. Han is the dominant ethnic group in that era. Guo Jing, Huang Rong, and Yang Guo were all Hans ☜"]},{"number":2885,"title":"Chapter 2885: Chapter 2837: The Red Madame","paragraphs":["Noticing the lack of response from Zu An, the soldier bucked up his courage and called out, “Milord? Milord?”","Zu An snapped out of his daze and asked, “What did you just say?”","“The Red Madame has brought her people here to raid our prison. I hear she’s here to rescue a scholar;y mooch she’s interested in,” the soldier anxiously replied.","Zu An slowly remembered the details surrounding his character.","Hong Chengchou’s current position was Shanxi’s Provincial Administrative Commissioner[1].","His position should have brought him great comfort and power during peacetime[2], but unfortunately, they were in the final years of the Ming Dynasty. There were frequent clashes with the Manchus in the Dongbei region, and the increased taxes on the populace had sparked rebellions all over the northern areas.","It was exceptionally bad in Shanxi. Many peasants had turned to banditry, and the Red Madame was a regional heroine with many brothers under her command. Few had seen her real face, though most recognized her by her trademark red clothes.","Black streaks appeared on Zu An’s face. Even peasants are blatantly raiding the prison now. Are you sure it’s possible to re-establish order in Great Ming?","His original intention had been to rush to the Forbidden City to meet up with Chu Chuyan and Isabella, but he couldn’t turn a blind eye to this matter. I guess I’ll take a look first before considering my next move.","Let’s see. The prison should be in this direction...","He tapped into the original Hong Chengchou’s memories and soon found the location. With a single stride, he was already at the prison’s vicinity.","The soldier who was left in the room exclaimed in astonishment, “I didn’t know Lord Hong was this formidable. We’re saved!”","Meanwhile, the prison was in complete chaos. Dozens of masked bandits charged ferociously at the wardens, breaching their defensive line.","Zu An noticed that these people weren’t fighting like normal feudal soldiers; they were utilizing cultivator methods.","Our appearance here must have induced some changes in the world’s background setting. Even ordinary troops have grown considerably stronger.","“Here comes another dog official!”","The bandits’ eyes lit up upon seeing Zu An’s official robes, and they immediately charged at him with their sabers.","Zu An was speechless. And I was still thinking about which faction I should align myself with.","With a harrumph, he grabbed the incoming sabers and twisted them.","The bandits were left dumbstruck. In the blink of an eye, they were all lying on the ground.","“All hail Lord Hong!”","The wardens were moved to tears. They quickly captured the collapsed bandits before cheering for Zu An.","Before Zu An could react, a sweet, feminine voice echoed, “We’ve captured the target. Retreat! Hm?”","A red figure dashed out of the prison with a scholar in her hand. She was about to urge her subordinates to leave when she stiffened up upon seeing the situation outside.","Whispers broke out. Who could have thought the legendary bandit would be such a beauty?","Zu An figured that since the Red Madame was so well-known, it could be worthwhile to capture her and gather more information. Thus, he made a move.","He flashed forward to the Red Madame to grab her, but the latter reacted swiftly. Her body twisted at an incredibly exaggerated angle to dodge his hand.","“Hm?” While Zu An had held back to avoid alarming those present, it was still beyond the means of a normal bandit to avoid his grasp.","So, he made a second move. This time, he made sure to block every single route of escape.","“We’re on the same side!”","Zu An frowned. The voice sounded familiar, but he couldn’t put his finger on who it was in the moment.","The Red Madame took off her veil, revealing a sweet smile and a dignified demeanor. Her appearance should have been at odds with her fierce reputation, yet it somehow went well together.","“Tang Tian’er?” Zu An hadn’t expected to meet her here.","She had close ties with the secretive Hub of Freedom, and she knew that its goal was to help the previous dynasty’s imperial grandson reclaim the throne. However, Zu An’s deeds back then had unintentionally resulted in the Hub of Freedom’s disappearance, and she’d refused to accept his bestowment.","They’d gone separate ways afterward. Little did he expect to bump into her here. The odds of that were smaller than finding a needle in the ocean.","Tang Tian’er dropped the scholar to the ground and leaped into Zu An’s embrace. “ Wuuu! I missed you! I thought I’d never see you again.”","Zu An’s arms remained open, feeling conflicted as to whether he should embrace her or not.","The nearby wardens and bandits were baffled. What’s going on? Our boss is hugging that official (bandit)?","Zu An knew it wouldn’t be good to do this in public, so he brought her to a private room to talk.","While being pulled away, Tang Tian’er didn’t forget to say, “Don’t hurt my brothers.”","So, Zu An issued the order.","The wardens replied with smiles, “Alright, alright.”","You must be kidding me. There’s no way we would dare hurt the subordinates of Lord Hong’s woman.","“Time to speak. What are you doing here?” Zu An questioned the woman before him.","“You’re the one who disappeared into thin air and abandoned me...” Tang Tian’er suddenly began sobbing as if she had suffered a huge grievance.","Zu An replied, “...When were we even together?”","“We shared a bath! You’ve seen and touched me from head to toe!” Tang Tian’er glared at Zu An.","Zu An huffed, “It was an urgent situation. Besides, I didn’t touch you...”","“You just didn’t want to take responsibility. That’s why I didn’t bother you.” Tang Tian’er harrumphed. “When the Divine Palaces appeared, I followed my heart’s will and entered the Chaos and Enigma Divine Palace. I went through a few trials and became stronger. Then, I was brought to this dungeon. I didn’t expect to bump into you here. Looks like we’re fated.”","She wrapped her hands around Zu An’s neck and looked at him with loving eyes.","Zu An knew she was a liar at her core, so he took her words with a pinch of salt. “What’s your goal in this dungeon?”","“I don’t have any goals. The Deity of Chaos and Enigma never set any objective for the trials. I concluded that all I have to do is survive.”","“Is it that simple?” It does make sense, considering Mi Li’s eccentric personality... Zu An quickly reined in those dangerous thoughts.","“It isn’t simple at all! All the worlds I entered are dangerous. This world, in particular, is extremely chaotic. However, now that I’ve bumped into you, it should be fine.” Tang Tian’er said with a smile.","“You should be worried about bumping into me instead,” Zu An scoffed. He ignored Tang Tian’er’s shocked expression and continued, “How did you end up as the Red Madame?”","“It was all to survive. I’ve created a space for myself using my fists. I also don’t know why everyone calls me the Red Madame.”","“Who’s the scholar you were rescuing?”","“That stinky scholar? I noticed that he had sharp wits and wanted to bring him in as my strategist to dominate the world, but he refused to join me. I was glad when I heard he was captured by the officials. I thought I could make him owe me a debt by rescuing him, but I ended up bumping into you.”","Tang Tian’er’s eyes glistened. “Now that I have you, I don’t need the scholar anymore. I’ll be following you from now on. Are you going to become the regent once more and conquer the world?”","1. He can be considered the highest administrative official managing Shanxi, akin to a feudal mayor but with greater supervision and accountability to the imperial court. ☜","2. Being the Provincial Administrative Commissioner means that he’s at the top of the hierarchy in the region. The only one who can threaten him is the imperial court, but it’s too far away to properly keep tabs on him. ☜"]},{"number":2886,"title":"Chapter 2886: Chapter 2838: The Conditions Back Then","paragraphs":["Zu An’s eyelids twitched. What the heck is she saying?","He was about to say something when a soldier outside anxiously reported, “Bad news, Lord Hong! Wang Zuohua, Miao Mei, and a few others have encircled Hancheng. Hancheng is on the verge of collapse!”","Zu An’s expression darkened. I’ve only arrived in this world, but trouble keeps knocking.","“Tell Yang He to dispatch reinforcements to Hancheng. Why are you reporting this to me?”","His current position was focused on administrative affairs, whereas Yang He was Shanxi’s Governor-General of the Three Frontiers[1]. Military affairs fell under the latter’s jurisdiction.","“Lord Yang doesn’t have soldiers to dispatch anymore, which is why I came to Lord Hong to seek help.”","Zu An was rendered speechless. Memories flooded into his mind. That Yang trash clashed with the traitors several times and lost the few garrison troops we have left.","The imperial court’s finances were in a disastrous state, and officials had been siphoning away public funds. That had severely limited Great Ming’s military force.","“Where am I supposed to find troops for you?”","Zu An wondered whether to personally make a trip over to resolve this issue, but he was worried that he would draw hatred if he stood out too much.","“I have them!” Tang Tian’er immediately lifted her hand. “My underlings are all valiant warriors. We have another hundred men in our den. Throw a few of your soldiers into the mix, and our forces should be sufficient to deal with the likes of Wang Zuogua and Miao Mei.”","Zu An didn’t turn down her offer. This is a world that caught the eye of a universal deity. I better make use of every resource within reach.","Tang Tian’er was overjoyed. She quickly gathered her underlings.","When they heard that they were going to cooperate with the officials to deal with other rebels, the bandits were confused. Something felt off here.","But they quickly remembered how formidable that Hong guy was. They were supposed to have been executed for raiding the prison, but here, they were given a chance to make up for their crimes. Our big sister must have fought for this opportunity for us.","The thought of that left them moved.","Zu An and Tang Tian’er rushed to Hancheng with their underlings. They successfully suppressed Wang Zuogua and Miao Mei’s armies, but they were still astonished by what they saw.","They’d expected those two armies to be weak, but their fighting prowess was on par with that of demihumans. They even had mages in their ranks.","“Our arrival must have completely shaken up this world’s power balance.” Unlike in the Deity of Death’s trial, Zu An’s abilities weren’t nerfed here. He thought about what Aragorn had told him and quickly came to a conclusion.","Shortly after, Shanxi’s Governor-General of Three Frontiers, Yang He, soon arrived and heaped compliments on Zu An. “Little brother Hong, you came with impeccable timing... You’re not only well-learned, but knowledgeable about military stratagems as well. I’m sure you’ll become a pillar of our empire in the future. I have already reported this matter to the imperial court. I’m sure you’ll be rewarded very soon.”","Zu An responded casually before returning to his room with Tang Tian’er. There, he asked, “The scholar you rescued is Li Yan?”","“How did you know?” Tang Tian’er widened her eyes.","“That person is indeed talented. He’d be an invaluable asset in times of chaos.” Zu An had specially paid a visit to the scholar to confirm his talents.","“You wish to recruit him? No problem. He owes me his life. I’m sure he’ll listen to me.”","“No, you should take him and join a rebel group under Li Zicheng.”","“???” Tang Tian’er was confused.","Zu An explained, “Basically, I want you to serve as a spy.”","With the advantage of precognition in this world, he knew that Li Zicheng would become the famous Thunder King and overthrow the Ming Dynasty... though later he would lose his empire to the Manchus at the Battle of Shanhai Pass.","Nevertheless, there was no doubt that he was the one who would uproot the Ming Dynasty. If the Order faction sought to protect the Ming Dynasty, Li Zicheng would be their greatest enemy.","In history, Hong Chengchou had successfully suppressed the uprising of the peasants, beating Li Zicheng down until he had to escape with eighteen cavalrymen.","Now that Zu An had become Hong Chengchou, he didn’t know how things would go down in this world, but he knew that he needed to start scheming now to control the situation.","Tang Tian’er pressed her lips together. “You want to use me as a honey trap? Can you bear to push me into the arms of another man?”","Zu An huffed. “Who told you to resort to a honey trap? I know that you’re skilled at playing mind games. Li Yan will be besotted with you, and you should be able to easily win Li Zicheng’s trust as well.”","“Thanks for your compliment.” Tang Tian’er smiled. She leaned in and asked, “Aren’t you afraid that I might betray you?”","Zu An fell silent for a moment. “I am afraid, but I’m willing to trust you.”","“Tsk. You’re giving me nothing but such empty words.” Tang Tian’er looked at him and asked, “Do you still remember promising me a favor back then?”","Zu An nodded. “I do.”","He’d promised to do her a favor if she helped to bring Yu Yanluo’s clansmen out of the city back then.","“You won’t go back on your word?”","“I won’t.”","Tang Tian’er opened her mouth, only to give up in the end. “Forget it. I know that you’re a gentleman, but even I think it’s too much to ask that of you right now. How about this? I’ll help you spy on Li Zicheng, and we’ll combine both favors. Once we settle things here, you’ll marry me.”","“Sure,” Zu An replied.","“What did you say?” Tang Tian’er stiffened up.","“I said I’ll marry you. But you should also know that I have a lot of lovers, so if you don’t mind...”","Before he could finish speaking, Tang Tian’er leaped up and exclaimed, “Why would I mind? Keke! There’s nothing I love more than fighting with others! Once I have so many sisters to fight with, I won’t feel lonely anymore.”","Her excitement didn’t seem to be feigned. Zu An felt dazed. I can’t tell if she’s being honest or just pretending.","He felt as if Tang Tian’er was wrapped in a veil, making it hard to determine her true nature or whether she was lying or not.","But that didn’t change the things they had been through. Tang Tian’er had made a huge sacrifice for him, so he felt obliged to take responsibility for her. He was no longer the immature youth he was back then, and he understood the importance of reciprocation.","Marriage could be considered a form of transaction, so he didn’t see any problem with that. Besides, the two of them were indeed attracted to each other.","“Shall we consummate our marriage today?” Tang Tian’er smiled sweetly but coyly.","Zu An burst into laughter. “I can’t wrong you like that. I’ll properly wed you once we clear this dungeon.”","Tang Tian’er was disappointed, though she also secretly breathed a sigh of relief. “Fine. No backsies.”","“I always keep my promises.”","“Tsk. According to the Hub of Freedom’s information network, back when you were in Brightmoon City, you were a scammer through and through.”","Zu An’s face reddened.","Tang Tian’er suddenly tiptoed and kissed him on the cheek. “Wait for me. I’ll marry you once I’m done with this.“","She shyly ran out before roaring at her subordinates to retreat. She was evidently in a good mood.","But Zu An felt uneasy. It feels like we’ve planted flags everywhere. Let’s hope everything goes smoothly.","An imperial edict was suddenly relayed from the sky, praising his merits for resolving Hancheng’s crisis. Then, he was commanded to return to the capital to meet the emperor, where he would be rewarded and entrusted with heavy responsibilities.","1. He guarded three borders, aka Yansui, Ningxia, and Gansu ☜"]},{"number":2887,"title":"Chapter 2887: Chapter 2839: Surprising Identities","paragraphs":["Looking at the imperial edict that had been delivered from thousands of kilometers away, Zu An was awed.","This is indeed a different world. If the imperial edict was delivered so fast, the communication networks here should also be much more efficient than in the ancient feudal dynasties. There might just be a chance to re-establish order.","Zu An accepted the imperial edict. Marked on it were the coordinates of the capital. He channeled his ki and was soon teleported to the capital.","The laws of this world were rather peculiar. Typically speaking, with his cultivation, Zu An should have been able to swiftly cover the distance between Shanxi and the capital. In fact, he had already tried it out. Yet he felt a bizarre rejection from the world when he tried to fly there himself, and the distance was much longer than he had expected.","The world must have adjusted itself in response to the increased strength of its inhabitants.","But with the imperial edict’s protection, Zu An could teleport there right away.","As soon as Zu An reached the capital, he made his way to the Forbidden City’s western wall to look for Isabella and Chu Chuyan.","But only Isabella was waiting for him there. She was dressed in palace clothes, exuding a youthful yet traditional charm.","“Big brother Zu!” Isabella spotted him and ran over excitedly. She had been waiting here for some time now.","“Little sister Bella!” Zu An’s nervous heart calmed down a little as he felt her trembling body.","Just then, a maid timidly reminded, “Your Highness, this is inappropriate. Rumors might arise if others see this.”","Zu An’s eyes widened. “Did you take on the role of a princess?”","“Yup,” Isabella replied via telepathy to prevent the maid from eavesdropping on their conversation. “I’m the Chongzhen Emperor’s second daughter, the Princess of Eternal Peace, Zhu Meichuo. My nickname is Lil’ Ninth.”","Zu An was speechless. To think that she became Lil’ Ninth, the pitiful princess who had her country destroyed and her arm chopped off by her father, the Chongzhen Emperor. [1]","“I’ve been waiting for you the last few days. You’re finally here. Hm? Why don’t I see big sister Chu?” Isabella looked around.","Zu An’s heart clenched up. “You didn’t see her either?”","“I didn’t. I thought you two were together.”","Zu An shook his head as he wondered where Chu Chuyan was.","“Don’t worry too much, big brother Zu. Big sister Chu is strong and sharp-witted. I’m sure she’ll be able to protect herself well. She’s probably on the way here now,” Isabella consoled him.","Zu An nodded. He was able to teleport here quickly thanks to the imperial edict. If Chu Chuyan had transmigrated to a faraway place, it would indeed take some time for her to get here.","Just then, the imperial edict glowed. A voice urged him to quickly enter the palace.","Zu An looked at Isabella and frowned. “Chongzhen is...”","“Yes, it’s the First Elder,” Isabella replied with a bitter expression. She had always been fearful of the stern First Elder. She didn’t think she would have to role play as his daughter in this world. This was a huge bummer to her.","...","It was only when Zu An arrived at the Imperial Library that he understood what First Elder Oberon intended.","Those who had been summoned here were all members of the Order faction.","First Elder Oberon was the lofty Chongzhen Emperor. Augustus was the Northeast Field Marshal tasked with the responsibility of fending against the Manchus, Yuan Chonghuan[2], whereas Adrian was Yuan Chengzhi.","This made Zu An’s heart pound rapidly. Is this the power of destiny?","But what shocked him more was the Second Elder’s identity. The devoted, dashing middle-aged man, who had charmed many women, was actually Wu Sangui[3]!","Wu Sangui was an infamous Han traitor in this world. In history, he was infuriated that Li Zicheng had held his concubine, Chen Yuanyuan, hostage after invading the imperial palace, so he granted the Manchus free passageway into the Central Plains. That made him a sinner for many generations to come.","How did the righteous Second Elder Hermes end up as this infamous Han traitor? Isn’t he known for his devotion to his lover? Did he fall in love with this world’s Chen Yuanyuan?","This feels impossible no matter how I look at it.","Fourth Elder Mastema was an official in charge of finance. Meanwhile, Sixth Elder Naraka was Sun Chengzong, a military official assigned to guard the northeast together with Augustus and Adrian. His responsibilities lay more toward the administrative and logistics side.","The others participating in the Order Ceremony were mainly their underlings.","While Zu An was assessing the others, the others were also assessing him.","Adrian asked, “Shouldn’t you be a historian or a missionary? How did you end up as a provincial commissioner?”","“I don’t know either. That’s the position I ended up with.” Zu An was confused as well.","“There’s something wrong with his identity!” Adrian told Oberon. “First Elder, I propose executing this fellow, or else he might derail our plan to re-establish order.”","Isabella opened her arms to protect Zu An. “Nonsense! With big brother Zu’s help, we will be a step closer to our goal. You’re just trying to exact vengeance on him!”","Adrian’s expression darkened.","Fourth Elder Mastema also spoke up cheerily, “Bella is right. We should get all the help we can right now. I’m sure he’d be of help as a Memory envoy.”","Augustus scoffed, “I just tore through the Manchu army. By this world’s time, it should take me no more than five years to quell the unrest in Liaodong. We don’t need help from an outsider.”","The others in the Order faction took the chance to fawn on Augustus.","From their words, Zu An understood that Augustus had just crushed the Manchu army under Hong Taiji’s command in the Battle of Ning-Jin[4]. No wonder he’s so proud that his ass is almost poking into the sky.","But why does the ‘quell the unrest in Liaodong in five years’ part sound so familiar to me? [5]","Isabella anxiously spoke up for Zu An. “Big brother Zu rescued the besieged Hancheng and defeated several rebel armies as well!”","Zu An had told her what he’d done on the way to the Imperial Library.","Adrian sneered, “Don’t be fooled by him. Whether it’s that Wang Zuogua or Miao Mei, they are merely a bunch of rabble. Any one of my underlings could easily subdue them. That’s no merit at all.”","“You!” Isabella was infuriated, but she didn’t know the situation well enough to refute him.","Fourth Elder Mastema stepped forward to defuse the situation. “There’s a huge gap in our finances right now. We don’t have the money to maintain an army in Shanxi. Even a skilled housewife will struggle to whip up a meal without rice. His ability to quell the rebellion with limited resources at hand is still praiseworthy.”","“Enough. I gathered all of you here to solve problems, not to squabble.” First Elder Oberon harrumphed as he set the tone straight. “I have looked into the Ming Dynasty’s woes. The root of its problem lies in the collapse of its finances. Silver import from the Americas has slowed, and Japan has closed its markets and forbidden export of silver. This has resulted in deflation.[6]","“Due to a lack of funds, additional taxes have been imposed on the populace. In particular, the Liaodong military levy, the bandit subjugation levy, and the troop training levy have inflicted great suffering upon the populace. This has resulted in the people falling into poverty and resorting to banditry.","“How should we resolve these problems?”","1. The Chongzhen Emperor was known to love his family. When rebel leader Li Zicheng invaded the imperial palace, the Chongzhen Emperor was afraid that his family would be tortured and forced into prostitution, so he tried to kill them. Lil’ Ninth lost her arm but survived the ordeal. ☜","2. Yuan Chonghuan was a national hero of the Ming Dynasty. He managed to defeat the Manchus on several occasions, hindering their war efforts. However, the Chongzhen Emperor later sentenced him to death by ‘slow slicing’. ☜","3. Wu Sangui was a Ming general who was later condemned as a Han traitor for defecting to the Qing Dynasty. When Li Zicheng stomped the imperial palace, he also held Wu Sangui’s family hostage. In response, Wu Sangui opened the Shanhai Pass for the Manchus to enter Beijing and establish their rule. ☜","4. Yuan Chonghuan, the general whom Augustus has transmigrated into, achieved this feat as well. ☜","5. Yes, Yuan Chonghuan famously made this declaration in history as well. Two years into the plan, he was framed for colluding with the enemies and sentenced to death by ‘slow slicing’. ☜","6. The Ming Dynasty tried to roll out copper coins and paper notes, but both attempts failed. Their dominant currency is silver. ☜"]},{"number":2888,"title":"Chapter 2888: Chapter 2840: The Beautiful Silhouette in the Palace","paragraphs":["Augustus spoke up. “There’s nothing difficult about that. The root of Great Ming’s problems is that it has lost more wars than it has won, causing military expenditure to become an insatiable black hole for the imperial court. But with my Holy Knight Order guarding the borders...”","He paused before adding, “...and with the aid of the Second Elder and the Sixth Elder, even if the enemies are backed by Annihilation worshipers, we should be able to quell them with ease and reduce the empire’s expenditure.”","First Elder Oberon nodded. “I’m at ease after hearing your words, captain.”","Fourth Elder Mastema interjected with a frown, “But even if the captain is adept at warfare, we’ll still need funds to get things into motion. The armies stationed at the borders need rations from the imperial palace, and we need resources to subdue the peasant rebels. We need money everywhere, but our coffers are empty.”","Sixth Elder Naraka remarked with a frown, “It’s just an ancient feudal empire. Can’t you settle it?”","“Be that as it may, our arrival here has stirred some tricky changes in the economy.” The Fourth Elder rubbed his head. “Second brother, you’re the one who manages our Conglomerate’s businesses. Do you have any ideas?”","Second Elder Hermes calmly asked, “What is the imperial court’s greatest expenditure aside from military spending?”","Fourth Elder Mastema pulled out the scrolls he had prepared beforehand. “Great Ming has enacted a series of foolish policies. For instance, noble titles are unconditionally passed down through the relatives of the imperial family, but at the same time, they are forbidden from taking the imperial examinations or taking official roles out of wariness. These people are worse than pigs! They aren’t bringing any good at all, yet they continue to eat into the empire’s coffers.”","“Why don’t you just cut them off? They’re useless anyway,” Sixth Elder Naraka asked. They were just passers-by in this world, so they had no intention of letting the relatives of the imperial family continue mooching off them.","Fourth Elder Mastema shook his head. “I’m afraid that’s out of the question. They are ultimately still Zhu clansmen[1]. We would risk diminishing imperial authority. The officials would also impeach us for arbitrarily straying away from tradition.","“That move would also risk provoking the feudal kings to action. If so, that would put us in a worse position. We’d have to deal with the invaders, the peasant uprising, and the revolt of the feudal kings simultaneously.”","Second Elder Hermes scanned through the scrolls with his powerful divine sense. “This is simple. We’ll use the next five years of salt and tea trade permits as leverage to issue war bonds. These war bonds will be buyable by officials and feudal kings, and we will not record the names of bond buyers.","“This way, the officials and feudal kings need not worry about the emperor misunderstanding and thinking that they have earned their huge wealth through corruption. We can kickstart the process by issuing them to the empress’ and consorts’ families first, so as to encourage others to follow suit.","“At the same time, we’ll start a system of earning an official position through donations. We’ll justify it by tying it to national defense. To reduce the backlash from officials who have risen through the ranks via imperial examinations, we’ll limit this system to feudal kings and imperial relatives for now. Once their donation hits a target, we’ll bestow them with the corresponding official position.","“To ensure that feudal kings donate, we’ll first crack down on a heinous, obnoxious feudal king, accusing him of going against ancestral teachings and being disloyal. That will win us the people’s hearts while intimidating the other feudal kings.","“We’ll establish an overseas offshore company, and encourage the feudal kings to invest in an armed merchant convoy and head toward Nanyang[2] with their people to build up their own fiefs. We’ll demand taxes on their land and revenue, and in exchange, we’ll recognize their autonomy. I’m sure many feudal kings would be incentivized by the opportunity to expand their borders.","“That will reduce the imperial court’s expenditure while opening a new source of revenue.”","“Great Ming is corrupted to its core, however. No matter how good the policies are, there is bound to be problems in their execution. That’s why we’ll need first brother and fourth brother to keep a close eye on the execution.","“By the time we’re back on track through issuing war bonds and dealing with the feudal kings, we should have already nurtured a batch of reliable underlings. With that, we can deal with the cartels within the imperial court and simultaneously resolve the land and tax problem.”","...","Second Elder Hermes spoke with clear logic. His points were so pinpoint and direct that it induced loud applause from the crowd.","Zu An was awed. I can see why the Second Elder manages the Universal Conglomerate’s businesses. His insights transcend this era. Under his sharp analysis, unsolvable problems become simple.","At the same time, he was perplexed. Second Elder Hermes was the most suitable candidate to become the finance minister, so how had he ended up as Wu Sangui? Should I warn the First Elder about his possible betrayal?","No, that won’t do. I’m on bad terms with the First Elder. He’ll think that I’m trying to sow discord among them. It’ll just put me in a tight spot.","Besides, it’s unlikely that the Second Elder will become a Han traitor like Wu Sangui. He’s practically in the same position as me. I’m also Hong Chengchou, but that doesn’t mean that I’ll side with Annihilation’s Manchus.","Zu An dispelled his reservations with a chuckle.","First Elder Oberon proceeded to allocate tasks. Even Zu An was appointed as the Minister of War, tasked with looking after Shanxi, Gansu, Yansui, and Ningxia.","The First Elder and the others viewed the peasant uprising as a pebble in their path; their biggest enemy was still the Manchus, who had been augmented with Annihilation power.","Only Zu An felt uneasy. I wonder if this world’s Li Zicheng will mature into the same formidable power that swept Great Ming off its feet in history. I might be overthinking it. There are so many experts from the Order faction here. I doubt even Li Zicheng can do much.","As he left the Imperial Library, his mind was filled with thoughts about Chu Chuyan’s whereabouts. Just then, he heard a coy laugh. “What a coincidence. You truly look dashing. No wonder Lil’ Ninth is so fond of you.”","Zu An turned around and saw a bewitching woman sashaying over with an entourage of eunuchs and palace maids. It was Fifth Elder Lilith.","“The noble consort has arrived!”","Zu An was startled. The only noble consort in Chongzhen Palace was Noble Consort Tian[3]. Is that the Fifth Elder’s identity in this world?","Lilith waved her underlings away. Isabella nervously stepped forward to protect Zu An.","“Oh? Are you protecting him? Are you worried that I’ll eat him up?” Lilith chuckled.","Isabella’s face reddened. Lilith was still her elder, after all.","“Why didn’t you join the earlier discussion in the Imperial Library?” Zu An asked.","“We have more than enough heads to handle an ailing feudal empire. I’m only here to enjoy myself,” Lilith said while eyeing Zu An. “But there’s nothing here but palace maids and eunuchs. The guards are too timid to do anything. Little brother, why don’t you stay in the imperial palace with me for a while?”","“Fifth Elder!” Isabella exclaimed angrily.","Lilith paid her no mind. “I’ll accompany you wherever you want to go if you stay with me.”","Isabella was no match for a veteran like Lilith. Her ears turned completely red.","Lilith was about to continue teasing Zu An when a dissatisfied voice echoed from the side, “Noble Consort Tian, please watch your words.”","Zu An’s heart quivered. He turned around to look at a familiar silhouette. He hadn’t expected to bump into her here.","1. The family name of the Ming Dynasty’s imperial family ☜","2. The Southeast Asia region ☜","3. Noble Consort Tian Xiuying was the Chongzhen Emperor’s favorite consort. ☜"]},{"number":2889,"title":"Chapter 2889: Chapter 2841: Passing Away","paragraphs":["A slender figure who resembled a lady from an ink painting slowly walked over. She wore a white palace dress, and her hair was fixed in place by a simple white jade hairpin. She exuded an air of loftiness and distance.","But when she met eyes with Zu An, her eyes rippled as if a peach blossom flower’s petal had fallen on the surface of a calm lake.","“Paying respect to Empress Yi'an,” the other palace maids and eunuchs greeted her.","Even the Fifth Elder had to bow as well. This lady was clearly of a higher stature than her in this world. Even though she was reluctant to lower her head, she couldn’t talk back to Empress Yi'an, or else she would risk exposing her identity and triggering a series of unpredictable chain reactions in this dungeon.","The various powers in the Myriad Worlds had learned this lesson from piling up corpses.","Zu An, through conversing with Isabella, had gotten a rough idea of the key figures in the imperial palace.","The previous emperor had no sons, so his empress had taken charge and invited his younger brother to inherit the throne. That younger brother was none other than the Chongzhen Emperor.","Due to that, the Chongzhen Emperor was extremely respectful to his imperial sister-in-law. As the two of them were of the same seniority, it wouldn’t do for his sister-in-law to be respected as the empress dowager, so she was respectfully addressed as Empress Yi'an instead.","To avoid exposing their identities, everyone treated her with utmost respect.","But that alone couldn’t shock Zu An so much. What astonished him was the fact that the esteemed Empress Yi’an was actually Zheng Dan!","Zu An didn’t let his astonishment show. He racked his mind, wondering if it could be another person in the Myriad Worlds who simply resembled Zheng Dan.","Empress Yi’an continued addressing the Fifth Elder as if she didn’t recognize Zu An. “Our empire is in crisis. Noble Consort Tian, I implore you to watch your words and actions, lest unsavory rumors start spreading.”","Fifth Elder Lilith was displeased, but she could only lower her head and apologize. “I’ll heed your teaching, imperial sister-in-law.”","She didn’t want to continue being lectured, so she turned around and left.","Isabella was about to leave with Zu An when Empress Yi’an said, “Lil’ Ninth, your mother seems to be looking for you.”","“Ah?” As much as Isabella didn’t want to part ways with Zu An, she had no choice but to leave for the time being. She sent a telepathic message telling Zu An to meet her outside the imperial city. She still had many things she wanted to tell him.","Only then did Empress Yi’an assess Zu An. “I hear that Lord Hong has contributed to our great empire by quelling the Shanxi rebels. It’s our Great Ming’s blessing to have a competent subject like you.”","Zu An’s heart sank. Is it just someone with the same face?","Then, he noticed her twitching pinky. Such a gesture wouldn’t have meant much to palace maids and eunuchs, but Zu An’s eyes lit up. That was how Dandan had teased him back then when he woke up in the morning.","Empress Yi’an continued speaking with a dignified air. “Lord Hong, do you think Great Ming’s sun can continue illuminating the darkness?”","Others thought that Empress Yi’an was worrying about national affairs, but Zu An had the latter half of the passcode.","“I’m sure it can. I’ll march into places where even the sun cannot reach,” Zu An replied.","Empress Yi’an smiled. “I’m glad to hear that from you, Lord Hong.”","With that, she departed with her entourage.","A eunuch was going to escort Zu An out, but he discreetly knocked out the eunuch and hid him behind a fake mountain before sneaking into Empress Yi’an’s bedroom. Unsurprisingly, the latter had already sent off her palace maids and eunuchs.","“Dandan!”","After a brief exchange of gazes, Empress Yi’an couldn’t hold herself back anymore and leaped right into Zu An’s embrace. “Ah Zu, I thought I’d never meet you again! Wuuu... ”","Feeling the tears on his chest, Zu An hurriedly consoled her. To his surprise, Zheng Dan suddenly leaned in and kissed him.","It didn’t take long for the atmosphere to heat up.","“I don’t think this is good. You’re the imperial sister-in-law now, whereas I'm an official. If they discover us...”","“Don’t worry. I'm of elevated stature in the palace. No one dares to come to my palace.”","“What about the eunuchs and palace maids?”","“I've sent them off. They won’t return anytime soon.”","“But...”","“Didn’t you say that you can enter even places where the sun can’t reach? You seem to be getting more timid as you grow stronger.”","That provoked Zu An. Naturally, he had to prove her wrong.","Zheng Dan’s arrogance slowly gave way to pleas of mercy. The cold palace suddenly felt warmer, and even the flowers outside the window began to blossom.","...","Zu An returned to the fake mountain where he had knocked out the eunuch and hypnotized the latter using the Soul Transference Method before leaving the imperial palace.","Isabella was overjoyed to see him. “Where did you go, big brother Zu? I thought you had left.”","“I went for a walk to see if I could find Chuyan.” Zu An felt sheepish. He couldn’t possibly tell her that he had slipped into the imperial palace to have a tryst with the empress.","“Big brother Zu, you treat big sister Chu so well.” Isabella suddenly frowned and began sniffing. “Hm? Something smells fragrant.”","Zu An knew Zheng Dan’s fragrance had gotten onto him. Worried that Isabella would notice it, he hurriedly changed the topic. “Little sister Bella, I've received an imperial edict and will be rushing back to Shanxi. I’ll have to count on you to help me investigate Chuyan’s whereabouts.”","The distraction worked on Isabella, who said, “Leave it to me. The First Elder has granted me command of the imperial guards to survey the officials and the feudal kings. I’ll tap into their information network to look for big sister Chu, and I’ll inform you the moment I receive any news.”","Zu An patted her shoulder. “Bella, you must take care of yourself. I fear that things won’t go as smoothly as expected in this Order Ceremony.”","“You too!” Isabella didn’t question Zu An’s remark. After what happened in the Deity of Death’s trial, she had absolute trust in Zu An’s judgment.","After they parted ways, Zu An invoked the imperial edict and returned to Shanxi with a grim expression.","Zheng Dan also entered the Order Divine Palace and completed a few trials before being transported here. Many familiar faces are gathered here. It feels as if some unknown power is orchestrating this.","He recalled Hong Chengchou’s plight and felt as if he was walking on a tightrope, where a misstep could lead to him falling down a cliff.","Isabella, Zheng Dan, and Tang Tian’er are in Great Ming, and I still don’t know where Chuyan is. There’s no way I can side with the Manchus.","Before confronting the boss beyond the borders, I should first deal with Li Zicheng.","The first thing he did was to put together an army. He led them to different places to quell the peasant rebellions and banditry.","The experience he'd amassed made him highly competent in fighting wars. To top things off, he had the Red Madame and Li Yan spying on his behalf. It didn’t take him long to vanquish the rebel groups that were gaining momentum. Even prominent rebel leader Gao Yingxiang was executed.","These battles built up an intimidating reputation for him. The rebellion began to lose steam, and morale in Great Ming soared.","While Li Zicheng fled into the mountains with eighteen cavalrymen[1], Zu An didn’t think much of it. It wasn't the same Great Ming that he knew, after all. With the aid of the Order faction, the imperial court rebuilt its economy and lifted the additional taxes[2].","With that, the rebels struggled to recruit more members to join their cause, so Li Zicheng couldn’t pose a threat anymore.","But shocking news was suddenly announced from the border.","Augustus and his Holy Knight Order’s elites were wiped out during a fight against the Manchus, leaving the borders in a precarious position.","“Impossible!”","Zu An was dazed when the news reached him. Despite their poor relationship, he had to concede that Augustus was extremely strong. In terms of individual prowess, he was even stronger than First Elder Oberon. How could someone like that die in battle?","—","TL note: A quick explanation of history","The Ming dynasty was ruled by the Zhu imperial clan, which was a Han clan.","Under the Wanli Emperor and Chongzhen Emperor’s rule, they notoriously put in place three taxes (the Liaodong military levy, the bandit subjugation levy, and the troop training levy) that caused great suffering among the people.","A famous Ming academic named Gu Yanwu wrote that “In that era a mu of land is worth 7 to 8 liang , whereas the tax itself already charges 10 liang .”","In history, Li Zicheng proclaimed himself King of Xinshun and founded the Shun Dynasty. He led 300,000 troops and successfully conquered Beijing. With that, he proclaimed himself emperor.","Great Ming thus fell.","A month later, Wu Sangui (Second Elder Hermes), who guarded the Shanhai Pass, allowed the Qing Manchus to pass right through this critical chokepoint. The Central Plains area is famously hard to guard due to its flat land, so guarding the chokepoints is of utmost importance.","By June, Li Zicheng was overthrown, and the Qing Manchus took over.","—","TL Note:","I’ll highlight places where details conform to or diverge from history, so that you know whether the ‘outsider butterfly effect’ has taken place, or if they're just marching down the same path.","—","(JUST INTERESTING TRIVIA TO ME)","Actually, Empress Yi’an led quite the dramatic life as well.","Her husband, the Tianqi Emperor, was illiterate (supposedly due to a learning disability) and highly dependent on his wet nurse Madame Ke and eunuch Wei Zhongxian.","Wei Zhongxian issued edicts on behalf of the Tianqi Emperor to place people he favored in positions of power while demoting officials who opposed him. His power was said to rival the emperor. He was considered to be the most notorious eunuch in history.","Madame Ke, despite being a wet nurse, was known to travel around in an extravagant sedan and with a huge procession comprising over a hundred people. She put on airs no humbler than the emperor. She starved and mistreated concubines whom the Tianqi Emperor had favored, causing them to suffer from miscarriage and even die. That was why the Tianqi Emperor had no offspring. Empress Yi’an reportedly suffered from a miscarriage because of her.","Empress Yi’an had actively tried to curb their influence but to no avail, as her attempts fell short due to the Tianqi Emperor protecting them.","When the Tianqi Emperor passed away, she pushed for the Chongzhen Emperor to take the throne. When the Chongzhen Emperor claimed the throne, he swiftly dealt with Madame Ke and Wei Zhongxian.","In the end, when Li Zicheng conquered the capital, Emperor Chongzhen ordered Empress Yi’an to commit suicide. The empress died by hanging.","1. This went according to history. ☜","2. In history, the additional taxes weren't lifted until Great Ming fell. When the Manchus took over, they lifted the taxes, saying that they had caused much suffering among the people. ☜"]},{"number":2890,"title":"Chapter 2890: Chapter 2842: Accepting Orders","paragraphs":["The battle at the border had to have been earth-shattering.","To think that the natives of this world were so strong that the Manchus defeated the renowned Marshal Yuan. Doesn’t that mean Great Ming is doomed? Who else in the imperial court is a match for the Manchus?","Those participating in the Order Ceremony were shocked beyond words. They knew how powerful Captain Augustus was better than anyone else. His reputation was forged from many years of slaying Annihilation worshipers.","Such a powerful expert had actually died in a dungeon that they thought was a walk in the park!","Did the Deity of Annihilation descend upon this trial?","Zu An shook his head. If a universal deity had descended, their tremendous power was bound to suffuse the world. There was no way the participants would have been oblivious to it.","While he was trying to figure out the situation, an imperial edict suddenly appeared in the sky. First Elder Oberon had to be flustered, as he was summoning everyone participating in the Order Ceremony to enter the capital and discuss the matter.","There were too many doubts in Zu An’s mind. He quickly settled matters here before returning to the capital via the imperial edict.","Meanwhile, Li Zicheng and his eighteen cavalrymen were galloping through the Shangluo Mountain with looks of despair.","That Hong Chengchou is too powerful, both in terms of individual strength and military prowess. He even crushed Gao Yingxiang! There’s no chance of turning the tables here.","His subordinates were also thinking of leaving the rebel group, but they knew that even if they returned to their hometowns, the officials would capture them and sentence them to death by slow slicing. They would have to live out their lives in the shadows.","Li Zicheng stood on the edge of the cliff with a cold heart as he listened to his subordinates’ gloomy chatter. He knew that none of his subordinates’ hearts were with him anymore.","Just then, a cloaked figure stood before him. “Do you wish to make a comeback?”","Li Zicheng flinched. Where did this fellow appear from? “Who are you?”","“It doesn’t matter who I am. I can grant you the power you desire to exact vengeance,” the cloaked figure said with a compelling voice.","Li Zicheng’s breathing hastened. “Yes, I want power.”","The cloaked figure asked, “Aren’t you going to ask about the price?”","“There’s no need for that. I have already lost everything. I want the power to avenge Gao Yingxiang and overthrow this goddamned Ming dynasty!”","“Good. I chose the right person. I shall grant you the power of reproduction. The number of subordinates under your command will snowball to the point where you have more than enough manpower...”","A bizarre light shone on Li Zicheng. His eyes began to gleam brightly. He turned to his subordinates and declared, “Brothers, let’s fight back! We shall get back what we have lost!”","...","There was a huge uproar in the imperial library. Everyone was fervently discussing the situation. It had dawned upon them that there was something amiss with this Order Ceremony.","Zu An and Isabella stood by the corner. “Bella, do you still have no leads on Chuyan?”","Something had to have happened to Chu Chuyan if she hadn’t reached the capital after so long. Zu An had also been using his connections to look for Chu Chuyan, but to no avail.","“I recently received a tip-off. Someone spotted a beautiful woman resembling big sister Chu overseas,” Isabella replied.","“Overseas?” Zu An widened his eyes. This world had become massive after they transmigrated here. It would make sense for Chu Chuyan to struggle to reach the capital if she was overseas.","“Big sister Chu was spotted on the Zheng clan’s land. The Zheng clan is antagonistic to the imperial court. That could be the reason big sister Chu hasn’t been able to make her way here,” Isabella explained.","Just then, the First Elder quelled the ruckus in the imperial library and began speaking. “The situation at the borders continues to worsen. It’s fortunate Hermes has been guarding Shanhai Pass, and Naraka has been keeping things in our border cities stable. Thanks to their efforts, we have been able to keep the Manchus at bay. What do you think we should do next?”","The crowd in the imperial library exchanged looks. The atmosphere felt heavy. Even the powerful Augustus had died in battle. The others didn’t think they would fare any better than him.","“Second Brother and Sixth Brother should be able to keep things at the borders stable.” Fifth Elder Lilith couldn’t maintain a nonchalant attitude anymore, so she participated in the meeting as well.","“We can’t maintain the status quo. The goal of our Order Ceremony is to restore order to Great Ming. We have to quell the invaders,” First Elder Oberon said with a darkened expression. “Neither Hermes nor Naraka are adept at warfare. They can guard key locations, but invading the enemy is beyond their means. Who do you think can deal with the Manchus at the border?”","Fourth Elder Mastema suddenly said, “I think Zu An can do it.”","The others turned to Zu An.","Isabella’s heart clenched. She hurriedly interjected, “Fourth Elder, big brother Zu is young. I don’t think it would be wise to entrust such a heavy responsibility to him. There are more competent elders here.”","She knew how dangerous the borders were. Naturally, she didn’t want the man she loved to face such danger.","The other members of the Order faction voiced their agreement.","“Why should we entrust this responsibility to an outsider when the other elders are here?”","“I trust the Second Elder and Sixth Elder more. I don’t think an outsider should be our representative here.”","...","Zu An also spoke up. “I also don’t think it’s appropriate. I don’t think I would be able to accomplish what Captain Augustus has failed at, and I don’t wish to get too involved in the Order Ceremony. I am a Memory envoy, after all.”","I have no ties with the Fourth Elder. Why did he help me in the Fortune Palace? Does he recognize my talent and wish to earn my goodwill, or does he have an ulterior motive?","“You have already proved yourself by subduing the rebels in the northwest. I reckon no one present here is more adept than you in warfare. There’s no one more qualified to deal with the Manchus than you,” Fourth Elder Mastema declared. “You aren’t just a Memory envoy. You’re also our Conglomerate’s future son-in-law. You aren’t an outsider here.”","“Fourth Uncle~” Isabella protested coyly, though his words stirred something in her heart.","She knew that many present didn’t approve of her marriage with Zu An, which was why they gave him the cold shoulder previously. While it seemed as if she was living the high life as the Acadias’ first miss, the role came with heavy responsibilities. Unlike normal people, she couldn’t act on her whims and preferences.","It would be ideal if the Universal Conglomerate recognized her relationship with Zu An. That said, the borders were still too dangerous. She couldn’t bear the thought of putting Zu An in danger.","She was about to reject the offer on Zu An’s behalf when First Elder Oberon suddenly interjected, “Very well. I shall assign him as the Jiliao Military Governor[1] to suppress the invaders.”","The others in the Order faction were horrified, but before they could protest, First Elder Oberon waved his hand and declared, “Say no more. There’s no one more suited than him for this role.”","Oberon turned to Zu An and said, “The imperial court will give its all to support your campaign. As long as you subdue the Manchus, not only will we recognize your relationship with Isabella, we’ll even grant you a place on the Round Table Council.”","Shocked gasps echoed in the imperial library.","Joining the Round Table Council would grant one untold influence and wealth. It was a position that countless coveted but to no avail.","Some even considered offering to lead the campaign at the borders, but on second thought, even the invincible Augustus had died on the battlefield. Heading there would be nothing more than an act of suicide for most. As tempting as it was to be the Round Table Council’s Eighth Elder, the odds were too severely stacked against them. It wasn't worth risking certain death for.","That thought calmed the hearts of many. Some even clamored for Zu An to take on the role.","Pressure was building for Zu An to accept the role, but he remained unmoved. He was aware of the dangers involved.","He was about to turn down the offer when Oberon suddenly remarked, “Isabella chose you. I hope you don’t prove that her judgment was wrong.”","Zu An turned to Isabella.","The latter shot him a look and told him telepathically, “Big brother Zu, you mustn’t go. Don’t worry about me...”","Zu An suddenly laughed. Since fate has planned these events for me, I have to confront them for a shot at survival. Besides, I shouldn’t be letting my lover down.","“Fine, I’ll go.”","1. Jiliao refers to the Jizhou and Liaodong area. In short, Zu An has been given high command over military affairs in that region. ☜"]},{"number":2891,"title":"Chapter 2891: Chapter 2843: Annihilation Envoy","paragraphs":["“Big brother Zu...” Isabella felt worried but moved, knowing that Zu An was doing this for her.","First Elder Oberon gave a heartened nod. “Good. I’ll leave the invaders to you, Zu An. Mastema, you’ll take on his responsibilities in the northwest, lest those rebels make a comeback.”","Fourth Elder Mastema looked troubled. He was reluctant to leave the prosperous capital for some rundown countryside province, but he knew how important this matter was. He had no choice but to swallow his grievances and accept the decision.","“You can’t laze around anymore, Lilith. You’ll be taking on Mastema’s work in coordinating logistics to the northeast and managing the imperial court’s finances,” First Elder Oberon said.","Lilith smiled. “Don’t worry, big brother. The Conglomerate’s survival is at stake. I know my priorities.”","Augustus’ death spelled the doom of one of Order’s two main powers. This was an earthquake for the Order faction. Just the thought of it sent shivers down her spine.","First Elder Oberon felt heartened by her remark. His flustered heart calmed down. With my brothers and sisters here, there’s no challenge we cannot surmount. He spoke with increasing gusto. “Bella, you’ll reach out to the Zheng clan and try to bring them under our fold. It’ll be a great help to our war effort if we can utilize their navy to attack the enemy’s main camp.”","“Yes!” Isabella was delighted to receive that order. That would put her in a better position to assist Zu An in investigating Chu Chuyan’s whereabouts.","First Elder Oberon continued the discussions while issuing tasks to those present.","Zu An left the Imperial Library to look for Zheng Dan.","This time, the mood between them wasn’t as light-hearted as their initial reunion. Zheng Dan worriedly said, “Ah Zu, I heard that many of our soldiers have died at the borders. You must make sure to tread carefully.”","Zu An consoled her. “I’ll only know what I’m up against once I’m there, but I won’t let my guard down. You have to be prepared as well. In history, Li Zicheng breached Beijing[1] and destroyed the Ming Empire. Empress Yi’an hanged herself shortly after. The same might not happen in this world, but you should have an escape plan just in case.”","Zheng Dan knew that he tended to have such random knowledge, so she didn’t doubt the credibility of his statements.","“Don’t worry. I've familiarized myself with the imperial court.” Zheng Dan’s expression suddenly darkened. “But if that happens, I doubt there’s any point in me escaping. I was transported here after taking on Order’s trial. The imperial palace’s fall spells the collapse of Great Ming’s order and the failure of my trial. I won’t be able to escape death if so.”","Zu An grabbed her hand and said, “You mustn’t give up until you’re truly cornered. Trust me. I’ll find a way to remedy the situation.”","He didn’t think this trial would be as difficult as the Deity of Death’s trial. In that trial, he, Firework, Isabella, and Yan Xuehen had been in different camps, and the setting decreed that only one of them could survive the trial. Yet he'd still found a way out.","This time, he had the Universal Conglomerate’s support. Great Ming’s circumstances were much better than they had been in history, and he, Tang Tian’er, and Zheng Dan were in the same camp. Things looked more positive.","All of a sudden, though, he felt a pang of unease. Chuyan is still nowhere to be seen. Could she be on the Manchus’ side?","But he quickly dismissed that thought. Isabella had found that Chu Chuyan was likely in the Zheng clan’s territory in Taiwan. It was unlikely that she was aligned with the Manchus.","“I’ll also do my best. I’ll let you know if I receive any news from the imperial palace.” After hearing her lover’s composed tone, Zheng Dan also slowly calmed down.","It wasn’t convenient for them to stay together in the imperial palace for too long, so they soon reluctantly parted ways.","With the imperial edict in hand, Zu An teleported to Ningyuan City, where the Jiliao Military Governor’s manor was located. He quickly gathered his subordinates to understand the current circumstances.","It turned out that Augustus and his Holy Knight Order had dealt a heavy blow to the Manchus[2] in the Battle of Ningyuan, slaying their commander. That greatly boosted the morale of the Ming army.","But Augustus hadn't been satisfied with that victory. His goal was to reclaim Great Ming’s land, vanquish the Manchus, and restore Great Ming’s order as tribute to the great Deity of Order.","Thus, he'd abandoned the Ming army’s conservative war strategy and pushed their defensivee line forward. He and his men had marched tens of kilometers northeast to rebuild Dalinghe City, hoping to use it as a base to attack the Manchus.","Initially, everything had gone smoothly.","They'd successfully transported a huge amount of military resources to Dalinghe City, and the Manchu soldiers had made no moves in the meantime. The Holy Knight Order thought that the Manchus were intimidated after their previous defeat, and that greatly bolstered their will to reclaim the northeast.","Who could have expected the missing Manchu army to suddenly appear one night and encircle Dalinghe City? Their forces were much stronger than what the Holy Knight Order had faced in the Battle of Ningyuan, and they'd even brought magic cannons along.","Augustus, living up to his reputation as the Holy Knight Order’s captain, had kept his cool and organized his subordinates to guard the city. Under his efforts, the Manchus struggled to take down Dalinghe City.","But the Manchus hadn't been planning to take down Dalinghe City in a single swoop. Instead, they'd resorted to a long-term encirclement strategy, tightly surrounding Dalinghe City to isolate it from the rest of the world.","When Second Elder Hermes and Sixth Elder Naraka learned about the encirclement, they'd immediately dispatched their armies to aid the Holy Knight Order. Unfortunately, their forces were ambushed and defeated.","The Manchu soldiers had been far stronger than before. The Annihilation power they wielded was far more potent than that in the Battle of Ningyuan. The two elders had sent reinforcements several times, only to suffer terrible defeats.","Only then did all of them realize that the Manchu army was baiting them out so that they could encircle them and slowly wear down Great Ming’s forces. However, they had realized it too late.","To make things worse, even though the Holy Knight Order had been stockpiling resources in Dalinghe City, they hadn’t had time to transport ample rations in.","Months had passed, and the troops trapped in Dalinghe began resorting to cannibalism. Annihilation's power had begun to grow. Augustus then knew that at this rate, Dalinghe City wouldn’t last long, so he gathered the Holy Knight Order and attempted to break out of the encirclement. He was confident that he could make a comeback as long as they could return to Jinzhou.","But the Manchus were prepared. The Holy Knight Order had been swiftly surrounded, and after a grueling battle, they were wiped out. Even the renowned Augustus had fallen in battle.","This battle greatly shook Great Ming’s morale. Were it not for the two elders’ firm stance, the Manchus could have succeeded in breaching Guanning’s defensive line.","That said, the situation still remained pessimistic. The Manchus had already advanced to Jinzhou, where Sixth Elder Naraka was holding the fort.","Just then, Second Elder Hermes arrived at the Jiliao Military Governor’s manor. As soon as he saw Zu An, he frowned. “Why are you here?”","“The First Elder and the others believe that I’m the most suitable person for this role, so they sent me here,” Zu An replied. “The situation has gone awry. Second Elder, I hope you can put aside our differences and work together with me to resolve the situation.”","Second Elder Hermes harrumphed. “I know what’s important.”","Zu An proceeded to inquire about the details of previous battles.","Hermes worriedly replied, “The Manchus are extremely strong. They harness pure Annihilation power. I suspect that the Manchus are backed by at least an Annihilation envoy, if not more.”","1. The capital of the Ming Dynasty ☜","2. Author Note: They were still called Jurchens at this point in history, but we’ll address them as Manchus for simplification's sake. ☜"]},{"number":2892,"title":"Chapter 2892: Chapter 2844: Danger","paragraphs":["“Annihilation envoy...” Zu An thought about the Doomsday Beast, which had been strong enough to single-handedly destroy the powerful Monster World.","An Annihilation envoy was bound to be much stronger than that.","“Mere soldiers harnessing Annihilation power can’t hope to defeat Augustus. It would take someone of the level of an Annihilation deity,” Hermes replied grimly.","“What about the others from the Holy Knight Order, like Adrian?” Zu An asked.","“They went missing after that battle. We didn’t find Adrian’s corpse, but Annihilation worshipers rarely leave intact corpses behind in the first place. It’s unlikely that he’s still alive,” Hermes snorted in displeasure. “I know you have a grudge against Adrian. You must be happy to hear that.”","Zu An was briefly speechless.","Instead of explaining himself, he proceeded to discuss their circumstances. “The imperial court’s reinforcements should be arriving soon. We just have to hold on in the meantime.”","“We should have no trouble holding on here, but I can’t say the same for Jinzhou, where the Sixth Elder is stationed. The Manchus are prepared to ambush any troops we dispatch. Sending reinforcements there will achieve nothing but weaken Guanning’s defenses.”","“I know that. Did you come here just to say these things? Speaking of which, Second Elder, do you know Chen Yuanyuan?”","Hermes was startled. He looked at Zu An warily and asked, “Why are you asking about her?”","Hermes’s reaction hinted that he had fallen in love with Chen Yuanyuan, just as history had dictated. Zu An sighed. “I find it hard to believe that the Second Elder, despite having met all kinds of beauties in the Myriad Worlds, would fall in love with someone here. May I meet her?”","“Hmph! She’s in Beijing. You should stop thinking about useless things and focus on this war.” Animosity flickered across Hermes’s eyes. He truly detested playboys like Zu An.","Zu An wasn't requesting a meeting with Chen Yuanyuan out of lust. Rather, he had a feeling that something wasn't right. Chen Yuanyuan was indeed famous in history, but Hermes, being in a position of power, had met all kinds of beauties. It seemed improbable for him to fall in love with a woman in a trial world.","He regretted leaving the capital so hastily. I should have met Chen Yuanyuan first. That could have resolved my doubts.","...","The meeting could hardly be considered pleasant. The two of them bickered for quite a bit before finally parting ways.","Thanks to the imperial edict, Zu An had the final say over Shanhai Pass. He knew that Ningyuan’s garrison troops couldtn’t be dispatched carelessly, even if it was to reinforce Jinzhou and the other regions.","He spent the next few days scouting the vicinity. He even ambushed some Manchurian scouts to get a grasp of their fighting prowess, but that only deepened his unease. The Manchus were stronger than he had thought.","A month later, the imperial court’s reinforcements arrived.","Jinzhou’s requests for reinforcements grew increasingly urgent. The Second Elder urged Zu An to rescue the Sixth Elder, but Zu An remained unmoved.","Now that he had some grasp of the Manchus’ military might, he understood that Jinzhou couldn’t have lasted this long if the Manchus were truly determined to take it down. Yet Jinzhou continued to hold on.","Clearly, this was more bait from the Manchus. They were counting on Great Ming to continue sending reinforcements, so as to weaken them bit by bit.","So, Zu An played along with the Manchus’ ploy and advanced slowly, focusing specifically on stability. He used Ningyuan City as a base to slowly gnaw at the Manchu troops. He took great care to ensure that their logistical line was never trailing too far behind.","Just like that, he secured a series of victories against the Manchus. He even crushed them at Rufeng Mountain.","The only problem was that he was still some distance away from Jinzhou.","Hermes was extremely unhappy with his fighting style. After enjoying a series of victories, he didn’t think that the Manchus were as fearsome as they initially thought them to be, and he kept urging Zu An to be more ambitious now that the winds were with them.","If they could fight their way down to Jinzhou and join forces with the Sixth Elder, their forces would grow much stronger. They could even be able to threaten the Manchus’ main camp.","But Zu An rejected his proposal. He remained convinced that the Manchus were still withholding their true prowess. He didn’t think their recent strings of victories over the Manchus, including at Rufeng Mountain, had truly hurt the Manchu army.","He had several fights with Hermes over this, but he still insisted on his strategy.","Not long later, First Elder Oberon dispatched a military supervisor named Chen Xinjia over. Evidently, Hermes must have reported him.","However, Zu An knew from history that Chen Xinjia’s interference had resulted in Great Ming’s disastrous defeat in the Battle of Songjin, so he continued to hold his ground.","That prompted the First Elder to issue an imperial edict to remind him that they had to do more than guard their territories. The Order faction had to defeat the Manchu army to complete the Order Ceremony before they could leave this world.","Zu An responded by informing the First Elder about the Manchus’ scheme and his worries, highlighting the dangers of being too hasty. At the same time, he also stated his solution to the problem. He would first slowly wear down the Manchurian forces while advancing to Jinzhou. Then, he would coordinate an attack with Zheng Jinzhou’s navy. The latter would attack the Manchus’ back line, while he eliminated them from the front.","This strategy required more time and was demanding in terms of rations, but it was stable. Fortunately, the imperial court had already launched a series of policies that could finance this war even if it dragged on.","After an intense discussion, the First Elder finally approved his plan. However, he also warned against dragging the war out too long, as Li Zicheng had made a comeback in the northwest. It was unlikely that the imperial court’s finances were sufficient to sustain a war on two fronts.","Zu An was baffled. I crushed this world’s Li Zicheng. How did he make a comeback?","On the whole, he was still glad that the First Elder had approved his plan. That lifted a boulder from his shoulders. At the very least, they had avoided the worst outcome in history. Once he defeated the stronger Manchu army, he could march back into the capital and quell the weaker Li Zicheng.","Just like that, Zu An continued grating away at the Manchu army.","Months later, he arrived at Jinzhou City. The fighting they'd done in the meantime had trained his soldiers up into elites. In contrast, the Manchus were growing weaker from the series of defeats they'd suffered.","Hermes, despite his strong initial objection against Zu An’s plan, slowly came to respect the latter for all he had achieved.","At Jinzhou, Zu An clashed a few times with the Manchus. Through coordinating with Jinzhou’s garrison troops, he was able to turn the tides and reverse encircle the Manchus instead.","But he still felt unnerved. Everything was so smooth that he felt he had overlooked something.","Just then, there was a commotion in the distance. A figure rushed over. The soldiers thought it was a Manchu assassin, so they stepped in to stop him.","The figure shouted, “I want to meet your commander! I have something to report!”","Zu An was shocked to hear that familiar voice. It was Adrian.","He quickly ordered his troops to bring Adrian before him. Adrian displayed nothing of his usual Radiant Son demeanor. His clothes were tattered, his body was covered in wounds, and his breathing was shallow.","Zu An was about to treat him when Adrian clutched his hand and said, “Sixth Elder Naraka is a traitor!”","It was as if Adrian had held on to say these words through sheer grit. Right after he finished his sentence, his eyes dimmed and he breathed his last.","Zu An felt goosebumps. No wonder Augustus died! No wonder Jinzhou didn’t fall despite so much time passing! I thought we'd encircled the Manchus, but the truth is that my army is the one sandwiched between the Manchu army and Jinzhou’s garrison troops!"]},{"number":2893,"title":"Chapter 2893: Chapter 2845: Fallen Divine Maiden","paragraphs":["Zu An hurriedly reorganized his forces to break free from the crisis, but deep down, he knew that the tides were no longer with him. There was no way his enemies would watch as he left with his army.","As expected, the Manchu army quickly noticed his intention and ordered an all-out attack.","Sixth Elder Naraka saw the signal and dropped the act altogether. He also led his troops out of the city to attack the Ming army. His soldiers were no longer emanating Order power, but potent Annihilation power.","The Ming army was confused. They'd thought that they could finally turn the tables on the Manchus and eradicate them for good, but why had the situation suddenly turned on them? They couldn’t comprehend why their allies in Jinzhou City had suddenly turned against them.","Commissioner Sun had been the highest commander for their border defense. Everyone had always heeded his orders. No one could have thought that he would betray them.","Zu An tried his best to struggle and break free of the encirclement, but the Manchus had designed this trap meticulously with Naraka to corner them. There was no way he would let them escape so easily.","Several times Zu An almost broke free of the encirclement, but the famed Manchu general, Dorgon, shoved him right back in.","Under the Manchu commander flag, a plump man dressed in a yellow robe watched the intense battle and remarked, “That Hong Chengchou is indeed a prodigy. If not for Naraka, we might not necessarily have won this battle.”","He was the Manchus’ Huang Taiji[1]. The Annihilation power shrouding him was so thick that it was almost tangible, sending shivers down the spines of those around him.","“Hong Chengchou is one of the major figures participating in the Order Ceremony, but he isn’t from the Universal Conglomerate. He’s a Memory envoy,” the strategist standing beside him, Fan Wencheng, replied.","“Oh? How did he end up with the Order faction?” Huang Taiji was confused.","“He was courting the Universal Conglomerate’s first miss, Isabella. That could be the reason he’s aiding the Universal Conglomerate.”","“Hahaha! Yet another lust-driven fool. That simplifies matters. Relay my order. I want him captured alive!”","“Yes!”","...","Zu An unleashed everything he had, but he couldn’t turn the tides single-handedly. In such a large-scale battle, his individual prowess was insignificant. The enemies he was up against weren’t ordinary feudal soldiers; these were worshipers imbued with the power of universal deities, mixed with experts from the Myriad Worlds.","In the end, Zu An and his troops were cornered on a mountain, with their rations and water supply cut. It was only a matter of time before they were defeated.","Zu An furiously racked his brains for a solution.","In truth, he knew deep down that Great Ming’s military force had suffered such a heavy loss here that even if he somehow broke free of the encirclement, the compounded problem from their internal turmoil and external invaders had already sealed the Ming Empire’s fate.","Their defeat was already set in stone.","Will everything unfold the way it did in history? Hong Chengchou was defeated in battle, captured, and became a notorious Han traitor. Later, he suffered under the Qing dynasty and was treated like a second-class citizen.","Great Ming also failed to stand its ground and lost its capital to Li Zicheng’s peasant rebel army.","Eventually, the Manchu army breached the pass, destroyed Li Zicheng, and united the world...","Hold on, I’m not just a Memory envoy, but also a Chaos and Enigma envoy. Even if history is already set in stone, I can still tamper with the process.","The thought of that made Zu An’s eyes light up.","...","The Ming Empire was utterly crushed in the Battle of Songjin. Its army was annihilated, and its highest commander died in battle. The news caused a huge stir when it reached the capital. Great Ming’s morale was greatly shaken. Isabella was anguished. Many times she tried to head to the borders to search for Zu An, only to be stopped by the elders.","Meanwhile, Zu An was in the Manchus’ main camp. He had been captured by them.","Influential officials like Fan Wencheng and Dorgon had visited him to persuade him to surrender, but none had been able to move him. His attitude remained firm even when Huang Taiji personally paid him a visit.","Huang Taiji laughed. “You don’t belong to the Order faction. We don’t have to be enemies, so why do you insist on dying with them?”","Zu An maintained his silence. Is this Huang Taiji an Annihilation worshiper? He’s terrifyingly powerful. No wonder even the powerful Augustus died to the Manchus.","Huang Taiji continued, “Are you doing this for the Conglomerate’s Isabella? A true man can have any woman he wants. Tell me the kinds of women you like. I’ll find you someone no worse than her.”","“I don’t think anyone can compare with her,” Zu An casually replied.","“I doubt that.” Huang Taiji laughed as he walked out.","Zu An had been deep in thought. He couldn’t understand why the Annihilation faction was so determined to bring him into their fold. The Manchus had a massive advantage over the Ming Empire right now, so his presence made no difference to them.","Unless... there's some kind of variable where my help is necessary. But what could that be?","Someone suddenly knocked on the door.","Zu An was perplexed. I’m a prisoner now. Is there any need for them to knock on the door?","“Da Yu’er[2] seeks an audience with Military Governor Hong,” a cold but pleasant voice echoed.","Zu An was surprised. There were rumors that Huang Taiji had ordered his women to seduce Hong Chengchou and persuade him to surrender... but was there a need for this Huang Taiji to do that here?","He hadn't thought that an Annihilation worshiper would need to sacrifice his wife to recruit him.","But why does that voice sound so familiar?","“You may enter.” Let me meet her first.","A tall, dignified woman entered with a vat of wine. She was dressed in ethnic clothes, though what was more eye-catching were her long legs draped in black silk. Feudal-era clothes paired with modern black silk stockings were a bizarre combination, but somehow, she was able to pull off this contradicting look.","This beautiful woman had the coldest look on her face until she saw Zu An and suddenly stiffened up. Disbelief filled her eyes.","Zu An was shocked as well. The woman before him was none other than Jiang Luofu!","Back then, they had traveled into a spacetime fragment to gather the ingredients required to save Xiaoxi from her Cruel Poison Constitution. However, Jiang Luofu’s determination to save Xiaoxi was so strong that it caught a universal deity’s attention.","The universal deity had summoned her elsewhere, and Zu An had lost contact with her since. He hadn’t expected to reunite with her here.","Zu An, being as quick-witted as ever, snapped out of his daze and quickly asked, “Miss Da Yu’er, is there something you need from me?”","Jiang Luofu’s eyes twinkled with a smile. She played along and said, “Our Khan heard that Military Governor Hong has been on a hunger strike for many days now, so he requested me to deliver some food to you.”","“Miss, what makes you think I’ll eat the food you delivered?”","“Please have pity on me, Military Governor Hong. The Khan will have me executed if you refuse to eat my food.”","Zu An noticed that Jiang Luofu wasn’t emanating any energy at all, so he telepathically asked her what was going on.","“Just like you, I am a prisoner.” Jiang Luofu’s previously cold eyes had regained some spirit. “I am an Order envoy. They captured me to drive me into depravity. For that, they coerced me to seduce the man residing in this room. I was planning to find a chance to end my life, but I didn’t expect that the man I was supposed to seduce is you!”","—","Some additional trivias about Da Yu’er:","Da Yu’er, also known as Empress Xiaozhuangwen, was quite the respected figure in history.","She was the mother of the Shunzhi Emperor, but she’s more well-known as the grandmother of the Kangxi Emperor. She aided the young Kangxi Emperor’s rise to power, encouraged him to learn from the regents, and helped him eliminate regents that threatened to usurp imperial power.","The Kangxi Emperor was considered one of China’s greatest emperors, leaving behind a huge legacy for his descendants. Additionally, he was extremely filial to Da Yu’er.","Her real name was Bumbutai, but the Qianlong Emperor issued a naming taboo, so most people didn’t know her real name. They called her Da Yu’er in performances, and the name stuck.","There are many Chinese dramas following Da Yu’er’s life.","1. He was the second Khan of Later Jin, but after annexing Great Ming, he became the founding emperor of the Qing dynasty. ☜","2. She was later married to Huang Taiji and later became the future Empress Xiaozhuangwen. Her son, the Shunzhi Emperor, later inherited the throne from Huang Taiji. ☜"]},{"number":2894,"title":"Chapter 2894: Chapter 2846: You Can’t Snatch It If I Don’t Give It to You","paragraphs":["“Order envoy?” Zu An was shocked. He would never have expected Jiang Luofu to have caught the Deity of Order’s gaze. “How did you end up here?”","I wonder what the Deity of Order is thinking. There are so many Universal Conglomerate elders and Holy Knight Order knights to choose their envoy from, but of all people, they chose Jiang Luofu.","“I was in an Order trial. I was about to succeed when I was captured by the Deity of Annihilation’s power and was placed here,” Jiang Luofu replied.","Zu An was startled. “The Deity of Annihilation personally made a move to capture you?”","“Of course. I am an Order envoy now. Ordinary Annihilation worshipers can’t hope to capture me. However, I didn’t see what the Deity of Annihilation looked like. I only briefly sensed their divine power before being transported here.” Jiang Luofu felt stifled.","“Having a universal deity personally make a move for you is something worth bragging about for a lifetime,” Zu An said with a smile, but he slowly frowned out of worry. “Based on what I know, Da Yu’er is one of Huang Taiji’s wives. Did they make things difficult for you?”","“They are Annihilation worshipers, whereas I am an Order envoy. We are sworn enemies. They were bound to make things difficult for me. It’s fortunate that I bumped into you here.” Jiang Luofu’s expression suddenly turned peculiar. “I guess I should be thankful for your philandering nature, or else I would have been in trouble.”","Zu An was confused. What does this have to do with me?","Jiang Luofu explained, “Da Yu’er has an older sister in this world named Harjol. Huang Taiji favors her more. Can you guess who Harjol is?”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. It can’t be Chuyan, right? According to the intelligence gathered, Chu Chuyan seems to be the princess of Taiwan’s Zheng clan.","“It’s the Fiend races’ Little Fiend Empress,” Jiang Luofu replied. “I was in despair after falling into the hands of the Annihilation worshipers. I thought I would suffer a terrible plight. I was lucky to have met her. She spared me from humiliation.”","Zu An’s heart sank. “Doesn’t that mean that she...”","Harjol was Huang Taiji’s most favored wife.","Jiang Luofu knew what he was thinking, so she replied, “Don’t worry. The Little Fiend Empress is now a Bliss and Desire worshiper, and she previously obtained a special ability from a trial that allows her to plunge others into a blissful illusion. She’s unharmed.”","“Not even the Annihilation envoy noticed her deception?” Zu An was astonished. He had just met Huang Taiji and was shocked by his overwhelming aura.","“The Bliss and Desire path is a peculiar one.” Jiang Luofu’s face reddened. “You should ask the Little Fiend Empress to show you.”","Zu An hadn’t expected to encounter so many friends in the Order Ceremony. It turned out to be a blessing in disguise. “On that note, Huang Taiji probably already sees you as his woman. Why would he still send you to me?”","“Annihilation worshipers are a bunch of despicable scum.” Jiang Luofu bit her lip as her eyes glistened. “He wants to conquer me because I am an Order envoy, and he thinks the way to do so is by making me succumb to depravity. So, he sent me to seduce you to trample all over my dignity and pride. He believes that converting an Order envoy into an Annihilation pawn would deal the greatest damage to the Order faction.”","Zu An understood Huang Taiji’s intentions. “But it’s not as if he can do anything if you refuse to do it after entering my room.”","“Don’t you think my complexion looks redder than usual?” Jiang Luofu looked embarrassed.","Only then did Zu An notice that her face was unusually red, and her breathing was more ragged than usual. He'd thought that she was just excited to meet him, but the truth was something else. “He drugged you?”","Jiang Luofu nodded. “Huang Taiji was worried that I wouldn’t follow his will, so he drugged me before sending me over. It just so happens that the Little Fiend Empress was occupied with other matters and couldn’t help me. I thought I was doomed. I never expected to encounter you.”","Zu An’s heart rippled. “So, it’s fine with you if it’s me?”","Jiang Luofu pinched him. “What do you think?”","The two of them had been platonic partners for a long time now. They had the closest bond in the world.","Jiang Luofu suddenly sighed. “I’m happy to reunite with you, but you’re the Ming Empire’s marshal. If even you have been captured, it means that the Order faction is doomed.”","“That’s not necessarily the case.”","“You have a way out?” Jiang Luofu looked at Zu An with surprised but hopeful eyes. Is this man able to pull off a miracle here as well?","But she soon shook her head, knowing how terrible their plight was. She couldn’t even sense the Deity of Order’s power here, let alone the Order faction. Otherwise, she wouldn’t have been captured so easily.","“I only have some vague thoughts in mind. We’ll have to take it a step at a time.” Zu An had a rough idea, but he needed to further work on the execution details.","A beautiful leg wrapped in black stocking suddenly stomped on the bed. Jiang Luofu leaned in with a reddened face, her breathing hasty. “I’m at my limit.”","“I’ll find a way to expel your poison.” Zu An quickly thought of ways to remove poison.","Jiang Luofu pushed him down onto the bed. “You rascal. Acting chaste at a time like this.”","The Order faction was doomed. She could feel danger looming over her, and she had no idea what would happen to her. She considered reuniting with someone she loved before her death as a silver lining to the situation.","Zu An wasn't someone who couldn’t read the mood. Seeing the usually mature and dignified lady showing rare cracks of weakness and helplessness, he spoke no more and instead leaned in to kiss her.","Jiang Luofu had been barely holding on with her strong willpower. Anyone else in her place would have long lost their rationality. Feeling the sensation of his warm lips, she felt like a desert traveler stumbling upon an oasis. Something snapped in her mind, and she dropped all self-control to embrace her lover.","The cold prison suddenly became as passionate as the wildest ocean. Even the flowers seemed to bloom more vibrantly.","...","In the meeting tent, the Manchur king Dorgon angrily glared at the plump khan. “Why did you give her to him instead of me?[1]”","He had been drawn to Jiang Luofu’s cold disposition ever since their first meeting. He had requested for Huang Taiji to give her to him several times now, but Huang Taiji turned him down using all sorts of excuses. He'd thought that Huang Taiji simply wasn’t done playing with Jiang Luofu yet.","He was displeased, of course, but in view of Huang Taiji’s greater strength and standing, he'd refrained from saying anything.","However, Huang Taiji had chosen to give Jiang Luofu to a prisoner instead of him. This was too much!","Huang Taiji glared at Dorgon. “She’s my spoil of war. I choose what to do with her. You don’t have a say in whether I give her to you or not.”","Dorgon was infuriated. He stood up and glared at Huang Taiji, placing his hand on his sword handle.","Huang Taiji narrowed his eyes. “Are you challenging me right now?”","Several expressions flickered across Dorgon’s face. In the end, he let out a harrumph, flung his sleeves, and left the room.","Fan Wencheng walked out from the shadows. “That fellow covets your position. You need to guard against him.”","“Don’t worry. He can’t escape my control,” Huang Taiji calmly replied. “What’s the situation in the prison?”","“The deed is sealed.”","“Hmph. That Order maiden pretends to be virtuous and chaste, but she turned out to be a cheap whore.”","1. After Huang Taiji died, Da Yu’er was rumored to have gotten together with Dorgon through levirate marriage (a practice in which a man marries his brother's widow)... but later, when Dorgon died, the Shunzhi Emperor exhumed Dorgon’s corpse and mutilated it. ☜"]},{"number":2895,"title":"Chapter 2895: Chapter 2847: Dissonant Melody","paragraphs":["“It’s because you trained her well, milord. Once we ruin the Order Ceremony, you can boast to the Myriad Worlds about your glorious feat of conquering Order's divine maiden,” Fan Wencheng said fawningly.","“Hah! Order will collapse once we’re done here. Conquering a mere Order divine maiden means nothing compared to that.” Huang Taiji laughed gleefully.","“You’re the first envoy to complete your mission, leaving the other envoys in the dust. I’m sure the great Deity of Annihilation will view you in a different light,” Fan Wencheng complimented him.","Huang Taiji smiled as well, but he felt a surge of contempt. This fellow is doomed to be an underling for the rest of his life. The collapse of Order would mean that I've reached the limit in my path. I’d have a chance to become a universal deity then; there would be no need for me to earn the Deity of Annihilation’s recognition.","...","In the prison, the usually cold and dignified divine maiden looked unkempt. Her smooth black stockings had been ripped into tatters.","Jiang Luofu had been feeling pessimistic and stifled all this while, but in this moment, she suddenly felt as if nothing else was important. As long as I can be with Ah Zu...","She had already felt unprecedented bliss when the two of them bonded their souls back then, but it was only in this instant that she understood what it meant for two bodies and souls to be united as one. This feeling was far richer and deeper than that.","There were even moments that she didn’t think that she was an Order envoy, but a Bliss and Desire worshiper. That thought made her feel like a sinner, yet it was so incredibly tantalizing.","...","Some time later, Huang Taiji came to check on them. When he saw her limping, he couldn’t help but look at Zu An with a bizarre expression.","This fellow is surprisingly violent despite his gentlemanly appearance. He doesn’t hold back.","But Huang Taiji couldn’t care less. He was after something greater. A mere woman was nothing.","“Have you finally found the meaning of life?”","Zu An was baffled. How am I supposed to answer that question?","“I have even given you my empress to express my sincerity. Do you think the Ming emperor would be willing to do the same?” Huang Taiji harrumphed.","Maybe not the empress, but his imperial sister-in-law , Zu An thought.","Sensing Zu An’s hesitation, Huang Taiji pressed on, “You might be unaware, but that woman is not just one of my empresses, but also an Order envoy.”","He reckoned that Jiang Luofu, to uphold her reputation, wouldn’t reveal her true identity. She would most definitely rather be shrugged off as an ordinary woman and be forgotten. Little did he know that Jiang Luofu knew Zu An and had already told him the truth.","Zu An reacted fast. He gasped in shock. “She’s an Order envoy?!”","“Now that you have tainted an Order envoy, there is no place for you in the Order faction. Think about it. We have even turned an Order envoy into our plaything; do you think the Order faction still has a future?” Huang Taiji spoke with a compelling voice that lured one into depravity.","Zu An played along and revealed a look of despair. “What other choice do I have? All I ask is for the great Khan to bestow that woman I met earlier to me.”","He was worried about Jiang Luofu’s safety. Even if the Little Fiend Empress was protecting her, it would still be safer for Jiang Luofu if he could bring her to his side.","“You’re getting ahead of yourself.” Huang Taiji was rendered speechless. “She’s my empress in this world. I can’t bestow her to you. But if you perform well, I may allow the two of you to meet again in the future.”","His empty promise had Zu An scoffing on the inside, though he played along and asked, “Khan, what do you need me to do?”","Even as a Time Scribe, he was still amazed by how adaptable history was. Important events were fixed in place, but subtle changes in the processes could still change the nature of the incident.","Da Yu’er had also convinced Hong Chengchou to submit to Huang Taiji in history.","“Help me conquer the Great Ming.” Huang Taiji looked at the south with fervent eyes.","“Pardon my directness, but you have already crushed the Ming Empire’s main force. Your victory is already set in stone. I don’t think you require my help.” This was Zu An’s biggest doubt.","“Great Ming is still supported by the remaining elders of the Conglomerate. They are not to be underestimated. For one, they resuscitated the Ming dynasty’s ailing finances. It might be at a disadvantage at the moment, but the Ming Empire is ultimately ten times larger than us. If they can unleash the full potential of the Great Ming, we’ll be in danger.” Huang Taiji briefly paused before adding, “Li Zicheng’s army is a threat as well.”","“Li Zicheng?” Zu An was confused. “We already crushed his army. It’s unlikely for him to make a comeback.”","A mere peasant rebel leader was nothing compared to Order’s and Annihilation’s experts.","Huang Taiji shook his head. “Reproduction never lacks soldiers.”","“Reproduction?” Zu An was baffled. He hadn’t expected Li Zicheng to get involved with the Deity of Reproduction.","“I have received news from my sources that Li Zicheng has been bestowed with Reproduction power and is amassing a huge army. Enemies he fights against will be unknowingly assimilated into his group and become his soldiers. We can’t let our guard down against such a formidable opponent.” Huang Taiji looked at Zu An. “You fought against him before, and you’re an expert at strategizing. That’s why I wanted to recruit you.”","“Thank you for your generous compliment, Khan.” Zu An clasped his fist. “May I ask about your true identity, so that I may know which exalted individual I am serving?”","“I am one of the Deity of Annihilation’s eleven envoys, Dissonant Melody.” Huang Taiji stood with an air of grandeur. He was clearly proud of his identity.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat.","The Doomsday Beast who destroyed the Monster World was nothing more than the vanguard. The envoys are bound to be far stronger.","Hold on. There are eleven of them...","He took this chance to ask, “May I know if each of Annihilation’s eleven envoys corresponds to each of the other universal deities?”","His name is Dissonant Melody, and he’s fighting against the Order faction now. His mission is probably something along the lines of destroying the Order faction.","Dissonant Melody glanced at him. “I can see why you’re a Memory envoy. There’s no point withholding the truth from you anymore. Yes, you’re right. The ultimate fate awaiting all beings in the Myriad Worlds is annihilation. The same is true for universal deities.”","Zu An was alarmed. Annihilation is making an enemy out of all the universal deities. Are they not worried about suffering the same fate as the Deity of Death and being lynched to death by the other deities?","“Death has died. Love and Beauty has fallen. After this battle, Order and Reproduction will no longer pose a threat. The annihilation of all things has become inevitable.” Dissonant Melody’s face twisted in frenzy. “Serve Annihilation well, and you may find a seat among us.”"]},{"number":2896,"title":"Chapter 2896: Chapter 2848: I’m Sure You Don’t Want That","paragraphs":["Zu An recalled the times he had foiled Annihilation’s plans. I’d be courting death if I joined the path of Annihilation, though Dissonant Melody doesn’t seem to be aware of the grudge between me and the Deity of Annihilation.","It makes sense. I might have gotten in Annihilation’s way several times, but a universal deity wouldn’t pay much attention to a mere human.","The first time I truly caught the attention of the Deity of Annihilation was during the Deity of Death’s trial, but Mi Li and Meng protected me. Even if the Deity of Annihilation was humiliated by that affair, there's no way they would tell their subordinates about it.","It’s normal for Dissonant Melody not to know about it.","So, Zu An replied with an excited tone.","Dissonant Melody could tell that Zu An wasn't being sincere, but he didn’t mind it. He figured that once the other universal deities fell from grace, Zu An would submit to Annihilation sincerely.","...","The Manchu army continued to advance with unstoppable momentum, breaching even Ningyuan City. The Ming army lost many of its strongholds, though it managed to stand its ground at Shanhai Pass.","Under Second Elder Hermes’ leadership, the remaining soldiers of the Ming army somehow managed to fend against the Manchus time and time again, despite their huge disadvantage.","Zu An had to concede that Hermes was truly a prodigy.","Shanhai Pass also lived up to its reputation as the number one stronghold. He had previously inspected the pass, and its sheer scale was thousands of times larger than that of his previous life. It was equipped with magic formations and star-vanquishing cannons.","That was why Dissonant Melody had failed to breach it.","The Universal Conglomerate had previously intended to subdue the Manchus, re-establish order, and offer this feat as tribute to the Deity of Order. However, after suffering a string of tragic defeats, they had learned their lesson and were focusing solely on defense.","Naturally, it wouldn’t be easy to breach Shanhai Pass when the Ming Empire was focusing solely on defense.","Zu An wasn’t assigned an important post after surrendering. He was left behind in the main camp, though he was happy to idle around. He spent his days gathering information about the Annihilation faction while looking for chances to reunite with Jiang Luofu.","It could have been due to Zu An’s previous request for Dissonant Melody to gift him Jiang Luofu, but the latter had chosen to hide Jiang Luofu deep inside the palace, thus stopping him from making contact with her.","Zu An was ultimately a defector. There were many eyes on him. It wouldn’t be easy for him to find a chance to slip into the palace.","An opportunity appeared one day when Harjol, the empress whom Huang Taiji doted on a lot, summoned him to the palace.","Zu An looked at Jiang Luofu and the Little Fiend Empress, who were seated on an elevated platform due to their high stature. The former was cold and mature, whereas the latter was bewitching. Their clothes were similar, making them look like sisters.","Both Jiang Luofu and the Little Fiend Empress’ eyes lit up upon seeing Zu An, but they couldn’t express their feelings as Huang Taiji had many eyes around them.","The Little Fiend Empress used the continued failure to breach Shanhai Pass as a pretext to ask Zu An if he had any suggestions as a former powerful official of the Ming Dynasty. At the same time, she secretly sent a telepathic message, “Don’t worry, Ah Zu. Little sister Jiang is fine. My previous slip-up nearly resulted in her being humiliated, so I’m keeping her close now.”","“Given the sturdiness of Shanhai Pass, I fear it’ll be impractical to breach it head-on...” Zu An replied on the surface while sending a telepathic message over as well, “It’s a huge relief you’re around. I can’t bear to think about what could have happened otherwise.”","“Hmph! You’re an important official from the Ming Empire. Our Khan went to a great extent to recruit you, but you can’t offer any useful ideas? What use do we have for you?!” The Little Fiend Empress feigned outrage while chuckling in her telepathic message. “That shows that you and little sister Jiang are meant to be. What are the odds of her bumping into you when in such a crisis? Do you know how shocked I was when I heard about it?”","“Please calm down, Your Majesty! While a frontal attack is impractical, we just need to heap pressure on Shanhai Pass. The Ming Empire is facing trouble within its walls. Li Zicheng’s rebel army has regained its momentum and is growing in scale. A change will happen soon, and that will be our Khan’s chance to strike...” Zu An replied with feigned horror, though he spoke gently telepathically, “It’s also fate that I met you under such circumstances.”","“Tsk, what a sweet tongue. That must be how you charmed little sister Jiang into giving you her heart.”","“It’s nowhere as sweet as yours. I’d love to taste it again.”","“There are too many eyes in the palace. I doubt we’ll have a chance any time soon. Speaking of which, what should we do now? Are we going to aid Annihilation in their fight against Order?”","“What’s the current situation within the Annihilation faction? Tell me about their inner structure.”","“Dissonant Melody, as an Annihilation envoy, wields absolute power here. Another notable figure within the faction is the Conqueror King, who is also known as Dorgon in this world. They seem to be on bad terms...”","...","Zu An and the Little Fiend Empress exchanged intelligence while pretending to discuss invading the Ming Empire.","The Little Fiend Empress and Jiang Luofu were currently Huang Taiji’s empresses; it would appear out of place if Zu An stayed for too long. So, he left once it was about time.","Shortly after he left the imperial palace, a cold voice suddenly snorted, “You’re in an illicit relationship with Harjol and Da Yu’er!”","Zu An was horrified. Killing intent flared from him. He knew that they would all be doomed should their relations come to light. He was about to make a move when he suddenly froze up.","Standing before him was a beautiful lady reminiscent of a butterfly. She wore a unique purple and white dress with sleeves resembling a butterfly’s wings.","“Zhao Xiaodie! Why are you here?” Zu An recognized the other party as the daughter of the Cultivation World’s King Qi, Zhao Xiaodie.","The lady paced around Zu An with her hands behind her back. Her lips crept into a smile as she replied tauntingly, “If you can be here, why can’t I?”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Come to think about it, Zhao Xiaodie entered the Annihilation Divine Palace in the Cultivation World. It makes sense for her to appear here.","“I’d have never expected our regal regent to end up as a prisoner. How the tides turn!” Zhao Xiaodie laughed in glee.","Zu An frowned. “Given your strength, I doubt you’d be of high stature in the Annihilation faction. You aren’t in a position to laugh at me.”","“Is that so?” Zhao Xiaodie snorted. “I should let you know that I’m a Qing princess!”","“A princess?” Zu An narrowed his eyes. “You’re Dorgon’s daughter in this world?”","“That’s right!” Zhao Xiaodie’s eyebrows shot up in glee. I finally see why novels love their cliched black horse trope. I didn’t know turning the tables on an enemy could feel so good.","After feeling his overwhelming strength in the Cultivation World, she'd thought she would never be able to exact vengeance against Zu An. But fate could be truly wondrous at times.","“What do you want?” Zu An asked grimly. Even though they shared an intimate history, judging from her current attitude, that could have been an act. In the worst-case scenario, he could have to silence her, but even that wouldn't necessarily be enough to conceal the truth.","“I’m sure you don’t want Huang Taiji to know your secret, right?” Zhao Xiaodie looked as gleeful as a little fox."]},{"number":2897,"title":"Chapter 2897: Chapter 2849: Ally","paragraphs":["Zu An was speechless. It kind of feels as if our roles are reversed.","“Aren’t you afraid that I might silence you?” Zu An surveyed the surroundings and confirmed that there was no one in the vicinity, but he still suppressed the urge to make a move.","This woman isn’t a fool. She must have prepared a hand before confronting me here.","“Forget it. We used to be friends, after all. State your conditions.”","Zhao Xiaodie’s eyes shook. Her smile widened as she said, “My entire clan died at your hands. Did you honestly think we were friends?”","“King Qi and I were merely in opposite camps; I have no grudge against you,” Zu An said with a sigh. “I thought that we were friends, but I now see that it was wishful thinking on my part.”","“Pui! Your mouth spews lies without missing a beat!” Zhao Xiaodie gritted her teeth in anger, but she eventually heaved a sigh and said, “There are so many reasons why I should hate you, and I often remind myself of the blood debt between us. But for some reason, I struggle to do so.”","Zu An was stunned. He hadn’t expected her to see him in such a light.","“After entering the Annihilation Divine Palace, I gained knowledge from all over the Myriad Worlds. It seems as if I'm suffering from something known as Stockholm syndrome,” Zhao Xiaodie said in self-derision.","“From the moment you chose your Divine Palace, you should have understood that even though there are countless paths in this world, only by following your heart will your mind truly open up. You don’t need to overthink things,” Zu An said.","“You always know the right words to say. It’s a good thing you didn’t make a move earlier, or else that could have hardened my determination.”","Zu An gently replied, “I'm not a vicious person. In the end, you're a victim yourself.”","“Hmph. You claim not to be vicious, but you struck my butt so hard back then...” Zhao Xiaodie’s face reddened, and she was too embarrassed to continue the topic. “Cough cough. My father is the one looking for you.”","“Your father?” Zu An was taken aback. Did King Qi return to life?","Zhao Xiaodie hurriedly explained, “In this world, I’m Dorgon’s daughter. He’s the Annihilation faction’s Conqueror King, wielding strength that nearly rivals the Annihilation envoys.”","Zu An recalled the brief overview that the Little Fiend Empress had provided him regarding the Annihilation faction. He asked contemplatively, “Why is he looking for me?”","“He’s probably thinking about recruiting you to his side. You’re a surrendered official. It would be wise not to offend him,” Zhao Xiaodie advised.","Zu An hadn’t expected her to worry about him. “Thank you.”","“Hmph. I’m not doing this for you. I have no allies in the Annihilation faction, and you can be somewhat considered an acquaintance. Let’s help each other from now on.” Zhao Xiaodie wasn't very sure what she was doing either.","“Of course. Our old grudges in the Cultivation World mean nothing in the Myriad Worlds.”","Zhao Xiaodie led Zu An to the Conqueror King’s residence. Dorgon welcomed him warmly.","When it was about time, Dorgon casually asked, “Don’t you find it a pity that someone of your capabilities isn’t able to put their skills to good use?”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. This is it. The Conqueror King is subtly trying to drive a wedge between me and Huang Taiji. “I am a surrendered official. The Annihilation faction is filled with talents. There’s no place for me to shine.”","“That’s not the main issue. Ultimately, your tie with the empress is a thorn in our Khan’s heart.”","Zu An thought that the Conqueror King was doing a terrible job of sowing discord. Dissonant Melody, being an Annihilation envoy, was unlikely to be fazed by romance. But he played along and replied, “I didn’t know she was the Khan’s empress. I wouldn’t have had the guts to touch her otherwise.”","“I wouldn’t put that beyond your guts. I've already heard about your affairs from Xiaodie,” the Conqueror King replied.","Zu An was taken aback. He glanced at Zhao Xiaodie while wondering what she had told the Conqueror King.","“You don’t need to be afraid. I only chose to reach out to you after hearing about your accomplishments. I won’t beat around the bush. I want you to aid me in overtaking Dissonant Melody’s authority!” the Conqueror King said.","Zu An was stunned. This fellow sure is straightforward.","“Dissonant Melody is an Annihilation envoy. I don’t think I have the power to interfere in your fight.”","The Conqueror King harrumphed. “You don’t need to be so humble. You’re a Memory envoy yourself. While the aura you emanate is weak, a person’s strength is built on an amalgamation of factors. Xiaodie has told me about your exploits, and I've seen your performance in the Ming Court. You are a capable person.”","“I’m flattered by your compliment, Conqueror King.”","“Stop beating around the bush and give me a straight answer. Will you join me or not?”","Zhao Xiaodie frantically blinked at Zu An, urging him to accept the offer. The Conqueror King had already revealed his intentions honestly. If Zu An turned him down, the chances were that he wouldn’t be able to walk out of this room alive.","But Zu An didn’t give a straight answer to the question. Instead, he said, “There must be a basis behind your confidence for you to scheme something like this. I want to know what cards you're holding. Otherwise, I’d just be walking to my doom by joining you blindly. I’d rather not go through so much trouble just to die.”","Zhao Xiaodie panicked. The Conqueror King is the one assessing you here, so why are you questioning him instead? Fearing that the latter would lose his temper, she tried to speak up to dissipate the tension.","Unexpectedly, the Conqueror King burst into laughter. “Good, good! You are indeed a talent. To be frank, I’d have doubted your intentions if you had joined us without asking any questions. You could have turned around and sold me out to Dissonant Melody right after.","“Dissonant Melody might be an Annihilation envoy, but I’m not any weaker than him. The only difference between us is that he wields the authority of an Annihilation envoy. Through years of observation, I discovered that he has a fatal flaw.”","“A fatal flaw?”","“I can’t delve into the details. All you need to know is that I have the power to deal with him. You’re a snubbed, surrendered official under him, but under me, you’ll be able to unleash your talent. I’ll let you aid me in conquering this world. A merit of this scale will surely earn you the universal deity’s acknowledgment. That will become an invaluable stepping stone for you to join the Annihilation faction.”","“Very well. I shall join you.”","Zu An could only marvel at the wondrous machinations of fate.","In history, Dorgon’s and Huang Taiji’s factions were also fraught with conflict. Who could have thought that they would be fighting like that within Annihilation’s faction as well?","He had been thinking hard, looking for a solution to this quandary, but he'd been lacking an impetus. That impetus had finally come.","The Conqueror King was overjoyed. “Hahaha! Now that we've joined hands, success is within reach. I heard from Xiaodie that you are an intelligent man with many ideas. How do you think we should deal with Dissonant Melody?”"]},{"number":2898,"title":"Chapter 2898: Chapter 2850: Upheaval In the Palace","paragraphs":["Zu An realized that this was the Conqueror King’s test. If he couldn’t answer this question well, he could lose his say in this alliance. In the worst-case scenario, the Conqueror King could even abandon and kill him.","Fortunately, he had already given much thought to this question. He was able to answer right away, “It'd be easy to kill him, but the bigger problem is how to make him die reasonably; otherwise, his subordinates could notice an anomaly and turn against us.”","The Conqueror King’s eyes lit up. “My thoughts exactly. What ideas do you have?”","“Dissonant Melody has a plump figure and an unusually red face. Has he ever suffered from cultivation deviation?” Zu An asked.","The Conqueror King was awed. “You’re right. He cultivated a highly domineering skill in his earlier years, which resulted in his body accumulating excessive vitality. To make things worse, he has absorbed the energies of many different experts over the years. It might have been nothing much at the start, but absorbing the energy of the Holy Knight Order’s Captain Augustus seems to have been the tipping point. It triggered all the underlying issues in his body that have accumulated.","“He's been suffering from frequent nosebleeds that easily fill dozens of bowls. If not for his overwhelming strength, he would have been dead by now.”","This was the trump card he'd uncovered from many years of investigation. He hadn’t been planning to share this information with Zu An, but who could have thought that the latter would notice it on his own?","“Let’s work on that. Get your subordinates to spread the news and exaggerate it, so that others won’t doubt a thing even if he drops dead abruptly,” Zu An said.","The Conqueror King nodded. “That can be done. The bigger problem is how we can kill him. I can design a ploy to assassinate him, and there’s a good chance of pulling it off. The problem is that given his strength, I won’t be able to do it discreetly. The commotion will inevitably draw the attention of others.”","Zu An spent a moment in thought before asking, “Is Dissonant Melody deeply in love with Empress Harjol right now?”","“He is. It is rather unusual for someone of his stature to fall in love with an indigenous woman from this world, though.” The Conqueror King was perplexed. “His affection for Harjol transcends normal boundaries. He might have sent Da Yu’er to convince you into submission, but there’s no way he could bear to let Harjol do the same.”","Zhao Xiaodie had a peculiar expression. She had known all along that Harjol was the Little Fiend Empress, but she'd chosen to withhold the information, thinking that it could prove valuable in times of need.","Now that she thought about it, the Little Fiend Empress was quite the impressive figure. The latter had first bewitched the old Fiend Emperor, then gotten Regent Zu An wrapped around her thumb; and now, she had completely won over the Annihilation envoy as well. It was almost as if she wielded some kind of sorcery that made experts fall in love with her.","Should I find a chance to seek advice from her?","“It seems the key lies with Harjol.”","“But Harjol and Dissonant Melody are in love with each other. Where can we strike from?”","“I’ll figure something out.”","“No wonder Xiaodie says you’re good with women. I’m impressed.”","“...”","Months passed, but the Manchu army was still unable to breach Shanhai Pass, which was guarded by Second Elder Hermes.","Dissonant Melody finally thought about Zu An and summoned him. “You participated in the discussions of the Order faction’s upper echelons. Do you have any ideas to overcome this impasse?”","“Hermes manages all of the Universal Conglomerate’s business deals. With his capability, there’s nothing much we can do if he remains steadfast in his defense. However, he has a weakness that we can exploit,” Zu An replied confidently.","“What is it?” Dissonant Melody hurriedly asked.","“He’s a sentimental person, and there is one woman who can become his downfall.”","“Everyone knows that Hermes fell in love with a woman back when he was younger, but no one knows who that woman is. Even if we know her identity, there’s no way we can find her in this world,” Dissonant Melody said with a frown.","“I might have a solution,” Zu An replied.","“What is it?” Dissonant Melody’s eyes lit up.","“Based on my interactions with him, he might have found a woman in this world who greatly resembles his past lover. If I head to Great Ming’s capital and make a move on that woman, we might be able to overcome this impasse,” Zu An replied.","“You want to enter Great Ming’s capital?” Dissonant Melody was stunned, but he soon replied with a smile, “We’re at war right now. You’ll be in trouble if someone discovers your identity. Why don’t you tell me who that woman is, and I’ll send someone to deal with her?”","Zu An sighed. Dissonant Melody doesn’t trust me. He fears that I’ll escape to the capital and never return. That would mean he sent Da Yu’er to me for nothing. “I’m not sure about the woman’s identity. I have to verify it in person first. We need to tread carefully, as if we alarm them, there won’t be a second chance.”","His plan upon arriving at the capital was to first look for Chen Yuanyuan to resolve his doubts before secretly meeting Isabella and Zheng Dan, lest they think he was really dead.","His words did little to dispel DIssonant Melody’s doubts. In the end, the latter didn’t agree to it.","When Zu An was taking his leave, Dissonant Melody suddenly remarked, “I heard that Princess Xiaodie is very fond of you. You’re good at winning the fancy of ladies.”","Zu An responded with a polite smile, but his heart turned cold. Dissonant Melody is trying to sound me out. Zhao Xiaodie is currently Dorgon’s daughter, yet she’s meeting me frequently. That’s bound to make people wonder what my relationship with Dorgon is.","If Dissonant Melody finds evidence of my alliance with Dorgon, he’ll surely kill us right away.","We can’t wait any longer...","Without any hesitation, he secretly slipped into Dorgon’s residence, and the two of them spent a long time hashing out their plans.","That night, Dissonant Melody made his way to Harjol’s bedroom as usual. Just thinking about her soft body, bewitching disposition, and understanding nature was enough to send a gush of heat through his body.","He had seen all kinds of beauties over the years, but none had moved him as much as her.","Even Order's divine maiden was a plaything to him. He had only married her to insult her, evident from how he had sent her to wait on other men. There was no way he would bear to send Harjol to do such a thing.","A wondrous time of relaxation and pleasure followed. Once again, he had to concede that Harjol was a woman among women. He had never felt such exhilaration from anyone else. To top it off, she'd called her little sister, Da Yu’er, over, so that the two of them could wait on him together.","What a virtuous woman!","But Dissonant Melody vaguely sensed that something was off today. It was a weird feeling of unreality, as if he was floating on clouds.","All of a sudden, his protective artifact activated. Something was attacking him.","An ancient copper coin appeared in midair, and all his protective artifacts were immediately rendered ineffective. It was the Treasure Sinking Coin!","A sword surged toward Dissonant Melody right after.","Dissonant Melody sneered. His greatest strength was to unleash destruction by altering the laws of the world. From the moment the Treasure Sinking Coin took effect, he had already rewritten the laws around himself to render all attacks ineffective.","To his horror, the sword pierced through his distorted laws!","It was none other than the Slaughter Fang[1]. This weapon could pierce through all defenses and was impervious to all laws, including distorted laws.","Exploiting the opening created by the Slaughter Fang, a pitch-black dagger surged in and slit Dissonant Melody's skin—the Poisonous Prick.","“Death’s divine power!” Dissonant Melody narrowed his eyes in shock. How could an envoy like him hope to alter the laws set by a universal deity?","1. The tooth taken from the Lord of Slaughter upon his death. Zu An said he would make it into a weapon later. ☜"]},{"number":2899,"title":"Chapter 2899: Chapter 2851: Spring and Autumn Calligraphy","paragraphs":["Dissonant Melody wasn't an Annihilation envoy for nothing. When he was on the verge of death, he suddenly unleashed a violent counterattack, determined to drag everyone around him down as well.","Just then, he saw a brush flowing across the air, drawing out a brilliant river that reflected the rise and destruction of countless nations, as well as the lifetimes of heroes and generals. It was the river of history!","His terrifying attack was scattered in the river of history, failing to hurt anyone in real life.","“Annals of History!” Dissonant Melody recognized the move as a Memory skill.","It’s that fellow!","It was all over.","Dissonant Melody was powerful, but Death’s power gnawed away at him until he had barely a breath left. He surveyed his surroundings with widened eyes, shocked that his beloved Harjol was simply standing off to the side, not intervening at all.","“Why?”","This question was neither directed at Zu An nor to Jiang Luofu. The former was in the enemy camp, whereas the latter was Order's divine maiden. It was understandable for them to move against him.","But why is Harjol not helping me?","The Little Fiend Empress let out a sigh. “Because I've been Ah Zu’s woman all along.”","She took her place next to Zu An.","Dissonant Melody spat out a huge puddle of blood. “Impossible. Was the time you spent with me all an act?”","You have successfully trolled Dissonant Melody for +999... +999... +999...","What could plunge a man deeper into despair than witnessing his beloved woman walking into another man’s arms?","The Little Fiend Empress twirled her finger, and five-colored lights swirled around her, emanating a sweet fragrance of lust.","Dissonant Melody had accrued enough knowledge in his lifetime to understand what he was seeing. He widened his eyes in disbelief and roared, “The power of Bliss and Desire! Everything I felt was a mere illusion! How could I have...”","He felt his life nearing its limit, but his face remained twisted. “You adulterous couple! I won't spare you even as a ghost!”","With that, he breathed his last, though he wasn’t worried in the slightest.","Entities like him had not just a powerful body, but a powerful soul as well. Even when his body died, he could still exert considerable prowess through his soul. On top of that, he had plenty of ways to return to life. He would make those who betrayed him regret ever being born.","Zu An sighed. “You won’t have a chance.”","Dissonant Melody’s soul tore itself away from his body to flee toward a place where he had kept a secret hand. With Annihilation power protecting his soul, death wasn't the end for him.","However, he suddenly felt extreme cold. It was a feeling of subjugation coming from the depths of his soul.","“How is this possible?!” Dissonant Melody couldn’t understand how he felt such deep fear toward Zu An despite being the stronger one here. It felt as if his very existence hinged on Zu An’s will. Furthermore, this feeling had only arisen after he died.","Zu An stared at Dissonant Melody calmly. Since he'd made a move, he was going to do a clean job and not risk trouble in the future.","He opened the Netherworld Book of Life and Death and invoked his authority as the Netherworld’s master. At his will, the powerful soul before him disintegrated.","“You are Death’s succe...”","Dissonant Melody couldn’t finish speaking. A powerhouse vanished just like that.","Zu An used the Kunpeng and Taotie’s devouring ability to absorb Dissonant Melody’s energy, and he could feel his strength growing rapidly. Dissonant Melody did live up to his reputation as a top-notch expert.","Zu An felt dazed. He had been fighting and absorbing the energies of all kinds of formidable foes. Before he knew it, he had suddenly reached level 90.","It had been a long while since he paid any attention to his level, as he hadn’t thought that the leveling system corresponded well with the Myriad Worlds’ power scaling. His level only made the experts of other worlds think that he was very weak, causing them to misjudge his strength.","But what did Dissonant Melody’s final words mean? Am I destined to be Death’s successor?","He'd definitely noticed his intricate ties with Death, such as the Netherworld Book of Life and Death, the Necropolis Emperor, and the Poisonous Prick. From the looks of it, the Poisonous Prick could have been the weapon used by the Deity of Death back then.","“Ah Zu, are you all right?” the Little Fiend Empress and Jiang Luofu anxiously asked Zu An. Both of them had sensed the terrifying power harnessed by Dissonant Melody’s dying counterattack.","“I’m fine. It’s all thanks to the two of you cooperating with me.” Zu An held their hands.","The Conqueror King had shared with him in elaborate detail Dissonant Melody’s cultivation and abilities. The one who knows you the best is not yourself, but your enemy.","On top of that, Dorgon had used his authority to dispatch Dissonant Melody’s aides elsewhere, leaving the latter unguarded. Even so, Zu An couldn’t have done this without the help of the Little Fiend Empress and Jiang Luofu.","Jiang Luofu had used her Order power to construct a space most suitable for them to counteract Dissonant Melody’s distorted laws. That had played a vital role in how Zu An killed Dissonant Melody so easily.","Now that their greatest enemy was dead, Jiang Luofu finally relaxed. “I didn’t help much. The Little Fiend Empress' ability is what’s truly formidable. To think that she plunged an Annihilation envoy into an illusion.”","The Little Fiend Empress looked melancholic. “As powerful as the Deity of Bliss and Desire’s power is, its effects would have been greatly weakened if he wasn’t willing to believe in them.”","JIang Luofu was truly impressed with the Little Fiend Empress' ability to deal with men, but it felt almost like an insult to compliment her in that aspect.","Zu An sensed the Little Fiend Empress' woe. “Are you thinking about your special constitution again?”","The Little Fiend Empress nodded. “My Sacred Widow Body is a curse. Anyone who marries me will not have a good end. Ah Zu, you must never have any title with me.”","That had been the case with the Fiend Emperor, and it was the same for Dissonant Melody as well. Even though they were only a couple in name, he couldn’t avoid the fate of random death. She was extremely worried that she would jinx Zu An as well.","Zu An pulled her into his embrace and consoled her.","Some time later, the two women looked at Dissonant Melody’s corpse with worried eyes. “What should we do next?”","Dissonant Melody had a huge following of loyal subjects. If they made a wrong move here, it could result in their doom.","“That’s easy.” Zu An smiled. He revealed the plan he'd devised beforehand to them.","They disposed of Dissonant Melody’s body, then Zu An impersonated Dissonant Melody using Myriad Transformations.","On a random day, Empress Harjol abruptly passed away from illness. Due to extreme grief, ‘Huang Taiji’s’ accumulated traumas from his cultivation deviation suddenly acted up, resulting in him becoming far weaker than before.","Whenever ‘Huang Taiji’ spoke with people from the Annihilation faction, he subtly let slip the immense sorrow and desolation he harbored in his heart, which became an omen to those around him.","One night, his symptoms suddenly acted up, and he died in the palace.","This process was written down using Zu An's ability as a Time Scribe, so no one doubted anything.","‘Dorgon’ hadn’t thought that ‘Huang Taiji’ would pass away just like that, but he was still overjoyed. However, he soon realized that his celebration was premature. ‘Huang Taiji’ still had many loyal subjects, and they supported his son in claiming authority.","So, ‘Dorgon’ decided to marry his ‘daughter’, Zhao Xiaodie, off to Zu An to win him over, in hopes that the latter would aid him in claiming the Annihilation envoy’s authority."]},{"number":2900,"title":"Chapter 2900: Chapter 2852: The End of Order","paragraphs":["Zu An didn’t turn down the marriage. He was no longer the innocent man he was. He understood that marriage wasn't just about love—one had to consider the pros and cons as well.","‘Dorgon’ had many enemies and needed to secure as many aides as possible. Refusing the offer to marry his daughter could sully their ties, resulting in them becoming enemies. It was especially important to band together during such times of danger and avoid making more enemies.","Besides, Zhao Xiaodie had helped him a lot this time. In particular, she'd kept the Little Fiend Empress’ and Jiang Luofu’s identities a secret from even ‘Dorgon’. He had to return this favor to her.","Of course, he didn’t dislike Zhao Xiaodie either, so he didn’t mind them being tied to the same ship.","Dissonant Melody had several sons, but none of them had been born through physical reproduction. He had kneaded them from dissonances in universal laws into cacophonies and granted them a sense of self.","His eldest son, Defiant Providence, wielded the power to distort prophecies and fate, compelling them to flow in the opposite direction. In this world, he took on the identity of Huang Taiji’s oldest son, Hooge. Naturally, he hoped to inherit his father’s authority.","The Conqueror King was on bad terms with him, so he tried to stop him. A bitter fight ensued, and it ended in a stalemate.[1]","Dissonant Melody’s subordinates were more favorable toward having his sons inherit his authority, but the Conqueror King wielded great influence as well. In fact, the Conqueror King had nearly become an Annihilation envoy back then.","Both the Conqueror King and Dissonant Melody had been created by the Deity of Annihilation, making them brothers. The Conqueror King was supposed to become an envoy, but an incident resulted in Dissonant Melody taking his place instead.","In other words, the Conqueror King had the legitimacy to inherit the Annihilation envoy's authority as well.","With both sides wielding comparable power and possessing legitimacy, neither was willing to yield to the other. The situation was extremely tense.","The Conqueror King visited Zu An with flames blazing in his eyes to ask the latter if he had any solutions to break the stalemate. He suspected that Zu An was behind Dissonant Melody’s quiet death, but no matter how he worked his imagination, he couldn’t figure out how the latter had done it.","In the end, he could only conclude that Dissonant Melody’s accumulated traumas had simply acted up. Otherwise, it would be too shocking if Zu An pulled it off alone.","Nevertheless, he still saw Zu An as someone with wits, courage, and luck. The latter could just have a solution for his quandary.","Zu An was already prepared for his arrival. “How confident would you be if it culminates into a fight?”","The Conqueror King spent a moment in thought before replying, “I am 60% confident of winning the battle.”","He was stronger than Defiant Providence, but Dissonant Melody still had many loyal subordinates. That was a considerable force that couldn’t be overlooked.[2]","“Assuming that you win the battle, would you still have the strength to subdue the Order faction’s Ming Empire and the Reproduction faction’s Li Zicheng?” Zu An asked.","The Conqueror King’s face stiffened. He also understood that even if he won the fight against Defiant Providence, it would be a narrow one. The Annihilation faction would surely suffer heavy losses, putting them in no position to deal with the Order faction and the Reproduction faction.","He was well aware that it didn’t matter to the Deity of Annihilation who the envoy was, be it him, Dissonant Melody, or Defiant Providence. But if they screwed this matter up, even if he obtained the envoy’s authority, the Deity of Annihilation would still strip it from him.","“Am I supposed to hand over the fruits of my hard work to Defiant Providence just like that?”","The thought of that outcome made the Conqueror King feel like spewing blood. Even his subordinates wouldn’t accept such an outcome!","“Of course not. Now that you’re at a stalemate, it’s only natural that neither side would allow the other to advance. However, there is a solution, and that is for both sides to take a step back.”","“How?”","“Both of you will relinquish the envoy position and instead grant it to one of Dissonant Melody’s younger and weaker sons. Dissonant Melody’s subordinates will not object to that, and upon losing their support, Defiant Providence won’t be able to stir any waves.","“That son will be grateful to you for supporting his rise to power. Furthermore, he’ll need your power to deal with his other brothers, who are vying for authority as well. You can exploit the situation to become the regent. When time is finally ripe, you can reclaim the authority.”","The Conqueror King’s eyes lit up. “You are indeed a talent! This is the perfect solution!” This fellow isn’t a Memory envoy at all. He’s obviously a member of the Chaos and Enigma faction!","Upon further discussion, they chose Dissonant Melody’s ninth son, Confounding Crossroads. In this world, he was Huang Taiji’s youngest son with Da Yu’er, Fulin.","The Conqueror King noticed that this was part of Zu An’s scheme to make Jiang Luofu the empress dowager in name, but he didn’t mind it. That woman was indeed required to stabilize the imperial harem.","During the Annihilation faction’s upper echelon meeting, the Conqueror King first angered Defiant Providence into marching out before exploiting his absence to reveal the proposal.","Unsurprisingly, many of the Annihilation faction’s higher-ups had grown weary of the ongoing infighting and wanted to avoid the worst-case scenario. When they realized that the proposal was to everyone’s benefit, they swiftly approved it.","Defiant Providence nearly spat blood when he learned about it. He considered declaring war against the Conqueror King there and then, but none of his father’s old subordinates supported him in that. He couldn’t turn around the situation by himself.","In the end, under the elders’ persuasion, he accepted the outcome. It was at least better than letting the Conqueror King obtain the authority.","Both sides joined forces once more to discuss invading the Central Plains and defeating the Order faction and the Reproduction faction.","Meanwhile, much had changed in the Central Plains.","Li Zicheng had made a huge comeback. Fourth Elder Mastema couldn’t stop his rise at all, so Li Zicheng’s peasant rebel army snowballed at a shocking pace.","To make things worse, the Fourth Elder didn’t report the true situation in the northwest to the imperial court. Perhaps he feared blame or wanted to deal with it himself, since Zu An had, at one point, crushed Li Zicheng till he was only left with eighteen cavalrymen. As a result, the imperial court devoted all its efforts to dealing with the Annihilation faction in the northeast.","Due to their previous armies being wiped out, the imperial court had to increase the taxes to recruit and train new soldiers. In their view, they had already quelled the peasant rebel army, so the momentum had already died down. The priority at hand was to deal with the Annihilation faction.","News only broke when the Fourth Elder’s city was breached, and the Fourth Elder himself died in battle. Only then did the upper echelons in Beijing realize that the situation was much worse than they had expected.","They quickly dispatched men to quell the rebellion.","Fortunately, many competent individuals had participated in the Order Ceremony, and they took on the roles of renowned generals such as Lu Xiangsheng and Sun Chuanting. These people won a series of battles, but they were unable to reverse the tides.","The power of Reproduction had spread. The peasant rebel army was growing at an exponential pace. The rate at which the Order generals were quelling the rebels turned out to be slower than the rate of the rebel army’s recruitment.","In the end, these renowned generals were outnumbered and defeated in battle. Their deaths caused a huge stir.","Everyone knew that it was over for the imperial court. Wherever Li Zicheng’s army appeared, the local military leaders would read the winds and surrender. It didn’t take long for the rebel army to reach Beijing.","Meanwhile, the Annihilation army was still kept outside Shanhai Pass by the Second Elder’s army. They panicked, fearing that the Reproduction faction would claim ultimate victory at this rate.","So, they sent Zu An to the capital to look for the woman who was the Second Elder’s weakness.","1. There was a fight between Hooge and Dorgon in history over the throne as well, but in the end, both of them came to a compromise and allowed the Ninth Prince Fulin to take the throne instead. ☜","2. In history, Hooge (Defiant Providence) inherited his father’s troops, which were the Upper Three Banners. ☜"]}]);
